id:640f137a021e733fcd018f83 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription "Proudly serving the community for more than 35 years, we are a leading UK Hospice providing inpatient and community palliative and end-of-life care services to people aged 16 and over across East Berkshire and South Buckinghamshire.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/0128825b-f495-436c-b218-8b56f5fd1678_2023-03-13T12:13:45.850Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Thames Hospice";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.thameshospice.org.uk/>.
id:640f1da74e4230f618e17f70 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """St Barnabas Hospice is a local independent charity and every year they support more than 9,000 people across Lincolnshire. They deliver free, high-quality, compassionate end-of-life care and support to adults living with a life-limiting or terminal illness, their family and carers.

St Barnabas offers the patient and their family hospice care and support via: specialist in-patient care, community ‘hospice at home’ service, day therapy, physiotherapy, occupational therapy & complementary therapy, welfare advice & support and bereavement support. All the services are free.

St Barnabas needs to raise over £5.5m a year to provide its support and care. Over 1,000 volunteers play a crucial role in the charity’s success.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/3361ebd8-3a4e-47ce-9af4-783e8691eafd_2023-03-13T12:59:01.992Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "St Barnabas Hospice";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://stbarnabashospice.co.uk/>.
id:640f1ddb4e4230f618e17f90 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "Julia’s House is not a typical children’s hospice. We provide practical and emotional support for families caring for a child with a life-limiting or life-threatening condition, providing frequent and regular support in their own homes, in the community or at our hospices.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/525d79aa-dfad-4a77-a732-6f20c6aa9ea5_2023-03-13T12:58:02.687Z.svg+xml>;
                            :organisationName "Julia's House Dorset & Wiltshire Children's Hospice";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.juliashouse.org/>.
id:640f31a8a02daffd7c36acfd :activityDescription "We would love to spread the word about our services here at Thames Hospice, please watch the video found on our Youtube Channel here: https://youtu.be/PUB81QhOB9o and then let your friends and family know what we do to support patients and their families facing life limiting illnesses.  ";
                            :activityOrganisation id:640f137a021e733fcd018f83;
                            :activityTitle "Find out about hospice and palliative care at Thames Hospice".
id:640f32af3d50e6d1eb9c7bad :activityDescription """Spend an hour clearing out your closet of any unwanted clothing, jewellery, books, DVDs, bric-a-brac and donate it all to Thames Hospice to help raise vital funds for specialist care for patients and their families when facing life limiting illnesses. 
We are open for donations on Monday 8th May at many of our shops, including: Bracknell, Camberley, Caversham, Gerrards Cross, Henley, Langley, Maidenhead, Windsor, Woodley, Dedworth, Wokingham and our Home store in Maidenhead. 
Thank you! """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:640f137a021e733fcd018f83;
                            :activityTitle "Clear out your Closet!".
id:640f45a78357cdfdce174514 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba5089b;
                            :organisationDescription """PDSA has over 100 community charity shops around the UK. Each one plays a huge role in raising the funds needed to care for the animals that arrive across our 48 pet hospitals each day. 

The success of our charity shops is all down to our amazing team of volunteers, and we urgently need your help to continue the life-changing work we do at PDSA. """;
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/2824967f-4052-4fdd-986e-fdb597e8ebe6_2023-03-14T12:05:44.923Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "People's Dispensary for Sick Animals  - PDSA";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.pdsa.org.uk/get-involved/volunteer>.
id:640f490c06c17cf4e1a808fd :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "Through our volunteer drivers we provide a pre-booked car service. Whilst a lot of our trips are for medical appointments, we can also take our passengers wherever they want to go. We urgently need more volunteer drivers. So, if you own a car and have some spare time please contact us on 01904 630080.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/abcefa8f-e851-4a4b-ae5a-344c261c5d34_2023-03-13T16:02:18.773Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "York Wheels Ltd";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.yorkwheels.org.uk/>.
id:640f4c22de33aaa483ed3619 :activityDescription "Through our Volunteer Drivers we provide a pre-booked car service for the elderly or disabled in York. Whilst a lot of our trips are for medical appointments, we can also take our  passengers wherever they want to go. So, if you own a car and have some spare time then please call us on 01904 630080. You can choose the hours, and days, which you work and you will be reimbursed for your car expenses on HMRC guideline rates.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:640f490c06c17cf4e1a808fd;
                            :activityTitle "Looking for Volunteer Drivers".
id:640f55f6185ebeaed23d95e4 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """Our vision is a world free from the fear, harm and heartbreak of dementia.
Our mission is to accelerate progress towards a cure.

If nothing changes, one in two of us will be directly affected by dementia – either by developing the condition ourselves, caring for someone with it, or both.

As the UK’s leading dementia research charity, we’re determined to stop this from becoming a reality.

We’re working to revolutionise the way we treat, diagnose and prevent dementia. But we will not stop there.

With your support, we will keep going until every person is free from the heartbreak of dementia. We exist for a cure.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/517ab4d4-3155-41f1-a2fe-d52532d5aa15_2025-03-31T11:23:25.022Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Alzheimer's Research UK";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.alzheimersresearchuk.org/>.
id:640f82aa999365a43398c57b :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """We are the charity that supports people as they become parents. We're here for you through pregnancy, birth, and early parenthood.

Our charity has a proud 65-year history of creating transformative change in the lives of parents. We are a trusted voice, a reassuring presence and a strong advocate, campaigning on the issues that matter most.

Today, we are a membership charity and a strong community of volunteers, practitioners, peer supporters, staff, students, advocates, and campaigners. We have a huge opportunity to positively influence the experience of millions more people as they become parents and to shape a bright future together. 
""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/0b73e514-ba1c-4f41-b8ee-46f6f9afe7cc_2023-03-13T20:26:30.335Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "NCT";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://nct.org.uk/>.
id:640f8491628b687cc5df579a :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription """Werrington Neighbourhood Council was established over 50 years ago and its aims are to:

- Represent and promote the best interests of the inhabitants of Werrington,
- Act as a forum for local opinion on planning proposals, amenities, the local environment and the development of the local area
- To improve the environment of the area and the condition of life for its inhabitants by working in partnership with Peterborough City Council and other agencies.
- To establish and maintain a Neighbourhood Forum, for the express purpose of promoting and improving the social, economic and environmental well-being of Werrington.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/874c1aef-3e8a-433b-8eb0-d7d9aa8b8298_2023-03-13T20:16:15.125Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Werrington Neighbourhood Environment Group and Neighbourhood Council (Peterborough)";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.werrington.org.uk/>.
id:640f8c15628b687cc5df5861 :activityDescription """WILDLIFE FRIENDLY WERRINGTON: Recording the Flora for Werrington
We aim to record the plant species that grow wild in Werrington. We want everyone to help us record the plant species in each if the nine 1km squares that Werrington covers

1) Download the iNaturalist App. You can find out more at www.inaturalist.org

2) Under the Projects Tab, find Wildlife Friendly Werrington and press 'Join'

3) Whilst out on your local walks, via the app, take photos of the leaves and flowers you see (or upload your photos to the website)

4) The system will identify them for you and will record their location on the map

This is a GREAT way to find out more about the environment 
This will help guide local conservation management plans. We can’t conserve something if we don’t know it’s there!
This will help monitor change
This will add knowledge to national databases. The information you record will be deposited with the Botanical Society of British Isles.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:640f8491628b687cc5df579a;
                            :activityTitle "Let's Record Werrington's Wildlife (Peterborough)".
id:640f928986d09cd3570ae2cf :activityDescription """Follow NCT Charity on Insta, Twitter or Facebook and share our stories, campaign and events with your friends to help us spread the word about what we do and how we support parents. 


""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:640f82aa999365a43398c57b;
                            :activityTitle "Show your support on social".
id:640f950b86d09cd3570ae32d :activityDescription """Getting out and about as a new parent can be a huge challenge and many new parents worry about what people might say if their baby starts crying in a public place or they need to feed their baby. 

You can take action and show your support for all new parents simply by sharing a smile, offering a kind word or holding a door open for a new parent struggling with a pram. 

Find more info about how we support parents on our website - www.nct.org.uk or get involved at www.nct.org.uk/volunteering""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:640f82aa999365a43398c57b;
                            :activityTitle "Show your support for a parent with a smile".
id:640f97e786d09cd3570ae401 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """We are based at in Thurnby, and are part of both Girlguiding and the Scout Association.

We are a thriving group with currently about 100 children meeting regularly in the different sections. We cater for both girls and boys between 4  and 25 in a range of activities and opportunities.

Each group has a tailor-made programme planned with the young members. Meetings include a variety of activities including making crafts, playing games, learning new skills and having fun with friends. There are also many opportunities to earn a badge or two and take part in any additional trips and events.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/b47d759b-0702-48f9-b4c2-3ddbc0353d12_2023-03-13T21:38:47.330Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Thurnby Scout and Guide Group";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.thurnbyscoutsandguides.org.uk/>.
id:640f99d486d09cd3570ae444 :activityDescription "We have a variety of ongoing volunteer roles to help run our groups for young people. There are a range of roles available at different days and times during the week. ";
                            :activityOrganisation id:640f97e786d09cd3570ae401;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer helper".
