id:640fa689b8d56f3f40e2f320 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "Our community shop came into being In 2017, following the retirement of the shop owners of 50 years. In 2019 we raised £160,000 from members of the community which, together with a mortgage, enabled us to buy the shop premises. The shop is run entirely by volunteers and there are many opportunities to join our team. You can also become a member of our Community Benefit Society. Our shop is valued not just as somewhere to buy local milk, eggs & bread, newspapers and other essentials; but for its friendly welcome and as a place to meet and work with other members of our community. ";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/43dfb610-c332-4da5-afab-c2978699e31f_2023-03-13T22:41:13.052Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Slaley Community Shop Limited";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.slaleyshop.co.uk/>.
id:640fa8107e7373ad35c470ed :activityDescription """We have many opportunities for volunteers:
- serving on the till
- delivering newspapers
- cashing up
- managing part of our product range
- helping maintain our shop building and garden
- collecting orders from our wholesaler
- helping with admin
- serving on our board of directors
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:640fa689b8d56f3f40e2f320;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer with Slaley Community Shop".
id:640fac34be177cf8b826ab19 :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895,
