                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089d,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription """Penistone Line Partnership, established in 1993 is a voluntary organisation, part of the Community Rail Network supported by the DFT (Department for Transport). Partnerships work to improve their community lines, stations, and services.  We work with Train Operating Companies (Northern, East Midlands Railway, Cross Country, and TransPennine Express), Network Rail, local councils, and organisations such as stakeholders and rail user groups.

Working alongside our partners our aim is to:

Engage with local communities to improve the stations
Increase passenger numbers
Help economic & social development
Promote diversity, equality, and inclusion
Encourage a sustainable travel option for all.

Community Rail is a grassroots movement that started in the late 1990s to address the decline of branch lines. The movement has grown significantly and is now overseen by the Community Rail Network (CRN) which manages over 80 Community Rail Partnerships and over 1,000 station adoption groups offering support and training, as well as organising the annual Community Rail Awards. 

The Community Rail Development Strategy, published by the Department for Transport in 2018, is intended to help rural and local railways onto a more sustainable financial footing. Railways as a whole, consume a large amount of public funding, and it is essential to demonstrate value for money. We aim to significantly increase the number of passengers using the line while decreasing reliance on government subsidies. The role of Community Rail has never been more important. Giving passengers and other stakeholders a platform to express their needs to the rail industry.

Around 3,200 volunteers contribute about 250,000 hours of work each year to the national community rail network, bringing in approximately £3.4 million extra value to the rail industry.

""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/3dcd0548-0347-4bb0-9792-bd0d4bb4fbe6_2023-03-13T23:05:20.754Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Penistone Line Partnership";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://penline.co.uk/>.
id:640fae825f5eb883daebb101 :activityDescription """Our station at Honley in Kirklees isn't adopted yet, and we don't have anyone tending to it on a regular basis. Lockdowns have not helped and we really need to sand down and repaint our platform fencing. We are organising a small group to come together and spruce things up. If you can help out on 8 May 2023 at Honley Station (or any other volunteering) please arrange to help by texting Sarah at 07912753817. 
BIG THANKS

All permissions, and health & safety requirements will be followed. We will provide any tools/materials required and high viz jackets for use at the station. 

Where:
Address: Honley, Holmfirth HD9 6LL
Honley railway station serves the village of Honley in the Holme Valley of West Yorkshire, England. Honley station lies approximately 3 miles from Huddersfield on the Penistone Line operated by Northern Trains. The station was opened by the Huddersfield & Sheffield Junction Railway in 1850.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:640fac34be177cf8b826ab19;
                            :activityTitle "Honley Station Tidy & Fence Paint".
id:64103163fe47d3be917501b0 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899;
                            :organisationDescription """We are delighted that Friday Club has reopened and we are back serving meals every week to our homeless and ex shelter and current shelter guests from a location close to Chalk Farm Station.

We need volunteers to serve front of house guests and we use corporate teams or community teams to cook a healthy meal each week.

For more information about how you and your team can help out, please email lorraine@c4wshomelessproject.org

""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/580b8dcc-2715-4210-bb6d-280156c0688c_2023-03-14T08:33:39.469Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "C4WS Winter Homeless Shelter";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://c4wshomelessproject.org/>.
id:64103255fe47d3be9175027f :activityDescription """We are delighted that Friday Club has reopened and we are back serving meals every week to our members from a location close to Chalk Farm Station.

For more information about how you or your team can help out, please email lorraine@c4wshomelessproject.org.

We need front of house volunteers to serve drinks, engage in conversation with guests and clear up afterwards.....(Not heavy work)""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64103163fe47d3be917501b0;
                            :activityTitle "Friday lunch for the homeless".
id:64103426d9c4923908ef3d93 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899;
                            :organisationDescription """The opportunity to use your skills and experience from a wide range of professions, helping release people from the burden of debt: meeting clients, understanding their financial situation and using your new training and existing skills to help them make major steps forward.

This work is a real challenge, and unlike other types of volunteering: it is stimulating and will give you insights into how our clients live and the problems that they face. You’ll have the chance to correct injustice and release people from the intolerable burdens of stress and debt that they have often carried for decades. The problems we solve are complex and intriguing. We have a very friendly team: we work in pairs with clients via WhatsApp video calls, plus regular team meetings. It’s a great atmosphere.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/7d8ace4b-fba1-4971-8003-f5f268e43b67_2023-03-14T08:45:25.926Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Money Matters Leicester";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.moneymattersleicester.org/>.
id:641034b5d9c4923908ef3de9 :activityDescription "This role might suit someone who is newly retired or working part time. You will ideally have experience in the legal profession or in a financial role or other professional experience. You will need excellent computer skills: we use online systems, Microsoft Office, Teams and Dropbox. Volunteering is ongoing and flexible: we notify our availability a few weeks in advance and it's open to changes as long as we know in advance. ";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64103426d9c4923908ef3d93;
                            :activityTitle "Debt Advice".
id:641035243a461379c458a2d2 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription "We're a social enterprise working to build fair and sustainable food for Sheffield. We work with surplus and locally grown food. We save 500 tonnes of food a year from going to landfill which makes over a million meals!";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/8a6dac42-069d-4894-ae81-d7edac0f3837_2023-03-14T08:49:39.771Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Food Works";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://thefoodworks.org/>.
id:6410357ed9c4923908ef3e28 :activityDescription "Café Volunteers make up the team that run our cafes. With the support of our trained chefs, you will cook nutritious and affordable meals, serve them up in a cafe, open to everyone and show what can be done with surplus food. ";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641035243a461379c458a2d2;
                            :activityTitle "Cafe Volunteering".
id:64103c352a0eedb6aef42d3d :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription "Oxfam is a global community of people who believe in a kinder, and radically better world, where everyone has the power to thrive not just survive. We believe we can overcome poverty by fighting the injustices and inequalities that fuel it.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/118da345-9185-4cda-b8cc-2f58ffeda2a6_2023-03-14T09:19:48.824Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Oxfam";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.oxfam.org.uk/>.
id:64103e0fd03655ce9b951710 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "Our community-based approach is aimed at providing a holistic solution to ending the cycle of poverty. We believe children should not grow up in institutions like orphanages, where they are isolated from society because of poverty, sickness, disease or death of parents. We aim to empower communities through education, healthcare, and income-generating initiatives. ";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/b84d05a7-fb0c-4cd8-8a65-3bee59416a07_2023-03-14T09:27:41.249Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "The Nasio Trust ";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.thenasiotrust.org/>.
id:6410436d0f64c8ee13976738 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "Please contact Communityinvolvementteam@wiltshire.gov.uk for more information and how to apply";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/73012d7c-949f-4c6b-a844-ca2e786fa283_2023-03-14T09:50:37.169Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Community Involvement Team".
id:641043ff0f64c8ee1397681a :activityDescription """The Community Involvement Team offer volunteering opportunities to mentor a vulnerable young person age 8-24 for a period of time who have or are involved in the Youth Justice Service within the Wiltshire area. We also offer mentoring to parents who have involvement or risk of child sexual exploitation. Our volunteering ranges from face to face or virtual in primary schools, doing activities out in the community, to supporting a young person in Swindon custody, to helping a young person develop life skills and be advocate for a young person in a youth custody panels.

Like to know more about volunteering please contact communityinvolvementteam@wiltshire.gov.uk""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6410436d0f64c8ee13976738;
                            :activityTitle "Making a difference".
id:64104421662e01ec873acd56 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "Inspire is a Charity based in Chorley Town Centre, close to bus station and railway.  We are open 7 days a week for young people to access a range of services and activities.  Please see our web site for specific programmes as they are subject to change.  Our building provides access to Climbing, arts/crafts, dance and drama, sports, music and cookery.  We run a range of tailored projects as well as informal youth work and more targeted support.  The agerange of our young people are 8 years to 25 year (with and additional need or disability)";
                            :organisationName "Inspire Youth Zone";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.inspireyouthzone.org/>.
id:6410449d0f64c8ee1397685e :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription """DEBRA UK is a national charity supporting 3,000+ members, which includes people living with EB, relatives, partners, or carers of someone with EB, healthcare professionals and researchers who work with EB.

DEBRA UK exists to provide care and support to improve quality of life for people living with EB, and to fund pioneering research to find effective treatments and, ultimately cure(s) for EB.

Our vision is for a world where no one suffers with EB, and we will not stop until this vision becomes a reality.

From discovering the first EB genes to funding the first clinical trial in gene therapy, we have played a pivotal role in EB research globally and have been responsible for making significant progress in advancing diagnosis, treatment, and daily management of EB.

We are committed to making sure that the estimated 5,000+ people living with EB in the UK and their families and carers get the vital and wide-ranging support they need.

The income we generate from our fundraising activities and our network of charity shops, enables us to provide care and support to improve the quality of life for people living with EB today, and fund pioneering research to find treatments and cure(s).""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/91e5d3a0-ce3e-4b75-b77b-7d8fd47e9b83_2023-03-14T09:55:41.095Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "DEBRA";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.debra.org.uk/>.
id:641044e10f64c8ee13976899 :activityDescription "youth worker to support young people on a range of activities between the hours of 5pm and 9pm Monday to SSaturday or Sundays 11 am til 2pm";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64104421662e01ec873acd56;
                            :activityTitle "youth worker".
id:641045120f64c8ee139768e3 :activityDescription """If you are 18 or over, empathetic and a good listener, we have the following volunteering opportunities for you: 

Community Mentors spend around an hour a week with a young person for up to a year and can provide support with self-esteem, social skills or working towards goals. 

Primary mentors spend around an hour each week in primary schools during the school day supporting children to build resilience by having fun and trying new things.

Parent mentors support parents whose child or young person is being exploited or at risk of exploitation

Transitional mentors support vulnerable young people aged 16 – 25 as they move into adulthood

For more information please contact:
CommunityInvolvementTeam@wiltshire.gov.uk


""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6410436d0f64c8ee13976738;
                            :activityTitle "Mentoring a YP or parent".
id:64104535551fd9765a2b9849 :activityDescription "The Nasio Trust is a small charity with a big online presence. Our supporters are extremely engaged and enjoy receiving regular updates from us. In order to reach our audience with our impact, projects, and appeals we need a creative person to manage our social media accounts to ensure quality posts. ";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64103e0fd03655ce9b951710;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer as our Social Media Manager".
id:6410485c551fd9765a2b99db :activityDescription """The Nasio Trust's flagship scholarship project, the Exceptional Girls Programme, provides a scholarship to vulnerable and/or orphaned girls in Kakamega and Samburu counties in Kenya to enable them to go to secondary school.
Help us create a network of role models and mentors to enable these young girls work towards their aspirations. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:64103e0fd03655ce9b951710;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer as a mentor for young disadvantaged girls in Kenya".
id:64104a51506e6c8b5704980a :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription "Greenpeace is a movement of people who are passionate about defending the natural world from destruction. Our vision is a greener, healthier and more peaceful planet, one that can sustain life for generations to come. ";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/38410a5d-e4d5-4ec2-93d4-20c303d30879_2023-03-14T10:19:58.791Z.png>;
