id:6419a23525513b8f6dac8cf8 :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895;
                            :organisationDescription """Caring Altogether on Romney Marsh aim to support mainly older people living on Romney Marsh and its surrounding rural areas, across to Tenterden, Rolvenden and everywhere in between,  who are socially isolated and / or lonely. Through this support, we aim to improve people's health and well-being, bring joy into their lives, form friendships and to help people remain independent for longer as well as enhance the quality of life of the rural communities where we operate. 
""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/0a8d4bfc-7581-47ea-8293-c7424ecf3c5c_2023-03-21T12:25:25.148Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Caring Altogether on Romney Marsh (CARM)";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.carmromneymarsh.org.uk/>.
id:6419aaa87f99aa898207c765 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """We support people in the community to maximise their well-being and independence. Our services help young people as well as adults.

The differences we make to our service users include:
*increased self-esteem and confidence
*increased independence
*people feel less excluded
*people are less dependent on services
*readmission to inpatient and residential care is reduced
*people are supported into training, volunteering and/or employment""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/c6fdc66b-c0d0-4bf4-8366-b0fee5229378_2025-07-15T09:11:32.326Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Andover Mind";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.andovermind.org.uk/>.
id:6419cdf31a746828c052df86 :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895;
                            :organisationDescription """AbilityNet is a pioneering UK charity with a global perspective. We believe the power of digital technology should be available to everyone, regardless of ability or age. Our free online resources and a network of over 300 community-based volunteers help individuals with any disability, of any age, to use all kinds of digital technology. 

Our teams of experts help organisations of all types and sizes to become more inclusive and to build accessible digital products and services. We are founder members of the global accessibility profession, work closely with some of the biggest businesses on the planet and organise TechShare Pro, Europe’s largest accessibility gathering.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/4d2c92ab-8377-42f2-8c7e-cfebbfabf7c2_2023-03-21T15:32:02.852Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "AbilityNet";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://abilitynet.org.uk/>.
id:6419d69324893dd0a45ea5e6 :activityDescription """We’re joining #TheBigHelpOut on Monday 8th May, helping volunteers throughout the UK who
make a real difference in your community. AbilityNet needs volunteers across the UK, so visit abilitynet.org.uk/volunteer to find out how you can join in and lend a hand - on the Coronation Day and beyond!

Are you passionate about the power of technology? Would you like to help us bridge the digital divide? Do you have a few hours available each month? Become an AbilityNet volunteer. You don’t need to be a tech guru to help. Typical help requests for a volunteer include:

Helping someone set up an email account
Showing someone how to use online video calling via WhatsApp or Zoom
Setting up a new device and connecting it to the internet
Giving advice on anti-virus protection and internet safety
Changing basic device settings to make it easier to use

We look forward to hearing from you! Visit us: abilitynet.org.uk/volunteer""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6419cdf31a746828c052df86;
                            :activityTitle "Become an AbilityNet volunteer to help disabled and older people in your community to use their digital devices".
