                            :longitude "-0.1603055"^^xsd:double.
id:641af535a22da3de4fe26170 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """We’re a strong community of disabled and non-disabled people with a shared vision of equality.

We provide practical advice and emotional support whenever people need them most. We do this through our Scope helpline, our online community, a range of employment and child sleep services, community engagement programmes, partnerships and more. Everything we do is with the aim to achieve our strategy, Everyday Equality.

We use our collective power to change attitudes and end injustice. We partner with others to increase our reach and impact. And we campaign relentlessly to create a fairer society.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/19848b9a-32ca-444b-8bb6-a842e44d8d82_2023-03-22T12:31:48.331Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Scope";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.scope.org.uk/volunteering/>.
id:641afb7afdca9c972649728a :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "RollaDome All Skate is a charity aiming to make a difference to young people by supporting their development through healthy, rewarding activities and life skills. We encourage young people to lead an active and rewarding lifestyle through recreational roller skating. ";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/70af6bf8-5d23-428e-b083-5f0cb47bd049_2023-03-22T12:58:31.681Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "RollaDome All Skate";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://rolladome.org.uk/>.
id:641b00ce7b82064c13876b00 :activityDescription """Monthly groups to support the carer, family and friends. 

Duties include: setting the room ready for the group, greeting people on arrival, making drinks and refreshments, chatting to service users and carers, refilling drinks, clearing room and tidying venue once everyone leaves. 

We have Carer Support Groups across 7 locations each month:

•	Burslem, Biddulph, Leek, Cheadle, Silverdale, Longton & Madeley

Why volunteer?
•	Get to know others in the community, making new friends and connections
•	Boost your CV
•	Gain experience in supporting people who need your help

Please see our website (approachstaffordshire.co.uk/how-can-we-help-you-dementia-services-staffordshire/carer-advice-and-support-sessions/) or phone 01782 214999, for details on venues, dates and times.

All applicants will have a DBS check and training will be offered. Volunteers may be reimbursed the actual costs of expenses incurred, including travel.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641843e14df4e3ad996e423c;
                            :activityTitle "Carer Support Group Volunteer".
id:641b13d4b3e348bce9dcc658 :activityDescription """Weekly activity groups in a variety of locations (including singing, pottery, gardening) across North Staffordshire and Stoke.

Duties include: setting the room ready for the group, greeting people on arrival, making drinks and refreshments, engaging with the activities with the group, refilling drinks, clearing room and tidying venue once everyone leaves.

•	Activity Groups - Burslem, Leek, Kidsgrove & bet365 Stoke 
•	Singing – Leek, Biddulph & Dougie Mac Hospice
•	Gardening – Biddulph
•	Pottery – The Dementia Centre, Blurton
•	Independent Activity Groups – The Dementia Centre (twice weekly)

Why volunteer?
•	Get to know others in the community, making new friends and connections
•	Boost your CV
•	Gain experience in supporting people who need your help

Please see our website (approachstaffordshire.co.uk/how-can-we-help-you-dementia-services-staffordshire/dementia-group-support/) or phone 01782 214999, for details on venues, dates and times.

All applicants will have a DBS check and training will be offered. Volunteers may be reimbursed the actual costs of expenses incurred, including travel.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641843e14df4e3ad996e423c;
                            :activityTitle "Activity Group Volunteer".
id:641b3495981c98ddbe837bbb :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "We show girls from 4 plus a world of possibilities big and small. One where every girl can laugh and learn and be herself. Girlguiding is what each girl wants it to be. It might be the thrill of doing something for the first time. Songs around a campfire. The buzz of getting a new badge. Coming home exhausted and full of stories. It’s a space where she can be herself, get creative, explore, and most of all have fun.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/233c5216-98a0-4f0f-a487-b12d4cd09df3_2023-04-18T15:06:22.158Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Girlguiding Hertfordshire";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.girlguidinghertfordshire.org.uk/>.
