id:641c2882a4c8e01bf064ec1b :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895;
                            :organisationDescription """We offer a range of services to enable older people to retain their independence and improve their quality of life. These include:
day centres
community warden service
Home support
Practical services/Handyperson
Sharing Time/Telephone Befriending
Information and Advice

In addition, we campaign both locally and nationally on matters which are important to older people and endeavour to make sure their voice is heard in decision making.

 """;
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/285398e8-c7c5-498c-aaf8-e7b3fa00f2d1_2023-03-23T10:22:58.044Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "AgeUK Cambridgeshire & Peterborough";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.ageukcap.org.uk/>.
id:641c2a8ba4c8e01bf064f04b :activityDescription """We have day centres in Cambridge, Huntingdon, March, Peterborough and Wisbech who welcome volunteer support with the activities to enable their service users to spend an enjoyable day in the company of others. 

They are also always keen to hear from anyone with a talent or skill who can share this with them on an occasional basis so that the centres can provide a range of interesting activities and entertainment for their service users.

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641c2882a4c8e01bf064ec1b;
                            :activityTitle "Day Centre Activity Volunteer".
id:641c2c2cc1ae33017aa21383 :activityDescription """Our volunteer handy people assist with installing key safes and grab rails to enable people to be discharged from hospital into their home. They also help with basic DIY, simple furniture moving and similar tasks along side professional staff.

The purpose is to enable an older person to return safely to their home or allow them to remain in their home.
Cambridgeshire and Peterborough
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641c2882a4c8e01bf064ec1b;
                            :activityTitle "Handyperson Volunteer".
id:641c43885f3bed0122822a23 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Dealing with cancer can be frightening and stressful. We can help. We bring treatment, expert advice and support to where it matters most; the heart of the community.

Give hope. Help cope.  

We’re Wales’ leading cancer charity, with a long and distinguished history and are widely recognized for the quality of our support, care and research.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/cc13de0a-d93c-4a25-ae53-3b48766fe460_2023-03-23T12:18:16.129Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Tenovus Cancer Care";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.tenovuscancercare.org.uk/>.
id:641c56e34c04e246950854f2 :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """We are proud to offer world class palliative and end of life care to everyone who needs it, whenever or wherever that may be. We are also here for the people closest to you.

We passionately believe in the words of our founder, Dame Cicely Saunders, who said: “You matter because you are you and you matter until the last moment of your life.” That means we’ll listen to your story, adapt our treatments and advice to suit your particular needs, and we won’t stop until we can give you the best possible support.

The hospice itself is a friendly, vibrant place, and as unlike a traditional hospital as we can make it. But rest assured, our medical and nursing care is excellent and our clinical teams are highly professional and devoted to doing their best for you.

Keeping services and activities running takes a team effort – with volunteers providing that extra mile of support, effort and care alongside staff.  Volunteers support all areas of St Christopher’s, so whether your expertise is sorting donations in our shops, cheering on others at a sponsored run event or providing companionship to others in the local community, we have a volunteer role with your name on it!

We are a place for everyone.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/db299604-bffe-41da-8f9e-f5df0bb611f0_2023-05-02T09:42:08.132Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "St Christopher's Hospice";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.stchristophers.org.uk/bighelpout>.
id:641c62477ea34dd5493a89b3 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Cumbria CVS (Cumbria Council for Voluntary Service) offers help, advice, training and support to third sector groups throughout Cumbria.

We bring organisations together to form a powerful voice for our sector.

We help local organisations to recruit volunteers.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/e4c9175b-1fa9-4d63-a916-596c4306a0d3_2023-03-23T14:29:26.952Z.jpeg>;
