id:641c74843741438d369e212e :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """\"The Rainbows experience, wherever you are\"

Rainbows cares for hundreds of families every year who have a child or young person with a serious or terminal illness that means that their lives will be shorter than most. We provide family centered short breaks, palliative and end of life care for children and young people across the East Midlands. Rainbows support every child and young person to fulfil their potential, and help families make the most of every precious moment, while capturing memories and keepsakes to treasure.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/fc28384e-96c5-421e-9854-3237a1c4b01c_2023-03-23T15:47:16.474Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Rainbows Hospice for Children & Young People";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://rainbows.co.uk/>.
id:641c7ebfdebe8c3c30566775 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription "We are a regional community-focused charity, providing emotional and practical support to people of all ages and with all types of cancer, as well as those carers and loved ones who may feel the impact of cancer. Established in 1981, we have four Cancer Support Centres spread across Hampshire, Dorset and the Isle of Wight and have recently launched an outreach programme to take our services to geographic and demographic communities we've not yet reached. ";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/621ea915-bfc0-4314-845f-46b8541c44f1_2023-03-23T16:30:54.603Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Wessex Cancer Trust";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.wessexcancer.org.uk/>.
id:641f2e579d3cee0d396d7cc8 :activityDescription """Come and join us as a unit leader volunteering on a weekly basis.

By volunteering with us, you’ll be helping girls build their confidence, have adventures and learn new skills. It doesn’t matter what your experience or background is, or how much time you have.  

Plus, volunteering for Girlguiding is a great way of meeting new people and taking a break from your daily routine. You can also build your own skills by taking our leadership development qualification, becoming a first aider or qualified outdoor activity instructor. 

https://www.girlguiding.org.uk/get-involved/become-a-volunteer/register-to-volunteer/""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6412288a05e7ccb6304832ad;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer as a unit leader with Girlguiding Weybridge district".
