id:6425ccb5a0624f3ab9fafb90 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Our purpose as a charity is to enable people to make more informed choices concerning their physical, emotional, mental and spiritual well-being, in a way which reflects our belief in unconditional acceptance in order to:
- Actively empower individuals
- Encourage their sense of self worth
- Help them realise their full potential

We will do this through appropriate and feasible feedback and sustained contact with other professionals.
The Matthew Project is a value driven organisation, believing in no compromise on hope for people's lives no matter what their situation. We pride ourselves on our ethos of compassion, care, creativity and integrity in all areas of work.

Through our varied services, young people and adults receive professional advice, information, counselling, support, care and education.

The Matthew Project has workers based throughout Norfolk and Suffolk in both rural and urban areas. Our work takes place in a variety of settings including schools, youth venues, police stations, courts, in the community and at our own premises.

We work with the individual but also worried parents, carers and young people whose parents use drugs or alcohol.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/MP_Logo_on_hope_.125x125.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "The Matthew Project";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://matthewproject.org/>.
id:6425ccbaa0624f3ab9fafc12 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "Step Change Studios is a pioneering dance company committed to making Latin and Ballroom dance accessible for everyone. We offer fun, engaging opportunities for disabled and non-disabled people to dance. We cater to all ages, abilities and needs. We provide weekly classes in Central London; deliver dance in schools, colleges, social care, healthcare and community settings; and we create imaginative bespoke dance projects and programmes. We want to support everyone to achieve their dancing ambitions - whether that is to dance for fun, to be active, to perform or compete.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/df2e593f-d53c-4d35-8771-d223e001bad5_2025-10-14T15:08:54.220Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Step Change Studios";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.stepchangestudios.com/>.
id:6425cce8a0624f3ab9fafdd4 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Enhancing people�s communication is what we strive for, and creating a better world where language does not stand a barrier.

Our vision is a world in which individuals and cultures feel integrated, valued and celebrated. We believe that linguistics skills are an important surviving tool that empowers human beings� advancement, happiness, as well as prosperity and therefore we strive to make it accessible to everyone no matter where they come from. 

Through this we will create a more united society with a stronger sense of purpose and connection; increased contentment and happiness; and less worry and hardship.

We have a burning passion to build a future that both children and adults, no matter what colour or background they have, can acquire more than one language and live without being afraid of the language barrier surrounding them. That is our sole purpose and vision, to help change the world by connecting people.

We are an organisation whose aim is to break the language gap around us by connecting skilled, qualified linguists to help those with less language skills through a safe learning environment. We are a group of linguists, who are inspired by and committed to the same vision.""";
                            :organisationName "Linguist Point";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://linguistpoint.co.uk/>.
id:6425cceba0624f3ab9fafe1a :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "The National Army Museum is a leading authority on the British Army and its impact on society past and present. Our vision is to be the leading authority on the history of the British Army and a first class Museum that moves, inspires, challenges, educates and entertains. The aim by 2022 is for NAM to have established itself as a world class Museum with national and international reach. It will seek to become the Army�s primary memory bank and act as a focus for creativity, learning and debate around the subject of Britain�s Army";
                            :organisationName "National Army Museum (NAM)";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.nam.ac.uk/volunteer>.
