id:6425cceea0624f3ab9fafe81 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "The MS Society is the UK's largest charity dedicated to supporting everyone whose life is touched by MS.  It provides respite care, a freephone MS Helpline, grants for home adaptations and mobility aids, education and training, specialist MS nurses and a wide range of information.  Local branches cater for people of all ages and interests, and are run by people with direct experience of MS.  The MS Society also funds over 50 vital MS research projects in the UK.Multiple Sclerosis is the most common disabling neurological disorder among young adults in the UK and around 85,000 people in Britain have MS.  MS is the result of damage to myelin - a protective sheath surrounding nerve fibres of the central nervous system.  When myelin is damaged, this interferes with messages between the brain and other parts of the body.For some people, MS is characterised by periods of relapse and remission while for others it has a progressive pattern.  For everyone, it makes life unpredictable.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/MSS-logo-orange_a838SUEMBvXrmcT8mBJg3.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "MS Society";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.mssociety.org.uk/>.
id:6425cd40a0624f3ab9fb07c7 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Volunteer with Shaw Trust and help create brighter futures for people in your community. 

Shaw Trust provides employment opportunities, skills development training, and health and wellbeing services across the UK. We operate charitable social enterprises and retail shops, and work alongside Shaw Education Trust, which runs a diverse chain of academy schools.

We add value to every service we deliver by investing back into community projects, such as our social enterprises, Community Hubs and national volunteering scheme.

Volunteers help us achieve our aim of empowering people and supporting them towards employment and/or helping with their mental health and wellbeing. They also help in our schools and Social Enterprises and they help us run our charity shops too.  

Shaw Trust volunteers are at the heart of everything we do. 

To find out more about becoming a Shaw Trust volunteer please email volunteers@shaw-trust.org.uk or visit shaw-trust.org.uk""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/118698566_3527629573943253_8508315933387443096_n.png>;
                            :organisationName "Shaw Trust";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.shaw-trust.org.uk/>.
id:6425cd4aa0624f3ab9fb08ed :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """We are your local society dedicated to supporting visually impaired people across Buckinghamshire.

If you would like to make a difference, this is an opportunity for you to join our fantastic team of volunteers, and to be a vital part of BucksVision's commitment to sight loss prevention and support.
 
Becoming a volunteer can be very rewarding and there are many ways that you can help support us.  By volunteering with us you can get involved in our wide range of services such as Fundraising, Home Services and our Social & Activity groups.
 
We make every effort to ensure that you receive the appropriate support and training, so that you can realise your full potential as a volunteer helping people with visual impairment.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/BucksVision_logo-no_writing.125x125.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "BucksVision Visual Impairment Charity";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.bucksvision.co.uk/>.
id:6425cd5ba0624f3ab9fb0ad6 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "GT Scholars (CIC) is a social enterprise that provides tutoring, mentoring and enrichment to young people from a range of backgrounds. We charge means-tested fees and use profits to provide our programme free of charge to young people from the lowest income groups.We're looking for volunteers that are passionate about potential! Our goal is to help more state school pupils gain access to the most selective universities and the most competitive careers.There are a range of charitable organisations and social enterprises offering programmes to improve the life chances of young people. However, The GT Scholars programme has the capacity to work with a wide range of pupils from disadvantaged backgrounds and pupils do not need to be referred by their school in order to qualify for support.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/400dpiLogoCropped_-_Copy.png>;
                            :organisationName "GT Scholars CIC";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.gtscholars.org/>.
id:6425cd5da0624f3ab9fb0b12 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Are you looking for a fulfilling opportunity to volunteer in East or West Kent, directly supporting unpaid carers and those they care for; those who may be lonely or struggling to cope with daily tasks while navigating Cancer or long-term health conditions?

With over 10 years' experience in supporting connections between volunteers and those navigating Cancer (and over 40 years' experience as a charity), the Crossroads Macmillan Volunteer Service can offer flexible, rewarding volunteering avenues for you to explore; get in touch today and make an immediate, positive impact on the life of an unpaid Carer and their loved ones - a little bit of time can truly make a huge difference.

""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/CR_Mac_Logo_Main.png>;
                            :organisationName "Crossroads Macmillan Kent & Medway Volunteer Service";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.crossroadskent.org/macmillan-service>.
id:6425cd60a0624f3ab9fb0b5b :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "Abbeyfield is a charity focused on preventing and alleviating the loneliness that can come with later life by creating communities that keep people connected. We see volunteers as crucial in helping us achieve our mission across the UK, particularly during the current COVID-19 outbreak, when we need your support more than ever. For more information about Abbeyfield please visit www.abbeyfield.com";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/group-masterlogo_solid-roundel-cymk_WHy6ko6tomyzQDqhpNZkEW.png>;
                            :organisationName "Abbeyfield";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.abbeyfield.com/>.
id:6425cd68a0624f3ab9fb0c4b :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "Sense is a national disability charity that supports people with complex communication needs to be understood, connected and valued. We are here for every person who faces communication barriers in a world that relies on being able to see and hear well to be connected. Our flexible and personalised services empower people to communicate and express themselves � be it through speech or sign, touch or movement, gesture or sound, art or dance. Together, we connect differently and campaign passionately for the right to lead connected and fulfilled lives.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Untitled_yrLMfaApyuQHzQkYGQUT5k.125x125.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "Sense";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.sense.org.uk/>.
id:6425cdb5a0624f3ab9fb11d4 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "KeyRing is all about listening to and working alongside people in their local communities so that they gain greater independence, improve their wellbeing and are part of a network of contacts and friends.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/New_logo_in_a_square_-_suitable_for_facebook.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "KeyRing Living Support Networks";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.keyring.org/>.
id:6425cdb8a0624f3ab9fb122e :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Crohn�s Disease and Ulcerative Colitis - two of the main forms of Inflammatory Bowel Disease (or IBD), affect more than 300,000 people in the UK. Yet it is largely a hidden disease, and one that causes stigma, fear and isolation. We�re the UK�s leading charity in the battle against Crohn�s Disease and Ulcerative Colitis. 

Our mission is to work with all those affected by these conditions to achieve a better quality of life, improve services, and ultimately find a cure. 

We want to see a world in which people�s lives are not limited by Crohn�s and Colitis. 

See how we work to make life better for the 300,000 people in the UK with Crohn�s, Colitis and other forms of Inflammatory Bowel Disease: www.crohnsandcolitis.org.uk""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Liverpool_14.05.16__680_of_803_.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "Crohn's and Colitis UK";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.crohnsandcolitis.org.uk/>.
id:6425cdcba0624f3ab9fb1471 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "Surrey Clubs for Young People (SCYP) is a charity dedicated to ensuring that young people across Surrey and South London have access to high quality youth provision. Our aim is to provide a range of exciting and challenging opportunities for young people, through which they can develop into confident young adults. We do this by supporting a large network of volunteers to run youth clubs and projects across the area.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/SCYP_Logo.png>;
                            :organisationName "Surrey Clubs for Young People (SCYP)";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.scyp.co.uk/>.
id:6425cdf4a0624f3ab9fb18fc :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """We�re working to improve life for children in the UK. 

Our vision is that every child and young person has a safe and happy childhood, and the foundations they need to thrive.

We put children at the heart of everything we do. Action for Children protects and supports children and young people, providing practical and emotional care and support, ensuring their voices are heard, and campaigning to bring lasting improvements to their lives.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/A.png>;
                            :organisationName "Action for Children";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.actionforchildren.org.uk/>.
id:6425cdf8a0624f3ab9fb196a :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "Missing People offers a lifeline for the 250,000 people who run away and go missing each year in the UK. For those left behind, we provide specialised support to ease the heartache and confusion, and help search for their missing loved ones.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Final-New-Missing-People-Logo-Rectangle.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "Missing People";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.missingpeople.org.uk/>.
id:6425cdfaa0624f3ab9fb19ba :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """Noah's Ark Children's Hospice is a community based hospice service providing clinical, emotional and practical support for families of children and young people with life-limiting/life-threatening conditions in the North London Boroughs of  Barnet, Camden, Enfield, Haringey, Islington and Hertsmere. 

Our current services include Specialist Play, Specialist Care, Family Activities, volunteer support in the home and a Family Link service. Noah's Ark volunteers are the backbone of our charity and play a crucial part in providing these services.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/8e16f65c-95d6-4d34-9aeb-ded6f310b142_2024-01-29T14:09:45.659Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Noah's Ark Children's Hospice";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.noahsarkhospice.org.uk/>.
id:6425ce43a0624f3ab9fb225b :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """We support people who have combined sight and hearing loss which affects their access to information, mobility and communication. We help them to live with their condition and to build their confidence and independence. 

Deafblindness affects everyone in different ways. Some people might have mild sight and hearing loss whereas others can�t see or hear anything. It can be isolating and lonely and can lead to mental health issues - but it�s far more common than many people realise. Around 400,000 people are affected by sight and hearing loss in the UK.
""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Deafblind.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "Deafblind UK";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://deafblind.org.uk/>.
id:6425ce66a0624f3ab9fb2662 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """RNIB, the Royal National Institute of Blind People, is the UK's leading sight loss charity. We offer practical and emotional support to blind and partially sighted people, their families and carers. We raise awareness of the experiences of blind and partially sighted people and campaign for change to make our society more accessible for all. We want to change our world so there are no barriers to people with sight loss.
 
Website at: www.rnib.org.uk""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/1b56297e-65a3-4b68-8e4a-344cf8a1a038_2024-02-08T13:44:41.573Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Royal National Institute Of Blind People - RNIB";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.rnib.org.uk/volunteering>.
id:6425ce71a0624f3ab9fb27d1 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription """The Young Lives Foundation is an independent children's charity dedicated to delivering quality services tailored to ensure we achieve effective outcomes in the lives of vulnerable and disadvantaged children, young people and adults. 

Our mission is to be alongside children and young people in need in ways that affirm their identity and worth, champion their rights, needs and interests and promote their well-being and development.

Our vision is that every young person in need shall have access to the resources and opportunities needed for them to achieve their potential and lead fulfilled lives. 

The Young Lives Foundation's team of volunteers are an asset to the charity and deliver the majority of its frontline activity across the county. The charity would not exist if it was not for their commitment and dedication.....

If you can find one hour per week to support and guide a young person, we'd love to hear from you.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Young_Lives_Foundation.125x125.png>;
                            :organisationName "Young Lives Foundation (The)";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.ylf.org.uk/>.
id:6425ce81a0624f3ab9fb29e5 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "DEBRA is the national charity that supports individuals and families affected by Epidermolysis Bullosa (EB) � a painful genetic skin blistering condition which, in the worst cases, can be fatal.DEBRA was founded in 1978 by Phyllis Hilton whose daughter Debra had EB � the charity was the world�s first EB patient support group. DEBRA funds pioneering research to find effective treatments and, ultimately, a cure for EB. We also provide care and support to individuals and families living with EB.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/77b9a2b3-fb40-46b2-bd2d-bf993da8775f_2024-07-09T08:49:42.003Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "DEBRA";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.debra.org.uk/>.
id:6425ce96a0624f3ab9fb2c61 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "Kidney Research UK is the largest funder dedicated to research into the causes and prevention of kidney disease and we've been going since 1961. The money we raise goes directly into research to find better treatments and ultimately a cure to help over three million people in the UK at risk of chronic kidney disease.Our vision:Lives free from kidney disease.Our mission is to:� Fund and deliver life-saving research into kidney diseases� Improve treatments for people with kidney diseases and enhance their quality of life� Increase awareness of kidney health.Volunteers play a massive part in the delivery of our work.  Without our dedicated and passionate volunteers we could not do what we do, or want to do.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/a2f0b7f5-9b81-40ea-b9f1-0b5484e646dc_2025-08-06T10:08:39.556Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Kidney Research UK";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.kidneyresearchuk.org/>.
id:6425cec6a0624f3ab9fb3209 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """At Hestia, we have been supporting adults and children across London in times of crisis since 1970. 2020 marked our 50th anniversary!

Last year we supported 14,007 men, women and children.
This includes victims of modern slavery, women and children who have experienced domestic abuse, young care leavers and older people. From giving someone a home, to helping them to get the right mental health support, we support people at the moment of crisis and enable them to build a life beyond a crisis. We are supported by nearly 950 volunteers across London who provide specialist skills such as art therapy, yoga, IT, gardening and cooking, as well as befriending and fundraising.
""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/hestia-logo-full-colour-rgb-1260px_144ppi__1_.png>;
                            :organisationName "Hestia";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.hestia.org.uk/>.
id:6425cecca0624f3ab9fb32ac :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "Team Up uses tuition, delivered by inspirational role models, to enable pupils from low income backgrounds to meaningfully increase their academic attainment, in order to improve the choices open to them.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/team_up_logo_small.png>;
                            :organisationName "Team Up";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.teamup.org.uk/>.
id:6425cedaa0624f3ab9fb3414 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Kent and Medway NHS and Social Care Partnership Trust provides mental health and social care services for Kent in partnership with Kent County Council. In Medway, we work closely with the local unitary authority to provide joined-up health and social care services.

As one of the larger mental health trusts in the country, we cover an area of 1,450 sq miles and serve 1.7 million people across Kent and Medway. Our annual revenue is �178 million and we employ 3,318 staff and 228 seconded staff who are located in 83 buildings on 47 sites.

Our services are predominantly provided around key urban centres including Maidstone, Medway and Canterbury, but we provide a range of services in community locations, reflecting the urban and rural mix of the area. The Trust has also introduced telemedicine to enhance accessibility.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/KMPT_Logo_pshnHV4GEgyPoaeWJv4FZJ.125x125.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "Kent & Medway NHS and Social Care Partnership Trust";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.kmpt.nhs.uk/>.
id:6425cee0a0624f3ab9fb34d5 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "Shelter helps millions of people every year struggling with bad housing or homelessness and we campaign to prevent it in the first place.We believe that everyone should live in a decent home because a safe and stable place to live forms the foundation of health, happiness and a decent chance in life.Shelter is the UK's leading housing advice, support and campaigning charity, we are recognised legal experts in housing. We help people to access their right to an adequate standard of living. We're here so no-one has to fight bad housing or homelessness on their own.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Shelter_Square_EDvV3vLFhHFDBHsw89DtWj.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "Shelter";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.shelter.org.uk/>.
id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "Our vision is that everyone who needs it should receive first aid from those around them. No one should suffer for the lack of trained first aiders. Everything we do at St John Ambulance must be judged by whether it brings about a world where everyone who needs it receives first aid.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/SJA_2D_pos_60mm_3K3s9ZrNiQA4yKXRPiiS3A.125x125.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "St John Ambulance1";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.sja.org.uk/>.
id:6425ceeaa0624f3ab9fb35fd :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """When a child or young person is diagnosed with cancer, their whole world (and their family’s) can feel like it’s falling apart. They need special treatment because their cancer is different to adults’, they can only be treated in certain hospitals, and they often travel miles and miles to get there.

The impact of cancer on young lives is far more than medical. Their anxieties are deep. Their education, mental health and social lives suffer. Their futures feel very uncertain.

Young Lives vs Cancer is the only charity in the UK with specialist social workers dedicated to providing tailored psychosocial support to children and young people with cancer, and their families.

We stop at nothing to make their voices heard and their unique needs understood, so they can get the right care and support at the right time. ​​​​​​

""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/dabc87b7-598e-474e-af6b-f88aae10334e_2024-02-12T15:14:33.473Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Young Lives vs Cancer";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.younglivesvscancer.org.uk/>.
id:6425cef7a0624f3ab9fb3783 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Milton Keynes Museum is a vibrant community museum run almost entirely by volunteers. With steadily increasing visitor numbers we are seeking new volunteers to help with all aspects of our activities.  We have many varied opportunities for volunteering from working in our shop/reception area, in our catering outlets, visitor guides, school programme and our maintenance team. Whatever your experience or interest there is something for everyone here at Milton Keynes museum. 

Museum Key Aims

1.\\tTo preserve, display and interpret the Stacey Hill Collection

2.\\tTo maintain and develop the land and buildings of Stacey Hill Farm in ways that:

a.\\tProvide a secure and appropriate environment for storage and display of the collection;
b.\\tReflect the history of the farm and changes in the use of its land.

3.\\tTo work with the people of Milton Keynes to help communities, groups and individuals preserve, understand and promote their own heritage in ways that are sustainable

4.\\tTo develop attitudes and provide training opportunities that encourage life-long learning and enable individuals to help raise standards in all aspects of collection care and interpretation

5.\\tTo encourage and provide facilities for research into the collection and social history of the area.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/LogoMaster.png>;
                            :organisationName "Milton Keynes Museum";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.miltonkeynesmuseum.org.uk/>.
id:6425cf21a0624f3ab9fb38d6 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Enrych supports adults with a physical disability to engage more fully within their local communities. We provide this service in Oxfordshire by \"matching\" our members' requirements to the skills and interests of volunteers.

Our aim at Enrych Oxfordshire is to help people with a physical disability enjoy a leisure, cultural or learning activity by pairing them with a volunteer who shares similar interests.

We just need you to commit to an hour or two once a week or fortnight. Being a volunteer will make such a difference to the lives of the physically disabled adult but very often really benefits the volunteer too. 

Volunteers receive training and ongoing support""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/ENRYCH-Oxford-wht-RGB-sml.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "Enrych Oxfordshire";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://enrychoxfordshire.org.uk/>.
id:6425cf4ba0624f3ab9fb3a33 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "Dimensions is a specialist not-for-profit provider of services for people with learning disabilities and people who experience autism. We provide support to over 3,000 people across England and Wales. Our employees support people to live as independently as possible.We offer a wide range of services to young people and adults of all ages, and our volunteers play a key role in helping us enable people to be actively engaged with and contribute to their communities; making their own choices and decisions about their life.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Dimensions_logo_in_500x500px.125x125.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "Dimensions";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.dimensions-uk.org/volunteering>.
id:6425cf69a0624f3ab9fb3d8d :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """The Buckinghamshire branch of the Campaign to Protect Rural England (CPRE) is an environmental charity dedicated to the protection of the countryside and its wildlife in Bucks. 

We aim to:

- Promote and enhance the character of the Buckinghamshire countryside
- Promote a more sustainable approach to land use
- Defend the Buckinghamshire countryside from damaging development

We do this by:

- Responding to planning applications which have a significant impact upon the countryside
- Campaigning on local issues to protect and enhance the countryside 
- Resisting infrastructure developments that irretrievably damage the countryside such as HS2
- Working with fellow organisations with similar aims and local communities to promote the beauty of Bucks
- Liaising with parish councils, district councils and other conservation bodies
- Preparation of responses to wider consultations, including planning appeals


We are a local branch of the national CPRE charity and rely on the support of our active volunteers and members.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/CPRE_new_logo.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "CPRE Buckinghamshire";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.cprebucks.org.uk/>.
id:6425cf6ca0624f3ab9fb3dd6 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """We began 2012 as The Prostate Cancer Charity. Merging with Prostate Action, we forged a new identity as Prostate Cancer UK: a bold, dynamic and very human organisation, with men at the heart of everything we do. 
 
The generosity of our supporters and of The Movember Foundation has allowed us to invest even more in world-class medical research and the best possible information and support for men.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/free-donation.125x125.png>;
                            :organisationName "Prostate Cancer UK";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://prostatecanceruk.org/get-involved/volunteer/opportunities>.
id:6425cf76a0624f3ab9fb3edd :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """West Sussex Libraries provide access to a wide range of local and council information and are an important community space where people of all ages, cultures and social background can come together. Books, information, life-long learning, free internet and Wi-Fi can all be found in our libraries. We also have a range of activities for all age ranges from Baby Rhyme Time, Knit & natter, Relax with Colouring Sessions, IT drop in sessions and basic computer support. 

We have a wide range of volunteer roles in our libraries across West Sussex. Whatever time or skills you have there is a role for you. Volunteering is a great way to meet new people, learn new skills and contribute to your local community. 

For details of all our current volunteering opportunities visit https://www.westsussex.gov.uk/libraries""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Library_service_logo.JPG>;
                            :organisationName "West Sussex Library Service";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.westsussex.gov.uk/libraries>.
id:6425cf77a0624f3ab9fb3f08 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """The Trust�s primary objective is to respect and preserve the treasured relationship between owners and their pets. To this end it works in partnership with owners to overcome any difficulties that might arise. A national network of over 15,000 community service volunteers has been established to provide practical help when any aspect of day to day care poses a problem - for example, walking the dog for a housebound owner. 

A national fostering service is provided for pets whose owners face a spell in hospital - volunteers take pets into their own homes and supply love and care in abundance until owner and pet can be reunited.

The Cinnamon Trust also provides long term care for pets whose owners have died or moved to residential accommodation which will not accept pets. Arrangements are made between owners and the Trust well in advance, so owners do have peace of mind in the knowledge that their beloved companion will have a safe and happy future.

If you require further information on becoming a volunteer with our charity please contact on 01736 758701 or email appeals@cinnamon.org.uk""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Cinnamon_Trust_Logo_7xabLVrWDjCscDMD2Ujhi5.125x125.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "The Cinnamon Trust";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.cinnamon.org.uk/>.
id:6425cf80a0624f3ab9fb3ffe :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """WORLDwrite is an East London based education charity and runs the unique and pioneering online Citizen TV channel WORLDbytes. Dedicated to advancing new knowledge, skills and ideas, the charity promotes excellence in citizen reporting and provides free �on the job� training to young citizens which combines practical film making with tackling challenging issues. On a daily basis we are involved in filming, set design, presenting, interviewing, research, marketing, admin, transcribing, teaching, centre maintenance, fixing kit, leaflet design, website updating, sound creation, computer maintenance, maintaining a centre garden, finance, fundraising, digital promotion, social media and more� The workload and opportunities to have a go at are endless. We are mainly volunteer run too!
Whether you can help out for an hour, half a day, a weekend or forever, we believe everyone can play a role in making Citizen TV matter. The opportunities are exciting and challenging. The potential impact in making hidden voices and lesser known views news, huge! You don�t need to be a Hollywood Director or a camera wizard or a sound engineer and we have an �open door� policy. You will need an interest in exciting ideas and want to help explore them.
Our Citizen TV project WORLDbytes� motto is �Don�t shout at the telly, change the message on it�.
Interested? We'd love to hear from you.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Worldbytes_colour.125x125.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "WORLDwrite";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.worldwrite.org.uk/>.
id:6425d041a0624f3ab9fb4baf :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "The Light of the World Trust will provide a free dog walking and pet feeding/grooming service to those in receipt of state pension and physically disabled adults in receipt of Disability Living Allowance. This service is currently available in Hillingdon and Harrow and has recently extended to Bucks, Berks and Hampshire. This free service is proving to be a genuine need of the elderly and physically disabled.";
                            :organisationName "Light of the World Trust";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.thelightoftheworldtrust.org/pets.html>.
id:6425d048a0624f3ab9fb4c7a :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Caudwell Children provide family support services, equipment, treatment and therapies for disabled children and their families across the UK. We also provide autism assessment and support at our purpose built Caudwell Internation Children's Centre based in Staffordshire. 

Passionate, positive and practical; we are motivated to improve the lives of the estimated 770,000 disabled children living in the UK, starting with the 400,000 living in or on the margins of poverty.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/RCN_Caudwell_Children_Logo_-_Primary.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "Caudwell Children Charity";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.caudwellchildren.com/>.
id:6425d08fa0624f3ab9fb4dbf :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """The Norfolk Hospice is committed to providing outstanding care for people in the local community living with life-shortening illnesses and to their carers, family and friends including bereavement support. 
The support provided is tailored to the individual, encompassing their physical, psychological, social and spiritual needs in an understanding, caring and compassionate way, ensuring dignity is maintained throughout.   
Care is delivered at the hospice in Hillington, either in the Inpatient Unit, Day Therapy Unit or via one-to-one sessions at the hospice. Care is sometimes provided in people's own homes.
The current services cost over £2.5 million per year to run; the NHS funds only 32% of this, with the majority coming from the support of local groups, businesses and individuals.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/1a2fddcb-ef81-4b14-86a0-59f83cf6f9a5_2024-10-25T14:40:22.048Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Tapping House";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.norfolkhospice.org.uk/>.
id:6425d131a0624f3ab9fb595b :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089d,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription """We volunteer at the Museum to share our enthusiasm for pens and our city’s history. Our contributions are essential in maintaining the museum’s operations, and in return, we can engage with people from all over the world, gain valuable work experience, and enjoy the diverse collection of quills, nibs, and typewriters in the museum!

Our volunteers range from the museum’s original founders in 2001 and other long serving volunters to students who were so engaged during their placements that they chose to stay on. Together, we form a collective of historians, pen aficionados, and calligraphers collaborating in the heritage and tourism industry. Our dedication is valued by visitors, who consistently praise our friendliness and knowledge as the highlight of their museum experience.

Interested in being part of this Museum and contributing to our cause? Consider volunteering at the Pen Museum!

""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Logo_2022-2.png>;
                            :organisationName "Pen Museum";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.penmuseum.org.uk/>.
id:6425d23da0624f3ab9fb70c5 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Tenovus Cancer Care is the leading cancer charity in Wales. 

If you have cancer or you�re close to someone who has, it can be frightening and stressful. They can help. 

They bring treatment, emotional support and practical advice to where it matters most; the heart of your community. Whenever you need them they're here for you, and as well as helping you cope their vital research offers you hope.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Tenovus_Cancer_Care.png>;
                            :organisationName "Tenovus Cancer Care";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.tenovuscancercare.org.uk/>.
id:6425d35ca0624f3ab9fb8bc3 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """We are a local, independent charity operating in Oldham, Stockport & Tameside - one of 269 Home-Start schemes operating in the UK.  

At the heart of each Home-Start�s work are our home-visiting volunteers.  Volunteers help families with young children deal with the challenges they face by providing regular one-to-one emotional and practical support tailored to each family.

A child�s early family life is vitally important in their development, and has a strong influence on their future life chances.  Children who are raised in a stable, loving, family environment are more likely to have a positive and healthy future.

Home-Start works because our volunteers are parents. They understand how hard it can be. They work alongside parents, in their own homes, to help them learn to cope with the stresses and strains of life and make sure they have the skills, confidence and strength they need to nurture their children.

We also support families in groups, hold day trips and Christmas parties and help them to access local services, as well as lots of other support.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/HOST_Logo_with_margins.125x125.png>;
                            :organisationName "Home-Start HOST";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://home-starthost.org.uk/>.
id:6425d46ba0624f3ab9fba3a3 :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """Coffee & Computers isa volunteer run community group (based in Haringey, North London) focussed on tackling digital exclusion to ensure equal and affordable access to digital devices and online services for all.

We host regular free digital training sessions, at which we offer advice and support to attendees, across three main areas...

- Digital skills training and support for all types of digital devices (smartphones, tablets, computers) and using online services, websites, apps etc.
- Advice and help with devices, including free to access computers, buying low-cost devices, and schemes that can loan or gift devices for those with limited finances.
- Options for internet connectivity, including using public WiFi, low-cost social tariffs for home broadband, and SIM cards with free data and calls via mobile network.

Through our parent Community Interest Company Tech Together CIC we can also offer subsidised low-cost IT advice and consultancy services to community groups and non-profits, as well as digital training and support to their members and service users.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/66949565-bfc1-4076-b88d-ac06d62adc49_2023-05-08T16:34:06.183Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Coffee & Computers";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://coffeecomputers.org/>.
id:6425d48ca0624f3ab9fba75e :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """We  

We, like everyone else, are aware of the pressures on the mental health service and the health service as a whole. We aim to do what we can to help anyone suffering with a mental illness.

Our advisers are trained in many different aspects of mental health and have a wide range of skill sets to aid any individual who needs our help,Services Offered Listening ear, Signposting, Help with letters/forms and Chat Board.

Were open from 9am till 12am 7 days a week.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/page__2_.png>;
                            :organisationName "J".
id:6425d4b7a0624f3ab9fbac79 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Established in 1977, Friendship Works is the UK�s first youth mentoring service and is a pioneer in the field.  We are a distinct service operating as part of the national charity Family Action. 

We improve the emotional well-being and life chances of children and young people who are facing multiple disadvantages on a daily basis. We provide the vital support these children need to brighten their experience of childhood and build resilience for the future, by matching them with friendship mentors who give one-to-one support for at least two years. We accept referrals for children and young people aged 5-16 in London.

The children and young people we help have a range of problems to deal with, such as living with the after-effects of domestic violence or alcohol and drug misuse, or supporting parents with mental health problems. Some of the young people have mental health issues themselves; some have learning difficulties or are struggling at school; others are caring for disabled or ill relatives at home. 

Whatever a child�s particular circumstances, regular contact with a mentor provides the extra support and friendship they need to help them manage everyday life, explore new interests, have fun, develop life-skills and build the resilience they need to cope with adversity and lead a fulfilling adult life. 

Our volunteers receive ongoing training and support from our dedicated team of professional caseworkers, who are always on hand to offer advice and guidance.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Friendship_Works_RGB_logo_small_wZXyqPMKzJP5kVpyK2KsEM.png>;
                            :organisationName "Friendship Works";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.family-action.org.uk/friendshipworks>.
id:6425d5cca0624f3ab9fbc60a :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Approach has been providing specialist support and advice for older people with dementia and related health issues in North Staffordshire since 1981. With the help and support of partners in the statutory and voluntarily sector; Approach is now a thriving, professional organisation providing a wide range of high-quality services to older people and adults who are socially disadvantaged.
Approach provides a range of service to support people with dementia as well as their carers such as a confidential advisory service, specialist day opportunities groups, 1:1 dementia support, free dementia awareness training and carers cafes.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/new_logo_large_strap_line.png>;
                            :organisationName "Approach";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.approachstaffordshire.co.uk/>.
id:6425d5f5a0624f3ab9fbc763 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Coram Beanstalk believes that when a child becomes a reader, they get the very best chance in life, and every child deserves that.  

Each week, across England, our trained volunteers deliver fun, interactive, reading experiences. They provide one to one support to children, who are behind, giving them the help and encouragement, they need to catch up - to switch onto reading, learn to read and become readers for life.  

We work with partner schools all across England.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Coram_Beanstalk_logo_RGB_REVISED_OUTLINED_Aug22.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "Coram Beanstalk - children's reading charity";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.beanstalkcharity.org.uk/>.
id:6425d5fca0624f3ab9fbc83b :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """Princess Alice Hospice is a local charity dedicated to providing free, high-quality compassionate care and support for patients, their families and carers. We care for people with cancer and other illnesses living in a large part of Surrey, south west London and Middlesex.

We aim to enable all patients to have the best possible quality of life to the end, responding quickly to their needs and wishes. We recognise that family, carers and friends have needs of their own and we are here to provide them with support, comfort and advice at every stage of illness and after death

Through our education and research activities we also work to improve end of life care

Founded by our local community, fundraising and community support are crucially important to our continued work as a charity""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/bff3ed1a-c104-4541-a1ee-6452e2727198_2024-02-22T15:43:15.183Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Princess Alice Hospice";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.pah.org.uk/>.
id:6425d641a0624f3ab9fbcccc :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "Home-Start Croydon is a voluntary organisation committed to supporting local families, in their own homes, who are experiencing difficulties or suffering stress, and who have at least one child under five years of age. Home-Start Croydon aims to increase the confidence and independence of the family by offering confidential support, friendship and practical assistance, through community volunteers visiting families. They can reassure parents that difficulties in bringing up children are not unusual and encourage them to enjoy family life, developing a relationship with the family in which time can be shared and understandings built. The approach is flexible to take account of different needs, encouraging parents� strengths and emotional wellbeing for the benefit of their children, encouraging families to widen their network of relationships and to use the support and services available within the community.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/HS_Croydon_Centre_Main_RGB.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "HOME-START CROYDON";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.croydon-homestart.co.uk/>.
id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "The Baytree Centre is a social inclusion charity for women and girls based in the heart of Brixton. We provide opportunities for women and girls to focus on their education and personal development.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/61d36779-770d-4e94-b9e0-b24e97b95ff4_2025-03-07T13:01:29.246Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "The Baytree Centre Brixton";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.baytreecentre.org.uk/>.
