id:6425d743a0624f3ab9fbe81a :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """Since 1993, we've supported families in these challenging moments by connecting them to trained volunteers in the form of befriending. At its core, befriending embodies the strength and complexity of friendship, enhanced by clear guidelines and mutual respect. It demands a long-term commitment from both parties, to break down walls, build trust and nurture growth – for good.  

We offer two services to the families we support:

Family Befriending - Whole family support for families facing multiple hardships which may include, mental health, family relationships, finances, and isolation. Our volunteers meet with their family for a few hours either weekly or fortnightly for a period of 6-12 months.
Big Buddies - Our Big Buddies volunteers support young people aged 10-18 for a few hours weekly or fortnightly over a period of 6-12 months.
""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/142d679b-169d-4fd1-b37a-485011043509_2025-07-16T12:37:53.930Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Family Friends Charity";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.familyfriendscharity.co.uk/>.
id:6425d74da0624f3ab9fbe92b :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Established in 2008, as a national not-for profit organisation supporting people impacted by hoarding behaviour, HoardingUK is now a UK National Charity (1172719).

We provide free helpline, email and remote advocacy support for people and professionals.

We provide talks to community groups and training to statutory and housing professionals.

We work with organisations throughout the country to set up and run support group development programmes.

We support ethical media and research.

From that day in 2008, HoardingUK has grown substantially.  Our recent Hoarding UK-Impact Survey-2015 validated that we are truly effective, truly inclusive and truly national.

When HoardingUK began its work, hoarding behaviour was largely considered a �lifestyle choice�.   Our work, alongside others, has improved understanding but there is still such a long way to go.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/HUKTRI_colour.png>;
                            :organisationName "HoardingUK";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.hoardinguk.org/>.
id:6425d78aa0624f3ab9fbf09d :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Charity providing Forest School, Environmental Education and Practical Nature Conservation sessions, programs, events and community projects in London.

Aims:

To run services for the community.
To be a not-for-profit organization.
To dedicate our services to take the community outdoor, specially the ones who are not so confident about themselves or around nature.
To promote nature activities, support volunteering and provide help to others organizations through community engagement.
Provide opportunities for the disadvantaged, elderly and school children among others.

Objectives:

To become one of the best outdoor services provider for young people and families who are facing challenges in their lives as well as general community.
To support young people in the transition phase from adolescence to adulthood � from dependence to independence
To become one of the best training provider for professionals working with youth.
To provide training schemes and exchanges of �best practice� with partner organisations in the UK, EU, as well as outside of the European Union.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/Nature_Vibezzz_logo_2.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "Nature Vibezzz";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://naturevibezzz.wordpress.com/>.
id:6425d85da0624f3ab9fc0a38 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Steel Valley Project, based in Stocksbridge, North Sheffield and established since 1988, is a countryside management partnership offering training and work experience to volunteers from a range of backgrounds. Its aims are to:
- improve conditions for wildlife
- provide training and skills development to volunteers
- increase people's enjoyment of the countryside by enhancing public access facilities and the natural surroundings
- support local community groups, such as schools and voluntary groups in order to raise awareness and increase knowledge of our natural history""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/SVP_full_colour_small.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "Steel Valley Project";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.steelvalleyproject.org/>.
