                            :organisationDescription """Marches Family Network is a dedicated charity (Charity No. 1047075) based in Herefordshire, supporting young people with disabilities, aged 3 to 25 and their families. Our core mission is to deliver a wide range of high quality, accessible short breaks, respite care and support services that promote independence, build confidence, and foster a strong sense of belonging.

We understand that families of disabled young people often encounter significant challenges in accessing suitable care and meaningful activities. Our services are specifically designed to meet the individual needs of each young person, while also offering parents and carers vital respite and reassurance. Our highly trained staff receive specialist training in areas such as epilepsy management, gastrostomy (tube feeding), personal care, and positive behaviour support, enabling us to safely and effectively support complex needs.

We deliver a variety of programmes to ensure every young person can enjoy social interaction, fun, and new experiences 
""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/08fa0316-2b55-4cce-9317-9e4e405cbe5a_2025-08-18T13:46:25.645Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Marches Family Network";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.marchesfamilynetwork.org.uk/>.
