id:6425f9b8f2d4b77a6e15f4aa :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """All Aboard Club provides opportunities for autistic and ADHD children to develop their social and communication skills using their special interest in trains.

Run by autism and ADHD specialists, All Aboard Club helps to reduce social isolation for autistic and ADHD children and their families. Our events and activity packs also provide opportunities for the children to develop their social and communication skills, whilst enjoying their interest in trains. 

Our events across London and the Surrey provide an understanding, inclusive and safe environment for children and their parents. The children can build and play with our huge train sets during our child-led play sessions. All our staff and volunteers have personal or professional experience with autism and ADHD, allowing us to support the children when required.

From our events, the children's parents develop a network of other families to share experiences. They also have an opportunity to relax while their children engage with our activities for up to two hours with minimal supervision. """;
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/All_Aboard_little_man_-_400x400_square.125x125.jpg>;
                            :organisationName "All Aboard Club CIC";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.allaboardclub.com/>.
id:6425f9bff2d4b77a6e15f5b0 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """WAITS is an Established, Award-winning Women's Charity that support women who have Experienced Domestic Abuse in and around Birmingham. We have 3 dedicated routes of support:

Domestic Abuse Team - Intensive Transitional support for women who have experienced Domestic Abuse

Community Integration Project - Floating support for Female offender, those at risk of offending and complex needs

Refuge - Independent Housing for Single women over the age of 21 (subject to assessment)""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/E63671D2-8736-4B97-BDEC-32A539581D8B.125x125.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "WAITS - Women Acting In Todays Society";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://waitsaction.org/>.
