id:64260070f2d4b77a6e16a5a5 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "The Sussex Archaeological Society (Sussex Past) is a registered charity whose charitable aim is to enable people to enjoy, learn about and have access to the heritage of Sussex. It does this by opening six historic sites across Sussex to old and young, as well as providing research facilities in our library, running excavations, providing a finds identification service and offering a variety of walks, talks and conferences through our membership programme.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/da7dc885-e74a-43b7-924f-ae174aabe73f_2025-07-03T11:45:16.106Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "The Sussex Archaeological Society";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.sussexpast.co.uk/>.
id:6426033eb9494fbbecde4e76 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "IAF is a small charity operating in the Mansfield and Ashfield area, that helps disadvantaged NEET (not in education, employment or training) young people (aged 16-24) find employment or move into education. Many of the young people we help are young offenders, homeless, suffer from poor mental health, have been abused, or have come from disadvantaged and poverty stricken families. IAF delivers outreach projects, employability training, work experience, and one-to-one mentoring.";
                            :organisationName "The Inspire and Achieve Foundation";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.inspireachieve.co.uk/>.
id:64260874def19e4770803295 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """The Prison Advice and Care Trust (Pact) is a national charity that provides support to prisoners, people with convictions, and their families. We support people to make a fresh start, and minimise the harm that can be caused by imprisonment to people who have committed offences, to families and to communities.

What we do:

Build stronger families and safer communities.
Reduce risk of harm to prisoners and their children.
Remove barriers and increase awareness in public services.
Influence commissioning, policy and legislation.""";
                            :organisationName "Prison Advice and Care Trust";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.prisonadvice.org.uk/>.
id:64260e77387d1275da349ec4 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "Let's Talk About Loss supports people aged 18-35 who have been bereaved, running peer-led monthly meet ups that provide a safe space to talk about grief and loss with others who understand. We also run a blog with advice and tips, events and campaigns to get everyone talking about loss, and we sell our own range of bereavement cards to offer an alternative to the cliched cards you often find!";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/e3895adb-ec48-4709-b08f-e4fa41a9e815_2023-04-21T21:32:23.964Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Let's Talk About Loss";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.letstalkaboutloss.org/>.
id:64260f5fde05bf8ae7c99a1c :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "We�re Rethink Mental Illness, a leading charity provider of mental health services in England. We support thousands of people through our groups, services, policy, campaigns and advice and information. Our work supports us in delivering on our mission: �A better life for everyone severely affected by mental illness.�";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/logo-regular.png>;
                            :organisationName "Rethink Mental Illness";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.rethink.org/>.
id:64260fb4de05bf8ae7c99d32 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """We help older people, families, children and young people.  We help them live safer and more fulfilled lives within their communities.

We understand what people need and how to provide it.  Caring is at the heart of what we do and we respect the dignity of the people we support.

We help people to feel less isolated and to retain their independence, we work with people with disabilities and we support carers.  We help people to build skills and confidence through volunteering.

 

So, what does Connex Community Support do?
Our charity is embedded in our local communities, and we provide a comprehensive range of services to local people:

We encourage people to get involved in their local communities, by providing information and support to volunteers .  We also help other charities and voluntary organisations, so they can find the volunteers they need.
Our Care and Support services provide highly regarded care for older people at home and to adults and children with physical, sensory or learning disabilities.
Over the years we have introduced other services to assist members of the public. These include Befriending,  and a volunteer-delivered Transport service, as well as our Home Maintenance and Cleaning services.  Derbyshire County Council and Derbyshire Fire and Rescue Service trust us to provide the Handy Van service in the north of the county, which helps ensure that people�s homes are safer and more secure.
In the Derbyshire Dales, our Readycall Macmillan service provides social contact and practical support to people affected by cancer or other life-limiting conditions.
 These are just a few of the ways that Connex Community Support can change people�s lives.  Why not explore our website to find out more about how we support and work with our local communities?

""";
                            :organisationName "Connex Community Support";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://volunteering@connex.org.uk/>.
id:64260fe2de05bf8ae7c99f64 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """The Middle Eastern Women and Society Organisation (MEWSo) is a registered charity set up to support Middle Eastern, North African and Asian women in London. We reject every form of discrimination, inequality, and exclusion and aspire to a society where every woman lives in safety with equal opportunities.  We hope for a community in which diversity is considered an element of strength and not of division. 
Founded in 2010, MEWSo aims to:
- Protect and prevent violence against women in BAME communities through its various campaigns.
-Offer emotional and practical support through our advice services with particular emphasis on Domestic Violence and other Welfare issues (e.g. housing, benefits, disability and health, etc.)
-Help women empower themselves to rebuild their lives after experiencing trauma/hardship with workshops and projects catered to the needs of survivors. 
""";
                            :organisationName "Middle Eastern Women and Society Organisation";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.mewso.org/>.
id:64261067de05bf8ae7c9ac7f :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """As the only Hospice in the Milton Keynes area for Adults, our services play a crucial role in the healthcare system of our local  community. Yet, the NHS funding we receive, covers less than a quarter of our costs which total £5.9 Million a year. 

The remainder is funded by you, our community. Our compassionate Specialist Palliative Care  is funded by your donations, by legacy gifts, by community fundraising events, by our network of high street and specialist shops, by our online stores,  by you playing our lottery or giving monthly. We are run by our community, for our community.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/108151cd-22f7-4fab-894d-a66e16577559_2023-05-05T09:03:14.177Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Willen Hospice";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.willen-hospice.org.uk/>.
