                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """Our aim is to be a dependable good neighbour to any St Albans City and District resident who needs help, particularly older people, who may be unwell, isolated, have special needs or may be dealing with a difficult situation and would benefit from our assistance.

We aim to provide help to anyone who needs our support, regardless of their age, ethnicity, background, or personal circumstances. We can help with lifts to medical or social appointments, shopping, odd jobs in the home or garden, and befriending for those who are lonely.

We are run totally by local volunteers.  We have 135 volunteers and 1132 clients that we help.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/0650caf5-3a2c-48a0-ac2c-e53364bc076b_2023-04-04T14:31:22.235Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "St Albans Good Neighbour Scheme";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.stalbansgoodneighbourscheme.org.uk/>.
id:642c3d3c4c0fa363085352f6 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "We are a not for profit social enterprise that has operated for over 25 years.  We provide volunteering, work experience, education and employment for adults with a wide range of needs, supporting them to fulfil their potential in a safe and enabling environment.  In order to do this we rely on volunteers from our community to help the small permanent staff to run the nursery, and perform back office and administrative functions.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/9656857c-85a2-46bb-a05c-bdb453d5cdd7_2023-04-04T15:07:40.600Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Braywick Heath Nurseries";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.braywickheath.co.uk/>.
id:642c3f7f95bfc04479ef0680 :activityDescription "We currently need loads of help to pot on our seedlings into larger pots, ready for them to grow and be sold to our customers.  The work of the nurseries enables us to continue to provide a place for adults with support needs in our community, and you would be working alongside like-minder volunteers who have supported us for a number of years.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:642c3d3c4c0fa363085352f6;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteering in our nursery".
id:642c41ddbdf96ad8d020e142 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """Today’s JLGB is a modern, thriving and innovative national voluntary youth organisation that is a model of professional youth work in the 21st century. JLGB is the United Kingdom’s longest serving Jewish youth organisation, bringing together the best of British traditions and Jewish values, and has been a way of life for tens of thousands of young Jewish people for now over 128 years.

JLGB is a charity that for over 128 years has delivered youth activities, education and employability skills to hard-to-reach groups, primarily in the Jewish community. Our focus as a charity is to ensure young people of faith and cultural backgrounds can fully take part in civil society, and remove all barriers to ensure that their beliefs and values are not compromised when taking part in youth programmes.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/5e69fb78-fbb4-456d-a8aa-6b54619f7276_2023-04-04T15:27:24.992Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Jewish Lads' & Girls' Brigade (JLGB)";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.jlgb.org/>.
id:642d72c05a53abc5bede6c76 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089d,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """We provide sports festivals during school holidays for young people who may not ordinarily have access to the range of sports on offer.
We know how important sport and activity are to both physical and mental well being.  It provides an opportunity to meet new and different groups of young people, encouraging inclusion, developing confidence and team work.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/e1dba4e0-63a8-4a02-9307-dd01a9f52c3c_2023-04-05T13:08:15.535Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Belper Youth Sports";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.bysf.community/>.
