id:64394d07e602e4dae8e05ccf :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089d;
                            :organisationDescription """Our vision
The Auckland Project aspires to change lives in Bishop Auckland by putting people at the heart of everything we do. Working hand in hand with the local community, we will ensure that future generations inherit a prosperous town, filled with hope and rich in opportunities. Meanwhile, our visitors will enjoy days and stays that enrich their minds, bodies and spirits, in the knowledge that their visit continues to revitalise this once forgotten town.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/80e45707-fb8b-43de-9f7c-142d63d2d21b_2023-04-14T12:54:30.980Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "The Auckland Project";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.aucklandproject.org/>.
id:643954dbae1d99f15213fb3a :activityDescription """A host of volunteering opportunities available, Spanish Gallery, Auckland Castle, Mining Art Gallery, Cafe, Weardale Railway, Education. We are about opportunities and choice, more information can be found at   http://bttr.im/4y5sw 
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64394d07e602e4dae8e05ccf;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteering in Heritage Visitor Attractions in Bishop Auckland ".
id:643d17147fe5176abce95133 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "We run a wide variety of activities within the village that attempt to support the community as well as working with other village organisations who have similar aims. We run a small conservation group called 'The Friends of Brook Hollows' which care and look after a small woodland in our village that is owned by East Staffordshire Borough Council.";
                            :organisationName "Rolleston Civic Trust";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://rollestoncivictrust.co.uk/index.html>.
id:643d191b8c28b888508b9d04 :activityDescription "A conservation group that meets monthly to do general maintenance on 'Brook Hollows' which is a small woodland located within the village of Rolleston on Dove. The land is owned by East Staffordshire Borough Council but as a registered group they allow us to complete tasks such as removal of non native plants like Himalayan Balsam and Snowberry, to maintain paths by edging and laying donated wood chip on them, litter picking and creating different environments for local wildlife.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:643d17147fe5176abce95133;
                            :activityTitle "Friends of Brook Hollows".
id:643d191b8c28b888508b9d05 :address "Rolleston-on-Dove";
