id:64404cd69e8cd1f7e6542aa0 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba5089b;
                            :organisationDescription """We’re an independent RSPCA Branch dedicated to helping Devon’s animals in need.  Being almost entirely self-funded means we rely on generosity and support from our local communities to exist. We take in, care for and rehome dogs, cats, rabbits, rodents, birds and ferrets.

We cover from Okehampton to Honiton and Tiverton to Kingsbridge, helping to rescue and rehome animals in the area. Some animals need our help because they have been badly treated or abandoned, others because their owners can no longer care for them.

We give them any necessary veterinary treatment and board them until we can find them a safe, happy new home. We also give advice to owners and, if necessary, help with the cost of veterinary treatment.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/f5934c8e-2b82-46ad-90e7-d4858ba448bf_2023-04-19T20:19:33.758Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Little Valley Animal Shelter - RSPCA Devon";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://rspca-littlevalley.org.uk/>.
id:64412dcf7e38abcd6643e0e3 :activityDescription """Help raise funds for the Hospices by helping within our Charity Shops. The role is varied and could include sorting donations, operating the till or assisting customers in the shop. We would be looking for a 4 hour commitment each week but you can choose to volunteer more if you wish.

What the role involves:

•	Assisting customers on the shop floor 
•	Serving customers at the till
•	Meeting donors and gaining sign ups to the Gift Aid scheme
•	Sorting/preparing donations ready for shop floor display, which may include steaming
•	Merchandising/rotating stock on the shop floor
•	Supporting any new promotions as they occur
•	Light cleaning duties 
•	Any other reasonable duties designated by the Manager in charge  


What's in it for you:

•	Meet new people
•	Try something new
•	Be part of your local community 
•	Learn a new skill or experience
•	Increase confidence and self esteem
•	Improve employment prospects
•	Be part of a team 
•	Use your skills to benefit others 
•	Give you a purpose or routine 
•	Evidence suggests that volunteering has a positive impact on your health and wellbeing

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6411a1316cda783f8fe77887;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Charity Shop Assistant- Leigh on Sea".
id:64412dcf7e38abcd6643e0e4 :address "Leigh Road, Leigh-on-Sea, Southend-on-Sea, Leigh-on-Sea SS9 1BT";
                            :latitude "51.5431535"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.6657466"^^xsd:double.
id:64413bd3adaac0673394551e :activityDescription """We are looking for volunteers to assist our staff at our in-patient unit at Little Havens.
The shift times are from 9am until 1pm (times can be flexible, but ideally 9am start) 

What The Role Involves:

•	Making tea and coffee for patients, visitors etc
•	Helping set up for the day
•	Sitting with patients and/or visitors when needed
•	Ensuring areas around beds are kept tidy and hazard free
•	Answering the call bell system, this may involve, assisting with drinks, opening and shutting windows, opening/closing curtains, operating the TV.
•	Taking menu orders from patients and their main carer
•	Assisting staff to serve meals/snacks to patients and their main carer
•	Removing used crockery/cutlery and return to the kitchen
•	To serve patient meals
•	Helping to maintain a general standard of tidiness throughout the In Patient Unit
•	Answering the telephone and Directing calls to the appropriate person.
•	Answering the telephone to the door system and showing relatives into patient rooms. (To ask care staff if appropriate and to check visitors list before showing them onto IPU)


What We Offer You:

•	Meet new people
•	Try something new
•	Be part of your local community 
•	Learn a new skill or experience
•	Increase confidence and self esteem
•	Improve employment prospects
•	Be part of a team 
•	Move towards making a career change 
•	Use your skills to benefit others 
•	Give you a purpose or routine 
•	Training in a key industry skill """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6411a1316cda783f8fe77887;
                            :activityTitle "Little Havens IPU Volunteer".
id:64413bd3adaac0673394551f :address "Havens Hospices, Priory Crescent, Southend-on-Sea";
                            :latitude "51.5558694"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.7058871"^^xsd:double.
id:6441505ec8ff6f41ae3250a8 :activityDescription "Volunteer Passport Scheme, based in Newcastle upon Tyne. Volunteers complete a single point recruitment process, including a one day training session with Newcastle City Learning, then gain access to a diverse range of 50+ volunteer opportunities.  To find out more contact: Pam.Robinson@volunteeringmatters.org.uk or call Pam on 07590417231";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64147964bdd313f63d021734;
