id:6446358c4be93957775a2d4c :activityDescription """Ever wanted to volunteer for your local charity but hadn’t had time? Our one off taster sessions are short, sweet and stress free.  

Each year we face the challenge of finding the money to cover our running costs. That’s why the work done by our highly motivated team of more than 700 volunteers is so vital to us. We appreciate all of our volunteers' hard work and do everything we can to make volunteering worthwhile. 

With 13 retail shops across the city of Sheffield, we are excited to welcome you to this one off taster session as part of The Big Help Out. With our one off taster sessions, we have variety of days and times available for those who would like to support their local hospice!

Our retail volunteers assist the Shop Manager in all aspects of running our shops; including preparing our donations for the shop floor, keeping our stock room clean and organised, serving customers and visual merchandising. 

Opportunities are varied and subject to change, and we will be in touch to confirm all the details. 
Sign up with the Big help out app and we will get in touch with our dates and times available to give it a go! 

Winners of the Sheffield Volunteering Award 2018 - The Sheffield Volunteering Award is awarded to an 'exemplary organisation working with volunteers'. It recognises the impact that volunteers make on an organisation, as well as the benefits of volunteering for those who take part.

Winners of the Queen's Award for Voluntary Service - This prestigious award recognises our wonderful Volunteers who since 1971 have shown true dedication to help Sheffield people affected by terminal illness.

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6410baa1bc31aec18e3dab80;
                            :activityTitle "Retail Volunteer - Taster Session ".
id:64466f641164d1e8643b5884 :activityDescription """Umbrella supports disabled children and young people to access activities, have fun, build friendships and learn life skills in a safe and supportive environment.
The role is to support our activity days with our Adult, Children & Family services.  The activity days will be run at our locations above or out in the community across the City & County.
Volunteers are asked to assist workers setting up activities for the day, interact with the children and young people, encourage them to engage in activities. Help to make drinks & snacks and clear away after the activity.  The activity days run continuous throughout the year, this includes the school holidays and weekends.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:643fd2304c906a5a4c57ff70;
                            :activityTitle "Activity Support Volunteer".
id:644701ee5674cd9c00167841 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription "We are Clean IT, an anti littering campaign founded with the initiative to make London litter-free. Our project is to collect any litter found on the streets and to encourage to do so as well. Today we are a growing community of sensible earth lovers implanted in England as well as in France and in Tanzania. Any help is precious to us. We are waiting for you!";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/92e80a2a-5e14-42e5-abc2-a966c8d8a0ea_2023-04-24T22:25:49.585Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Charity/environmental campaign";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.instagram.com/clean.it_/>.
id:6447a5d146c144859dd9a242 :activityDescription """The Green Gym is a funded project that aims to improve the mental health and wellbeing of people by connecting them to nature and each other, whilst learning some practical skills. We are delivering free outdoor nature and conservation sessions every other week led by a trained member of staff.

Examples of tasks we have done are dry-stone walling, raised bed construction, nature crafts, building bird boxes, green woodwork, yoga & mindfulness, bushcraft, path maintenance, willow weaving, hazel coppicing, tree planting and vegetation clearance.

We meet every other Wednesday. You don’t need to commit to coming to a certain number of sessions, I just ask you to let me know when you will be coming so I know to expect you on site. 

The sessions run from 10.30am until 1.30pm with a break for hot drinks and biscuits which 
are provided, all you need to bring is some water, some lunch if desired, weather appropriate clothing and sturdy footwear like work boots or wellies.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:642ee29e0a25edd5be9f46c0;
                            :activityTitle "Silverdale Green Gym".
id:6447a5d146c144859dd9a243 :address "Silverdale Country Park, High Lane, Silverdale, Newcastle";
