id:644f2916494c8ad3e5fff381 :activityDescription """Could you support people to be more engaged in their local communities? A number of our participants on the Work and Health Programme have difficulty engaging with services and activities in their local area, you can help them improve their ability to access opportunities and their overall social inclusion.


Examples of ways you can support participants are:

- Attending a training course or appointment

- Helping start a new activity, join a new club or find a new volunteering opportunity

- Help improve confidence travelling to, and being in, busy towns or cities


Your support will make a massive impact to our participants lives and help their overall mental wellbeing by allowing them to lead a more included life within their community. Our Health and Wellbeing Advisors can support volunteers in creating a plan to get participants more engaged.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cd40a0624f3ab9fb07c7;
                            :activityTitle "Social Inclusion Volunteer - Black Country".
