id:644f2919494c8ad3e5fff4bf :activityDescription """Are you able to help our participants  get ready for employment by supporting them to improve their IT skills and navigate online recruitment processes?

In recent years many recruitment processes have moved online but not everyone has the knowledge or experience to confidently apply for jobs this way.  Fear of IT also stops people progressing to gain valuable skills for work. 

As an IT buddy you would support individuals on a one-to-one basis at one of Shaw Trust's bases.
You could help with:

- Navigating online recruitment platforms and the internet in general
- Using email, sending attachments
- Basic functions of a desk-top or lap-top (including tablet or smart phones)
- Using Microsoft Windows based word processing system and Spellcheck
- Formatting documents such as a CV
- Building confidence around IT use

By providing this assistance you will help to significantly improve the ability of individuals to look for work and apply for jobs, as well as increasing their confidence.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cd40a0624f3ab9fb07c7;
                            :activityTitle "IT Buddy".
id:644f2919494c8ad3e5fff4c0 :address "Mafeking Rd, Smethwick B66 2BT, UK";
                            :latitude "52.4999784"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.9673423"^^xsd:double.
id:644f291a494c8ad3e5fff52c :activityDescription """Are you able to help our clients on their journey to employment?

We're looking for volunteers to support with 121 support via the telephone or a virtual platform. The job search support is an opportunity for our clients to  work with a volunteer and get assistance with anything related to their search for work.

You will have the opportunity to share your knowledge and experience of employability and IT skills with a diverse group of people. Furthermore, you will work closely with members of our local team to make a significant impact on our clients lives.

Some examples of activities are:

- Assisting with basic IT tasks, such as adding attachments to emails and navigating job sites
- Reviewing CVs and cover letters - Including amending CVs to suit specific roles
- Helping complete job applications
- Helping prepare for interviews

By offering this help, you will give our clients a helping hand in their search for work and share your experience and knowledge from your own career.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cd40a0624f3ab9fb07c7;
                            :activityTitle "Virtual - Job Search Support - cpa1/west".
id:644f291a494c8ad3e5fff52d :address "Mafeking Rd, Smethwick B66 2BT, UK";
                            :latitude "52.4999784"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.9673423"^^xsd:double.
id:644f291b494c8ad3e5fff5f6 :activityDescription """Volunteer with us at Shaw Trust Enterprises and help people in  your community grow. 

Our Growing Places are social enterprise projects, based on horticulture, that provide wellbeing support to adults and young people with a learning disability, autism, or mental health to become more independent, healthy, and connected within their community.

As a Growing Places Mentor, you will support people at our project to access this valuable time in their week by giving them the support and confidence they need to carry out tasks allocated to them. The people you help may have:
-	Mild to moderate learning disabilities, 
-	Autistic Spectrum Disorder, 
and/or  
-	Mild-moderate neurotic mental ill health (such as stress, anxiety, depression) 

The daily tasks they will take part in all help us make sure the enterprise runs smoothly and is a great place to be for both our Participants and customers. This could be anything from looking after the plants in stock to helping customers.

Some key duties include:

To provide mentoring and coaching support to participants of the service 

To support participants with daily activities such as growing plants, site maintenance, retail & customer service, and housekeeping.

To provide support both one-to-one and in a group setting as participants are taught new skills to enable them to become more independent, healthy, socially connected, and toward employment.

To help individuals to maintain written records relating to the tasks they completed that day.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cd40a0624f3ab9fb07c7;
                            :activityTitle "Growing Places Mentor".
id:644f291b494c8ad3e5fff5f7 :address "Scadbury Park Nature Reserve, Old Perry St, Chislehurst BR7 6PT, UK";
                            :latitude "51.414866"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.08728040000000001"^^xsd:double.
id:644f291d494c8ad3e5fff6bc :activityDescription """Are you able to help our clients get ready for work by supporting them to improve their employment search?

You would be supporting individuals with either 1-2-1 sessions or in a small group at one of the Shaw Trust sites supporting people with:

 - Interview Skills

 - Mock Interviews""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cd40a0624f3ab9fb07c7;
