id:644f291f494c8ad3e5fff7a5 :activityDescription """Looking for an exciting experience in a retail environment? 

Join our friendly team as a retail team member, and you will enjoy the experience of being part of something remarkable in your local community. Join a charity that’s based all over the UK - Shaw Trust. 

As a volunteer retail team member, you will be asked to bring to your role a positive attitude, good organisation and people skills. Depending on your experience and according to your shop manager, you will be involved in different tasks that can help you to improve your knowledge and grow within the charity. You’ll also be able to bring new ideas to the shop. New ideas are always welcome!

Not sure if this is for you? Don’t worry! As a team, we will help and support you to develop all the skills and confidence that are necessary to succeed in this new and exciting role. 

Are you interested in finding out more? Apply as a Volunteer Retail Team Member today and we will get in touch with you.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cd40a0624f3ab9fb07c7;
                            :activityTitle "Retail Team Member - Swindon".
id:644f291f494c8ad3e5fff7a6 :address "45 Havelock St, Swindon SN1 1SD, UK";
                            :latitude "51.559146"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.785524"^^xsd:double.
id:644f9ea58b3911f95a03a9c5 :activityDescription """We are looking for volunteers who can provide administrative support to the Early Intervention Team.   This project supports children and young people with wellbeing and currently offers one to one and group wellbeing support and universal education sessions on substance misuse.

No professional experience is necessary but you do need to be able to perform admin tasks with minimal supervision.

Tasks may include, but not limited to:
•	data inputting
•	general office duties, e.g. photocopying, shredding confidential material, filing
•	taking basic contact details and information from anyone enquiring about the service
•	setting up client files
•	answering the telephone and addressing any queries where possible.  Promptly passing on any message, query or concern to the relevant team member when necessary.  This may entail listening to and reassuring distressed people.  The volunteer will not be expected to offer advice or emotional support, but react in a calm, welcoming and informative manner (we can provide training to help you do this).
•	assisting the team members to organise their appointments activities
•	typing as required (Microsoft Word)
•	preparing information packs / sending out leaflets

A Volunteer Administrator must also abide with strict confidentiality rules
Personal qualities are also important such as:- 
•	good listening skills 
•	positive attitude
•	reliability
•	good communication skills 
•	commitment to recovery principles
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ccb5a0624f3ab9fafb90;
                            :activityTitle "Admin Volunteer".
