id:644fb8f43bb95d9ede5c07bf :activityDescription """As a volunteer befriender you would be asked to visit a person or couple at home that we are supporting, to offer companionship and a friendly, listening ear at a difficult time. Those we support have cancer or other long-term health conditions, or are caring for a loved one who is seriously unwell.

Our companionship volunteers may find themselves reading to someone, accompanying them on a walk, an outing to a garden centre or the shops for a coffee. It may be sharing in a game or puzzles, or performing some practical tasks in the home or garden, filling in a form, perhaps making a phone call for them.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cd5da0624f3ab9fb0b12;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Befriender".
id:644fb8f43bb95d9ede5c07c0 :address "Kimberley Way, Ashford TN24 0SD, UK";
                            :latitude "51.1348066"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.8759588"^^xsd:double.
id:644fb8f43bb95d9ede5c081f :activityDescription """This is an opportunity to help someone who can no longer manage to look after their garden through ill health associated with cancer. If you love to be outside, doing something physical and enjoy gardening, this is a role for you; mowing the lawn, looking after the borders or trimming a hedge.

Many people can no longer look after their garden and cannot afford a gardener, so to have a volunteer to help can provide great comfort and peace of mind and a difficult time in their lives.

Volunteers will not be involved in any personal care, manual handling or lifting, and will not handle medication""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cd5da0624f3ab9fb0b12;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Gardener".
id:644fb8f43bb95d9ede5c0820 :address "Parade, Canterbury CT1 2SG, UK";
                            :latitude "51.2784139"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "1.0810664"^^xsd:double.
id:644fb8f53bb95d9ede5c0873 :activityDescription """This opportunity involves:

•	driving people to and from hospital appointments, especially for chemotherapy and radiotherapy treatment and escorting  them where necessary. These appointments are usually for 15 or 20 minutes. As these treatments often last over a period of several weeks, on a number of days each week, our drivers often volunteer as part of a rota.

•	driving people, who rarely leave their house, for an occasional shopping trip or an outing locally or further afield if you are willing.
You will be reimbursed by Macmillan Crossroads Kent and Medway Volunteer Service and the client at 40p per mile. If you have a friendly, warm and welcoming personality and enjoy meeting new people and making conversation, this could be the ideal volunteering opportunity for you.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cd5da0624f3ab9fb0b12;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Driver".
id:644fb8f53bb95d9ede5c0874 :address "Kimberley Way, Ashford TN24 0SD, UK";
                            :latitude "51.1348066"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.8759588"^^xsd:double.
id:644fb8f53bb95d9ede5c0884 :activityDescription """This is an opportunity to help someone who can no longer manage to look after their garden through ill health, age or infirmity. If you love to be outside, doing something physical and enjoy gardening, this is a role for you; mowing the lawn, looking after the borders or trimming a hedge.

Many people can no longer look after their garden and cannot afford a gardener, so to have a volunteer to help can provide great comfort and peace of mind and a difficult time in their lives.

Volunteers will not be involved in any personal care, manual handling or lifting, and will not handle medication.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cd5da0624f3ab9fb0b12;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Gardening".
id:644fb8f53bb95d9ede5c0885 :address "Kimberley Way, Ashford TN24 0SD, UK";
                            :latitude "51.1348066"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.8759588"^^xsd:double.
id:644fb9f43bb95d9ede5c0bd4 :activityDescription """Who we are

Papworth Trust is a leading disability charity. Our vision is a world where disabled people are seen for what they can do, and our mission is for disabled people to have equality, choice and independence.
OWL Bikes is a team of staff and volunteers who deliver bicycle related sessions to adults with a learning disability. 
We run pop up events in Cambridge and the surrounding area and rely on donated bikes to support our work. We collect about 1000 per year, aiming to refurbish 500 of those.
Where will you fit in?
As one of our bike shop volunteers, you will be asked to support service users in goal focused bicycle related work, in our bikes workshop. You will also have the opportunity to undertake a range of shop based tasks, working with staff, service users and customers into the bike shop. Tasks required will vary day to day but will be based within the shop area of the service. 

Key tasks: 
•	Supporting service users to carry out shop related tasks.
•	Maintenance and repair of bicycle
•	Supporting staff to carry out community based pop up events
•	Working with shop customers
•	Support service users to manage the online E-bay shop.
•	Collect bicycles from local donors (Depending on suitability and holding a current driving license.)
•	Other shop related tasks that arise day to day.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64105c72506e6c8b57049b84;
                            :activityTitle "Bike Shop Volunteer".
id:644fb9f43bb95d9ede5c0bd5 :address "Cowley Rd, Cambridge CB4 0DN, UK";
                            :latitude "52.2311124"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.1591812"^^xsd:double.
id:644fbb83aacc9d0373430874 :activityDescription """Motivate and Inspire positive and long-lasting change! Unlock your own potential and make a difference to your community by supporting vulnerable adults while helping them to unlock their own potential so they can make a valuable contribution to the community in which they live.

We are looking for Community Connection Volunteers in who can volunteer around 2-3 hours per week.

About KeyRing Living Support Networks

KeyRing's support is based on people living in their own homes but sharing their skills and talents with each other and with their communities. We have a volunteer in each Network. The volunteer sees Members regularly and helps the group work together. The volunteer is like a good neighbour who will help out if difficulties arise. Because the volunteer lives in the community, they know what's going on and are able to help Members make links.We also have Community Support Workers and Supported Living Managers who make sure that Members get the support they need. KeyRing believes that Community Connections are very important. We encourage people to make good links in their neighbourhood. Our Members have saved lives, campaigned for street lights and run neighbourhood improvement campaigns. Our Small Sparks fund enables Members with an idea for their community to get a bit of funding to make things happen.

Have you overcome any challenges in your life? Have you got a skill or a talent you would like to share with others? If so, get in touch! We’ll train you as a KeyRing’s Volunteer so you can help vulnerable adults to improve their mental health and wellbeing and to support them to gain greater independence.

Come along for a chat – we want to hear about the things you’re great at and we’ll let you know how you can get involved with KeyRing. We want you to share your skills and talents and help to inspire vulnerable adults. You can be part of many different projects we currently run where you can use your skills to motivate and encourage others to take a part while enjoying the things you love.

Want to learn something new about yourself? Want to help others? Want to make a difference to your community? Or perhaps you want to boost your CV and learn new skills to help your future career! You can improve your confidence and communication, learn how to deal with difficulties and how to improve your wellbeing by supporting vulnerable adults throughout their difficult journeys in life.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cdb5a0624f3ab9fb11d4;
                            :activityTitle "Community Connection Volunteers".
id:644fbb83aacc9d0373430875 :address "Fisher Rd, Oldbury B69 4EL, UK";
                            :latitude "52.50100759999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.9988367"^^xsd:double.
id:644fbb83aacc9d0373430885 :activityDescription """We are looking for a Community Living Volunteer in our Sandwell network who can give 14 hours per week of 'good neighbour' support to the KeyRing Members who live locally in their own homes within the area.

As a Community Living Volunteer you do need to live in the Network area in order to offer the flexible local support and to know the local community resources well.

KeyRing can provide accommodation in the Network area if required.

KeyRing provides support for vulnerable people to live independently in their own homes, including housing brokerage and community inclusion. Our support includes structured tenancy related support; good neighbourly help; help with getting to know the community better; and the facilitation of meeting new friends and maintaining such relationships. We work to enable KeyRing Members to take control over their lives, make informed choices and decisions, to create their own personal networks of support, find meaning in their lives and contribute as active citizens""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cdb5a0624f3ab9fb11d4;
                            :activityTitle "Community Living Volunteer".
id:644fbb83aacc9d0373430886 :address "Fisher Rd, Oldbury B69 4EL, UK";
                            :latitude "52.50100759999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.9988367"^^xsd:double.
id:644fbd0d449fb9795b2fb5e4 :activityDescription """We are looking for a pool of event stewards to help us with around 5 events a year to assist with our programme of garden & community events 

The role may involve 

•	Meet and greet stall owners, entertainers & event visitors
•	Checking in on stall owners
•	Crowd monitoring; counting attendees, crowd density,
•	Aid with rapid response to emergency situations, emergency evacuation, & control, monitoring safety equipment etc. Look out for & report suspicious activity.
•	Site clearance & litter picking
•	Response to complaints from members of the public.
•	Stall holding and craft based activity
•	Stage management & Sound technicians: ensuring set up is correct and safe, 
•	Marketing: handing out leaflets, ect.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641834de11ac4e5fee26ed1e;
                            :activityTitle "Event Steward".
