id:644fbea4449fb9795b2fc1d0 :activityDescription """Proactively promote partnership working to improve community safety by:

• Maintaining and improving our three social media platforms, plus YoutTube channel when relevant, to improve our social media presence. (Facebook, Twitter and Instagram)

• Sharing information with our partners to further promote NottsWatch via their social media.

• Regularly updating information on our existing Facebook,Twitter and Instagram pages by:
-Building strong sources to follow to RT/share.
-Promote original content sharing neighbourhood watch success stories plus NottsWatch goals & achievements and events.

• Compiling a register of positive & successful FB community groups NottsWatch may
engage with to share information.

Liaise with Comms Team and contribute to preparing quarterly reports for NW Review meetings.

Attend majority of quarterly Review meetings. (First Friday afternoon October, January, April and July at Dunkirk Community Centre, NG7 2JW)""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d8d2a0624f3ab9fc184e;
                            :activityTitle "Social media editor ".
id:644fbea4449fb9795b2fc1d1 :address "The Old School, Montpelier Rd, Dunkirk, Nottingham NG7 2JW, UK";
