                            :longitude "-1.1817303"^^xsd:double.
id:644fbf84449fb9795b2fc297 :activityDescription """Are you a friendly, reliable, community-focused person, with previous experience working or volunteering with children?

Caudwell Children are looking for Birmingham-based volunteers for our ongoing project, “All Roads Lead to Alexander”. This project is an opportunity for life stories from Commonwealth families to be told, from the time they left their country until the time they arrived in the West Midlands, as told through the eyes of their disabled and abled children.

The Birmingham 2022 Commonwealth Games will be a global stage to showcase the talent and diversity of Birmingham and the West Midlands. We will use that global stage to lift up disabled children, working to create abled and disabled co-operation and to foster new relationships between communities.

We need volunteers to assist with creative workshops for children. Responsibilities will include:

- Assisting Caudwell Children staff member(s) in running the community activity music and engagement sessions
- Help to ensure all children are safe during the activity sessions
- Support staff members with planned activities
- Participate in setting up an activity and helping with the set down
- Communicate and work with the children to ensure they have fun
- Contribute to and represent Caudwell Children as part of the ‘All Roads Lead to Alexander’ Commonwealth Games project
- Contribute to the legacy of the project within the community through legacy lifeskills sessions

If you’re looking to gain community connections, communication and teamwork skills, and experience working with children, please apply.

Suggested commitment of 8-12 hours per month - full training and support will be provided.

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d048a0624f3ab9fb4c7a;
                            :activityTitle "Children's Activity Volunteer (ARLTA)".
id:644fbf84449fb9795b2fc298 :address "Messenger Rd, Smethwick B66 3DX, UK";
                            :latitude "52.4940011"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.9565199"^^xsd:double.
id:644fbf8a449fb9795b2fc53e :activityDescription """We need partnerships to deliver incredible change on the ground, where we can have greatest impact in supporting all children with disability and their families. Partnerships to help us better understand the problems and to find the solutions to tackle obstacles at key transition points in a child’s life. Partnerships to raise our voice, raise our profile and increase our relevance and presence within educational, health & social care and corporate professions and environments. Partnerships which help us grow in scale and sustainable support for our mission. And partnerships to raise awareness - that we should ‘See the child, Not the disability’, And partnerships which create ‘Time to Shine’ opportunities for children focusing on their ability not their disability. 

Roles and Responsibilities:
•	Assisting with pre-developed partnership campaigns 
•	Building prospect development target lists 
•	Conducting specific research on organisations/ individuals to understand their interests 
•	Engage with specific targets to build their interest in the Caudwell cause. 
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d048a0624f3ab9fb4c7a;
                            :activityTitle "Campaign Support Specialist ".
id:644fbf8a449fb9795b2fc53f :address "Caudwell International Children's Centre Keele Science & Innovation Park, Innovation Way, Newcastle-under-Lyme, Newcastle ST5 5NT, UK";
                            :latitude "53.00165209999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.2627464"^^xsd:double.
id:644fbf8a449fb9795b2fc590 :activityDescription """The Grants deparment has been at the centre of that growth, securing additional restricted funding in order to drive forward services, create new services and generally grow the charities income. The wider Fundraising team has grown, with new income streams being developed that can aide services.  

Roles and Responsibilities:

•	General administration duties to support Grants function 
•	Researching trusts and foundations 
•	Inputting data into relevant spreadsheets and/ or client-based systems 
•	Contacting trusts and foundations in regards to existing applications  
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d048a0624f3ab9fb4c7a;
                            :activityTitle "Grants Administration Assistant Volunteer ".
id:644fbf8a449fb9795b2fc591 :address "Caudwell International Children's Centre Keele Science & Innovation Park, Innovation Way, Newcastle-under-Lyme, Newcastle ST5 5NT, UK";
                            :latitude "53.00165209999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.2627464"^^xsd:double.
id:644fbf8c449fb9795b2fc673 :activityDescription """Established in 2000, Caudwell Children is a national charity which works to transform the lives of disabled children and their families, enabling them to challenge the barriers they face throughout childhood by providing practical and emotional support.

The charity is going through an exciting period of growth having recently opened a new state-of-the-art facility for multi-disciplinary therapy programmes for childhood disability and research of neurodevelopmental conditions, including autism, within the grounds of Keele University.

The energy redress scheme is a funded project to support parents/carers of disabled children -  to identify, engage and support families to address energy efficiency and affordability, in another important step to transforming the lives of disabled children.

The duties of the volunteer role are as follows;
• Deliver essential services and support families ensuring homes are warm and efficiently heated
• Conduct personalised home surveys and provide a combination of information and support to understand energy bills, energy improvements and reduce energy costs
• Understand specific needs of families with disabled children""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d048a0624f3ab9fb4c7a;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Disability Energy Champion".
id:644fbf8c449fb9795b2fc674 :address "Nottingham, UK";
                            :latitude "52.9540223"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.1549892"^^xsd:double.
id:644fc0c5449fb9795b2fc792 :activityDescription """Our Volunteering Office will be closed from 24th December 2020 till 3rd January 2021. We will respond to all enquiries as soon as we can from 4th January.  

Compassionate Neighbours is free, community-led support for people nearing the end of life through age or illness, or who are lonely or socially isolated. 
People living with serious, long-term or terminal illness often struggle with loneliness and could do with extra support. Compassionate Neighbours can really make a difference. They are a network of trained volunteers who are willing to offer their time, companionship and support to people living in their community.
We are looking for volunteers who can give 1-2 hours of time a week to visit people in their local community. You might: 
•	Offer companionship, emotional support and a listening ear
•	Provide practical support such as making a cup of tea or changing a light bulb
•	Help people stay connected to their friends, family and the community
•	Guide and assist people to access services that are likely to be of help to them. 
•	Provide a break for a carer
You could make a real difference to someone in your local neighbourhood.


Please find online Application Form here:
https://www.pah.org.uk/volunteer-roles/compassionate-neighbour/

If you have any questions please don't hesitate to contact us 01372 461856 or volunteering@pah.org.uk""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d5fca0624f3ab9fbc83b;
                            :activityTitle "Compassionate Neighbour".
id:644fc0c5449fb9795b2fc793 :address "South St, Epsom KT18 7PX, UK";
                            :latitude "51.3307575"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.2699623"^^xsd:double.
id:644fc0ca449fb9795b2fca1d :activityDescription """Our volunteers help with serving customers, sorting and pricing goods, making displays, and other roles.
If you have a few hours, a half day or a whole day that you could spend with us we would love to hear from you.
The role is great fun and you will be working in a very supportive and inclusive team.

Our charity shops contribute significant funds to the Hospice to enable it to continue to support patients and their families across our catchment area. This volunteer role will assist in the day-to-day running of our Princess Alice Hospice shops, with the purpose of maximising sales and profitability.

Tasks include:
- Assisting and serving customers
- To actively sell Hospice lottery tickets when on the till
- Promoting gift aid to donors
- Assist with the moving and handling of some bulky items
- Operating the till and cash handling
- Assisting in keeping the shop clean and tidy
- Positively contributing to team working in the shop
- Promoting the public understanding of the work of Princess Alice Hospice

Training and support:
All volunteers will receive training and support throughout their time at Princess Alice Hospice. All volunteers will be invited to a group induction training course, have access to online learning and our wider education programme.

Benefits of the role:
You will be volunteering in a friendly and inclusive retail team. This is a great opportunity to develop your skills and give something back to the local community.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d5fca0624f3ab9fbc83b;
                            :activityTitle "Shop Volunteer in West Ealing".
id:644fc0ca449fb9795b2fca1e :address "Ealing Broadway Centre, 64 The Broadway, London W5 5JY, UK";
                            :latitude "51.5126255"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.3031617"^^xsd:double.
id:644fc0e9449fb9795b2fca5f :activityDescription """Please note that although many of our volunteer roles are currently paused to help prevent the spread of Coronavirus, our volunteering team is vitally important to us and we still want to hear from anyone who would like to support us in this way, so that we can welcome them on board once the current situation improves. If you have any questions please contact the Volunteering Team on 01372 461856 or volunteering@pah.org.uk


This is a great opportunity for families to support Princess Alice Hospice.  As Family  Community Fundraisers you will lead the collection tin activity in your local area, placing tins in local cafes, shops etc. At least every 3 months you will collect the full tins and replace with new ones, returning the funds to the Hospice. You will also support other varied community fundraising activity such as delivering posters etc to your local Princess Alice Shop as well as distributing leaflets.

Time commitment
A flexible commitment of around 4 hours a month at a time to suit you and your family, will the expectation that you will come to the Hospice every one – two months. 

Age Requirements
We really want to encourage children and young people to participate in volunteering.  As a family you are welcome to bring your children with you when you visit shops to replace the collecting tins.  From age 7 children will be registered as volunteers on our database and we will count their volunteer hours.  Certificates will be awarded for 10, 25 and 50 hours of volunteering.  You will be responsible for your children at all times when you are volunteering and you must volunteer together as a family.  Children can only volunteer independently when they are 16 years old.

Tasks and activities
•	Retrieve existing collection tins from an agreed section of the catchment area local to you, replacing with new tins around every 3 months and returning the full tins to the Hospice
•	Identify opportunities to place new collection tins in your local shops, cafes etc and then commit to collecting them around every . Complete the required paperwork to record their location and details
•	Deliver event and marketing materials (leaflets, posters) to local shops and businesses including Princess Alice shops
•	Share information about local community events that PAH could have a presence at. 
•	Occasionally support leaflet deliveries in your local area""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d5fca0624f3ab9fbc83b;
                            :activityTitle "Family Community Fundraiser".
id:644fc0e9449fb9795b2fca60 :address "Harold Ave, Hayes UB3 4QW, UK";
