                            :longitude "0.0229726"^^xsd:double.
id:644fc4eea3c53c19c9b7513b :activityDescription """Our Vulcan and Cold War volunteers take lucky ticketholders on a journey of a lifetime. They are the Cold War enthusiasts who make peoples dreams, of sitting in our Vulcan and Phantom, come true.
 
We are proud to offer the chance to join a very special team that offers our visitors the rare opportunity to take part in the Vulcan and Cold War Experience. This starts with the chance to sit inside our stunning Avro Vulcan B2 before being taken on a tour of London’s Cold War aircrafts and ending in a cockpit tour and the chance to sit in the pilot seat of the McDonnell Douglas Phantom FGR.2. The experience has been carefully crafted by our team of volunteers with the guidance and support of our events and collections teams. 

For the last few years, these extra special access events have taken place on the last Tuesday of each month; and every year we sell out in a matter of weeks. So now we are looking to offer more sessions and give people the chance to buy a very sought after ticket. We will be offering the experience on alternating Wednesday’s and Saturdays, once a month, throughout 2020. We have an excellent Tuesday team, so now we are after a Wednesday and Saturday team.

Would you like to be the person who gets up close and personal inside the Vulcan, to share your knowledge of the cold war and be a part of an amazing team?
 
We will offer training; all you need to apply is, some knowledge, and a lot of enthusiasm for Cold War History and the RAF. You will start off being trained on the tour, then you will move on to accessing the Phantom, before moving to accessing the Vulcan. 
With
•	Our visitors
•	Our 3D Collection
 
 	When
•	alternate Wednesday or Saturday 
•	10.00am – 2:30pm 	

Frequency
•	Ad hoc
•	Monthly

Further Information
•	Attendance at a training/selection sessions is required to be considered for the role. These events are taking place on Wednesday 20 November at 1.00pm – 4.00pm or Sunday 24 November at 1.00pm-4.00pm.  
•	Further information about the training/selection session will be provided when you sign up to book your place, after your initial application.
•	Reminders for upcoming shifts are sent a few weeks before the session
to confirm your availability
•	At the start of the event, a briefing meeting takes place, where we provide you with relevant information specific to that event, your roles for the day and a reminder of the expectations.

 


Closing Date: Sunday 10 November 2019

To support and thank our volunteers we offer:
•	Flexible opportunities
•	Skills development
•	Food and travel expenses	•	Invitations to special events
•	Museum discounts
•	References""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425dc2aa0624f3ab9fc643f;
                            :activityTitle "Aircraft Access Volunteer (Vulcan & Cold War Experience)".
id:644fc4eea3c53c19c9b7513c :address "Grahame Park Way, London NW9 5LL, UK";
