id:644fca22a3c53c19c9b76a57 :activityDescription """Do you have a passion to support people on their journey of rediscovering their strengths and aspirations through art and craft?

If so we would love to hear from you!

We are looking for passionate and committed volunteers to support the Folkestone Haven.

About The Folkestone Haven

The Folkestone Haven will be open 365 days for people fromacross the whole of Folkestone & Hythe District, from 18:00 – 23:00 (Mon-Fri) and 12:00 – 23:00 (Sat / Sun & bank holidays). The service will support people who are experiencing a self defined 
 mental health crisis. These might be local people who are known to primary health, and secondary mental health services, but equally who may be unknown to all statutory and voluntary mental health services, but experiencing a mental health crisis which may cause them to struggle to cope. The Haven will provide a welcoming, friendly and nonstigmatising environment on Sandgate Road, Folkestone, to cater for each individual’s needs: an initial assessment process, 1:1 support sessions with social prescribing, access to counselling, social activities, chill out space and hot and cold refreshments.

Location: Folkestone Town Centre""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cec6a0624f3ab9fb3209;
                            :activityTitle "Arts and Crafts Facilitator Volunteer - Folkestone Haven".
id:644fca22a3c53c19c9b76a58 :address "69 Sandgate Rd, Folkestone CT20 2AF, UK";
                            :latitude "51.0782756"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "1.1783798"^^xsd:double.
id:644fcac1a3c53c19c9b76c03 :activityDescription """Share your IT skills with chatty Victoria

 

Our member Victoria is a very friendly, chatty lady however due to her health she struggles to get out of the house and spends all of her time at home.  While she has the support of her carers for her physical needs, due to their workload they don't often have time to stop and chat and Victoria finds herself becoming increasingly lonely and isolated and feeling cut off from society.

 

She would love to find a volunteer befriender to visit her at home and teach her some new IT skills so she can access the wider world through her devices. By  learning some IT skills she will be able to communicate with her friends and family more often which will help fight her loneliness.

 

No experience is required simply a warm heart, a chatty and friendly manner and some basic IT skills.

 

Could you be the person who can open Victoria's world up? Apply today and make a huge difference.....""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ce43a0624f3ab9fb225b;
                            :activityTitle "Help Victoria Get Online".
id:644fcac1a3c53c19c9b76c04 :address "";
                            :latitude "0"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0"^^xsd:double.
id:644fcac2a3c53c19c9b76c68 :activityDescription """Shari would love to get out more to the theatre, cinema  and exhibitions - could you be the one to help her make this happen?

 

Our Member Shari lives alone in the Hammersmith area and has a real passion for the theatre and films with audio descriptions. Due to her sight loss, she finds it really difficult getting out and about and lacks the confidence to travel alone. Subsequently, she is beginning to feel quite isolated and cut off from so much available to her locally.  Ideally Shari is looking for a volunteer who shares the sames interests and who would also benefit from a friendly companionship.

 

Shari not only enjoys films and plays but also has an interest in psychology, history and archaeology - she would also enjoy keeping a bit more fit and maybe going to the gym. Shari is flexible with times and we would provide you all the training you needed to become Shari's volunteer including guiding skills. No experience is required simply the enthusiasm and desire to be a positive change in one of our member's life's.

 

Could you brighten up Shari's week - then apply today""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ce43a0624f3ab9fb225b;
                            :activityTitle "Befriender - Enjoy the arts with Shari".
id:644fcac2a3c53c19c9b76c69 :address "London W6 0BU, UK";
                            :latitude "51.4940852"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.2281893"^^xsd:double.
id:644fcb79a3c53c19c9b76cdb :activityDescription """Our Place are looking for enthusiastic volunteers who would like an opportunity to share their passion, knowledge and experience with the people who attend the weekend drop-in groups. 

The new CREW (Creative, Recreational, Educational and Wellbeing) project aims to bring people from the community to share their passion with other local people at the centre to increase understanding, reduce loneliness and inspire others to get involved. 

Would you like the chance to share your enthusiasm for scrap-booking, knitting or yoga? Been on an interesting holiday and fancy sharing stories from your adventures? Enjoy playing music and would be up for giving a small impromptu concert?

Whatever moves you, please get in touch. 

This could be 
... Art sessions
... Crafting sessions
... An interesting talk on a subject you are passionate about 
... A gentle exercise class
... or something completely different.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:643e7be1d1225c29a0e396e3;
                            :activityTitle "'CREW' Volunteers".
