id:644fcc58a3c53c19c9b7738a :activityDescription "Our Support To Court Service provides assistance in applying for protective orders through the civil courts.  Our trained MacKenzie friends can help write statements for court, assist with submitting paperwork to the court and can attend hearings.  We also support through child arrangement proceedings.  Our Support To Court team support women all over Kent virtually and are able to attend court at Medway, Dartford and Canterbury.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425dc9da0624f3ab9fc7194;
                            :activityTitle "Support To Court volunteer - SATEDA (Swale Action To End Domestic Abuse)".
id:644fcc58a3c53c19c9b7738b :address "Magpie Hall Rd, Chatham ME4 5XJ, UK";
                            :latitude "51.366714"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.5294022"^^xsd:double.
id:644fcc59a3c53c19c9b773e7 :activityDescription """We hold x 2 Hubs a week, where refugees are welcome.  We have welcome packs and care packs, which are delivered to new refuges. We make the pick-ups on site; we also have plenty of items to donate to the refugees, to try and help the easing into a new country as easy as we can.  We support through benefits, housing, work, and whatever needs we are met with. We have a safe place, so ensure that Safeguarding is followed. Ukrainians meet, have a coffee and a chat, and build communities.

We are looking for volunteers to welcome Ukrainians to the Hub, making sure policy is covered with signing in; to support with making care and welcome packs; help sort donations; and to be a friendly, approachable face.

To not be afraid to ask a question, or for support. To recognise the fragility and vulnerability of refugees, and be able to highlight any concerns.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425dc9da0624f3ab9fc7194;
                            :activityTitle "Hub Support - Sittingbourne & Sheppey Helping Ukraine".
id:644fcc59a3c53c19c9b773e8 :address "Ave of Remembrance, Sittingbourne ME10 4DD, UK";
                            :latitude "51.3382218"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.7336492"^^xsd:double.
id:644fcc5aa3c53c19c9b77459 :activityDescription """We provide support to young people in care, at risk of entering care, or young people leaving care.  In addition, we provide early preventative support to young people experiencing mental health and wellbeing trauma, those involved in risk-taking behaviour, and to young people struggling to engage in education.

Volunteers are matched with a young person who shares similar hobbies/interests, and meet each other weekly/fortnightly/monthly, and take part in an activity together, e.g. bowling, bike ride, dog walks, museum visit - anything!

Goals are agreed at the outset and worked towards.

Volunteers must be good at listening, have a non-judgemental approach, be understanding, and have patience and empathy.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425dc9da0624f3ab9fc7194;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Mentor/Befriender - The Young Lives Foundation".
