id:644ffb4812535322aa32c680 :activityDescription "Do you have a couple of hours to spare each month to help someone with sight loss to get out and about? RNIB's Young People's Group are looking for volunteers to take part in the activities with the young people (aged 18 – 30) as well as doing sighted guiding.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6411fb368eab8ac79a6603e4;
                            :activityTitle "Young People's Group -8714 (Leeds)".
id:644ffb4812535322aa32c681 :address "Leeds LS2 8JU, UK";
                            :latitude "53.8010328"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.542523"^^xsd:double.
id:644ffb4912535322aa32c6ea :activityDescription """Do you have an interest in how technology can enable people with sight loss to live connected, independent lives? We'd love you to get involved in our regional hubs, working with our technology service coordinators to help people with sight loss develop the knowledge, skills and confidence to use everyday technology.

Assistive Technology Training; New technology training; Support people with IT development""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6411fb368eab8ac79a6603e4;
                            :activityTitle "Tech Hub Support - Barking Library -12179 (London)".
id:644ffb4912535322aa32c6eb :address "Barking IG11 7NB, UK";
                            :latitude "51.5365698"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.08005050000000001"^^xsd:double.
id:644ffb4a12535322aa32c74b :activityDescription """Would you like to play a key role in supporting blind and partially sighted people in your local area? Are you great at communicating, love meeting others and enjoy using your admin and organisational skills? If this sounds like you, you’re the person we’re looking for to support our Erdington Sight Loss Support group meeting. The group began in 2019 and we resumed meeting face to face in May 2022.

We would like your help with:

• Planning and organising group meetings
• Liaising with the venue
• Contacting and booking guest speakers
• Supporting volunteers with sight loss with their volunteering activities.
• Sighted guiding
• Giving practical help to individuals so they can take part in the events.

*Helping to organise speakers for the event
*Liaising with the café
*Assisting with paperwork
*Assisting with accessing information
*Sending, receiving & replying to emails about the group""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6411fb368eab8ac79a6603e4;
                            :activityTitle "Community Volunteer - Erdington Sight Loss Support Group -12191 (Birmingham)".
id:644ffb4a12535322aa32c74c :address "High St, Erdington, Birmingham B23 6RH, UK";
                            :latitude "52.5261049"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.8370516"^^xsd:double.
id:644ffd4812535322aa32c978 :activityDescription """The Assessor role is interesting, challenging and very rewarding.  You will be making a real difference to people's lives and will be part of a very happy team of volunteers and staff.

Runnymede & Spelthorne Citizens Advice need volunteer Assessors for our Addlestone and Sunbury Office.  Full training is provided for the role.  You will interview clients and undertake an initial assessment to explore what problems they have come to help with.  You will provide information and practical help using a variety of sources with support from the Advice Session Supervisor.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:642ac0e6a63b9e51055abc5d;
                            :activityTitle "Citizens Advice Assessor".
id:644ffd4812535322aa32c979 :address "The Old Library, Church Rd, Addlestone KT15 1RW, UK";
