                            :longitude "-0.4937167"^^xsd:double.
id:644ffe2012535322aa32ca64 :activityDescription "In a time when funding and service support is tight, our clubs make a real contribution to local communities and the young people they serve.  Being a trustee for one of our clubs could help ensure its current and future stability, a high quality youth provision, a well trained volunteer team, a well respected community asset.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cdcba0624f3ab9fb1471;
                            :activityTitle "Youth Club Trustee (Woking)".
id:644ffe2012535322aa32ca65 :address "Commercial Way, Woking GU21 6EN, UK";
                            :latitude "51.31912879999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.5580725"^^xsd:double.
id:644ffe2112535322aa32cace :activityDescription "Youth clubs offer a safe environment where young people can meet up, make new friends and participate in a range of worthwhile activities.  Volunteers provide a vital resource to these clubs.  As a Club Co-Ordinator volunteer, you would be based in one of our youth clubs / projects, where you will provide support to the club leaders, but also ensuring necessary administration is carried out along with two-way communication to parents, volunteers and trustees.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cdcba0624f3ab9fb1471;
                            :activityTitle "Youth Club Co-Ordinator (Woking)".
id:644ffe2112535322aa32cacf :address "Middle Walk, Woking GU21 6XT, UK";
                            :latitude "51.3187826"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.5593485"^^xsd:double.
id:644fffae12535322aa32cd4c :activityDescription """Are you looking for a really rewarding volunteer opportunity? People with sight loss often struggle with everyday tasks that we may take for granted, like shopping. This is where you can help! 

This is an opportunity to engage in a voluntary role which helps blind and partially sighted people remain independent. We are looking for Shopper Volunteers to either collect the client from their home or meet at an agreed venue and accompany them shopping whilst acting as a guide and eyes to help them make their purchases. Some of our clients ask for help shopping on a regular basis, while others may request occasional help, perhaps to choose clothes or gifts. Some members also require assistance with unpacking once home, but this would be agreed beforehand with both client and volunteer.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cd4aa0624f3ab9fb08ed;
                            :activityTitle "High Wycombe Shopper".
id:644fffae12535322aa32cd4d :address "Oxford Rd, High Wycombe HP11, UK";
                            :latitude "51.6317699"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.7556131"^^xsd:double.
id:6450e344308102717faa0c12 :activityDescription """Wanting to get more involved at St Christopher’s? We have a huge range of volunteering roles for you to chose from. 

Whether its baking a cake every now then or visiting patients in the community we’d welcome your support. 

You can find out what roles we have available here: 
www.stchristophers.org.uk/volunteering-opportunities""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641c56e34c04e246950854f2;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer for St Christopher's Hospice ".
