id:6451086cc667ad7444afa933 :activityDescription """The volunteer visits an older person each week to help alleviate feelings of loneliness and isolation. 
As far as possible, we try to  match the volunteer to the service user according to their interests and background, so that there are shared interests.

These visits take place at a mutually convenient time for the volunteer and service user and can be at weekends or in the evenings. 

Cambridgeshire and Peterborough""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641c2882a4c8e01bf064ec1b;
                            :activityTitle "Sharing Time Volunteer".
id:64510882d03e47f216d73ece :activityDescription """As a charity we provide attachment focused support to girls and boys in school. We aim for every child who we support to feel safe, seen, soothed and secure.

Cherished is our service to support girls, delivered by our female mentors. All mentoring sessions run for a minimum of 1 hour a week, for 12-weeks. A good mentor has excellent listening skills, excellent relationship skills and helps to improve the well-being of girls who are referred to us for support.

As a 1:1 mentor you will support a girl in primary or secondary school on a 1:1 basis. You will plan your sessions accordingly to meet the unique needs and interests of your mentee. You will complete sessional records following each mentoring session and will also complete evaluation forms at the end of the mentoring course.

As a mentor you will be required to complete our Cherished Mentor Training, where you will work towards your Level Three Mentoring Qualification. You will complete Safeguarding training and training on Adverse Childhood Experiences.

If you would be interested in becoming a Cherished Mentor, please get in touch.

Birmingham - West Midlands based.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641061b0e33a74ff7511b5d9;
                            :activityTitle "Cherished 1:1 - Female Mentor".
id:64510882d03e47f216d73ecf :address "Boldmere Road, The Royal Town of Sutton Coldfield, Birmingham, Sutton Coldfield B73 5UE";
                            :latitude "52.5448793"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.840628"^^xsd:double.
id:64510a58911f2b77fbb95b5c :activityDescription """At Cherished, we are always producing creative resources to best support our young people.

These resources are used for mentoring, workshops, school courses and care packs. 

As a volunteer you can support us by putting together our resources and supporting us in our office, or remotely at home. (Please note you will be required to travel to and from our office to collect the resource materials).

Resource creation could include: laminating, cutting, sticking or simple craft.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641061b0e33a74ff7511b5d9;
                            :activityTitle "Cherished Resource / Office Volunteer".
id:64510a58911f2b77fbb95b5d :address "Boldmere Road, The Royal Town of Sutton Coldfield, Birmingham, Sutton Coldfield B73 5UE";
                            :latitude "52.5448793"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.840628"^^xsd:double.
id:64516b3857d588ae4560f772 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription "We are a group of residents of Ainslie Wood Road E4, who are working with Waltham Forest Council to turn the road into a bee friendly street. We are looking for volunteers to join us once a month to help keep the road clear of weeds and plant native flowers to ensure beneficial wildlife can thrive in our area. No prior experience required!";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/784ff897-7c2b-4c4a-a569-57d4a1c2b8ad_2023-05-02T19:57:43.574Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Ainslie Wood Bee Friendly Street";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100087443191756>.
id:64516c1730bf811bcd697642 :activityDescription """Join us on the third Sunday of every month to help clear Ainslie Wood Road of weeds, plant native flowers and meet our neighbours!

We are a group of residents of Ainslie Wood Road E4, who are working with Waltham Forest Council to turn the road into a bee friendly street. We are looking for volunteers to join us once a month to help keep the road clear of weeds and plant native flowers to ensure beneficial wildlife can thrive in our area. No prior experience required!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64516b3857d588ae4560f772;
                            :activityTitle "Ainslie Wood Road - Gardening Volunteer Group".
id:64516c7230bf811bcd697707 :address "Ainslie Wood Road, London";
