id:64523fbd0076ca958b7f179e :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription "Blackthorn Trust is a Maidstone-based Health and Community Hub where people can recover, grow and develop. We have been running for over 35 years, supporting people with physical and mental health conditions. We offer workshop activities and specialist therapies at our unique site which includes a large biodynamic garden, craft, kitchen & woodwork studios and therapy rooms. Our work is based on the belief that more than medication is required to affect positive change.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/956fd021-3478-4ef1-9f8f-8731ec9ab30a_2024-03-25T14:23:54.850Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Blackthorn Trust";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.blackthorn.org.uk/>.
id:645259c4017b3fcb4bab5b74 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "We are an active Scout Group offering a wide range of development opportunities to Beavers (aged 6-8), Cubs (aged 8-10.5) and Scouts (aged 10.5-14).";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/87ad6885-ef3a-434c-81f6-1b5c1a08b2b0_2023-05-03T12:55:28.579Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "13th Cambridge Scout Group";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.13thcambridgescoutsgroup.co.uk/>.
id:64525b03d57002d0ed6500c4 :activityDescription "Join our experienced team of adults to engage our young members (6-8 year olds) in a variety of activities both indoor and out. Beavers meet on a Tuesday evening from 6-7pm. Training and support provided, no previous experience necessary just a willingness to join in.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:645259c4017b3fcb4bab5b74;
                            :activityTitle "Assistant Beaver Leader".
id:64525b03d57002d0ed6500c5 :address "Marmora Road, Cambridge CB1 3PY";
                            :latitude "52.1956807"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.1500155"^^xsd:double.
id:64525de6fd6d9840d75c0c80 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """With guiding, girls have fun, adventure and the space to discover their potential.

They go to their first ever sleepover, canoe on rivers, learn about body confidence, and lead their own camp. Or sometimes they simply have fun and try new things with friends.

Girls take what they do in guiding with them as they grow up. Everything from working in a team, to taking the lead, to speaking out on issues they care about. It helps them develop the skills and confidence to become the young women they want to be. And to make a difference to the world around them.""";
                            :organisationName "Washington & Houghton Girlguiding";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.girlguiding.org.uk/get-involved/become-a-volunteer/register-to-volunteer/>.
id:645265f3787711d9da60fbf0 :activityDescription """We have several opportunities within our Division and we’re so glad you’re thinking of joining us. 

Thanks to our valued volunteers,  we’ll be able to help even more girls know they can do anything. And we hope that you’ll enjoy everything guiding has to offer too.  You don't need to have been involved in guiding before or have loads of time to make a big difference. Whatever your skills and interests, whether it’s volunteering with girls directly or supporting behind the scenes, there’s a role to suit you. 

The roles available: 
- Unit Helpers
- Unit Leaders 
- Support Roles 
- Administration 

At the heart of guiding are the unit meetings that girls go along to regularly. Volunteering at unit meetings means getting stuck in, meeting new people and running activities that help girls know they can do anything. You’ll volunteer directly with young people and can choose to work with girls of different age groups between 4 and 18 years in Rainbows, Brownies, Guides or Rangers. Unit meetings are usually once a week for around an hour. 

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64525de6fd6d9840d75c0c80;
                            :activityTitle "Washington & Houghton Girl Guiding Division Need You! ".
id:64526692a06f5da3c4eee36c :address "Washington, Tyne and Wear";
                            :latitude "54.89743199999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.517366"^^xsd:double.
id:64527196358835be4772631c :activityDescription """Volunteering in our shops is varied, exciting and rewarding. No two days are the same and you have the chance to flex different skills regularly. Below is a flavour of some of the tasks you may help with in our shops: 
Talking to our customers and making them feel welcome.
Rotating stock, sorting, steaming and tagging donations.
Serving at the till to process those all-important sales of clothing and accessories.
Housekeeping and tidying window displays to keep the shop looking it's best.

To find out more and sign up to volunteer in one of our shops, please visit our website at: https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/get-involved/volunteer/volunteer-in-our-shops""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6438281587df93ec1032b350;
                            :activityTitle "Shop volunteer- nationwide".
id:64527196358835be4772631d :address "Redman Place, London";
                            :latitude "51.5430805"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.0115352"^^xsd:double.
id:6452783f16798622c6e8c83e :activityDescription "Matched with a child in care (aged 8 - 16+) the role involves building a long term relationship that has trust and respect at its heart. Volunteers act as role models, meeting up regularly and spending time together. The service is independent of social services and the professionals involved in the lives of children once they come into care. Based in Hounslow (but as children in care can be placed outside their Local Authority Borough), we recruit volunteers in Bexley, East London, Kent and Essex. We pay travel expenses and there is a budget for volunteers and young people to use for activities when out and about having fun and enjoying themselves.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64147964bdd313f63d021734;
                            :activityTitle "Befriending a child in care - a Hounslow Ally".
id:6452783f16798622c6e8c83f :address "Hounslow";
                            :latitude "51.46092179999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.373149"^^xsd:double.
id:64527b338a4866dcdf01a926 :activityDescription """We are looking for Befriending Volunteers to support our Brent Mental Health service in the London Borough of Brent. Volunteers must be based within this area to take part in face-to-face befriending activities.

You will be based at home but will be required to travel across Brent to meet with service users and carry out your role. Ideally, you will be able to commit a minimum of 2 hour per week to volunteering. You will be supported by a Befriending Volunteer Coordinator who will provide support as and when needed.

Please visit our website to find out more and to apply - https://bit.ly/3nyBgDI""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64260f5fde05bf8ae7c99a1c;
                            :activityTitle "Befriending Volunteer".
id:64527b338a4866dcdf01a927 :address "Brent";
                            :latitude "51.5672808"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.2710568"^^xsd:double.
id:64527dcdc1b542dc0bb04dfe :activityDescription """Grandmentors is an inter-generational programme that recruits, trains & provides ongoing support for volunteers aged 45 plus, who draw on their wealth of personal & professional experience to help young care experienced people (16-25 years) in the Milton Keynes area, on their pathway to independence. Grandmentors come from diverse backgrounds & all walks of life. This enables them to understand & meet the range of needs of their mentees; forge trusting & positive relationships that supports, & empowers the mentees to unlock their skills & shape their future. Volunteers meet regularly with a young person to boost their confidence & work towards the young person's personal goals. Volunteers support where they can to help young care leavers find their feet and reach their full potential. Full training and ongoing support are provided and all expenses are covered. Volunteers need to commit to meeting with their young person on a regular basis for a minimum of 12 months, but timings and frequency of meetings are fully flexible and are up to each mentoring pair to agree on themselves depending on what works best for them.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64147964bdd313f63d021734;
                            :activityTitle "Grandmentors Milton Keynes".
id:64527dcdc1b542dc0bb04dff :address "Milton Keynes";
                            :latitude "52.0406224"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.7594171"^^xsd:double.
id:6453837dff94bbfa3c9c7cf9 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription "Marie Curie is the UK’s leading end of life charity. We provide frontline nursing and hospice care, a free support line and a wealth of information and support on all aspects of dying, death and bereavement.";
                            :organisationName "Marie Curie";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.mariecurie.org.uk/>.
id:645394f2942173c58288dc8f :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089d;
                            :organisationDescription """Building on this wonderful repository of artworks, the Art UK website is rich in story content and learning resources, and it offers many ways for everyone to engage with art.
 
Through our work, we make art accessible to all – for enjoyment, learning and research. Thanks to our generous supporters, it's all free.

Tagger is a crowdsourcing project inviting the public to tag artworks. The resulting tags help visitors to use Art UK.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/66103d70-6e85-4a19-b91f-b08bb505037f_2023-05-04T11:20:18.606Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Art UK";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://artuk.org/participate/tagger>.
id:645395b91dd47e97c7675780 :activityDescription """Our charity shops rely on generous donations made by the public to raise crucial funds for Marie Curie. From clothes, homeware and books, to CDs and DVDs, we sell a wide variety of products.

We are looking for volunteers to help us sort through all these donations, pick out the best items and prepare and sell them to our customers. Without the help of our dedicated volunteers we could not provide our customers with high quality items at affordable prices.  This allows us to raise funds so our nurses can continue to provide care to terminally ill people and support for their families.

Your role will include some of, but is not restricted to, the following tasks:
Sort through donations, being aware of the possibility of a hidden gem and better quality brands
Prepare items for sale by checking, hanging, steaming, sizing and pricing them
Work on the shop floor and provide excellent customer service to our shoppers
Operate the till 
Help out with basic housekeeping to keep the shop clean and tidy
Young Volunteers
Please note: A signed Parent/Guardian Consent Form is required for all volunteers aged 14-17 years.

For more information or if you have any questions regarding this volunteer role, please contact john.cardno@mariecurie.org.uk 07515134703""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6453837dff94bbfa3c9c7cf9;
                            :activityTitle "Marie Curie Retail Volunteer ".
id:645395b91dd47e97c7675781 :address "Marie Curie Charity Shop South Bridge, South Bridge, Edinburgh";
                            :latitude "55.94977129999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-3.18712"^^xsd:double.
id:64539799fcedb918d65ee248 :activityDescription "Help us make art from the UK's museums and galleries more searchable online! Tagger is a crowdsourcing project inviting the public to tag artworks. Anyone can tag artworks with descriptive words to make it easier to find them. Tagging is easy, fun and safe – your tags will only go live once they are verified by other people. Have a go and contribute to making Art UK more searchable by tagging people, places and things – and discover new art and artists along the way: https://artuk.org/participate/tagger";
                            :activityOrganisation id:645394f2942173c58288dc8f;
                            :activityTitle "Micro-volunteering with Art UK Tagger: Help make art more accessible online".
id:6453a4a5fde7c5f4f27a072c :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """Treetops Hospice provides nursing care and emotional support for anyone affected by a life-limiting illness or bereavement in Derby, Derbyshire and Nottinghamshire.
Treetops supports people with illnesses such as cancer, motor neurone disease and multiple sclerosis. It also supports their carers and families. All services are provided free of charge.

Treetops Hospice is a registered charity, which costs £4.3 million each year to run. We have to raise 70% of this, £8,300 a day, through voluntary donations, our shops, fundraising events, lottery memberships and gifts in wills.""";
                            :organisationName "Treetops Hospice";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.treetopshospice.org.uk/>.
id:6453be651e0dd96195871cdb :activityDescription """Do you have 3 hours a week and are looking to help out in one of our Clacton shops? 

St Helena Hospice has boutiques, vintage shops, book shops, music shops, furniture shops and everything in between!

We are looking for someone who is passionate about hospice care and possesses the following skills and attributes:

Customer service experience
Ability to handle customer complaints
Cash handling
Excellent communication skills
Previous experience of working or volunteering in a retail environment desirable
Computer literate
Attention to detail
Comfortable handling cash
Excellent communication skills
Personable and approachable
Reliable, trustworthy and flexible to meet the demands of the business
Team player with a friendly outlook
All required training, including till operation and gift aid will be provided. Online health and safety training is mandatory and repeated annually.

Job Type: Volunteer

Benefits:
Employee discount

Schedule:
Monday to Friday
Weekend availability

To apply, please visit our website: https://www.sthelena.org.uk/how-you-can-help-us/volunteer#jobListingForm""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6418308548beab57a5aa8cdb;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer retail assistant - Clacton".
id:6453be651e0dd96195871cdc :address "Clacton-on-Sea";
                            :latitude "51.789534"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "1.153035"^^xsd:double.
id:6453c5401e0dd961958724eb :activityDescription "Our charity shops exist to raise funds for us and increase awareness of our services among the local community.   We are looking for volunteers to support our charity shops, we have general shops and furniture stores and a £1 shop.  Volunteers help with a variety of tasks from sorting donations, to stock rotation, customer service and serving at the till.  No experience is necessary as training will be provided.  To find out more visit our website to find your nearest shop then pop in and speak to the shop manager.  Application forms are available from the shop.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6453a4a5fde7c5f4f27a072c;
                            :activityTitle "Charity Shop Volunteer (Ilkeston)".
id:6453c5401e0dd961958724ec :address "32 South Street, Ilkeston DE7 5QJ";
                            :latitude "52.9691875"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.3092788"^^xsd:double.
id:6453d0ccff5548e6484ee56c :activityDescription """We are always looking for friendly and active volunteers to join our busy charity shop teams. You may be serving customers and operating the till or be out the back sorting, steaming and preparing goods for sale.

You could learn new skills, have fun and make new friends. Our charity shops are in the heart of local communities raising vital funds to provide cancer care support services to people living with cancer.

We will provide you with training and support and you can volunteer for as little as two hours a week, or more if you have time.

Become a Shop Assistant""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641c7ebfdebe8c3c30566775;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Retail Assistant".
id:645413ec24210def92706c49 :activityDescription "Oxfam shops are local communities - but they are part of a global community. A global community of people united by a belief in a kinder, radically better world.  If you believe a fairer world is possible, join us today to overcome poverty - by fighting the injustices and inequalities that fuel it.  Just five minutes is enough to find your local shop and apply to volunteer:  https://volunteering.oxfam.org.uk/  By creating window displays, sorting and pricing donations, helping customers, or creating social media content, you can find a role that suits your skills and interests. No experience is necessary as full training will be given, all we ask is you're happy to work as part of a diverse and inclusive team. At Oxfam we know that everybody can make a real difference.  You will get to meet new people from your local community, and become part of a friendly and thriving team, helping make a positive change around the world.  To sign up, follow this link:  https://volunteering.oxfam.org.uk/ ";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64103c352a0eedb6aef42d3d;
                            :activityTitle "Oxfam Shop Volunteering".
