id:6454b590e405a94f571679a9 :activityDescription """As the nation comes together to mark the King's Coronation by giving back through #TheBigHelpOut campaign, why not uplift the next generation by volunteering with JLGB? 

Be a hero! Jewish children and young people are counting on you! 

Young people have been through a lot over the last few years. For many, JLGB has been a lifeline and local activity groups are at the heart of the JLGB experience. 

Now, more than ever, we need support to keep running our existing local groups and to expand into new communities. We need people like you. To be yourself. Your best self. To help uplift the next generation of Jewish children and young people. 

Our current local group meets on Tuesday evenings 6-9pm in Leeds and requires Group Leaders and Adult Volunteers. We are also looking to open other groups across the north of England 

We are looking for fun, enthusiastic people to join our team to support our members aged 7-18 
 
No experience needed, training will be given. A DBS and references will be required. For more information please visit www.jlgb.org/heroes """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:642c41ddbdf96ad8d020e142;
                            :activityTitle "Group Leaders/Volunteers needed - Leeds".
id:6454dd378b685b86a97a02e3 :address "Leeds";
                            :latitude "53.8007554"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.5490774"^^xsd:double.
id:6455018ad1ed7f1083d77a6d :activityDescription """Help set the record straight about diabetes by becoming an events volunteer. We are looking for Volunteers to attend local events within the district of Thanet (Kent). Ideally you'll have an excellent local knowledge and be able to suggest local events to our regional team and proactively seek out opportunities, so if you have some time to spare, this could be the role for you.

As an events volunteer, you will be working with Diabetes UK staff, talking to members of the public and handing out information about diabetes.

The events range from stands in shopping centres and high streets, to big events such as county shows. You don't need any previous knowledge or experience about diabetes or Diabetes UK. We give you all the information and support that you need""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641879d4cf71f77116117e87;
                            :activityTitle "Diabetes UK Events Volunteers - Kent".
id:64550590ec215eafb6924be4 :address "Kent";
                            :latitude "51.2787075"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.5217254000000001"^^xsd:double.
id:64550edd30a49781f3f51ebf :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "The Children’s Society fights for the hope and happiness of young people when it is threatened by abuse, exploitation and neglect. We take inspiration from the courage and hope we see in young people every day. It fuels our belief that a  good childhood is something every young person deserves. Driven by hope and working alongside young people and supporters,  we will not rest until together, step-by-step, we’ve created a society built for all children.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/fd3d2a77-42fc-4ce3-9923-5389136d04d0_2023-05-05T14:12:45.236Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "The Children's Society";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.childrenssociety.org.uk/>.
id:6455265cd7ed30d953c7e75f :address "Haig House, Borough High Street, London";
                            :latitude "51.5022433"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.0921761"^^xsd:double.
id:6455317b48b1d9f990fee872 :activityDescription """Do you want to support women are girls who are survivors of sexual abuse and sexual violence? 

We have volunteer positions available if you are:
- Women 18 years+
- Empathetic, non-judgemental & good listeners
- Self-aware & emotionally resilient
- Interested in discussing and understanding rape & sexual violence, and its impacts on women and girls
- Able to maintain confidentiality & anonymity
- Able to work independently using initiative & be part of a team
- Able to commit to three shifts per month, either from our offices or remotely. See times here: https://cambridgerapecrisis.org.uk/helpline/ 
- Share CRCC’s survivor-focused ethos

Your responsibilities in the role would be:
- Provide emotional support to women and girls over the phone and email.
-  Regularly reflect on your practice with other volunteers
- Follow CRCC policies and procedures around data protection
- Attend reflective practice, volunteer meetings and ongoing training
- Maintain confidentiality and anonymity.

If you are interested in the role, email volunteering@cambridgerapecrisis.org.uk. If you prefer to discuss volunteering with us over a call, please let us know. 

More info on our helpline and email volunteering: https://cambridgerapecrisis.org.uk/emotional-support-volunteers/ """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6414c018ba2db48cb2ad2068;
                            :activityTitle "Helpline and email volunteering - provide emotional support to local women and girls ".
id:645531b048b1d9f990fee901 :address "Cambridge";
                            :latitude "52.1950788"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.1312729"^^xsd:double.
id:645536338392bf6632d1fdf6 :activityDescription """Become a guest speaker and provide students with an insight into the world of work, your own career journey and what employers look for, based on your own experience.  

We like to show students that careers develop at different stages; there are knockbacks and changes; how to build resilience and confidence, so encourage our volunteers to share their experiences and learnings.

We set these sessions up and co-ordinate with you and the school. They are often in person and sometimes virtual.

Sessions often run for 1 hour max and take around half an hour of prep time.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:644bc4a4c54eb451c678b300;
                            :activityTitle "Industry Insight Volunteer Speaker (in schools)".
id:6455375693e82bbfc35852e1 :activityDescription """Deliver our ready-made 1-hour workshops to young people, and make a difference to their career journeys. 

Topics include: presentation skills, interview skills, teamwork, problem-solving and networking.

We provide the content and a session plan for you to follow. 

We set these sessions up and co-ordinate with you and the school.  They are often in person and sometimes virtual.

Sessions often run for 1 hour max and take around an hour of prep time.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:644bc4a4c54eb451c678b300;
                            :activityTitle "Employability skills workshop facilitator (in schools)".
