id:6456a81c458f4c3fb6347252 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """We'd love you to join in with our Scouting activities. You just need to be over 4 years old. Under 18s can join a youth section and those over 14 can help to organise the Group by joining one or more sections with the youth or by becoming a trustee.

Search the Scouts.org website for more information about the different sections and activities.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/db40bd93-274f-437c-9588-1c9c0730907f_2023-05-06T19:18:51.607Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Sissinghurst Scout Group";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.sissinghurstscouts.org.uk/>.
id:6456ac9687e0e3e3739b01e5 :activityDescription """We'd love you to volunteer with us, helping our young people to learn SKILLS of LIFE. We do a variety of activities. We're sure you'll enjoy helping to organise and joining in.
We also need trustees to help with the 'back-room' work, fundraising, recruiting, PR, etc.
You'll get free training for your role and any extra expenses paid.
Volunteering with us is 'GOOD for YOU\" and a great addition to your CV!
Get in touch""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6456a81c458f4c3fb6347252;
                            :activityTitle "Sissinghurst Scout Group".
id:6456ac9687e0e3e3739b01e6 :address "Sissinghurst, Cranbrook, Kent";
                            :latitude "51.10907359999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.5601507"^^xsd:double.
id:6456ccfb4267ad541a337574 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089d;
                            :organisationDescription """Acton Ealing Whistlers Football Club is a Community Club run entirely by volunteers, and without their support and commitment, the Club could not operate. We are keen to involve more like-minded people in the running of our Club and would like to welcome volunteers from various backgrounds with diverse skills and experiences.

There are many different roles required to run a football club, from physical roles such as Coaches, to behind the scenes roles such as Club Secretary and Treasurer. Currently, our volunteers:

- coach and manage our teams (U7 to U18, Soccer School, Whistlers SSE Wildcats);
- help prepare our pitches for training and matches, setting up goals and marking lines;
- organise fixtures and manage our business administration;
- help maintain our ground and the clubhouse;
- support our welfare and safeguarding responsibilities;
- run our kitchen for our community;
- help fundraise and organise events; and
form our Committee.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/426f542a-612f-4d70-9677-edf486deec19_2023-05-06T21:56:10.748Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Acton Ealing Whistlers FC";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.aewfc.co.uk/>.
id:6456d019929561aadc79fcc2 :activityDescription "help prepare our pitches for training and matches, setting up goals and marking lines;";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6456ccfb4267ad541a337574;
                            :activityTitle "Groundskeeping assistant ".
id:6456d03c4267ad541a33792b :address "Hillcrest Road, London W5 1HW";
                            :latitude "51.5242745"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.2956778"^^xsd:double.
id:645755c90b75bd1b62ff7a27 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "The 5th Bristol St Lukes Scout Group is one of the oldest groups in Bristol. It all began somewhere around 1907–08. We cant be sure of the exact date - it is believed that the group originated from the drum and bugle band which was formed to raise money for the building of St Annes Church which was completed around 1906. Over the years the 5th Bristol Scouts have been a big part of the local community providing the opportunity for thousands of Young People to experience scouting. ";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/51f889ab-9bb9-42f1-9c89-62cc41ae2f73_2023-05-07T07:39:52.895Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "5th Bristol Scout Group";
                            :organisationWebsite <http://www.5thbristol.co.uk/>.
id:6457588c31f4659b25fd035c :activityDescription """Volunteering can be a brilliant way to boost your mental wellbeing. It’s a great feeling knowing you’re helping young people get skills for life, and you might even learn a lot about yourself along the way, we are on the look out for new leaders to help run our 3 sections (Beavers, Cubs & Scouts).

Scouts can make you feel good in other ways too. We’ll guide you to an opportunity where you’ll: 

Make friends and meet people 
Try new things and challenge yourself 
Get outdoors and get stuck in 
Positively impact your community 
Create vital opportunities for young people 
Make memories that'll last a lifetime 

If you can only occasionally help, that’s OK. Whether you’d like to be an activity planner, tea-maker or craft creator, we appreciate any time you can spare.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:645755c90b75bd1b62ff7a27;
                            :activityTitle "5th Bristol Scout Group".
id:6457588c31f4659b25fd035d :address "Brookside Road, Brislington, Bristol";
                            :latitude "51.435618"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.5477455"^^xsd:double.
id:64575b85c50a3029db838f33 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """Through fun, friendship, challenge and adventure we empower girls to find their voice, inspiring them to discover the best in themselves and to make a positive difference in their community.  

More than 300,000 girls meet as Rainbows, Brownies, Guides and Rangers. We fire their imaginations through challenges and adventures for all personalities and abilities, from 4 to 18 years old.

Guiding is so much more than an after school club. Here's why we're special.  

We give girls a space just for them

Girls face pressures and expectations in every area of their lives. They’re limited by gender stereotypes and face barriers to accessing things they need to feel happy. They tell us they don’t feel safe in their daily lives.  

In our relaxed and encouraging all-girl spaces, every girl can be herself and feel at home. No pressure, no judgement – just fun and learning with other girls, guided by our inspiring volunteers.

We won't tell them an activity is 'for boys'. Our girls get to score tries at rugby, go bouldering or simply play the games that they enjoy most.

We give girls somewhere they can talk openly about what affects them and get support from other girls.

Girls speak, then we listen and act 

We’ve been by girls’ sides for over 100 years. Today, we’re squarely focused on what drives, challenges and excites girls here and now. We listen to what girls tell us, and this guides what we offer and what we fight for. 

All girls in Girlguiding get the chance to choose what they do - from Rainbows picking activities, to Rangers sitting on our council. 

Girls don't stand still, so neither do we 

Throughout our history, Girlguiding has evolved as the needs of girls have changed. 

We run music events just for our members like our girl-only festival Wellies and Wristbands. 

And at their regular meetings, girls take part in loads of activities related to things that matter to them. 

Whoever you are, wherever you're from – all girls are welcome. At Girlguiding, we give all girls an equal sense of belonging. """;
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/01576e8e-cb2a-429e-974b-f7a32ed6805a_2023-05-07T08:04:20.183Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "1st Ainsdale Green Rainbows";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.girlguiding.org.uk/>.
id:64576140931151d7b8a98d03 :activityDescription """Come and join a small group of Rainbows who need regular volunteers to help run the group in Ainsdale. We offer Rainbows aged between 4 - 7 years old the opportunity to have fun, learn new skills,meet new people in a safe place.

We enjoy doing different activities from painting, singing, dancing, getting messy through adventures both indoors and outdoors, exploring, trips out, sleepovers, sports. Opportunities for everyone.

We always like to try new things as well as support our community.

We meet every Monday evening 6:00 - 7:15pm""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64575b85c50a3029db838f33;
                            :activityTitle "1st Ainsdale Green Rainbows".
id:64576140931151d7b8a98d04 :address "Ainsdale Village Church URC Cornerstones, Station Road, Ainsdale, Southport";
                            :latitude "53.602479"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-3.0406158"^^xsd:double.
id:64578e3fe090332d33ff0a0a :activityDescription "Unfold are currently looking for volunteers who can mentor on either our Mentoring for Mothers programme (female mentors only) or our Mentoring for Children and young people’s programme (female and male mentors) both of which have an adaptive programme to support asylum seekers.   On both programmes you will:  Over 12 to 24 weeks, support your mentee to help them achieve their goals and get them where they want to be through encouraging your mentee to consider future options and assist them in developing strategies to attain their goals.    Develop a trusting, supportive and non-judgemental relationship, empowering mentees to identify goals they wish to achieve.     Provide emotional, social and practical support to your mentee   Support your mentee to make social connections with their local community, services or groups.  ";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64183a63685ab4e440f10c5e;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteers Mentors Needed to provide 1-2-1 Mentoring for Children and Young People and Mothers ".
