id:6458595605e4c47d855f57a1 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba5089b;
                            :organisationDescription """We need volunteers in all areas. From wildlife care to administration and maintenance. From 3 hours a week to fu time we need your support to continue our vital work.  
Find our more here https://hawr.co.uk/2023/01/17/volunteering/
Harper Asprey Wildlife Rescue  is an emergency wildlife hospital, it is a registered wildlife charity that works 24/7, 365 days a year. We  rescue, rehabilitate and release our native wildlife. From tiny dormice to the majestic deer and everything in between.
We are a small charity,  we provide a unique and vital service to our local community as the local hospital to help wildlife. Each of the thousands of animals we help every year has a unique story and a person, who cared enough to stop what they were doing and bring the animal to the rescue centre.
""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/74192144-f35d-4df9-b467-f9061c5ce1e5_2023-05-08T02:15:53.236Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Harper Asprey Wildlife Rescue ";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.hawr.co.uk/>.
id:645867efd0b65c9da6b8dd69 :activityDescription """We are always in need of help at the rescue. The work is endless, from wildlife care to administration to events to fundraising to maintenance.  We are here seven days a week, and all those hours need covering. From three hours a week to full-time help, the choice is yours. Full training given 
You will meet great people, great wildlife, get lots of coffee and biscuits and know you are helping wildlife and our community.  What's not to love?

Please look at the link here https://hawr.co.uk/2023/01/17/volunteering/ for more details or email stacey@hawr.co.uk  """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6458595605e4c47d855f57a1;
                            :activityTitle "Wildlife Rescue Volunteer ".
id:645872c64bf4784bd68b8b2e :address "Pears Hill, Westwood Road, Windlesham";
                            :latitude "51.3730392"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.6471662"^^xsd:double.
id:645891a4b84b5c3dc0dd891e :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription """Exeter Community Alliance is a collective that is supporting Climate Action Hub Exeter to acquire and set up a physical hub in central Exeter using the Climate Emergency Centre model from which to help our members work on fixing the climate, social and ecological crises.

We aim to build a better Exeter and a better world.""";
                            :organisationName "Exeter Community Alliance ";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.exetercommunityalliance.net/>.
id:6458936058116f3bbd42fff0 :activityDescription """We need volunteers at the Climate Hub to meet and listen to members of the public as they talk about their concerns around climate change.

We are dividing the shifts into two shifts per day with a fortnightly rota. Shifts will be from 10am until 1pm and 1pm to 4pm. If you would like to volunteer for a shift please email us at info@climateactionhubexeter.net .""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:645891a4b84b5c3dc0dd891e;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer at the Climate Hub ".
id:6458a6d804ba9b4b7b153b92 :address "Climate Action Hub Exeter, Bedford Street, Exeter";
                            :latitude "50.72316679999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-3.5273026"^^xsd:double.
id:6458a987c32ae098a0c56362 :activityDescription """Join us on the first Saturday of every month for repairs, refreshments, community causes and kids' activities! Lindfield Repair Cafe is all about saving items from landfill and giving them a new lease of life. 

Our volunteer repairers range from clock mechanics to sewing volunteers to woodworkers, electricians and general repairers! As a repairer, you'll fix people's items and teach them new skills while they wait.

If you're not repair-minded, there are still ways to get involved! We welcome volunteers to greet visitors, run the check-in desk, serve refreshments, help out in the community lounge and play with the children on the kids' table.

Visit www.lindfieldrepaircafe.org or email lindfieldrepaircafe@gmail.com for more information.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6450f2b4c88d13ac05954eb2;
                            :activityTitle "Lindfield Repair Cafe".
id:6458c4b0352b341b7fdc87fb :activityDescription """Befriending volunteers visit a befriending client in their home for 1-2 hours a week.  A highly rewarding role . 
Befriending volunteers are needed to visit people in their own homes for a chat on a regular basis. We have vacancies across the Romney Marsh, Tenterden and surrounding rural areas and would be delighted to hear from you if you could spare an hour a week and can help.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6419a23525513b8f6dac8cf8;
                            :activityTitle "Befriending Volunteer".
id:6458c4b0352b341b7fdc87fc :address "Tenterden";
                            :latitude "51.069358"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.689122"^^xsd:double.
id:6458dae813923e3bb1244ab1 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089d;
                            :organisationDescription """Berkhamsted Raiders is a youth football club with over 1,300 players across boys, girls, inclusive, futsal, walking and senior teams. We are one of the biggest and best youth football clubs in the country and our 200+ volunteers are the lifeblood of our charity and experience across managers, coaches, referees, Trustees, HR, Marketing and Welfare roles
""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/03ce3d86-99e7-41da-9686-41d9c1685319_2023-05-08T11:20:07.863Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Berkhamsted Raiders CFC";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.berkhamstedraiders.com/>.
id:6458e297b9b37550691a7ba0 :activityDescription """We are an award-winning local youth football club in Berkhamsted and we are looking for volunteers with a HR or Education background to help with our Welfare and HR volunteer teams. 

As a Welfare or HR volunteer you will work with our Welfare and HR Trustees and wider Welfare team to support any ad-hoc actions or projects that arise across the club that include a welfare or safeguarding perspective including either dealing with DBS certifications, investigating complaints, responding to safeguarding or welfare questions, ensuring best practise. 

Estimated time commitment is 4-5 hours per month on an ad-hoc, as required, basis with the opportunity to support with more time as you are available.

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6458dae813923e3bb1244ab1;
                            :activityTitle "HR/Welfare Volunteer".
id:6458e297b9b37550691a7ba1 :address "Berkhamsted";
                            :latitude "51.75976600000001"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.5678569000000001"^^xsd:double.
id:6458f7d24cb071423b012c69 :address "High Street, Lindfield, Haywards Heath";
                            :latitude "51.0151571"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.0792262"^^xsd:double.
id:6458f81c783916447547b4d6 :activityDescription """Coffee & Computers are a North London based community group offering digital support services, helping to enable local residents to engage with the digital world and access key online services.

We are looking for volunteers who can help at our regular training and support sessions, teaching learners the basic digital skills, and helping to build confidence, of using smartphones, tablets and laptops. 

You don't need to be an IT expert, just have a basic understanding of day-to-day digital activities, be good at problem solving, and keen to help others learn new skills.  Most important is to have lots of patience to explain things clearly and slowly to our (mainly elderly) learners.

Volunteers would also have the opportunity to help with other essential tasks like organising and hosting sessions, communications to help promote our activities, developing support guides and tutorials, and updating the website and social media channels.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d46ba0624f3ab9fba3a3;
                            :activityTitle "Digital Training & Support Volunteers".
id:645a2db8160258e51a62fc3d :activityDescription "Maintaining the orchard and meadow for future generations. Scrub bashing, tree planting, pruning, apple picking, juice making";
                            :activityOrganisation id:644016e2f8e88d26cae1d607;
                            :activityTitle "Hands on management of the orchard and meadow".
id:645a301f9c5ea33125c3ca4f :address "Harston Community Orchard, The Limes, Harston, Cambridge";
                            :latitude "52.1386073"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.0865613"^^xsd:double.
id:645a57ea244a06d48d0629be :activityDescription """St Leonard’s Hospice provides care and support for local people with life limiting illnesses. Our retail department raises vital funds through the sale of second hand goods through our shops and is a valuable face of the hospice in local communities. Our Donation Centre in Acomb processes donations from the public to send to the shops.

When am I needed?
At present we can take in volunteers every day except Sundays! The Donation Centre is open Monday to Saturday, 9am-4pm.  Someone with an interest and knowledge of books and media would be more than welcome on Thursday and Saturday mornings.

Monday to Saturday (excluding Friday) we are looking for someone who has knowledge of clothing and can spot a designer label or two and knows their brands!

Friday and Saturday we are looking for a friendly and confident person to greet and accept donations from the public. This involves advising on what we can accept and promoting our Gift Aid scheme.

We are also looking for volunteers who have a specialist interest and knowledge of cameras, toys, collectables, and electrical equipment.

What will I be doing?
•	Working alongside staff and other volunteers in the warehouse in Acomb, York
•	Accepting donations from the public and promoting the Gift Aid scheme
•	Moving and processing donations to sell in our shops 

What skills and qualities will I need?
•	Ability to maintain confidentiality and discretion
•	Ability to deal with enquiries from the general public 
•	Good sense of humour
•	Ability to work under the instruction of the manager and work as part of a team of volunteers

How will I benefit from being a volunteer in the Donation Centre?
•	Be part of a friendly and inclusive team 
•	Have the feeling that you have made a difference to someone’s day
•	Be valued and respected 
•	Have full training and support

Support and Supervision
Retail volunteers report to the Donation Centre Manager/ Retail Coordinator who will provide you with full training and liaise closely with you over all aspects of your role.  The Retail Office staff will help with your induction. 

Volunteers will be expected to attend any meetings or training where appropriate.
For all volunteering enquiries please contact the Volunteer Services Office on 
01904 777765 or email volunteers@stleonardshospice.org.uk""";
