                            :longitude "-1.4796433"^^xsd:double.
id:645d0ada32c0fab219e12953 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """
Throughout our Trust, which includes community sites as well as hospitals in Warwick, Leamington and Stratford, volunteers play a vital role in enhancing our patients’ experience. From befriending, helping with activities, assisting with admin work, escorting patients to hospital appointments and more. Volunteers not only dedicate their time and energy but also share their valuable skills and knowledge with us and the people they volunteer with. Those who give, gain.

Volunteering makes a real difference to our patients and staff and can be a great way to make a difference to your local hospital or community and boost your confidence and skills. No two days are ever the same and you get to meet lots of people from staff to patients and their family members.

Here at South Warwickshire University NHS Foundation Trust we have over 600 volunteers who are making a real difference on a daily basis. They are actively involved in and around our hospital sites and within our community. They have become a valued part of our organisation and we really appreciate the impact our volunteers make to enhance the quality of patient care.

We are so grateful that you are thinking of sharing your wide variety of talents to enhance the work we do here at the Trust.
""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/5e454b02-5a60-4bfd-9a07-f18c29c3eff6_2023-05-11T15:37:19.781Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "South Warwickshire University NHS Foundation Trust";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.swft.nhs.uk/join-us/volunteer>.
id:645d219e90efeb4b2bb2ddc0 :activityDescription """This is a really exciting opportunity for volunteers to get involved across the hospital. You will be at the cut and thrust of the hospital demand involved in a variety of different services. 

Some of the tasks you will be doing include:

•	Visiting patients on a ward who is confused or lonely – serving refreshments and providing companionship
•	You could be a Ward Activity Volunteer, the aim is to improve the hospital experience by helping patients to engage in conversation and in a range of activities during their stay
•	You could be helping to discharge a patient, collecting medication, packing clothes, helping coordinate transport or sitting with patients whilst waiting to be discharged

This role is very diverse and you will always be very busy doing something that will be of support and impact to the wards, patients or visitors that you help on the day. 

If you are interested in the volunteering role; please contact via Email: Volunteering@swft.nhs.uk""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:645d0ada32c0fab219e12953;
                            :activityTitle "Response Volunteer at Warwick Hospital, Lakin Road, Warwick, CV34 5BW".
id:645d224490efeb4b2bb2ddf3 :activityDescription """In view of all the extensive work that is intended at Warwick Hospital, we need friendly volunteers to assist our patients visiting the hospital, helping them to find out where their appointment is and how to check in.

•	Greet visitors at the volunteers’ allocated areas, to find out if they need guidance around the Hospital
•	Direct visitors to the correct appointment Check in Desk or Kiosk
•	Call for wheelchairs and taxis when requested
•	Communicate clearly and effectively with both staff, patients and visitors
•	 Ability to stand/walk for 3-4 hours

If you are interested in the volunteering role; please contact via Email: Volunteering@swft.nhs.uk

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:645d0ada32c0fab219e12953;
                            :activityTitle "Wayfinding Volunteer at Warwick Hospital, Lakin Road, Warwick, CV34 5BW".
id:645d24fcad02dd852f5bc2bf :address "Warwick CV34 5BW";
