id:646c820d593cc2729ac2aab7 :activityDescription """WE ARE LOOKING FOR PEOPLE TO VOLUNTEER IN SECONDARY SCHOOL EVENTS ON A PANEL OF JUDGES!

Through this volunteering opportunity, you will: 
- Volunteer 2 hours of your time /per event.
- Be able to do a one off commitment or as much as you like. 
- Have flexibility to choose what event you want to attend. 
- Support the development of young people in becoming active citizens.
- Connecting with your local community.

First Give runs social action programmes in 200+ secondary schools across England and Wales. Our programme empowers students to work together and make a difference in their local community, building up to the School Final that you would be involved with! At the School Final, students from a whole year group present to win a £1,000 donation from First Give for their chosen charity, and the JUDGING PANEL deciding the winner.

AS A JUDGE, you would be responsible for holistically judging students on the incredible work they’ve done as part of the programme. This includes the quality and content of the students’ presentations on their chosen local charities as well as the creativity and impact of their classes’  social action. The judging is based on the knowledge, creativity and delivery of the presentations, and the commitment to charity, creativity and impact of the class social action. 50% of marks go to presentation elements, 50% of marks go to the class social action project element. You will receive further instruction and a briefing at the event.

You will joined by other judges on the panel that can include:
- school Headteachers
- school governors
- teachers
- local councilors

This opportunity is available during times when secondary schools are open and within our partner school regions in London, Essex, Wales, the Midlands, Yorkshire and the Humber.  Our busiest months of the academic year (when there will be the most volunteering opportunities) are December before the holidays, March, April, June and July.

Please visit out website or email us to learn more and express interest directly: 
https://firstgive.co.uk/judge/ 
info@firstgive.co.uk""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6448fb162604f81f95a28474;
                            :activityTitle "First Give Community Judge".
id:647864bcc3cb92f48fd7c60a :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "We work with separated young refugees and asylum seekers, also known as UASC (Unaccompanied Asylum Seeking Children). These are young people aged 16 to 24 who have arrived in Kent alone and are claiming asylum. We provide them with a safe, positive space and support them to succeed.";
