id:651ad679d74a5f9dbd3638d6 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "We are a charity who have been supporting young people since 2011🤩 We believe young people are the future, and support them to make a positive difference in their community. Sign up to our programmes today! ";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/7d2a9a9e-562a-4e47-b08f-47d2e0c1a22a_2023-10-02T14:40:55.502Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Youth Leads UK";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://youthleads.uk/>.
id:651ad6dd3ddd308cda823dd8 :address "Greater London";
                            :latitude "51.4309209"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.0936496"^^xsd:double.
id:651ada1b330408d6da074b4c :activityDescription """Youth Leads UK has a vision of a country where youth leads – where young people feel listened to, part of their communities, and ready to make change through skills development opportunities.

As a youth charity, it is important that we are youth-led. And that is why we have developed the Youth Advisory Board!

This will be your chance to have a say; you will participate in discussion-based activities, designed with and supported by our Youth Engagement Team, to work together to move the charity forward.

Your feedback, experiences, and ideas are most important. We believe the voices of young people are what will move us forward, and this initiative will make this possible!

Follow the link to apply: https://youthleads.uk/yab/""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:651ad679d74a5f9dbd3638d6;
                            :activityTitle "Join the Youth Advisory Board!".
id:651ae8d7cbfc7db24827820a :address "Youth Leads UK, Salford";
                            :latitude "53.4731027"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.2994406"^^xsd:double.
id:6538dd860eb6adbb4ad32e5e :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """We give thousands of blind and partially sighted people the opportunity to borrow our Touch to See books from a free postal library.

Our books are enjoyed at home with family and friends, in schools, or for adults as members of one of our community Touch to See Book Clubs around the country.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/604c34c3-336b-44b9-90c5-190456f26e79_2024-04-03T11:55:36.912Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Living Paintings";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://livingpaintings.org/>.
id:65a47a18434568000b8edfd6 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """The Lunch Club tackles food insecurity and social isolation by providing freshly cooked lunches in a friendly, safe and welcoming environment for vulnerable people in our local community who are struggling to feed themselves or their loved ones. We offer a hot meal service, offering a nutritious and balanced menu. There is a warm space for people to sit down to eat but we also offer a takeaway service. The charity will rely on the local Streatham retail community such as supermarkets, stores, restaurants, cafes, bars and pubs for donations of food. We will then cook with the food waste that these businesses create but which will be the lifeblood of our charity. The lunch club will also provide an environment where beneficiaries can socialise and form new friendships, helping to alleviate loneliness and social isolation. 
Once we have established our core service, and have got to know our beneficiaries and any concerns or issues they may be facing, we would act as a gateway to other charities, organisations and the local authority to support these individuals. We are already building partnerships for us to be able to achieve the.
The Lunch Club will take place at a central Streatham venue, initially once a week on Fridays and will look to increase this by one day a week every three months, with the aim of having a Monday-to-Friday service at the start of our second year. 
By providing this service we hope to care for people’s physical and mental well-being. It is a holistic initiative that combines meals, social engagement, and collaborative efforts to support the lives of those most in need.
""";
                            :organisationName "The Lunch Club";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.thelunchclub.org.uk/>.
id:65a485e6384f5de9483cd25a :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """LGM FoodBank, located at Leeds Grand Mosque, is a halal foodbank dedicated to supporting individuals facing food insecurity.

Initially established in March 2020 to aid those affected by Covid-19, it has evolved into a permanent facility since October 2020. Serving all communities in Leeds, irrespective of faith or background, we provide halal food and strive to include staple items cherished by diverse cultures.""";
                            :organisationName "Leeds Grand Mosque Food Bank";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.leedsgrandmosque.com/>.
id:65a51d5a07f25bbd4af1468e :activityDescription "We are currently seeking dedicated volunteers to assist us in collecting food surplus, sorting and packaging it, and distributing it to individuals and families in need.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65a485e6384f5de9483cd25a;
                            :activityTitle "FOOD BANK Surplus FOOD Collection, Sorting, Packaging, and distributing VOLUNTEERS REQUIRED".
id:65a51d5a07f25bbd4af1468f :address "Grand Mosque, 9 Woodsley Rd, Woodhouse, Leeds LS6 1SN, UK";
                            :latitude "53.8065185"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.5680998"^^xsd:double.
id:65b0de4c4da37652874985cd :activityDescription """There are lots of different admin roles to support the work that is done in Young Barnet Foundation, including supporting Governance and Committees, Human Resources, Bookkeeping, and general administration.  Volunteer Admin roles will depend on the type of experience you have or are looking to gain.

This role is for a volunteer who enjoys being part of a smaller team, basic IT skills are essential, this can be good for work experience or looking to gain hands on experience in a new area. The role can be office based or a work from home role.

The commitment for this role is flexible, although a minimum of 4 hours per week is suggested.

Training will depend on the level of experience you already have of administration tasks.

Valuing inclusion:
Our volunteers come from a range of backgrounds and we particularly welcome applications from disabled people, people with physical or mental health conditions, LGBT+ and non-binary people, and people from Ethnic Minority communities.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ea6cc794380477b6fb03;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Admin Assistant".
id:65b0df6de7ffce25e6a6b81f :address "85 Brookhill Road, London, Barnet";
