id:65d467b3ad4075b5012b4f8a :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """Healthwatch Swindon is the towns independent champion for people who use health and social care services. We’re here to make sure that those running services, put people at the heart of care. 
As an independent statutory body, we have the power to make sure that NHS leaders and other decision makers listen to your feedback and use it to improve standards of care.
We are here to listen and understand the needs, experiences and concerns of people who use health and social care services and to speak out on their behalf.
We focus on ensuring that people’s worries and concerns about current services are addressed. We are totally independent and can provide you with impartial and independent signposting advice.
We are part of a network of 150 local Healthwatch across England and cover the whole of Swindon.
""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/88182a18-ddac-4e8d-9671-2e5b050ffbc8_2024-02-20T08:49:51.850Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Healthwatch Swindon";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.healthwatchswindon.org.uk/>.
id:65d46acd8905da0e1cb4149e :activityDescription """You will work with staff to support the research function of Healthwatch Swindon as we gather people’s views and experiences of using different health and social care services.

Why should you be a Healthwatch Research volunteer?
If you like exploring and getting to the heart of issues that affect people, this is the right role for you. We have a vital role to play in ensuring people in Swindon are engaged, listened to and provided with an avenue to tell us their views and opinions about health and social care services. By people sharing their experiences with us we can bring these to health and care providers and decision makers in Swindon to influence services to make them better. We need your help to be the best that we can be.

What will the role involve?
• Working with Healthwatch volunteers and staff team to plan and deliver research activities with other volunteers and staff members
• Assisting in the production and implementation of surveys, focus groups and other research methods
• Recording and analysing data
• Assisting in the production of research reports
• Engaging people using online platforms e.g. Zoom, Teams
Personal specification/requirements
• Effective planning and analytical skills and ability to ask questions and listen well to engage with people
• Able to work as part of a team with other volunteers and staff
• Experience of using Microsoft Office, including Word
• Access to the internet/email
. Be comfortable volunteering from home and using online meeting platforms e.g. Zoom or Microsoft Teams (training can be provided in the latter)
• Respectful of confidentiality

How we will support you? 
As well as our volunteer handbook, you will have regular contact with a member of the Healthwatch team to provide you with support and guidance throughout. You’ll receive full training including induction to Healthwatch and be part of a team who’ll make sure your volunteering experience is positive.

How much time is involved?
Our volunteering roles are flexible and fit around your schedule. Ideally, our local Healthwatch Volunteers would be able to make a regular commitment to the role on a weekly or monthly basis, but this role can also be ad-hoc to suit your lifestyle.
We will always work closely with you to ensure your volunteering role fits with your other personal and social commitments.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65d467b3ad4075b5012b4f8a;
                            :activityTitle " Research Volunteer".
id:65d46acd8905da0e1cb4149f :address "Sanford House, Sanford Street, Swindon";
                            :latitude "51.5616607"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.7839131"^^xsd:double.
id:65d5fc7c1db001584ab38d70 :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """Age Concern Windsor is a local charity based at the Spencer Denney Centre in Windsor, focusing on supporting vulnerable individuals, particularly those with additional care needs such as mobility issues, dementia, or frailty. The Day Service operates from Wednesday to Friday, providing group and individual activities, along with a nutritious meal, offering respite to unpaid family/carers. Tuesday Entertainment sessions cater to more able clients for socializing, lunch, bingo and quiz afternoons, tabletop gardening, informational talks and discussions and entertainment, while the Monthly Sunday Lunch Club provides a three-course meal in a friendly environment.

The Befriending Service pairs clients with volunteers for regular chats, fostering confidence and facilitating social interactions. The Meals on Wheels Service operates four days a week, delivering over 100 hot, healthy meals to individuals who cannot go out, struggle with cooking, or are recovering from illness. The pandemic has exacerbated the fragility of clients, leading to health deterioration and decreased interest in life. The Befriending Service aims to re-engage clients with social activities and groups, while Meals on Wheels improves clients' diets and eases the burden on their caregivers.

The charity's services have increased social contact, alleviated feelings of isolation, and enhanced a sense of connectedness to the community. The testimonials highlight the positive impact of the friendly volunteers and the overall improvement in clients' well-being through these essential services.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/b6a92515-d31e-4fb8-87aa-4c2e83b5e3f3_2024-02-21T13:36:57.986Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Age Concern Windsor";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.ageconcernwindsor.org.uk/>.
id:65d604686123f8876966688d :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "FoodCycle has been nourishing communities with food and conversation for 15 years. Every week, thousands of volunteers across the country transform surplus food into healthy, nutritious meals for anyone that would like them, no questions asked. Each community meal offers a safe, warm space to enjoy a free cooked meal and company, which helps guests save on food and electricity bills and build social connections. ";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/cbefa010-c45b-44f6-9cc7-5dc0bfec9c02_2024-06-03T16:19:00.317Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "FoodCycle";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://foodcycle.org.uk/>.
id:65d76bc27e65d3565b067735 :activityDescription """What will I be doing?

We are looking for volunteers to help us with our lunch day service. There are various roles which cover the following areas:
- Food preparation
- Chef’s assistant
- Setting up for service
- Welcoming beneficiaries
- Serving food and hot drinks
- Talking with beneficiaries
- Cleaning and packing up

For some roles, such as food prep, talking with beneficiaries and cleaning, we would see everyone getting involved. The other roles are flexible and we are happy for people to choose where they feel they would be best suited.

We are also looking for other volunteers to help us with backroom roles, such as:
- Volunteer management
- Social media content
- Fundraising
- Food donation pick-ups
- Marketing

What impact will this have?

By volunteering with The Lunch Club you’ll be helping provide nutritious cooked lunches to vulnerable people who, for whatever reason, struggle to provide this for themselves or their families.

You will also be able to provide support, conversation and friendship to people who may be facing social isolation and loneliness.

By doing this we hope to care for people's physical and mental wellbeing by providing healthy food, social engagement and support to the lives of those most in need.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65a47a18434568000b8edfd6;
                            :activityTitle "Lunch Day Team Members".
id:65d76de87e65d3565b0677aa :activityDescription """What will I be doing?

The Lunch Club provides freshly cooked lunches to vulnerable people in our local community. The meals will be available to either eat in or takeaway.

Lunches will be prepared from surplus food sourced from the supermarkets and shops in Streatham along with surplus food supplied by food distribution groups. 

Cooks will need to be flexible and adaptable in their approach and cook with the ingredients to hand. There will be a small amount of funds each day to purchase any other vital ingredients. Think Ready, Steady, Cook!

Our aim is to provide the most nutritious meal that these people will eat that day, helping to support their physical wellbeing.

What impact will this have?

By volunteering with The Lunch Club you’ll be helping provide nutritious cooked lunches to vulnerable people who, for whatever reason, struggle to provide this for themselves or their families.

Our lunches will be the core service we provide, but once we have regular beneficiaries coming along, and we get to know them better, we will act as a gateway to other charities and organisations to help with any concerns or issues they may be facing. Our cooks will be key in attracting people to eat with us.

By doing this we will be caring for people's physical and mental wellbeing by providing healthy food, social engagement and support to the lives of those most in need.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65a47a18434568000b8edfd6;
                            :activityTitle "Lunch Day Cooks".
id:65d8ace24ea4343767a740fa :activityDescription """We have recently undergone a re-brand and have a new website. Our marketing team would value help with the development and ongoing maintenance of the website.

Key Activities
• support with digital needs
• uploading content from documents into WordPress
• editing webpages
• working alongside the marketing team to adapt our website, following all data protection guidelines

You'll need to have some basic knowledge of web content management but the friendly team will help you become familiar with hospice procedures.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d08fa0624f3ab9fb4dbf;
                            :activityTitle "Digital and web support ".
id:65d8ae7c4ea4343767a74173 :activityDescription """Our receptionists are the first point of contact for the hospice, providing a pleasant and welcoming atmosphere for patients, their relatives and staff. They answer the phone and greet visitors in a warm, compassionate and professional manner, directing all enquiries to the correct person or place. They also carry out a wide range of admin tasks that are essential to keeping the hospice running smoothly. You'll get full training on all of this.

The team share the shifts, each covering four hours between 9am and 5pm, Monday to Friday. You'll be asked to cover once a week - we especially need people on Fridays.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d08fa0624f3ab9fb4dbf;
                            :activityTitle "Receptionist".
id:65d8b435d4e1c22a720abcf4 :activityDescription """We've opened another charity shops in Wells and need volunteers to to join this new team. Help us raise vital income for Tapping House hospice.

Our shop is located on the high street opposite the post office. You'd be serving customers, keeping the shop floor tidy and operating the till. If you're creative you could be asked to set up an attractive window display!

It would be great if you could make a regular commitment for the hours you're happy to come in - this could be as little as one or two hours at a time if you can't manage a full four hour shift.

If you've worked in a shop before that's ideal but you'll get full training and support, including how to apply and follow our safety measures.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d08fa0624f3ab9fb4dbf;
                            :activityTitle "Shop assistant - Wells next the Sea".
id:65d8b59dd4e1c22a720abd1b :activityDescription """Join the team at Tapping House and help with the upkeep of the internal and external areas of the hospice and our retail shops. We’re looking for a volunteer to support our maintenance team for a few hours a week by:

- assisting with painting and decorating
- undertaking basic DIY and minor repairs
- carrying out routine maintenance, indoors and outdoors
- occasional driving of hospice vehicles 

If you have skills in DIY and repairing things, particularly painting, decorating or carpentry, we’d love to hear from you!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d08fa0624f3ab9fb4dbf;
                            :activityTitle "DIY".
id:65d8b7e8bebadfd23a93eb0d :activityDescription """We're recruiting volunteers to support patients and their families, mainly in patients' own homes - it's a new project for the hospice so you'd be helping to shape what we do.

As a Butterfly Volunteer you will be supporting those approaching the end of their life. You will be providing company, comfort, reassurance and emotional support to patients and their families. This is a non clinical role.

If you would like more information before deciding to apply please email volunteers@tappinghouse.org.uk""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d08fa0624f3ab9fb4dbf;
                            :activityTitle "Butterfly care volunteers".
id:65d8b8c97c1db8b343de8883 :activityDescription """Our care services cost huge amounts each year and this year alone we must raise £5 million. This is where our busy fundraising team comes in – and this volunteer role supports our fundraising team with admin duties.

What you’ll do

·        scan documents

·        use our database

·        other general admin duties

We’d like you to come in for two or three hours a week but you can choose a day to suit you.

If you’ve worked in an office before that’s ideal but you’ll be shown what to do by our friendly team.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d08fa0624f3ab9fb4dbf;
                            :activityTitle "Fundraising Admin".
id:65db3ecd717f2134331b297e :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription "Based within the Royal Borough of Kingston, New Era is an expanding grass roots, community led non-profit organisation. It runs projects that address social isolation, food poverty and the cost of living crisis; with a goal of a more sustainable future for everyone. With local volunteers we collect safe surplus food for redistribution, run free, thriving community cafes, maintain a community fridge & pantry aiding those in need but also to reduce landfill. We also cultivate two allotments for the wellbeing of volunteers who thrive in the outdoors and to redistribute fresh produce to our food projects.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/dc5651c6-1299-4d4d-a33a-ceeb50a33943_2024-02-25T13:21:16.555Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "New Era Community Projects CIC";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://newera-communityprojects.org/>.
id:65db4836ae90d230b76d38d5 :activityDescription """Square 1 Cafés are a free of charge, safe and inclusive space where anyone, including those facing loneliness, isolation, or hardship, can find solace and friendly companionship. It’s a welcoming environment where people can meet new people, engage in meaningful conversations, catch up with existing friends and savour a delicious light lunch - all without any financial burden.

This Square 1 Cafe will open to support Wheels For All who hire the track at Weir Archer stadium exclusively on Mondays to allow disabled people and people with learning disabilities who may otherwise be unable to cycle on our roads, enjoy the experience with fully adapted cycles and trikes.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65db3ecd717f2134331b297e;
                            :activityTitle "Cafe Manager - Square 1 Cafe - Kingston KT1".
id:65db4836ae90d230b76d38d6 :address "Weir Archer Athletics and Fitness Centre, Kingston Road, Kingston upon Thames";
                            :latitude "51.4052927"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.2836903"^^xsd:double.
id:65dc76893c6380b8db3500a6 :activityDescription """Brigstowe is looking for two Admin Volunteers to support our Office Manager for one day each, preferably on Mondays and Fridays.  

The role will include:  

*Admin for our peer support group – calling members of the group, recording attendance and client feedback  
*General office admin (including front-of-house reception duties) 
*Answering/making phone calls and transferring calls to colleagues  

You will be working in the office alongside our committed and supportive staff team. You will be supervised and supported by Brigstowe’s full-time Office Manager. Full induction will be provided as well as ongoing training opportunities. In return, we require a minimum commitment of six months. 
The role would suit someone with some admin experience who is comfortable with IT.  

Brigstowe is a Bristol-based HIV support charity. We support people living with HIV and other long-term health conditions in Bristol and the surrounding areas and have been doing so for over 30 years. 

Hours: One day or 2 half-days a week (preference for Mondays and Fridays) 

Closing date:  1st April 2024, 9am

Brigstowe is committed to reducing inequality, valuing diversity and enabling inclusion. We welcome applicants with the appropriate skills of any background or identity. 

If you would like to know more about the role, please call our office number 0117 955 5038 and ask to speak with Sofia.  

To apply for this role, please complete our Volunteer Application and Equal Opportunities Form and send them to info@brigstowe.org""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425e92cc794380477b6dc27;
                            :activityTitle "Admin Volunteer".
id:65dc76893c6380b8db3500a7 :address "40-42 Chelsea Road, Easton, Bristol";
                            :latitude "51.46349"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.5629679"^^xsd:double.
id:65de69ab18cafe210c7be087 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089d;
                            :organisationDescription """The Group the Musical is a disability theatre academy with registered charity status in Shrewsbury (UK). It was a production team with background in performing arts and working with people with disability. Our cast and ensemble are currently rehearsing a musical which raises awareness of autism and disability, and offer an inclusive theatre academy to adults and young people with disability and people from the community of Shropshire. 
""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/94b60680-f2bb-4832-853f-5b29b789eb13_2024-02-27T23:00:59.124Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "The Group the Musical";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.thegroupthemusical.org.uk/>.
id:65df0654f98d04f1ffca76d8 :activityDescription """ 

Our amazing team of volunteers help us run over 100 shops across England and Wales.

Every donated item that you sort, prepare and sell helps to raise vital funds to support us in our mission to make sure no one, no matter how complex their disabilities, is isolated, left out, or unable to fulfil their potential. Our shops are at the heart of local communities – sharing the work of Sense, and helping to secure support for our life changing work.

 

We’re looking for volunteers who are:

Reliable and friendly
Respectful of others and their diversity
Passionate about customer service
Interested in learning about and supporting the work of Sense
 

Volunteering in one of our Sense Shops will involve a variety of tasks that you can get involved with. These include:

Welcoming and assisting customers, providing great customer service and a fantastic shopping experience
Receiving donated goods from members of the public
Sorting, steaming, tagging and preparing donated goods for sale
Creating eye catching window and in-shop displays
Keeping the shop floor well stocked, tidy, clean and organised
Processing sales and serving on the till
Promoting Gift Aid and other Sense fundraising initiatives
Acting as an ambassador for Sense; promoting the shop and Sense in your local community
Supporting with the recruitment and training of new volunteers
Following new health, safety and social distancing measures to ensure the safety of everyone
 

We believe that volunteers enable us to bring people together and provide opportunities for people with complex disabilities to communicate and experience the world. This is why it is important to us that our volunteers feel supported and rewarded. Here is what we can offer you as a volunteer:

A full induction and ongoing support and guidance from your Shop Manager to make sure you feel confident in your role
Support to develop new skills, knowledge and experience, in particular of a retail environment, but also skills such as teamwork, customer service, communication and using your initiative
A reference for other paid or voluntary work (available on request)
The opportunity to share your existing skills and experience to benefit others
The chance to meet new people from a wide range of backgrounds and to join a passionate and committed team
The opportunity to make an invaluable contribution to Sense by raising vital income and raising the profile of Sense in your local community; changing the lives of those who have complex disabilities and are deafblind.

For everyone living with complex disabilities. For everyone who is deafblind. Sense is here to offer personalised support to help people communicate and experience the world. We believe that no one, no matter how complex their disabilities, should be isolated, left out, or unable to fulfil their potential. Our experts offer support that’s tailored to the individual needs of each person, whether that’s at our centres, through our holidays and short breaks, or in people’s own homes. In addition to practical support, we also provide information to families, and campaign for the rights of people with complex disabilities to take part in life.

 

 Apply online at https://volunteers.sensecareers.org.uk/234279DOIT""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cd68a0624f3ab9fb0c4b;
                            :activityTitle "Charity shop volunteer".
id:65df0654f98d04f1ffca76d9 :address "Walworth Road, London SE17 2TG";
