id:65e09d1a4a3343b239bca62f :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription """Since 1935, we’ve been doing everything we can to ensure everyone can enjoy nature on foot.

On 1 January 1935 the Ramblers Association was officially created. We're the only charity dedicated to removing barriers so everyone can enjoy walking in green spaces, and to improving Britain’s most popular and least-known walking places. We’re committed to campaigning to keep our countryside open to all and to fighting for the things that matter most to walkers. We lead the way, and the walks, for a vibrant community united by the joys of walking, helping everyone get more out of their walks.    """;
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/7187c113-5807-4857-a3bd-8ed7deaac819_2024-02-29T15:04:57.818Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "The Ramblers";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.ramblers.org.uk/>.
id:65e0a7b056644aa47a706dd2 :activityDescription """A welcoming, friendly person who is a great listener and happy to talk to anyone about anything. Will be required to make and serve refreshments and clear away at the end.

Places of Welcome is a national initiative aimed at providing a network of community venues where anyone can go to find a friendly face and for a cuppa and a chat. By becoming a Place of Welcome Host, you help us to provide a free social meeting place for those who may live alone or feel isolated, are new to the area or have little opportunity to meet other people in their neighbourhood. Over a period of time groups may develop in a variety of ways, depending on the skills and interests of those participating, and the volunteer hosts would be instrumental in passing these ideas to library staff for consideration.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65c4a6d2e0a49d3490116b28;
                            :activityTitle "Places of Welcome Host (Stapleford)- Inspire Culture, Learning and Libraries ".
id:65e0aa6305ccea527174fa36 :address "Stapleford Library and Learning Centre, 25 Church Street, Stapleford, Nottingham NG9 8GA";
