id:65e9eaec04993ab8e7c864c0 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription "Magpas Air Ambulance provides the very best pre-hospital emergency care, in the air or on land, including treatments usually only available in hospital. Operating 24/7, we answer on average four calls for help a day, treating around 900 patients in life-threatening emergencies every year.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/c7b6ea7d-f59d-4f48-84b0-b3f69ac0ae64_2024-03-07T16:27:23.971Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Magpas Air Ambulance";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://magpas.org.uk/>.
id:65eae1dffc81beee77e2559d :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """The Kids Network supports children at a crucial time in their lives, in the lead up to and often during the transition from primary into secondary school. We do this by providing them with a volunteer mentor, a local hero from their London community.

We exist because 50% mental health issues can be diagnosed before the age of 14. Way too early there is exam pressure, social media addiction, bullying, and gang grooming.

Children are stressed, depressed, anxious and angry and it affects the disadvantaged disproportionally.

The Kids Network focuses on the individual needs of the child, building confidence and resilience and developing the tools for a positive future. Mentors are trained to deliver child-led sessions, which help them overcome the challenges and complexities of their young lives.

Our programme has a proven impact with 93% of children reporting an increase in their wellbeing.""";
                            :organisationName "The Kids Network";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.thekidsnetwork.org.uk/>.
id:65f029d39bdbb8394895747e :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """Adullam Social Enterprises (ASE) is a not-for-profit Community Interest Company Limited by guarantee.

We use our profits to provide free services to the community, in order to build stronger communities, supporting sustainability to improve people’s lives. ASE achieve this through the activities we provide, specifically targeting the most vulnerable, people living in areas of deprivation, and people who are facing a multitude of barriers.

ASE works with the most vulnerable client groups in society, including both Adults and Young Persons. Issues range from homelessness, complex needs, mental health, substance dependence, people fleeing domestic violence, people facing financial difficulties as well as supporting people into employment.

 

Principle Activities:
The principal activity of Adullam Social Enterprises is to trade goods and services across a number of regions, in order to fund and deliver social value activities that create positive outcomes for residents and our environment.

Our Mission is to create Social Outcomes through our business enterprises, which are affordable, accessible, whilst ensuring that we put people and the environment at the heart of everything we do.

Our Vision is to facilitate, enable and support positive changes across communities, benefiting both People and Planet.

We Value Innovation, Passion, Creativity and Motivation.

 

Social Value Delivery Plan
ASE developed a Social Value Delivery Plan which sets out our commitment to achieving our objectives.

 

Objectives:
Social Value by Design – embed social value into the core processes of Adullam Social Enterprises.
Set Social Value Outcomes and Outputs as a minimum criteria for any initiatives we fund or set up.
Through Equality, Diversity, and Inclusion, create social value initiatives that positively impact on people and the environment within which we operate.
Ensure that the projects we fund, support, or set up, provide more creative ways of changing people’s lives.
Create sustainable enterprises around the “Build to give back” concept through co-production and community involvement and inclusion.
 

Key area of Social Value delivered over the past 12 months:
Raising awareness in Equality, Diversity and Inclusion
Providing financial donations to a Hardship Fund
Delivering free training and business support
Providing financial assistance supporting co-production activities
Providing financial assistance to tackle Food Poverty
Providing funding and supporting mental health and wellbeing projects
Supporting digital inclusion in the community""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/96508420-d9c7-412e-badc-18192d3be57c_2024-03-12T10:09:15.950Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Adullam Social Enterprises";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://adullamsocialenterprises.org/about-us/>.
id:65f02d2f3522495a3cf39598 :activityDescription """Enjoy meeting people?  the main line operation of Tornado means we need on-train volunteers and support crew. 
CARRIAGE HOSTS & SUPPORT TEAM
The Trust has a highly successful on-board team – Carriage Hosts are responsible for the safety of our passengers and provide information about who we are and what we do. The Support Team promote our merchandise and they also attend events with the Trust’s goodies.  The range of Tornado merchandise continually changes and includes books, badges, DVDs and mugs (which can be bought online via this website as well!).  The dedicated group who do this will always welcome new volunteers, particularly if some geographical spread can be added to the mix. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:65ba391228fa46c5f1725938;
                            :activityTitle "Steam Locomotive Train Steward ".
id:65f02d2f3522495a3cf39599 :address "Birmingham New Street, Station Street, Birmingham";
                            :latitude "52.477754"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.898958"^^xsd:double.
id:65f041d12daded1e01d2bd64 :activityDescription """Do you have a creative flare online and have a passion for marketing and conducting product/market research?

We are looking for someone either studying marketing/social sciences or something similar/already working in the industry or just has a passion and flare in this area.

The role will be working from home and you will be responsible for obtaining content to upload to our social media platforms and also conduction market research to tell us what we can do better.

Full training will be provided.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65f029d39bdbb8394895747e;
                            :activityTitle "Research/Marketing volunteer".
