id:66018f2bb795b51c01e3394d :activityDescription """Café volunteers are needed to work serving customers and/or in the kitchen. Our busy café is open weekdays 10am to 3pm, providing a range of hot meals, cakes and drinks for staff, service users and the public. DBS checks are required for all Blackthorn Trust’s volunteers and staff.

Volunteers work either front of house (assisting service users, taking customers’ orders, serving food and drinks, taking payments etc.) or in the kitchen (assisting service users, washing up, helping prepare food, taking food to customers as part of the café’s table service etc.). Those volunteers working front of house are required to work unsupervised if the Café Manager is working in the kitchen or is absent.

Time commitment: A minimum of 1 weekday per week (9.45am to 3.30pm).
We most urgently need volunteers on Tuesdays and Fridays but would love to hear from people who match the skills description and are available any weekday.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64523fbd0076ca958b7f179e;
                            :activityTitle "Blackthorn Café Volunteer".
id:66018f2bb795b51c01e3394e :address "Blackthorn Trust (charity), Saint Andrew's Road, Maidstone";
                            :latitude "51.268494"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.4866879"^^xsd:double.
id:66019e005c34bc86641dcf9c :activityDescription """Arts for Health MK are looking to expand their pool of volunteers to help look after some of the green spaces at Milton Keynes University Hospital.

Volunteering sessions are great way to meet other like-minded people, who enjoy the wellness benefits of the great outdoors. We just know you will go away with a sense of accomplishment that you have helped keep the Creative Courtyards looking their best for patients, staff and visitors. Read the full details of this opportunity on our website here:  
https://artsforhealthmk.org.uk/Blog-Call-for-Volunteers""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64261398de05bf8ae7ca1490;
                            :activityTitle "Creative Courtyard Volunteers".
id:66019fb7f3478cdf6a17182e :activityDescription "An opportunity to gain experience in the day-to-day role of a exhibitions and collections team at a hospital. This opportunity can be tailored to interests, duties can include experience helping to curate and install a temporary exhibition or helping to document an care for the permanent collections. Support with events as and when projects arise.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64261398de05bf8ae7ca1490;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Exhibitions & Collections Assistant".
id:660291aa30e5e4070a84728e :activityDescription """Garden volunteers are needed to work helping with gardening or plant nursery workshops for people attending our Mental Health and Long-Term Health Conditions programme. DBS checks are required for all Blackthorn Trust’s volunteers and staff.

Volunteers work either in our garden (including fruit and vegetable plots and a small orchard) or plant nursery (we have two large greenhouses - workshops take place outside in hot weather). Garden and Plant Nursery volunteers are required to work unsupervised when the Garden Workshop leader is in meetings or is absent; this will sometimes involve running a workshop for service users with tasks set by the Garden Workshop Leader.

Time commitment: A minimum of 1 weekday per week (9am to 4pm). We need volunteers on Mondays (for the plant nursery workshop) and Tuesdays (for the outdoor garden workshop).
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64523fbd0076ca958b7f179e;
                            :activityTitle "Blackthorn Garden Volunteer".
id:660291aa30e5e4070a84728f :address "Blackthorn Trust (charity), Saint Andrew's Road, Maidstone";
