id:6606d2423e6ece5acc53861a :activityDescription "The Education team offers the opportunity for young people to take their classroom based learning and come to understand its importance in a real world setting. Our curriculum linked Earth School workshops have been developed with teachers in mind, with a focus on STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics), the Arts and Human History for Key Stages 1-4. Every workshop is designed to make full use of our woodland, meadows, farmland, rivers and wetlands, and heritage sites. They are run by an Earth Trust staff member, working with the teachers / support workers. Our Education Support volunteers assist the education team to deliver Earth School sessions to a mainstream primary audience. This is a rewarding role where you can match your love of people with your love of the outdoors.  Our Earth School education volunteers assist the Earth Trust staff member and engage with teachers and children. Activities include:  Supporting staff throughout the day, ensure school staff and children feel looked after  Setting up before sessions and packing away after  Assist staff to run hands on activities in the afternoon ";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ed04c794380477b73fa1;
                            :activityTitle "Earth School Education Volunteer".
