id:660bd8efd1ae799860e74f0c :activityDescription """Why our Change Makers are important to us:
They represent and promote the work of Healthwatch on a local level. They gather insight from the public on issues and concerns around Health and Social Care on a local level that help to make change possible and crucially they provide information and signposting to other local services offering support.

In your role as a Change Maker you will:
- Speak to members of the public to understand their concerns regarding our health and social care provision in Kent.
- Provide information to the public on local services that offer support.
- Have the opportunity to attend events and promote the role of Healthwatch across Kent and Medway.
- Gather insight on local health and social care issues to improve the output of Healthwatch reporting and influence.

The commitment required of a Change Maker:
- Our Change Maker opportunity is a flexible and great way to get involved in Healthwatch and making a positive change towards an improved health and social care service within Kent.
- Typically a Change Maker will commit to giving 2 - 3 days on a monthly basis.
- Additional hours may be available depending on our project engagement plan for a particular month or time period.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:660bcf34ad53bc3f4a8f1cf8;
                            :activityTitle "HEALTHWATCH KENT CHANGE MAKER".
id:660bdb13d1ae799860e75010 :address "Dartford";
                            :latitude "51.44621"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.216872"^^xsd:double.
