id:660e7e8911657c6e1a86debf :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """All Saints Youth Project provides recreational and informal educational opportunities and support for young people aged 10 to 19 years old (up to 25 for those with disabilities) to enhance their lives and grow their social/personal development. Whilst much of our work is aimed at the young people themselves, we look to promote family well-being and help parents/carers in dealing with issues that their young person is facing. These issues facing the family – they may be about the parent’s drug or alcohol abuse, poverty, domestic violence or just improving the communication between the young person and parents/carers.
The Project has contact with over 500 individual young people and over 250 families each year. A team of staff and volunteers deliver support/services: Four open access youth club sessions and three sessions for young adults with learning disabilities every week, a young volunteers in the community scheme, counselling and one-to-one support, special projects and workshops, holiday schemes, residentials, family support though individual family interventions, support groups (eg ADHD) and courses (eg Teen Triple P). We are an inclusive project with over 50% of young people with disabilities. In addition, we have a very high proportion of young people who are vulnerable through family circumstance (eg on the edge of crime, domestic abuse) and many of these are referred to us by other youth agencies, doctors, social work contact and even police.

READ MORE ABOUT ALL SAINTS YOUTH PROJECT HERE : https://www.allsaintsyouthproject.org.uk/
""";
                            :organisationName "All Saints Youth Project";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.allsaintsyouthproject.org.uk/>.
id:660e84aa518fa112d75efa43 :activityDescription """This is a varied and interesting hands on role, completing a wide range of assembly tasks in the production of the special books for children who are blind.

Main duties include:

• working in the production room and making plastic raised tactile images using a simple machine

• cutting and punching plastic and paper pages and assembling into books

• laminating and comb binding

• completing any necessary repairs on these publications when required

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6538dd860eb6adbb4ad32e5e;
                            :activityTitle "Book Assembler".
id:660e84d063851fe9470f93fe :activityDescription """-	Organising fundraising events and (e.g. comedy night fundraisers , raffles with prizes from local businesses) – possibly including support from any suitable well-known ‘patron(s)’
-	Generating support from with local businesses via a longer-term (annual) sponsorship or support arrangement 
-	‘Marketing’ the project to larger businesses or corporation in the city who may be willing to financially support ASYP on a longer term basis as part of ‘Corporate Social Responsibility’ activities
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:660e7e8911657c6e1a86debf;
                            :activityTitle "All Saints Youth Project - Fundraising team".
