id:660fbbe03d0504cd0bafcfd0 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription """Our vision is to develop renewable energy projects and deliver energy education to empower our community.

Croydon Community Energy was born from the idea that clean, renewable energy should be accessible for all. We have the below goals:

- Developing renewable energy and renewable heating projects in Croydon
- Reducing the carbon footprint of the local area
- Involving people from the community in our projects
- Creating community ownership of renewable assets
- Supporting the local community’s progression to a low carbon economy
- Promoting and offering retrofit & energy efficiency advice to the local community
- Offering climate action education to the local community""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/2fb4e590-ebd7-42e8-b318-131939be69ca_2024-04-05T08:52:47.223Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Croydon Community Energy";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.croydoncommunityenergy.co.uk/>.
id:660fc3bf99da6807b04a3743 :activityDescription "Croydon Community Energy are developing new workshop sessions called Sharing Spaces, which helps community groups share information, skills and practical tips about living in a low-cost, low-impact way. They have successfully applied to run sessions over a potential 12 weeks from April – July 2024, and are aiming to engage 380 unique people. They would like support from a Skilled Volunteer in preparing these events, including supporting with event promotion, logistical planning, collecting feedback, and tracking impact.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:660fbbe03d0504cd0bafcfd0;
                            :activityTitle "Sharing Spaces organiser".
id:660fd7c3e43bd6e415e13c1d :activityDescription """The Kids Network is looking for committed, fun and passionate volunteers who live in or around Islington to make a difference to the children of London. 

Our structured mentoring programme supports 8-11 year old's, based accross 8 London boroughs*, to support with their social and emotional development before they transition into secondary school.

As a mentor, you will hold weekly one on one sessions of 1-3 hours. You will help to build confidence, resilience and help your mentee to manage feelings through a series of fun and positive experiences and activities.

The weekly sessions can be flexible between weekdays and weekends. You'll have a monthly budget to spend exploring London with your mentee.

Whether you’re playing games or discussing goals, you’ll be making a difference to a child’s life by building their confidence, resilience and developing the tools for a positive future. You’ll get to learn new things about yourself and develop your skills and connections through our peer mentoring network.

All volunteers will go through two compulsory days of in-person training, where you'll gain skills and knowledge to support you as a mentor.

*We run programmes accross Brent, Hammersmith & Fulham, Westminster, Camden, Islington, Hackney, Southwark & Lambeth.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65eae1dffc81beee77e2559d;
                            :activityTitle "Children's Mentor - Change a Little Londoner's Life".
id:660fd7c3e43bd6e415e13c1e :address "London Borough of Brent";
                            :latitude "51.5672808"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.2710568"^^xsd:double.
id:66101bafa69642b9605b17b3 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899;
                            :organisationDescription "The IMB helps to ensure that proper standards of care and decency are maintained. ";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/86ec33a1-679b-403a-bd4f-b2af1f903071_2024-04-05T15:41:34.602Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Independent Monitoring Boards";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://imb.org.uk/>.
id:66101c6cfdcb64bfd8465d9b :activityDescription """The Independent Monitoring Boards (IMB) helps to ensure that proper standards of care and decency are maintained in prisons across England and Wales.
We recruit for new members numerous times each year. Please visit our website for further information. If we are not currently looking for new members near you, please add your name to our register and we will contact you when a new opportunity arises in your area.
Applicants do not need any special qualifications or experience as we will provide all necessary training and support. Candidates need to be over 18 years of age and live within a reasonable distance of the prison (up to one hour travel time). You need to be enthusiastic, open minded, possess effective communication skills and have the ability to exercise sound, objective judgement. 
We encourage applications from people from minority ethnic communities, young people, those of working age, and people with disabilities, as these groups are under-represented on our existing Boards.
This is an unpaid, voluntary role, but we pay your travel expenses and in certain circumstances, some loss of earnings and childcare/carer costs.
The time commitment is approximately 2 to 3 visits per month, although this will be higher in the first year as members go through induction into the role.
Please visit the IMB website for further information and to apply:   Prison volunteering vacancies - Independent Monitoring Boards (imb.org.uk)""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66101bafa69642b9605b17b3;
                            :activityTitle "Members for Independent Monitoring Boards – Prisons in England and Wales".
id:66101c6cfdcb64bfd8465d9c :address "Leicester";
                            :latitude "52.6368778"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.1397592"^^xsd:double.
id:6614fb0a9ee886ced3a4fa1c :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """Action Tutoring unlocks the potential of children and young people who are facing disadvantage. We are tackling the attainment gap head-on by forging partnerships with schools nationwide. Our trained volunteer tutors are empowered to enable pupils to make meaningful academic progress, opening doors to future opportunities.

""";
                            :organisationName "Action Tutoring";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://actiontutoring.org.uk/>.
id:661540a7f99b360e23d6e0cf :activityDescription """Are you thinking about volunteering, but can’t decide which role is best for you?

Do you like meeting people? Are you a good listener? Maybe you’re a fantastic organiser or someone who loves to get stuck into admin? We’ve got volunteering opportunities for everyone. Do you have time to spare? Then you could volunteer with us. Whether you can volunteer for a couple of days each week, month or year we have a role to suit you. We need people with a wide variety of skills and experience and embrace diversity, offering a welcoming and inclusive environment for all our volunteers.

Our ‘Introduction to Volunteering’ sessions run regularly, for approximately one hour, and provide the opportunity for you to meet the volunteer team and find out more about volunteering opportunities. 

Upcoming sessions:
Tuesday 21 October 2025 6pm
Wednesday 19 November 2025 2pm
Wednesday 7 January 2026 2pm
Thursday 19 February 2026 6pm
Tuesday 31 March 2026 10.30am
Wednesday 6 May 2026 6pm
Wednesday 3 June 2026 2pm

Please book your place at this event here:  https://www.pah.org.uk/volunteer-roles/introduction-to-volunteering/  """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d5fca0624f3ab9fbc83b;
                            :activityTitle "Introduction to Volunteering".
id:66169d5247af10a843126434 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089d;
                            :organisationDescription """Craft your writing skills, so you can evoke the desired emotions and interests with your audience, or if you wish to improve and refine your English grammar to articulate your writing to a higher standard.

Then the Writers Initiative can help you with the cultivation of your writing, so in turn the better you will be able to entertain, inform or educate your readers.""";
                            :organisationName "The Writers Initiative";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.writersinitiative.com/>.
id:6616a201ad08dd3a925f90d1 :activityDescription """This opportunity is for those interested in writing articles/blog posts for the Writers Initiative website. 

Those that volunteer for this opportunity will have flexibility in writing articles that they want to write. As long as they fall into the area of fiction or non-fiction writing, or social and economic issues that can affect people.

Please see the website to further look into the kind of articles that the organisation posts.

www.writersinitiative.com

This role can be carried out from home or anywhere as long as the volunteer has access to a PC and internet connection. The hours are also very flexible, and this work can be fitted around the schedule of the volunteer.

Note: For some reason the posting is saying 36000 hours! You will only be asked to write 1 article to start with and then more if you want to. It will not be 36000 hours of work!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66169d5247af10a843126434;
                            :activityTitle "Freelance Writer of Blog/Article posts ".
id:6616a40fad08dd3a925f9197 :activityDescription """General Maintenance Volunteers work with the General Maintenance Officer and the Operations
team to care for the buildings and outside spaces around Earth Trust Centre and ensure our
facilities are well maintained, attractive and safe. Come and work in a beautiful setting in the
stunning Oxfordshire countryside with us and you’ll be helping to make sure we’re a welcoming
space for our visitors, from families and schoolchildren to researchers and wedding parties.
There is always a lot to be done at Earth Trust HQ, and we’ve got some exciting new projects
coming over the next few months too.
What does the role involve?
The role is varied and suitable for all skill
levels. Tasks include:
o Repairs and maintenance - painting,
woodwork, plumbing, fencing.
o Site presentation - strimming,
landscaping and maintaining the
outside spaces at the centre (hedge
work, jet-washing, litter picking).
o Project work – planning and delivering
improvements to the site.
o Support setting up for events.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ed04c794380477b73fa1;
                            :activityTitle "Centre Maintenance Volunteer".
id:6616e9014d3296dd39bafb62 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription "Been There is the only registered charity helping adults (18+) with body image issues and related mental health concerns by connecting them, for free, with a Mentor who has ‘Been There’ too. All our Mentors are rigorously vetted, trained and supported by us. They communicate 1:1 with Mentees via the discrete safe-space of our app. Our Mentors are here to support, empower and, most importantly, listen so mentees know that they are not alone.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/7757201a-8039-441a-8f8f-cf0fa6f22efb_2024-04-10T19:38:14.805Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Been There";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://beenthereapp.com/>.
