                            :organisationDescription "This year Royal Greenwich Heritage Trust (RGHT) celebrates a decade looking after key structures, objects and historic records within the Royal Borough of Greenwich in Southeast London, the most important of these being the Grade I listed Jacobean Charlton House. ";
                            :organisationName "Royal Greenwich Heritage Trust".
id:6645e23d47e8e5047c62a089 :activityDescription """Royal Greenwich Heritage Trust

This year Royal Greenwich Heritage Trust (RGHT) celebrates a decade looking after key structures, objects and historic records within the Royal Borough of Greenwich in Southeast London, the most important of these being the Grade I listed Jacobean Charlton House. 

We are seeking a range of talented people to join our board of Trustees, and help run our charity, as we look forward to the next 10 years. 

We have exciting plans for Charlton House, as we seek to drive the Trust’s commercial and community activities and build towards a sustainable future for our heritage assets, as well as opening up the museum collection and archive to more visitors.  

The role of a Trustee is to ensure the management and future success of the organisation, drawing on your skills and experiences to date and having the opportunity to develop new ones.

Previous experience as a Trustee is not required. Being a Trustee is a voluntary appointment. 

What are we looking for?

Active people who support the Trust’s purpose. We are especially keen to appoint candidates with skills and ideas around strategic and creative thinking; fundraising and income generation, commercial development, marketing; heritage interpretation; and finance. 

How much time is involved?

Board meetings are bi-monthly. In addition there is an annual half day strategy meeting and a small number of ad-hoc meetings throughout the year. Board members have the opportunity to join sub-committees. In person attendance at these meetings is desirable but not always essential. 
To help deliver success you will be supported by a wonderful team of staff, volunteers, and Trustees, with tremendous goodwill from the wider community.

How to apply
Please download our pack from our website: greenwichheritage.org and send your full and up to date CV together with a covering letter detailing why you are an excellent fit to join our Trustees to info@rght.org.uk.

The closing date is Monday 10 June. We aim to schedule interviews in the third and fourth week of June.
Royal Greenwich Heritage Trust is committed to diversity and welcomes applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6645e14ec1ca12b02ca5aa54;
                            :activityTitle "Trustee";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
