                            :longitude "-0.1469688"^^xsd:double.
id:6659a839f34c87192cec76e4 :activityDescription """Our befriending scheme can receive referrals from anyone who is suffering from extreme loneliness.  Befriending is a means to reduce isolation and increase independence.

Clients are placed with a befriender who will call or visit them for one hour a week in their own home and chat to them whilst encouraging them to make positive choices and help them to help themselves.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66263dc4ad36b057002b816b;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Befriender ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6659a839f34c87192cec76e5 :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:6659b47fe1b400c8af807192 :activityDescription """Cancer Research Shop Assistant Volunteer - Fulham:

As a Shop Assistant at the Cancer Research UK Shop - Fulham, is  an  exciting and rewarding way to start your day!. No two days are the same and you have the chance to flex different skills regularly. There are always new opportunities to keep you engaged and help you grow and develop in your role.

Cancer Research Fulham shop volunteers are helping us beat cancer right now. If you volunteer at a Cancer Research UK shop; Fulham, you too could make a real difference to what we can achieve. Nothing we do would be possible without amazing volunteers like you.

We are looking for shop volunteers in our Cancer Research UK shop, on North End Road in Fulham, who can help with tasks detailed below:

• Sorting through donated items and pricing stock  
• Serving customers, taking cash and providing good all-round customer service  
• Working on window and shop displays  
• Keeping the shop tidy, clean and well organised  
• Interacting with the general public  
• Following new health, safety and social distancing measures  

This shop has shifts available every day of the week.

You don’t need any experience to volunteer, you just need to be motivated, hardworking and enjoy being part of a team. 

There’ll be a full induction as well as ongoing training opportunities to make sure you’re fully confident and able to excel in your role. 

Website for further information and how to apply:
https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/get-involved/volunteer/shop-volunteer-fulham
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6426107cde05bf8ae7c9af41;
                            :activityTitle "Shop Assistant Fulham - Cancer Research";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6659b47fe1b400c8af807193 :address "Cancer Research UK, 350 North End Road, London, UK";
                            :latitude "51.48170760000001"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.1996679"^^xsd:double.
id:6659b80aa5270223a4b47650 :activityDescription """Come and see the magic of volunteering with Girlguiding ! No matter how much time you have to give, there's an opportunity waiting for you.

There are lots of fun and flexible ways to get involved. You don't need to have been involved in guiding before or have loads of time to make a big difference. Whatever your skills and interests - whether it’s volunteering with girls directly or supporting behind the scenes - there’s a role to suit you.

By volunteering with us, you’ll be helping girls build their confidence, have adventures and learn new things. You might help out for an hour at a unit meeting or go on a residential trip. You might support your local unit by sourcing resources for an activity or helping them with a fundraising event.  If you’re qualified in first aid, you might teach girls important life skills. Or if you have an interesting job, you could go along and share what you do. 

Volunteering for Girlguiding is a great way of meeting new people and taking a break from your daily routine. You can also build your own skills by taking our leadership development qualification, becoming a first aider or qualified outdoor activity instructor. 

Ready for a new adventure? Register as a volunteer  here: https://go.girlguiding.org.uk/join-us/join-as-volunteer/
For more information on registering as a volunteer, see here: https://www.girlguiding.org.uk/get-involved/become-a-volunteer/register-to-volunteer/
And for the different ways you can volunteer, see here: https://www.girlguiding.org.uk/get-involved/become-a-volunteer/ways-of-volunteering/
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65b8d056381db807e5fb1584;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer with Girlguiding";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6659b80aa5270223a4b47651 :address "Hereford, UK";
                            :latitude "52.05639799999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.715974"^^xsd:double.
