id:6659b975f747be023fe1804c :activityDescription """Come and see the magic of volunteering with Girlguiding ! No matter how much time you have to give, there's an opportunity waiting for you.

There are lots of fun and flexible ways to get involved. You don't need to have been involved in guiding before or have loads of time to make a big difference. Whatever your skills and interests - whether it’s volunteering with girls directly or supporting behind the scenes - there’s a role to suit you.

By volunteering with us, you’ll be helping girls build their confidence, have adventures and learn new things. You might help out for an hour at a unit meeting or go on a residential trip. You might support your local unit by sourcing resources for an activity or helping them with a fundraising event.  If you’re qualified in first aid, you might teach girls important life skills. Or if you have an interesting job, you could go along and share what you do. 

Volunteering for Girlguiding is a great way of meeting new people and taking a break from your daily routine. You can also build your own skills by taking our leadership development qualification, becoming a first aider or qualified outdoor activity instructor. 

Ready for a new adventure? Register as a volunteer  here: https://go.girlguiding.org.uk/join-us/join-as-volunteer/
For more information on registering as a volunteer, see here: https://www.girlguiding.org.uk/get-involved/become-a-volunteer/register-to-volunteer/
And for the different ways you can volunteer, see here: https://www.girlguiding.org.uk/get-involved/become-a-volunteer/ways-of-volunteering/
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65b8d056381db807e5fb1584;
