id:665d9cec7445b3ab28b9c4a1 :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """AbilityNet is a pioneering UK charity with a global perspective. Established more than 25 years ago, we believe the power of digital technology should be available to everyone, regardless of ability or age. Our free online resources and a network of over 450 community-based volunteers help individuals with any disability, of any age, to use all kinds of digital technology. Our vision is a digital world accessible to all.

Our teams of experts help organisations of all types and sizes to become more inclusive and to build accessible digital products and services. We are founder members of the global accessibility profession, work closely with some of the biggest businesses on the planet and organise TechShare Pro, Europe’s largest accessibility gathering.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/957ed62e-e9c0-4af1-bea2-b6e53d57d15e_2024-06-03T10:37:31.929Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "AbilityNet";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://abilitynet.org.uk/>.
id:665dad56103207cef4a1b743 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """Shake My Hand is a media campaign working to increase the number of rape and sexual abuse Survivors who are reporting their experiences to the Police. We plan to do this in a number of ways. These will include Awareness Training facilitated by Survivors for the organisations helping and supporting Survivors at the time of them considering reporting their experiences, as well as providing 1:1 Peer Survivor Support and supporting National Petitions.
The Campaign is very much in its early days - we have just created our social media accounts and website. The Campaign Founder; award-winning mental health UK Blogger with over 1.3 million readers and sexual abuse and rape Survivor; Aimee Wilson, is currently working on our Campaign Strategy and various organisational documents to then begin collaborations and securing endorsements with her already established connections with the Chief Executive in the NHS and the Mental Health Lead of the Police. 
We will then be looking to hire Volunteers in various positions. 
Our social media accounts are @shakemyhandUK on both Twitter (X) and Instagram as well as our page on Facebook (Shake My Hand Campaign) and our website is set to launch June 17th. """;
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/d22b2d5b-0db7-43dd-a7b7-d1c71b436732_2024-06-03T11:47:33.350Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "Shake My Hand Campaign".
id:665dcfdfca576482e2321ffa :activityDescription """VOLUNTEER VACANCY
