id:667c1c9edb72698393842582 :activityDescription "Join our wonderful community of volunteers sewing reusable sanitary pads from home (or in self-made friendship/community groups. This is a zero-commitment volunteering opportunity for anyone with a sewing machine and some spare time: individuals, school groups (DofE), community and craft groups, for example. All instructions and templates are provided as well as fabric on request. This is a positive, friendly and supportive community.  Since founding in 2020, we have sent 120,000 volunteer-made sustainable pads to people suffering from period poverty, providing dignity, keeping girls in schools and allowing women to work and carry on their normal activities during their periods.  We have taken 15,000 people out of period poverty in countries including Lebanon, Syria, Turkey, Greece, Italy, Lativa, Ukraine, Uganda, Pakistan, the USA and in the UK. We send quarterly newsletters with all the project updates and every pad delivery is acknowledged by email and we tell you where they are going. Come join our lovely community!";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64232da230af56b4590e0d51;
                            :activityTitle "Sewing reusable sanitary pads from home for refugees and people suffering from period poverty";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:667c27673fe0f24f10753cfa :address "From Home";
