id:667efc6ecb9fcb152a10fc36 :activityDescription """Purpose of the Role: 
To deliver creative and inclusive knitting sessions at the Baytree Centre, helping participants of all skill levels enjoy a shared activity, build connections, and feel part of a welcoming community. By leading the sessions and creating a positive environment, the role ensures that activities run smoothly and that participants feel comfortable, valued, and included. 

 

Main Responsibilities: 
- Lead and deliver weekly knitting sessions for participants of varying skill levels. 
- Prepare and set up the space, ensuring all materials and equipment are available and organised. 
- Provide guidance, demonstrations, and encouragement to help participants develop their knitting skills. 
- Create a supportive and inclusive environment where participants feel comfortable to learn, share, and ask questions. 
- Encourage connections and engagement between participants through their shared interest in knitting. 
- Collect feedback from participants to help improve future sessions. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and procedures. 

Skills and Qualities Required: 

- Strong knitting skills and the ability to teach and demonstrate techniques clearly. 
- Patience, empathy, and cultural sensitivity to support participants of different skill levels and backgrounds. 
- Good organisational skills to ensure smooth preparation and delivery of sessions. 
- Strong interpersonal skills to foster a positive and inclusive atmosphere. 
- Effective communication skills to provide clear instructions and constructive feedback. 
- Interest in crafts, creativity, and community-based activities. 
 
Commitment: 
- Deliver weekly knitting sessions, (day and time subject to the timetable). 
- Minimum commitment of 2 terms for continuity and effectiveness. 
- Location: The Baytree Centre. 
 
Benefits: 
- Gain experience in delivering and leading creative group activities. 
- Develop skills in facilitation, teaching, and cross-cultural communication. 
- Contribute to participants’ confidence, creativity, and social connections. 
- Be part of a supportive and welcoming volunteer community. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female Knitting Facilitator ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:667efd25559c851ae45dad95 :activityDescription """Purpose of the Role: 
To deliver engaging and supportive Life in the UK test preparation sessions at the Baytree Centre, helping participants gain the knowledge and confidence needed to pass the test. By leading the sessions in a welcoming and inclusive environment, the role enables participants to explore British culture, history, and government, improving their understanding and readiness for the test. 

Main Responsibilities: 
- Lead and deliver Life in the UK test preparation sessions. 
- Prepare and set up the space, ensuring all materials and resources are available and organised for each session. 
- Provide clear explanations of test content, answering questions and offering guidance. 
- Create a supportive and inclusive environment where participants feel comfortable learning and asking questions. 
- Encourage connections and peer learning among participants. 
- Share study strategies and tips to help participants prepare effectively. 
- Collect feedback from participants to improve future sessions. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and procedures. 
 
Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Strong knowledge of the Life in the UK test content, with the ability to teach and explain topics clearly. 
- Patience, empathy, and cultural sensitivity to support participants from diverse backgrounds and knowledge levels. 
- Good organisational skills to ensure smooth preparation and delivery of sessions. 
- Strong interpersonal skills to foster a positive and inclusive atmosphere. 
- Effective communication skills to provide clear instructions and constructive feedback. 
- Interest in education, citizenship, or community support. 
 
Commitment: 
- Deliver weekly Life in the UK test preparation sessions (day and time subject to the timetable). 
- Minimum commitment of 2 terms for continuity and effectiveness. 
- Location: The Baytree Centre. 

Benefits: 
- Gain experience in delivering educational group sessions. 
- Develop skills in facilitation, teaching, and cross-cultural communication. 
- Contribute to participants’ confidence and readiness for the Life in the UK test. 
- Be part of a supportive and welcoming volunteer community. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female  Life in the UK Test Practice Support Volunteer for the Women Service";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
