id:667efea75e843d8fd2edca35 :activityDescription """Purpose of the Role: 
To provide personalised support and companionship to ESOL (English for Speakers of Other Languages) students at the Baytree Centre, fostering their English language skills, understanding of life in the UK, and integration into the community. By engaging in one-to-one interactions and creating a welcoming environment, the role contributes to the social inclusion and well-being of participants from diverse backgrounds. 
 
Main Responsibilities: 
- Provide tailored one-to-one support to ESOL students, focusing on conversation skills and knowledge of life in the UK. 
- Share insights about cultural aspects, daily life, and community resources to support integration. 
- Create a friendly and supportive atmosphere that reduces feelings of isolation. 
- Offer basic information and assistance to help access services and navigate resources. 
- Maintain consistent attendance and communication with paired students. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and procedures. 

Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Sufficient English to engage effectively in one-to-one conversations. 
- Empathy, patience, and cultural sensitivity. 
- Good interpersonal and listening skills. 
- Flexible and adaptable to varying schedules and needs. 
- Reliable, punctual, and committed to the agreed schedule. 
- Interest in community support, integration, and language development. 
 
Commitment: 
- 1 hour per week, (day and time subject to the timetable). 
- Minimum commitment of 2 terms for continuity and effectiveness. 
- Location: The Baytree Centre. 

Benefits: 
- Gain experience in cross-cultural communication and mentoring. 
- Contribute to the integration and confidence of adult ESOL learners. 
- Be part of a welcoming and supportive volunteer community. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female Adult Befriender for the Women Service";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:667eff2a0ce2d20db71e61af :activityDescription """Your role is in fostering a positive learning environment and facilitating the educational journey of students. By collaborating with the teaching team, providing classroom assistance, you directly contribute to improving the learning experiences of ESOL (English for Speakers of Other Languages) and Literacy students

Purpose of the Role: 
To support the delivery of engaging and inclusive ESOL (English for Speakers of Other Languages) and Literacy classes at the Baytree Centre, helping students improve their language skills and confidence. By collaborating with the teaching team and providing classroom assistance, the role contributes to creating a positive learning environment that supports the educational journey of adult learners from diverse backgrounds. 

Main Responsibilities: 
- Collaborate with the teaching team to assist in ESOL and Literacy classes. 
- Provide classroom support and identify students who may need extra help. 
- Offer additional assistance as required, working closely with the teacher to ensure a cohesive and supportive learning environment. 
- Reinforce positive behaviour and acknowledge achievements to motivate students. 
- Ensure all lesson materials and resources are prepared and organised. 
- Support an inclusive classroom environment that values diversity and promotes learning. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and procedures. 
 
Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Strong communication skills to effectively interact with both students and educators. 
- Empathy, patience, and cultural sensitivity to support students with diverse needs.
- Good organisational skills to help ensure smooth running of classes. 
- Ability to collaborate as part of a team while remaining flexible to classroom needs. 
- Reliable, punctual, and committed to supporting learners’ progress. 
- Interest in language learning, education, or community support. 

Commitment: 
- Assist in ESOL and Literacy classes, (day and time subject to the timetable). 
- Minimum commitment of 2 terms for continuity and effectiveness. 
- Location: The Baytree Centre. 

Benefits: 
- Gain experience in supporting adult language learning and classroom facilitation. 
- Develop cross-cultural communication and organisational skills. 
- Contribute to the confidence, skills, and integration of adult learners. 
- Be part of a supportive and inclusive volunteer community. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female ESOL Teaching Support Volunteer for the Women Service";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:667eff7d5e843d8fd2edcaad :activityDescription """Wellbeing Facilitator 

Purpose of the Role: 
To deliver engaging and inspiring wellbeing sessions at the Baytree Centre, fostering a healthier and happier community. By sharing your expertise and creating a supportive environment, the role empowers participants to explore different aspects of wellbeing and adopt positive lifestyle choices. Topics may include mindfulness, creative arts, physical fitness, nutrition, gardening, dance, drama, or other wellbeing-related activities. 

Main Responsibilities: 
- Lead and deliver wellbeing workshops on agreed topics. 
- Prepare and set up the space, ensuring all materials and resources are available and organised for each session. 
- Create a supportive and inclusive environment where participants feel comfortable to learn, share, and engage in discussions. 
- Encourage connections between participants and support the development of positive networks. 
- Provide guidance, encouragement, and practical tips to help participants integrate wellbeing practices into their daily lives. 
- Collect feedback from participants to help improve future sessions. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and procedures. 

Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Expertise or experience in one or more wellbeing areas such as mindfulness, creative arts, fitness, nutrition, or similar. 
- Strong facilitation skills to engage participants and encourage active involvement. 
- Patience, empathy, and cultural sensitivity to support participants from diverse backgrounds.
- Good organisational skills to ensure smooth preparation and delivery of sessions. 
- Excellent communication skills to convey information clearly and encourage meaningful discussion. 
- Interest in health, wellbeing, or community engagement. 

Commitment: 
- Deliver wellbeing workshops, (day and time subject to the timetable). 
- Minimum commitment of 2 terms for continuity and effectiveness. 
- Location: The Baytree Centre. 

Benefits: 
- Gain experience in delivering community-based wellbeing activities. 
- Develop skills in facilitation, teaching, and cross-cultural communication. 
- Contribute to participants’ confidence, wellbeing, and social connections. 
- Be part of a supportive and welcoming volunteer community. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female Well-being Facilitator for the Women Service";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:667effc870e64aadbb70e949 :activityDescription """Your role is to provide support smoothly running of activities at the Baytree Centre to benefit women and girls of the local community and to support the administrative work of the Baytree staff, ensuring all records and data are comprehensive and up to date with the aim of 
facilitating evaluation and reporting.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
