id:667f001f0ce2d20db71e6434 :activityDescription """Purpose of the Role: 
To provide one-to-one academic and personal development support to girls aged 10–18 at the Baytree Centre, helping them overcome challenges in subjects such as Maths, English, and Science. By offering guidance, encouragement, and role-modelling positive behaviour, the role supports young people in building their confidence, achieving academic milestones, and developing life skills through the Character Development Framework. Sessions are delivered both face-to-face and online. 

Main Responsibilities: 
- Provide individual academic support to girls aged 10–18, focusing on areas where they may be struggling, including Maths, English, and Science. 
- Act as a positive role model, inspiring mentees to pursue their educational goals with determination and enthusiasm. 
- Assist mentees in setting and achieving academic and personal milestones, celebrating progress and fostering motivation. 
- Support mentees’ personal growth through guidance on goal setting, time management, study skills, and confidence-building techniques. 
- Maintain regular communication with mentees and programme coordinators to ensure consistency and progress. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and safeguarding procedures. 
 
Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Strong academic background, ideally with GCSE or degree-level education in Maths, English, or Science, enabling the delivery of competent academic support. 
- Excellent interpersonal skills to build rapport and trust with mentees. 
- Patience, empathy, and the ability to understand the challenges faced by young people. 
- Commitment to creating a supportive and encouraging environment for learning. 
- Organisational skills to plan and structure sessions effectively. 
 
Commitment: 
- One session per week for 1 hour during the academic year. 
- Weekday sessions run between 4:00 pm and 6:15 pm (Monday to Thursday). 
- Final day and time to be confirmed based on the programme timetable. 
- Commitment to ongoing training and support provided by the programme coordinator. 
- Minimum commitment of two terms (approximately 6 months) to ensure continuity and integration. 
 
Benefits: 
- Gain experience in mentoring and academic support for young people. 
- Develop skills in youth engagement, coaching, and personal development. 
- Contribute to reducing attainment gaps and supporting educational success. 
- Be part of a welcoming and supportive volunteer community. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female Youth Mentor for the Youth Service";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:667f006a604d511dc6b369a3 :activityDescription """Purpose of the Role: 
To provide one-to-one academic and personal support to newly arrived migrant girls aged 11–19 at the Baytree Centre, helping them adapt to formal education in the UK. By supporting them in a range of subjects such as Maths, English, and Science, and assisting them in developing their English language skills, the role helps mentees build confidence, overcome challenges, and integrate successfully into school life. The role also involves fostering personal development, goal setting, and confidence-building in line with the Character Development Framework. Sessions are delivered both face-to-face and online. 

Main Responsibilities: 

- Provide individual academic support to girls aged 11–19, focusing on areas where they require extra assistance, including Maths, English, and Science. 
- Support mentees in developing their English language skills in a fun, supportive, and inclusive environment. 
- Bridge communication gaps by creating a welcoming atmosphere for girls who are learning English. 
- Act as a positive role model, inspiring and motivating mentees to pursue their academic and personal goals with determination and enthusiasm. 
- Assist in setting and achieving academic milestones, celebrating progress, and building a sense of achievement. 
- Foster personal development through guidance on goal setting, time management, study skills, and confidence-building techniques. 
- Maintain regular communication with mentees and programme coordinators to track progress, address challenges, and provide feedback. 

Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Strong academic background, ideally with GCSE or degree-level education in Maths, English, or Science, enabling the delivery of competent academic support. 
- Excellent interpersonal skills to build rapport and trust with mentees from diverse backgrounds. 
- Patience, empathy, and cultural sensitivity to understand the unique challenges faced by newly arrived young people. 
- Ability to inspire, motivate, and empower mentees to achieve their goals. 
- Ability to speak Spanish or Arabic is highly desirable, as many mentees use these as their first languages. 
- Organisational skills to plan and deliver effective sessions. 

Commitment: 
- One session per week for 1 hour during the academic year. 
- Weekday sessions run between 4:00 pm and 6:15 pm (Monday to Thursday). 
- Final day and time will be confirmed following review of the programme timetable. 
- Commitment to ongoing training and support provided by the programme coordinator. 
- Minimum commitment of one academic year to ensure continuity and integration for mentees.

Benefits: 
- Gain experience in mentoring and academic support for newly arrived young people. 
- Develop skills in cross-cultural communication and English language support. 
- Contribute to the academic success and integration of migrant girls in the UK. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female Into School Mentor for the Youth Service";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:667f00e0604d511dc6b369e1 :activityDescription """Your role is to provide support to the Into School programme, which is designed for newly arrived migrant girls aged 11-19 who are out of education. These girls may be waiting for a school or college place or have not applied yet. We provide a range of positive, extracurricular 
activities and workshops for the girls to participate in while waiting for a place in formal 
education, including cookery, wellbeing/fitness sessions, and off-site workshops (ceramics, art galleries, etc.).""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female Into School Session Volunteer for the Youth Service (e.g. cookery, well-being)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:667f00e0604d511dc6b369e2 :address "The Baytree Centre, Brixton Road, London";
                            :latitude "51.4699586"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.1128963"^^xsd:double.
id:667f0148559c851ae45daf23 :activityDescription """Purpose of the Role: 
To support the delivery of engaging and inclusive academic sessions for newly arrived migrant girls aged 11–19 at the Baytree Centre as part of the Into School programme. The role involves assisting teachers in creating a positive and supportive learning environment, helping students with subjects such as ESOL (English for Speakers of Other Languages) and Maths, and providing one-to-one support to those needing extra assistance. By offering guidance, encouragement, and structured support, the volunteer will contribute to the girls’ confidence, academic progress, and integration into formal education. 

Main Responsibilities: 
- Collaborate with teachers in delivering ESOL and Maths lessons. 
- Assist with lesson plans and activities to ensure classes run smoothly. 
- Provide one-to-one support to students, helping them overcome learning challenges and participate actively in lessons. 
- Foster a positive and inclusive classroom environment where all students feel supported and able to contribute. 
- Encourage students’ academic progress while promoting motivation and engagement. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and safeguarding procedures. 

Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Strong academic background, ideally with GCSE or degree-level education in Maths and/or English, enabling competent academic support. 
- Excellent communication and interpersonal skills to work effectively with students from diverse backgrounds and language levels. 
- Patience and empathy to support students with varying learning paces and needs. 
- Enthusiasm for creating a supportive and engaging learning experience. 
- Ability to work collaboratively with teachers and other volunteers. 
 
Commitment: 
- One session per week for at least one term (usually 10–12 weeks). 
- Please refer to the Into School timetable for exact session times. 
- Final day and time will be confirmed following review of the programme timetable. 
- Meeting location: The Baytree Centre. 

Benefits: 
- Gain experience supporting academic learning for students from diverse backgrounds. 
- Develop skills in ESOL support, Maths tutoring, and inclusive education. 
- Contribute directly to the educational progress and integration of newly arrived young people. 
- Be part of a supportive and welcoming volunteer community. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea
This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female Into School Teaching Support Volunteer (Academic Focused) for the Youth Service";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:667f018e559c851ae45daf5a :activityDescription """Purpose of the Role: 
To support the delivery of engaging and inclusive art sessions as part of the Baytree Centre’s GEMS (Grow Enjoy Move Study) programme for girls aged 5–18. By creating a safe, inspiring, and welcoming environment, you will help participants explore creative activities, develop new artistic skills, and build confidence in their imagination and self-expression. Working alongside staff, you will assist in planning and delivering activities that nurture creativity, personal growth, and enjoyment of the arts. 

Main Responsibilities: 
- Assist in preparing and facilitating art-focused after-school sessions, providing guidance and encouragement to participants. 
- Support the delivery of age-appropriate creative activities that promote learning, self-expression, and personal development. 
- Foster a supportive and inclusive environment where girls feel confident trying new techniques, sharing their work, and working collaboratively. 
- Assist with administrative tasks such as attendance tracking, activity planning, and organising resources to ensure smooth running of sessions. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and safeguarding procedures. 

Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Empathy and patience to work effectively with girls of varying ages, backgrounds, and abilities. 
- Strong communication skills to engage positively with participants, other volunteers, and staff. 
- Creativity and enthusiasm for developing and delivering engaging art activities. 
- Reliability and commitment to attend scheduled sessions consistently. 
- Ability to work collaboratively as part of a team. 
 
Commitment: 
- One session per week for at least two terms. 
- Sessions are held Monday to Thursday between 4:00 pm and 6:00 pm and last for 1 hour. 
- Final schedule will be confirmed after reviewing the Youth Timetable. 

Benefits: 
- Gain experience supporting art and creativity-based youth activities. 
- Develop skills in youth engagement, activity facilitation, and arts education. 
- Contribute to the confidence, self-expression, and personal growth of participants. 
- Be part of a supportive and welcoming volunteer community. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female GEMS Art Club Volunteer for the Youth Service";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:667f01e5604d511dc6b36a1b :activityDescription """Purpose of the Role: 
To support the delivery of engaging and inclusive after-school book club sessions as part of the Baytree Centre’s GEMS (Grow Enjoy Move Study) programme for girls aged 5–18. By encouraging a love of reading, you will help create a safe, welcoming, and inspiring environment where girls can build their confidence, develop their literacy skills, and enjoy exploring new stories. Working alongside staff, you will assist in planning, delivering, and supporting activities that promote reading for pleasure and personal growth. 
 
Main Responsibilities: 
- Assist in preparing and facilitating book club sessions, providing guidance and encouragement to participants. 
- Support the delivery of age-appropriate reading activities that promote learning, creativity, and personal development. 
- Help foster a supportive and inclusive atmosphere where girls feel comfortable expressing their ideas, building confidence, and sharing opinions about books. 
- Assist with administrative tasks such as attendance tracking, activity planning, and organising resources to ensure the smooth running of the programme. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and safeguarding procedures. 
 
Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Empathy and patience to work effectively with girls of varying ages, backgrounds, and abilities. 
- Strong communication skills to engage positively with participants, other volunteers, and staff. 
- Creativity and enthusiasm for developing and delivering reading-focused activities that inspire a love of books. 
- Reliability and commitment to attend scheduled sessions consistently. 
- Ability to work collaboratively as part of a team. 
 
Commitment: 
- One session per week for at least two terms. 
- Sessions are held Monday to Thursday between 4:00 pm and 6:00 pm and last for 1 hour, depending on the club joined. 
- Final schedule will be confirmed after reviewing the Youth Timetable.

Benefits: 
- Gain experience supporting literacy and reading-based youth activities. 
- Develop skills in youth engagement, activity facilitation, and group discussion. 
- Contribute to the literacy development, confidence, and personal growth of girls. 
- Be part of a supportive and welcoming volunteer community. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female GEMS Book Club Volunteer ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:667f022370e64aadbb70e9a7 :activityDescription """Purpose of the Role: 
To support the delivery of engaging and inclusive cookery sessions as part of the Baytree Centre’s GEMS (Grow Enjoy Move Study) programme for girls aged 5–18. By creating a safe, welcoming, and inspiring environment, you will help participants learn new cooking skills, explore different recipes, and build confidence in the kitchen. Working alongside staff, you will assist with planning, facilitating, and supporting activities that encourage creativity, teamwork, and healthy living. 

Main Responsibilities: 
- Assist in preparing and facilitating cookery-focused after-school sessions, providing guidance and encouragement to participants. 
- Support the delivery of age-appropriate cooking activities that promote learning, creativity, and personal development. 
- Foster a supportive and inclusive environment where girls feel confident trying new recipes, expressing themselves, and working as part of a team. 
- Assist with administrative tasks such as attendance tracking, activity planning, and organising resources to ensure smooth running of sessions. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and safeguarding procedures. 

Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Empathy and patience to work effectively with girls of varying ages, backgrounds, and abilities. 
- Strong communication skills to engage positively with participants, other volunteers, and staff. 
- Creativity and enthusiasm for developing and delivering engaging cooking activities. 
- Reliability and commitment to attend scheduled sessions consistently. 
- Ability to work collaboratively as part of a team. 
 
Commitment: 
- One session per week for at least two terms. 
- Sessions are held Monday to Thursday between 4:00 pm and 6:00 pm and last for 1.5 hour. 
- Final schedule will be confirmed after reviewing the Youth Timetable. 
 
Benefits: 
- Gain experience supporting cookery and life-skills-based youth activities. 
- Develop skills in youth engagement, activity facilitation, and creative teaching. 
- Contribute to the confidence, independence, and wellbeing of participants. 
- Be part of a supportive and welcoming volunteer community. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea


 """;
