id:667f0268604d511dc6b36a40 :activityDescription """Purpose of the Role: 
To support the delivery of engaging and inclusive football sessions as part of the Baytree Centre’s GEMS (Grow Enjoy Move Study) programme, which provides after-school clubs for girls aged 5–18. By working alongside the football coach, you will help create a safe and encouraging environment where girls can develop their skills, build confidence, and enjoy being active. The role also involves assisting with the planning and smooth running of sessions, as well as fostering positive relationships among participants. 

Main Responsibilities: 
- Assist in preparing and facilitating football sessions, providing guidance and encouragement to participants. 
- Support the football coach in delivering engaging, age-appropriate activities that promote learning, creativity, and personal development. 
- Help maintain a supportive and inclusive atmosphere where girls feel comfortable expressing themselves, building confidence, and working as a team. 
- Assist with administrative tasks such as attendance tracking, activity planning, and organising equipment to ensure sessions run smoothly. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and safeguarding procedures. 

Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Empathy and patience to work effectively with girls of varying ages, backgrounds, and abilities. 
- Strong communication skills to engage positively with participants, other volunteers, and staff. 
- Creativity and enthusiasm for delivering fun, skills-based activities. 
- Reliability and commitment to attend scheduled sessions consistently. 
- Ability to work collaboratively as part of a team and take direction from the coach. 
 
Commitment: 
- One session per week for at least two terms. 
- Sessions are held Monday to Thursday between 4:00 pm and 6:00 pm and last for 1 hour. 
- Final schedule will be confirmed after reviewing the Youth Timetable. 
 
Benefits: 
- Gain experience supporting sports-based youth activities. 
- Develop skills in youth engagement, teamwork, and coaching support. 
- Contribute to the physical wellbeing, confidence, and personal development of girls. 
- Be part of a supportive and welcoming volunteer community. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea
""";
