- Assist in preparing and facilitating literacy and creative writing-focused after-school sessions, providing guidance and encouragement to participants. 
- Support the delivery of age-appropriate reading and writing activities that promote learning, creativity, and personal development. 
- Foster a supportive and inclusive atmosphere where girls feel confident expressing themselves, sharing their work, and exploring ideas. 
- Assist with administrative tasks such as attendance tracking, activity planning, and organising resources to ensure smooth running of sessions. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and safeguarding procedures. 

Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Empathy and patience to work effectively with girls of varying ages, backgrounds, and abilities. 
