- Final schedule will be confirmed after reviewing the Youth Timetable.

Benefits: 
- Gain experience supporting literacy and creative writing-focused youth activities. 
- Develop skills in youth engagement, literacy facilitation, and creative arts education. 
- Contribute to the confidence, self-expression, and personal growth of participants. 
- Be part of a supportive and welcoming volunteer community. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea

