                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:6687e1ea49881a6c21954545 :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089d,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription """The Centre for Computing History (CCH) is a national not-for-profit educational charity and museum. We collect, preserve and interpret artefacts - where possible, still working - and memories of computing history, particularly as it relates to the UK and to the unique local context of Cambridge.  

Our core purpose is to use our collections, displays, learning programmes and events to explore the social, cultural and historical impact – the lived experience - of developments in computing. Future generations will wonder how this massively important and transformative cultural development happened within just 70 years.  Through our hands-on and inclusive experiences, visitors of all kinds learn how these powerful devices became an inextricable part of all our lives and changed our world. """;
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/ccb6a49b-3464-4a38-9c7d-76ed0438dd6c_2024-07-05T12:07:06.341Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "The Centre for Computing History";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.computinghistory.org.uk/>.
id:6688101e4435668103b1c65a :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """By funding the right research into the most promising treatments, we get closer to a cure every day. Until then, we're here for everyone affected by Parkinson’s.

We'll find a cure. Together.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/740b4062-f7f7-40bb-9dce-4486d0e49835_2025-07-18T09:36:59.458Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Parkinson's UK";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.parkinsons.org.uk/>.
id:668821204004cc88d7bbc8f8 :activityDescription """We need volunteer help to stay on top of social media posts about our work. Our online presence is important to us and we need to promote our events and our important collection to drive both physical footfall to the museum and to increase engagement with our collection for our digital audiences.

Can you help? We need someone who can closely with our staff teams to  create fresh and impactful posts with consistency and attention to detail! We need you to:

Create exciting and informative content.
Promote products, services and events, in a way that is consistent with our brand and our broader audience growth and marketing strategies.
Schedule social media posts using Hootsuite.
Contribute to interacting with visitors and dealing with visitor enquiries via our social media platforms.
Help us develop new strategies and campaigns to grow our target audiences.

If you have a flair for creating exciting content or perhaps you're looking to break into a new career in social media marketing, we'd love to hear from you.

We primarily use Facebook, X (formerly Twitter), Instagram and LinkedIn but we'd be open to using other platforms too.

We are a relaxed and welcoming team. The working atmosphere is fun, relaxed but professional. Tea and coffee is available for free from our 'Pac Lunch Shop' and as a volunteer you are welcome to all of our special events for free. 

It would be great if you could come and work with us in person, but you may be able to do some work remotely. 

We are open from Wednesday to Sunday, 10am to 5pm, every week throughout the year and every day in most school holidays. 

Times are flexible though, especially for remote work. The amount of time you can offer us is entirely up to you, and it need not be the same each week. All we ask is that you let us know in advance.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6687e1ea49881a6c21954545;
                            :activityTitle "Social Media Marketing Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:668c305e153ca5f70b160f0a :activityDescription """We are seeking an experienced and innovative Digital Marketing Specialist to join our team. 

This remote position is ideal for a digital marketing professional who is passionate about social media, community engagement, and cultural exchange. 

The successful candidate will play a crucial role in enhancing our online presence, engaging our audience, and driving our mission forward through effective digital marketing strategies.

Develop and implement comprehensive digital marketing strategies to promote Linguist Point's mission and initiatives.

Manage and grow our social media presence across platforms including Facebook, Twitter, Instagram, LinkedIn, and YouTube.

Create, curate, and schedule engaging and relevant content to attract and retain our target audience.
Monitor, analyse, and report on social media performance metrics and adjust strategies to optimise results.

Collaborate with the team to design and execute email marketing campaigns and newsletters.
Utilise SEO best practices to enhance our website's visibility and search engine ranking.

Engage with our online community, responding to comments, messages, and inquiries in a timely and professional manner.

Stay updated on the latest digital marketing trends and tools, applying innovative approaches to our marketing efforts.

Work closely with internal teams to ensure consistent branding and messaging across all digital channels.

Conduct market research to identify opportunities for growth and engagement within our community.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cce8a0624f3ab9fafdd4;
                            :activityTitle "Remote Digital Marketing Specialist";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
