id:66a25277f07fd8891513c06f :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription "We provide lifelong support to serving and ex-serving RAF personnel and their families. We'll consider any request for assistance, however big or small, providing a tailor-made approach to each individual situation. From mobility aids and confidential counselling to financial grants, we offer a range of support tailored to the individual's needs.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/116c7c79-45df-4d05-89ae-ccc0c64f569c_2024-07-25T13:26:14.178Z.png>;
                            :organisationName "RAF Benevolent Fund";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.rafbf.org/get-involved/volunteer>.
id:66a7aa6a34e168c65310b0ae :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """We are a young and growing charity with over 100 volunteers active in more than 30 schools across London, supporting some 300 children. We are looking for additional volunteers for school year 2024-25.

There are volunteers helping children to read in practically every primary school; we seek to do the same for maths.

Volunteers need to be enthusiastic about helping children achieve their potential and to be able to commit for a full school year.  The only maths required is basic arithmetic, and we will provide training.""";
                            :organisationName "Number Champions";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.numberchampions.org.uk/>.
id:66a7b1fd7373df0b33c6144a :activityDescription """We will train you to use games and other creative activies to help young children aquire interest, confidence, and skills in maths.

You will run one-to-one sessions in a local primary school with chidren selected by their teacher as able to benefit from help in numeracy. Sessions are half an hour weekly, in school hours, for the whole school year.  Typically volunteers support three children, for a commitment of an hour and a half each week.

Former teachers also volunteering with us will give you support and advice throughout the year.

You need to bring enthusiasm and interpersonal skills to engage young children.  We will provide everything else.

You will have the satisfaction of knowing you have helped children achieve their potential - and every so often the privilege of seeing an \"Aha\" moment when the child understands something they have been stuggling with. Yu will also become more involved with your local community.

Schools provide very positive evaluations of the impact of our volunteers' work with children, as published in our Annual Reports on our website.

We partner over 40 London primary schools, so if there is no school local to you listed below please check our website or contact volunteer@numberchampions.org.uk.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66a7aa6a34e168c65310b0ae;
                            :activityTitle "Primary school numeracy supporter";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
