id:66e048c241d7ccf39ebe916b :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """Healthwatch collects feedback from local residents about publicly funded health and social care services. Based on what you tell us, we develop reports and recommendations on how services should be improved. 

We share data and recommendations with service providers and service commissioners. We monitor if and how the recommended changes are implemented.

We signpost people to relevant services and provide advice: this includes helping residents put forward a complaint about services, signposting to advocacy and local support organisations, and explaining how to navigate changes in services.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/2023cc1f-650b-4008-b33d-1d701724c56c_2024-09-10T13:25:22.319Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Healthwatch Westminster";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.healthwatchwestminster.org.uk/>.
id:66e04a49b60370c68995ad6f :activityDescription """We are currently looking for local people with an interest in health and social care to join the Healthwatch Westminster Advisory Board. This is an ongoing commitment. 

The Advisory Board is responsible for setting Healthwatch Westminster's priorities, ensuring that we are working on issues that are relevant and meaningful for local communities. The group meets once every 2-3 months to discuss progress on current projects and potential new areas of work. The term of office for members is two years. 

We are looking for people with the following qualities...
 - Reside/work or have an affiliation with the borough of Westminster
 - Able to work as part of a team and support others
 - Able to use IT and web-based applications (meetings are run via Zoom)
 - Possess a strong interest in health and social care services.
 - Can commit 2-3 hours per quarter for meetings, plus additional time to read and engage with papers
 - Respect diverse viewpoints and are dedicated to equality and diversity
 - Good local knowledge of Westminster, its local communities, and organisations
 - Good understanding of the health, social care and wellbeing policy issues and challenges facing the NHS and local authorities 

If you are interested, please send a CV and brief expression of interest to info@healthwatchwestminster.org.uk, highlighting why you think you would be a good fit for the role.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66e048c241d7ccf39ebe916b;
                            :activityTitle "Healthwatch Advisory Board Member";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:66e04a49b60370c68995ad70 :address "From Home";
