id:66e835daa65e666c5453382a :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """EM Tuition is a not-for-profit company that provides free tuition for financially disadvantaged children from 4-16, we are looking for volunteer tutors that can give at least one hour a week to help students in need. This is a Volunteer role and therefore unpaid.

We're looking for volunteer tutors who can work 1 - 1 with students online, who could not normally afford tuition, to support the children with either English, Maths or Science through Lesson Space.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/741f7427-24fd-4685-8bd8-a3b3dad053e3_2024-09-16T13:42:50.123Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "EM Tuition";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://emtuition.org.uk/>.
id:66e83baf47e8716f73c13d15 :activityDescription """EM Tuition is a not-for-profit company that provides free tuition for financially disadvantaged children from 4-16, we are looking for volunteer tutors that can give at least one hour a week to help students in need. This is a Volunteer role and therefore unpaid.

We're looking for volunteer tutors who can work 1 - 1 with students online, who could not normally afford tuition, to support the children with either English, Maths or Science through Lesson Space.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66e835daa65e666c5453382a;
                            :activityTitle "EM Tuition";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:66e83c7e7445a36e9f30e247 :address "https://emtuition.org.uk/job/volunteer-tutor/";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:66eaaeb2f44dbf55a0e8d531 :activityDescription """Our Cats Protection shops play a key part in raising the funds needed to help thousands of cats and kittens each year. Our shop assistant volunteers help with all aspects of the day to day running of one of our fantastic shops. They serve customers, help with stock rotation, create displays - and everything in between! They are part of a passionate retail team that make sure our shops are enjoyable places for customers to visit, leading to repeat custom and vital funds being raised to help our feline friends in need.    

What can you expect to be doing?
●	Serving customers 
●	Arranging and replenishing stock
●	Helping make changes to the shop layout, pricing and stock rotation
●	Sharing your passion for cat welfare
●	Promoting the work of the Cats Protection
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6426130dde05bf8ae7ca00f0;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Shop Assistant";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:66eaaeb2f44dbf55a0e8d532 :address "725 Wilmslow Road, Didsbury, Manchester";
                            :latitude "53.4165655"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.2315266"^^xsd:double.
id:66ebff86941fcccf03075ca6 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """Roy Castle Lung Cancer Foundation is the only charity in the UK that is dedicated to supporting all those impacted by the disease. Because of the support of individuals like yourself, we are able to continue our advancements in improving life expectancy and the quality of life of those diagnosed with lung cancer. We are also dedicated to supporting not just those diagnosed with the disease, but all those impacted by a diagnosis. If you would like any information or support, please let me know. 

Our research into early detection has laid the groundwork for lung cancer screening and we are proud to be supporting NHS England on the rollout of its Targeted Lung Health Check programmes, which 76% of people are being diagnosed at an early stage and offered curative-intent treatment.
We recognise, however, that lung cancer screening will not be available to everyone which is why we remain committed to helping everyone get diagnosed as early as possible. Our ongoing work in symptom awareness, challenging disease misconceptions and empowering self-advocacy remains vital and at our core, as does our research into the development of new early diagnostic techniques, including blood tests and sputum swabs. 

In addition to funding over £30 million into lung cancer research, Roy Castle Lung Cancer Foundation supports thousands of people living with the disease, including financial support of which demand is at an all-time high. 
A lung cancer diagnosis already creates physical, emotional, and financial turmoil. The cost-of-living crisis is making the hardest of times even more desperate. Our patient grants offer a momentary let up from the constant anxiety many face. 
It for all of these reasons that we, once again, thank you so much for supporting our charity because we cannot do this without you. 
""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/3dbc6776-abef-4135-be57-c59d43dabfff_2024-09-19T10:40:05.611Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Roy Castle Lung Cancer Foundation ";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://roycastle.org/>.
id:66f1b5c088a121b149c2dda4 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089d,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription """This is a not-for-profit start up. The Journal of West Studies is a partially open
access journal that brings together academics with interests in the
history and heritage of the West, contemporary problems of the West,
across the entire range of activity the West is involved in. The journal will appeal to policy makers, practitioners, and an interested lay readership.  We are looking for volunteers to help in all aspects of the production and creation of the journal. It may appeal to current students or anyone who is looking for experience in the publishing world.  """;
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/de31990b-48f3-41da-bdbe-4de7a8e4016e_2025-01-21T13:29:45.446Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "The Journal of West Studies";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://jws.org.uk/>.
id:66f3c5260d5460264e37bf17 :activityDescription """Life changes when you choose reading! 

We train volunteers from local communities to go into one of our partner primary schools to support the same few children each week to grow a love of reading. 

We have over 50 years of experience of training volunteers to find reading for pleasure. You will listen to children read, read to them, engage in book chat and help them find books they will love. 

You will be trained through small group, live, interactive group sessions and then be matched to one of our partner schools.

Once trained we offer ongoing support through an online portal, additional training sessions and you will be linked to a dedicated support rep who you can speak to if you have any questions or queries. 
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d5f5a0624f3ab9fbc763;
                            :activityTitle "Coram Beanstalk Reading Helper Role";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:66f3c5260d5460264e37bf18 :address "Wood Terrace, Hanley, Stoke-on-Trent ST1 4LR, UK";
                            :latitude "53.0186966"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.1825322"^^xsd:double.
