id:66faca680bf1a2bc199dbfe5 :activityDescription """Join us for the landmark arts event of the year and help us light up Leeds this autumn!

On 23rd and 24th October, Light Night Leeds takes over the city, showcasing spectacular projections, interactive installations, and absorbing street art to 200,000 visitors as part of the UK’s largest light festival. We want you to be part of our team for Light Night Leeds this year. 

'I thoroughly enjoyed every aspect of the Light Night experience, from the captivating art installations to the constant flow of people rushing in to see what was happening on Millennium Square and Briggate. One of the most fulfilling parts of volunteering was being able to guide visitors to different locations, offering brief explanations about the shows and installations.' Rashida – Visitor Support Volunteer 2024

We are looking for volunteers who:
•    Are friendly, engaging and confident communicating with the public
•    Are interested in arts, culture or events
•    Are enthusiastic and flexible
•    Enjoy being part of a team and working with others
•    Are reliable and responsible
•    Are over 18

What will you be doing?
You’ll be the face of Light Night, welcoming visitors, supporting them to engage with artworks and providing information and directions to other artworks across the city. You’ll interact with visitors and be on hand to answer their questions. Based in a specific zone of the city that hosts multiple artworks, you’ll experience a variety of brilliant installations and performances. Your energy and enthusiasm will create an extraordinary experience for visitors of all ages.   

What commitment do you need to give?
Light Night Leeds runs over two evenings – Thursday 23rd and Friday 24th October 2025. You’ll need to be available for at least one shift of up to 6 hours during this time, plus one training session prior to the event, either in person or online. 

What’s in it for you?
As part of our volunteering team, you will:
•    Get up-close experience of Light Night artworks
•    Have a memorable night with like-minded people
•    Be part of something huge – Light Night Leeds attracts over 200,000 visitors
•    Support your local community and enjoy the amazing atmosphere of Light Night Leeds
•    Develop skills and experience that could support you in your personal and career development
•    Receive Volunteer Team Leeds merchandise

We provide all the information and training that you’ll need to fulfil your role, and staff will be on hand to support you throughout your volunteering experience. We know that a diverse volunteer community will help us to provide the best visitor experience and we’re committed to creating an inclusive culture where everyone can be themselves and achieve their potential. If you need support to submit an application, please email lightnightvolunteers@leeds.gov.uk 

Be part of the action and volunteer with Light Night Leeds 2025!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ddbea0624f3ab9fc888d;
                            :activityTitle "Light Night Leeds: Visitor Support Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:66faca681860892f0404c36d :activityDescription """Join us for the landmark arts event of the year and help us light up Leeds this autumn!

On 23rd and 24th October, Light Night Leeds takes over the city, showcasing spectacular projections, interactive installations, and absorbing street art to 200,000 visitors as part of the UK’s largest light festival. We want you to be part of our team for Light Night Leeds this year. 

'I thoroughly enjoyed every aspect of the Light Night experience, from the captivating art installations to the constant flow of people rushing in to see what was happening on Millennium Square and Briggate. One of the most fulfilling parts of volunteering was being able to guide visitors to different locations, offering brief explanations about the shows and installations.' Rashida – Visitor Support Volunteer 2024

We are looking for volunteers who:
•    Are friendly, engaging and confident communicating with the public
•    Are interested in arts, culture or events
•    Are enthusiastic and flexible
•    Enjoy being part of a team and working with others
•    Are reliable and responsible
•    Are over 18

What will you be doing?
You’ll be the face of Light Night, welcoming visitors, supporting them to engage with artworks and providing information and directions to other artworks across the city. You’ll interact with visitors and be on hand to answer their questions. Based in a specific zone of the city that hosts multiple artworks, you’ll experience a variety of brilliant installations and performances. Your energy and enthusiasm will create an extraordinary experience for visitors of all ages.   

What commitment do you need to give?
Light Night Leeds runs over two evenings – Thursday 23rd and Friday 24th October 2025. You’ll need to be available for at least one shift of up to 6 hours during this time, plus one training session prior to the event, either in person or online. 

What’s in it for you?
As part of our volunteering team, you will:
•    Get up-close experience of Light Night artworks
•    Have a memorable night with like-minded people
•    Be part of something huge – Light Night Leeds attracts over 200,000 visitors
•    Support your local community and enjoy the amazing atmosphere of Light Night Leeds
•    Develop skills and experience that could support you in your personal and career development
•    Receive Volunteer Team Leeds merchandise

We provide all the information and training that you’ll need to fulfil your role, and staff will be on hand to support you throughout your volunteering experience. We know that a diverse volunteer community will help us to provide the best visitor experience and we’re committed to creating an inclusive culture where everyone can be themselves and achieve their potential. If you need support to submit an application, please email lightnightvolunteers@leeds.gov.uk 

Be part of the action and volunteer with Light Night Leeds 2025!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ddbea0624f3ab9fc888d;
                            :activityTitle "Light Night Leeds: Visitor Support Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:66fbc83b1893b3e509699506 :activityDescription "The Amazing Northampton Run CIC takes place on the 14th September 2025 as we need to build an incredible team of 130 volunteers to make sure that the event runs safely and the runners feel well supported.  The event team is divided in to 8 individual teams each with a supervisor and full briefing and home made cake so you will be well looked after ";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425db8ba0624f3ab9fc55d4;
                            :activityTitle "The Amazing Northampton Run CIC ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:66fbc83b1893b3e509699507 :address "Northampton";
                            :latitude "52.23706499999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.8944420999999999"^^xsd:double.
id:66fd60528acd8edaf290ed96 :activityDescription """Family Support Volunteers support families with children under 5 years on a one-to-one basis, either in the family’s home or in their local community (we support families across the Croydon borough.) By meeting with a family for 2-3 hours each week Family Support Volunteers offer emotional support and practical assistance to a family going through a difficult period in their life.
No special qualifications are necessary to become a Family Support Volunteer, but Home-Start volunteers are usually either parents or grandparents themselves, or people with experience of young children and family life.
We also ask that you are:
able to visit a family for 2-3 hours once a week*
available for supervision every 6 weeks
able to commit for at least 6 months
prepared to complete our training course plus some additional training sessions throughout the year
prepared to undergo an Enhanced Disclosure and Barring check (DBS) and provide 2 referees
*Most families require support during school hours. Volunteers are able to take a break during the school holidays if required.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d641a0624f3ab9fbcccc;
                            :activityTitle "Family Support Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:66fd60d0b6d00f4169477ba5 :address "Church St, Croydon CR0 1RF, UK";
                            :latitude "51.3730991"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.1062719"^^xsd:double.
id:66fe9b516534078e701b1008 :activityDescription """Life changes when you choose reading! 

We train volunteers from local communities to go into one of our partner primary schools to support the same few children each week to grow a love of reading. 

We have over 50 years of experience of training volunteers to find reading for pleasure. You will listen to children read, read to them, engage in book chat and help them find books they will love. 

You will be trained through small group, live, interactive group sessions and then be matched to one of our partner schools.

Once trained we offer ongoing support through an online portal, additional training sessions and you will be linked to a dedicated support rep who you can speak to if you have any questions or queries. 
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d5f5a0624f3ab9fbc763;
                            :activityTitle "Coram Beanstalk Reading Helper Role";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:66fe9b516534078e701b1009 :address "Barkerend Rd, Bradford BD3 8QX, UK";
                            :latitude "53.7981561"^^xsd:double;
