id:670e5d70a13637b8376ea8a6 :activityDescription """Do you have a love of reading? 
Could you share that love with children in a local primary school?
Can you make a weekly afternoon commitment?

If you answered yes to these questions; we need you!

Coram Beanstalk has a long standing history of training volunteers to go into local primary schools and support children to grow a love of reading. 
You will be trained how to not just listen to children read, but also how to engage them in conversation about books and how to encourage them to find books they love. 

We provide training in small, online, interactive group sessions with one of our trainers as well as providing ongoing support once you are placed in school.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d5f5a0624f3ab9fbc763;
                            :activityTitle "Coram Beanstalk: In person reading help in school";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:670e5d70a13637b8376ea8a7 :address "Tunbury Ave, Chatham ME5 9HY, UK";
                            :latitude "51.3341256"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.5222876"^^xsd:double.
id:670e9723ca6e7511e964d153 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899;
                            :organisationDescription """We're all human, yet around the world we see minority groups being discriminated, demonised, dehumanised, their rights eroded – paving the way to mass atrocities.
This isn't a new story. It's predictable. It's also preventable.
Help Prevent!""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/f5d9fe06-15a8-4984-9201-0f009aa945d5_2024-10-15T16:24:02.812Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Rights for Peace";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.rightsforpeace.org/>.
id:670e9c16ed3cdda1d69994e2 :activityDescription """The role of Finance Assistant will provide the incumbent with an opportunity to support a small charity start-up established in 2019 as it grows and learn about charity fundraising and accounting. Our income has grown from £19K in our first year and was £167,500 in 2022 with expected growth in coming years. Funding is mainly from private and institutional donors through restricted grants. During this phase we need support with accounting to, as well as specific project budgeting and accounting, making GiftAid claims and other tasks.

The Finance Assistant will work closely with the Head of Finance and the Director.

The role involves:
●	Monthly updating of the charity accounts (on XL) against bank statements, allocating receipts and expenditures to the relevant restricted grants
●	Financial reporting to donors (using their templates)
●	Supporting management and accounting of sub-grants with our partners
●	Preparing bank transfers against expenditure requests
●	Processing receipts and payments (grant invoices, refunds, donations, expenditure requests, expense claims, receipts, etc.)
●	Supporting the drafting of budgets for funding proposals ensuring accuracy, efficiencies, correct exchange rates, etc.
●	Processing GiftAid claims
●	Preparing and updating the Annual and Quarterly Budget

The incumbent would ideally have:
●	Excellent MS Excel Skills 
●	Experience in accounting or book keeping, ideally with a charity
●	Experience or interest in supporting the growth of a human rights organisation working in fragile states.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:670e9723ca6e7511e964d153;
                            :activityTitle "Finance Assistant";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:670e9c16ed3cdda1d69994e3 :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
