id:671f5738e90364cc97187f57 :activityDescription "We are looking for a volunteer book keeper to help our charity manage payments and invoices, match receipts to spend, manage petty cash and update our excel spreadsheets with credit card transactions/payments etc. Ideally the volunteer will be able to commit to 4-8 hours a week (or 2 -3 days a month) and will have qualifications and experience within finance. We need a long term volunteer as we will be giving access to banking facilities and IT systems. As we work with vulnerable young people we will also need to carry out a full DBS check. The post can be remote, hybrid, or office based. our office is in Mansfield, Nottinghamshire. ";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6426033eb9494fbbecde4e76;
                            :activityTitle "Book keeper";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:671f5738e90364cc97187f58 :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:671fa7cdf34de1578062ba7d :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription "BeScience exists to inspire, equip, and connect young people with the skills and curiosity needed to thrive in STEM fields. Our mission is to create meaningful learning experiences that bridge education and industry, encouraging sustainable innovation and a lifelong passion for science and technology.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/89bb352a-0db9-4042-989b-e8c204e480ab_2024-10-28T15:03:38.081Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "BeScience STEM";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://bescience.org.uk/>.
id:6720b4fd25befcb723b95a33 :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """Counselling in the Community was formed in 2017 by 2 counsellors working with 4 people a week. Now, we have 116 volunteers and at our busiest we see over 170 people a week from 1 of our 3 service hubs. 
Our hubs are at Waterloo Road, South Shore, Fleetwood Hospital and we have a dedicated Children and young person's centre in Bispham. 
We offer counselling to those who cannot afford to see a private therapist or can't wait to be seen by on a traditional pathway. """;
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/4e7bab9f-fd09-43e3-99b4-e25aae681bf5_2024-10-29T10:12:13.206Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Counselling in the Community";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://citc.team/>.
