id:6740a10180724d9befe4879e :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:65b83004defe4a058207b6a8;
                            :organisationDescription """We are a sports event company specialising in the game we call Tenball it is also known as football tennis amongst other names.

Our aim is to get people involved in playing sport, learning new skills, to improve health and social life through community""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/b00ae5fb-a3f3-4ea3-99b9-8eee8b8a2f3a_2024-11-22T15:19:29.050Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Tenballuk ltd";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://tenballuk.com/>.
id:6740a7c7c707ad78bf524f00 :activityDescription "At Tenball, we're passionate about community involvement and the spirit of teamwork, which is why we offer exciting volunteering opportunities to help run our sports events. Volunteers play a crucial role in bringing our vision to life, assisting with everything from event setup and equipment management to participant registration, refereeing, and even post-event cleanup. By joining our volunteer team, you'll gain hands-on experience in sports event management, develop leadership skills, and contribute directly to the health and happiness of your community. Whether you're a sports enthusiast, a community leader, or someone looking to give back, there's a place for you here. Volunteer with Tenball and be part of creating memorable experiences while promoting an active, connected, and skilled community.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6740a10180724d9befe4879e;
                            :activityTitle "Tenball Sports Event Volenteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6740a878eeb8f3659ffe3161 :address "Keele, Newcastle ST5 5BG, UK";
                            :latitude "53.0028422"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.2723725"^^xsd:double.
id:67432d79bd5d97a37146de9d :activityDescription """Role Purpose

To support the Director of Operations, Engagement and Services and the Treasurer in maintaining the financial records and managing financial administration of Mast Cell Action, ensuring accurate and timely reporting to aid decision-making and compliance with legal and regulatory obligations.

---

Key Responsibilities

- Assist with processing income and expenditure, ensuring all transactions are recorded accurately. 

- Maintain and update financial records using appropriate software or spreadsheets. 

- Support the preparation of monthly and quarterly financial reports for the charity's leadership team. 

- Collaborate with the Treasurer to prepare financial documentation for the annual audit and other statutory requirements. 

- Ensure financial records are organised and easily accessible for reporting and compliance. 

- Monitor income streams, such as donations, grants, and fundraising events, providing regular updates. 

- Assist with creating and monitoring budgets for specific projects. 

- Liaise with other volunteers and staff to ensure financial information is collected and processed efficiently. 


---


Skills and Experience

- Basic understanding of financial processes; familiarity with charity finance

- Qualified as an accountant or other relevant financial qualification

- Proficient in using spreadsheets (e.g., Excel or Google Sheets). Experience with accounting software is desirable. 

- Strong organisational skills with excellent attention to detail. 

- Good communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively in a team. 

- Commitment to the values and mission of Mast Cell Action. 
---
Reports to: Director of Operations, Engagement and Services 

Hours: Flexible, approximately 3–5 hours per week 

Location: Remote 

Role Type: Volunteer """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:65f3026f18277cf997bc34ad;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Finance Coordinator";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
