id:674e0a65db36e9109d9b6fc8 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "We are a maritime organisation, based on Naval traditions, aiming to guide children into young adults. The aim of our organisation is to give young people the best possible head start in life. Volunteers guide cadets into adulthood.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/f1bedd68-f945-4dc9-a09b-4a13533b7e63_2024-12-02T19:28:36.356Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Sutton Coldfield Sea Cadets";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.sea-cadets.org/suttoncoldfield>.
id:67582fb646ba4e08a55f0c6b :activityDescription """Position Title: Web Design and Management Volunteer
Organization: Be Epic! London International Film Festival
Location: Remote / occasional vide meetings 
Duration: [6 month - 1 year]
Time Commitment: [flexible work 2-3 h a week]

Overview
Be Epic! London International Film Festival is a dynamic and globally-focused film festival that celebrates cutting-edge cinema and creative expression. As part of our team, you'll be instrumental in shaping the digital presence of the festival by designing, developing, and maintaining the festival’s website. This is a fantastic opportunity for individuals passionate about web design, digital media, independent cinema and supporting the arts.

Key Responsibilities
Website Design and User Experience (UX)

Collaborate with the festival team to create visually engaging, user-friendly web pages. Our page is hosted and designed in Wixx.
Develop and refine the design of the festival’s website, ensuring it reflects the creative and professional standards of BELIFF.
Focus on improving website navigation, layout, and interactive elements to enhance the user experience (UX).
Optimize the website design for responsiveness on various devices (desktop, tablet, mobile).
Website Management and Content Updates

Manage the day-to-day content updates of the website, including festival schedules, film listings, ticketing information, press releases, and other relevant materials.
Work with the marketing and communications teams to integrate relevant content, such as sponsor logos, trailers, and event updates, into the site.
Ensure website content is up-to-date and accurately reflects festival activities, changes, and announcements.
Technical Support and Maintenance

Monitor the website for any technical issues and provide solutions when needed.

Optional.
Implement basic search engine optimization (SEO) best practices to improve the festival’s visibility online.
Assist with website analytics, tracking visitor behavior, and providing insights to improve web traffic and engagement.
Collaboration and Communication

Other Responsibilities:
Work closely with the marketing, content, and tech teams to ensure that the website supports the festival’s broader goals and objectives.
Participate in team meetings, offering input on design updates and sharing progress on web-related tasks.
Creative Input and Innovation

Contribute creative ideas for new features, designs, or sections of the website that could enhance the festival’s online presence.
Stay up-to-date with the latest web design trends and technologies to bring fresh, innovative ideas to the team.
Required Skills and Qualifications

Ability to work independently and meet deadlines in a remote or hybrid working environment.
Strong communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively with diverse teams.

Desirable Skills

Desire to learn and navigate web design skills.
Experience with web accessibility principles and best practices.
Experience with web animation or motion graphics.
Familiarity with integrating e-commerce or ticketing systems into websites.
Benefits of Volunteering
Gain hands-on experience in web design and management in the context of a prestigious international film festival.
Build a portfolio of work that demonstrates your design and technical skills.
Collaborate with a diverse team of passionate professionals in the film and digital media industries.
Contribute to an exciting and culturally significant event while supporting the arts.
Network with industry professionals, filmmakers, and creatives from around the world.
Be a part of the Be Epic! London International Film Festival’s digital transformation and make your mark on the festival’s online presence! Apply now to join our team as a Web Design and Management Volunteer.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425f3b8f2d4b77a6e155b67;
                            :activityTitle "Web Design and Management Volunteering Position for Be Epic! London International Film Festival";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67582fb646ba4e08a55f0c6c :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:67584a128d4c7779f2c3c5a8 :activityDescription """If you have DIY skills up your sleeve and want to put them to use then we have just the role for you!
We need a handy volunteer to help us with the general maintenance of our Charity Headquarters, which is used for hundreds of client groups every year as well as providing office space for our hardworking team.  
The role involves sourcing and fitting fixtures and fittings, putting together furniture and carrying out small cosmetic repairs.  These tasks help keep our aging building fit for purpose – so that we can continue to provide a welcoming and safe place for the local community to use.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66422f0e845341afe3f25e16;
                            :activityTitle "Maintenance Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67584a128d4c7779f2c3c5a9 :address "Grosvenor Park, Tunbridge Wells TN1 2BD";
                            :latitude "51.1372423"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.2634372"^^xsd:double.
id:6759b70cee2dbe9aa2a57471 :activityDescription """Volunteer Receptionist for the Creighton Centre

Our community centre is a very friendly space with lots of different groups and clubs meeting throughout the day.  We are looking for volunteers who would be responsible for greeting visitors to the centre, dealing with enquiries about the different projects run by The Creighton Centre and assisting with simple administrative tasks.

Full training, DBS check and support provided 

AIMS	
To greet people who come into The Creighton Centre in a welcoming and professional manner.

MAIN RESPONSIBILITIES	
To deal with all reasonable queries/issues from people coming into the building:

•	Greet all visitors
•	Advise staff and volunteers when a visitor arrives.
•	Check the availability of staff and volunteers to accept visitors.
•	Take messages for staff who are unavailable
•	For enquiries of a general nature suggest visitors take copies of project flyers. If more detailed information is needed then call a member of staff for assistance.
  
 Make sure stand where project flyers are kept is well stocked and tidy.  If more flyers  are needed inform project manager

 Keep reception and kitchen area looking clean and tidy

 Accept deliveries and inform relevant person that the delivery has been made

 If anyone mentions that tea, coffee, toilet rolls etc have run out let a member of staff know.

 For people attending groups or clubs direct them to the appropriate room or advise     them to take a seat to wait for the group to start.

 Make sure all staff, tenants and visitors sign in and out of the building

 Carry out some basic administrative duties if required

EXPERIENCE, SKILLS, QUALITIES	
•	Experience of dealing with members of the public in a professional way.
•	Ability to work in a busy environment
•	Good level of spoken English.

TIME EXPECTATION
(hours, length, flexibility)	
•	Volunteering for two hours per week minimum
•	Occasional training sessions.
•	One month probationary period required.

WORK LOCATION	
The Creighton Centre, 378 Lillie Road, London, SW6 7PH

To find out more contact:
Caecilia Isidore 
07534 647999 / 020 7385 9689 option 2
Email: cisidore@creightoncentre.org  
Website: https://www.creightonhouse.org/volunteering-creighton-centre












""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6426107cde05bf8ae7c9af41;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Receptionist ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6759b797e126ba46245c3e4a :address "378 Lillie Road, London SW6 7PH";
                            :latitude "51.4835778"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.2178703"^^xsd:double.
id:675af3d9abbd5c1269148d0d :activityDescription "We're looking for a volunteer to help the Family Support Team by identifying and suggesting suitable venues for Day of Memories. This very special event offers families a chance to remember and reflect, and to celebrate the children who have sadly lost their lives to cancer.  ";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641467dde7584a6b4d61e011;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Venue Scout";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
