id:676e815b40596eddf6974d1a :activityDescription """What will I need to do?
Our garden volunteers play a vital role in transforming our hospice grounds into a vibrant and welcoming haven where our families and children can play and make special memories. Dive into a range of exciting tasks spread across our award-winning gardens, making sure that everyone can enjoy a safe and welcoming outdoor area. Celebrate your accomplishments with a well-earned tea break with new friends. Join us and let your green thumb make a real impact!

Typical tasks the role could involve:
- Green-Fingered Guru: As the seasons change, take advantage of your skills to cultivate new plants, trim and prune small shrubs, and observe your hard work. 
- Master of Tools: Command an array of equipment—from shearers to spades and rakes—like a seasoned pro, transforming the landscape with each stroke.
- Battle of the Weeds: Battle unruly weeds, reclaiming the garden from their invasive grip and restoring order to the grounds.
- Nourish and Flourish: Care for our botanical treasures, watering and tending to their health to ensure they thrive in their lush surroundings.
- Transformative Touch: Sweep away debris and unveil the hidden beauty of our gardens, leaving behind an enchanting landscape that beckons all who pass.
- Team Triumphs: Collaborate with others in creating new layouts for new plant additions or preparing for an event. Teamwork makes the dream work! 

Will it suit me?
If you have a knack for hands-on tasks, a passion for the great outdoors, and a keen eye for garden upkeep and landscaping, then joining our gardening team is your perfect match! Embrace the opportunity to work as part of a dedicated team, turning our outdoor spaces into beautiful, thriving environments. Let your skills and enthusiasm make a difference!

When would I need to volunteer?
Either Monday or Wednesday, minimum of 2 hours between 9am-2pm. 
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641c74843741438d369e212e;
                            :activityTitle "Gardening Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:676e82dfe7151b701f2cd80b :address "Lark Rise, Loughborough LE11 2HS";
                            :latitude "52.7465907"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.216143"^^xsd:double.
id:6778feec86e5a4747ba894c6 :activityDescription """We are looking for a new designated safeguarding lead & deputy safeguarding lead to take over the safeguarding roles at Pawsitive Squad CIC. Please note these are voluntary & remote roles. The time required will vary depending upon concerns at any time. 



We are a small non profit organisation which provides dog centred services for disabled children and adults. 



Responsibilities will include:

Creating and commiting resources to safeguarding actions and issues.
Supporting and directing staff & volunteers on safeguarding matters.
Taking lead responsibility for safeguarding and child protection (including online safety) within Pawsitive Squad CIC.
Being available for all staff & volunteers to discuss any safeguarding issues or concerns.
Ensuring that all staff and volunteers are aware of the DSL and deputy contact details.
Ensuring that cases of suspected or actual child protection or safeguarding concerns are referred to the appropriate agencies.
Attending bi-monthly team meeting virtually.

We are ideally looking for someone with at least 1 year of experience in a voluntary safeguarding role (voluntary or paid) or who has completed some formal safeguarding training - this is desirable but not vital. If you haven't already completed the training please do apply if you are willing to attend a safeguarding lead training course before taking on the role. 

This role is subject to DBS checks and 2 references.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425f5bbf2d4b77a6e158f1b;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Safeguarding Lead and Deputy safeguarding lead";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6778feec86e5a4747ba894c7 :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:678000831b9eeb19831a7e04 :activityDescription """Do you have a love of reading? 
Could you share that love with children in a local primary school?
Can you make a weekly afternoon commitment?

If you answered yes to these questions; we need you!

Coram Beanstalk has a long standing history of training volunteers to go into local primary schools and support children to grow a love of reading. 
You will be trained how to not just listen to children read, but also how to engage them in conversation about books and how to encourage them to find books they love. 

We provide training in small, online, interactive group sessions with one of our trainers as well as providing ongoing support once you are placed in school.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d5f5a0624f3ab9fbc763;
                            :activityTitle "Coram Beanstalk: In person reading help in school";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:678000831b9eeb19831a7e05 :address "Leigh St, Leigh WN7 4TP, UK";
                            :latitude "53.4987177"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.5411912"^^xsd:double.
