id:67866d3963f1bedc10067ca4 :activityDescription """Update data (times/locations/bus routes) in a Publisher file to help 100s of Coventry older people each year to find a suitable local support / social group. This can be completed as a corporate volunteering day by individuals.

Good Neighbours Coventry's Activity Guides are used by 100s of older people each year to find a suitable local group. We have 10 Activity Guides (CV1-CV6, men, women, dementia, bereavement groups) which are printed out for older people who can't use the internet, to choose & access groups near them.

Social groups are constantly opening, closing & changing, so these Activity Guides need to be kept up to date.

This role involves using Publisher to update an Activity Guide with the latest group data (which will have been collected for you). You need to have an eye for details - both to make sure each page is accurate, and that it's neat (e.g. fonts are the same, maps are not wonky). You will also need to research bus routes using Google Maps, and take suitable screenshots of the map to insert into the Activity Guide.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64133c00f55a359b1f6936a3;
                            :activityTitle "Use Publisher to update older people's social groups leaflet";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6786d6718ba9164aee2bd538 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "Shanti Bhavan is a boarding school exclusively for children born into India's lowest socioeconomic class. We provide high-quality education from pre-kindergarten through 12th grade, and then through college, to help break the generational cycle of poverty. Our commitment to each and every child is from the first day of school to the first day of work.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/ad7fa736-e685-45b6-8452-c829175ee942_2025-01-14T21:26:06.646Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Shanti Bhavan Children's Project";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.shantibhavanchildren.org/volunteer/>.
id:6786e0cddcd3c77ae9815560 :activityDescription """Shanti Bhavan’s volunteers help break the cycle of poverty by contributing to our children’s world-class education. Volunteering at Shanti Bhavan is an experience unlike any other. Your work as a volunteer at our school will be challenging, culturally enriching, and life-changing.
Shanti Bhavan provides all volunteers with free on-campus accommodations and meals. Read our volunteer FAQ for more information on the volunteer experience.

We accept volunteers based on the application cycle below. Your application may list prospective dates, and we can discuss specifics throughout the interview process. Volunteer placements will be determined by program needs and space availability at our two campuses.

Volunteer Application Timeline 
We offer three volunteer terms throughout the year — Fall, Spring, and Summer. Applications received after a deadline may be considered on a space-available basis. Please visit our website for details. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6786d6718ba9164aee2bd538;
                            :activityTitle "Break the Cycle of Poverty: Volunteer Teach In India.";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
