id:6788db2ef530251625b6647f :activityDescription "We require volunteers to support us on the days the foodbank is open to the public. We need people to help us serve those using the foodbanks on the days it is open - Tuesdays and Thursdays. You would be sorting food items, packing them and handing out food parcels to residents as they come in. You would be supporting by validating their foodbank vouchers and ensuring they are able to use the foodbank without issues. ";
                            :activityOrganisation id:664c7216a8d2b072637b948f;
                            :activityTitle "Colindale Foodbank ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6788db2ef530251625b66480 :address "Avion Crescent, London NW9 5QY";
                            :latitude "51.6010953"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.2390547"^^xsd:double.
id:6788e0778f0288901120e578 :activityDescription """Are you thinking about volunteering, but can’t decide which role is best for you?

Do you like meeting people? Are you a good listener? Maybe you’re a fantastic organiser or someone who loves to get stuck into admin? We’ve got volunteering opportunities for everyone. Do you have time to spare? Then you could volunteer with us. Whether you can volunteer for a couple of days each week, month or year we have a role to suit you. We need people with a wide variety of skills and experience and embrace diversity, offering a welcoming and inclusive environment for all our volunteers.

Our ‘Introduction to Volunteering’ sessions run regularly, for approximately one hour, and provide the opportunity for you to meet the volunteer team and find out more about volunteering opportunities. 

Upcoming sessions:
Tuesday 21 October 2025 6pm
Wednesday 19 November 2025 2pm
Wednesday 7 January 2026 2pm
Thursday 19 February 2026 6pm
Tuesday 31 March 2026 10.30am
Wednesday 6 May 2026 6pm
Wednesday 3 June 2026 2pm

Please book your place at this event here:  https://www.pah.org.uk/volunteer-roles/introduction-to-volunteering/  """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d5fca0624f3ab9fbc83b;
                            :activityTitle "Introduction to Volunteering";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6789268ffe50a6db6b101041 :activityDescription """Chatterbox Befrienders offer one-to-one telephone support and will call a client once a week offering companionship and a listening ear for an individual who might otherwise go unheard. Chatterbox volunteers befriend a variety of people including carers, socially isolated individuals who are struggling with loneliness, people with ill health and those that 
have been bereaved.

THIS ROLE COULD BE FOR YOU IF:
- Would like to make a real difference in someone’s life
- Want to challenge loneliness and can commit to a weekly phone call
- Are a good listener
- Are empathetic, patient and of a caring nature
- Have good verbal and inter-personal communication skills
- Recognise the importance of confidentiality and can uphold this in practice
- Are committed to inclusion and treating people with dignity and respect

REQUIREMENTS OF A BEFRIENDER INCLUDE:
- Calling your client once a week for a chat of up to 45 minutes; this is a 26 week initial commitment, at the end of which each client’s needs are reviewed
- Completing an online call log record promptly after each phone call
- Ensuring immediate contact with the Chatterbox Coordinators if you feel that the client might be a risk to themselves or others
- Liaising with the Chatterbox Coordinator on a regular basis regarding the service, as well as discussing personal learning and development needs
- Respecting service standards, appropriate boundaries and recognising the range of policies and procedures that impact on befriending vulnerable adults

BENEFITS OF THE ROLE MAY INCLUDE:
- Knowing you are making a difference to someone’s life
- Joining the Omega Team who are taking action against loneliness and isolation
- An opportunity to enhance your CV or learn new skills
- An opportunity to engage with your community

SUPPORT AND TRAINING PROVIDED:
- Omega Chatterbox induction program
- Safeguarding training
- Ongoing support from Chatterbox Coordinators for all questions, concerns, and support
- Out of pocket expenses are reimbursed and a mobile phone can be provided if appropriate
- Monthly Befriender group support meetings via the Zoom app

LOCATION OF THE ROLE:
- Home-based

WHEN ARE YOU NEEDED:
- Provided on enquiry

A Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check is required for this role. If you have a criminal record this does not automatically prevent you from being considered as an Omega Chatterbox Befriender. We will take into account the nature of the offence, when it happened and whether it is relevant to the voluntary role. If you are shortlisted, this will be discussed with you during the recruitment process.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66b32cf2774a29bc1fb44ef7;
                            :activityTitle "Chatterbox Volunteer Telephone Befriender";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:678950631d28fa5987e397ce :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Read Easy Bristol is one of some 80 other groups affiliated to Read Easy UK

We offer free, one-to-one coaching to adults who want to learn to read via our trained volunteer Reading Coaches. Our goal is for all adults in the UK to have the reading skills they need to fulfil their potential and live life to the full.  

There are 2.4 million adults in England alone – over 7% of the working age population – who can barely read or cannot read at all. For people who come for help with us it is a life changing experience. See https://readeasy.org.uk/success-stories/





""";
                            :organisationName "Read Easy Bristol";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://readeasy.org.uk/>.
id:678f7e887c84aa2c9ba98617 :activityDescription """The Journal of West Studies and its sister organisation the think tank, Centre for West Studies are seeking a volunteer to assist with publicity on social media. These politically non-aligned organisations are opening a space to research and discuss the West in a free and open manner. 

- Experience, if only personal rather than organisational, will be valued but is not essential. 
- A strong interest in publicity, press relations and/or social media promotion will be necessary but training in aspects of this work can be provided. 
- Experience or interest in film-making and YouTube and other platform programming could prove useful for this role, too. 

Role:

Assist with social media publicity for both organizations.
Promote our work and events on various platforms.
Engage with our audience and expand our reach.

What We Offer:

A chance to be part of a dynamic and thought-provoking community.
Opportunities for training and skill development.
A platform to showcase your creativity and ideas.
A reference & experience to enhance your CV
Contribute to impactful projects that have a global reach.
Gain valuable experience in the context of academic research and journalism.
Flexible remote work environment.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66f1b5c088a121b149c2dda4;
                            :activityTitle "Social Media Publicist";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:6790e2b0fb3104315a31fb22 :address "Princess Alice Hospice, West End Lane, Esher";
                            :latitude "51.36713870000001"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.3766358"^^xsd:double.
id:67924f3726514ba9aebb240c :activityDescription """Do you have a passion for AI and its transformative potential in academic research and journalism? Are you skilled in leveraging AI to support the creation of databases, bibliographies, and collaborations with authors? If so, JWS (The Journal of West Studies) has an exciting volunteer opportunity for you!

Who We Are: JWS is a partially open access journal that unites academics with interests in the history, heritage, and contemporary issues of the West. Our mission is to provide a platform for scholarly discussions and to address the wide range of activities and problems the West is involved in.

Role Overview: As a Volunteer AI Specialist, you will play a critical role in advancing our research and journalistic efforts for as little as 2 - 4 hours per week. This is a unique opportunity to contribute to meaningful projects and help shape the future of scholarly communication.  

Key Responsibilities:

Utilise AI tools to support the research process and enhance academic databases.

Liaise with authors and researchers to gather and organise relevant information.

Assist in creating AI-driven methodologies to improve the accuracy and efficiency of our research projects.


Skills:

Experience with AI tools, not necessarily in academic research and journalism.

Analytical and problem-solving skills.

Communication and collaboration abilities.


Benefits:

A great reference & experience to enhance your CV

Contribute to impactful projects that have a global reach.

Gain valuable experience working with AI in the context of academic research and journalism.

Collaborate with a passionate and diverse team of professionals.

Flexible remote work environment.


Join us in advancing the field of academic research and journalism through the power of AI!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66f1b5c088a121b149c2dda4;
                            :activityTitle "AI Specialist";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
