id:6798ef25bd417971ef936603 :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """BEfriend is a registered charity (no 1072538) established in 1994, providing one-to-one volunteer befriending to support socially isolated people in the west London boroughs of Ealing and Hounslow.

We work with local volunteers who give their time to connect with people who may otherwise go for weeks on end without having a conversation with anyone.

We believe that simple human connection can make a huge difference to physical and mental wellbeing.
 """;
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/8fed9a2f-b135-4099-b237-21efde1cf115_2025-01-28T14:52:20.835Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "BEfriend";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://befriend.london/>.
id:6798f8fab0bd4e5878e0c291 :activityDescription """Our Linked Minds Befriending Project supports people who are socially isolated in Ealing and Hounslow due to a diagnosed mental health problem.

This is an opportunity to become a Befriender.

On successful completion of excellent mental health training, the Befriender is matched with someone suitable, by a Co-ordinator who then acts as a (non-clinical) supervisor for the befriending period, which is limited to a year. (Where applicable, this can count towards continuous professional development).

Befriender, client and supervisor make a plan together with a goal to work towards, and the Befriender makes a weekly 1-2 hour visit to the client's home, where they might stay in and chat over a cup of tea, go out for a walk together, visit a café or undertake a local activity. 

These visits make such a difference for the client, increasing their confidence and helping them explore and work towards getting a job, joining a club, meeting other people or whatever their goal may be.

The aim is that, by the end of the year, clients feel better about themselves, more valued, resilient, empowered, more linked to their community and better equipped for their journeys in recovery.

But volunteering with BEfriend not only enriches the lives of those who are isolated, it also offers immense personal rewards.

As a Befriender, you’ll get to know inspirational people with fascinating stories, develop new skills and be part of a supportive team that values compassion and connection.

For more information, visit https://befriend.london/volunteer
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6798ef25bd417971ef936603;
                            :activityTitle "Befriender – Mental Health";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6798f9c5e692d58f05c59678 :address "Bath Rd, Hounslow TW3 3EB, UK";
