id:67a3764bb264d55f76ce3165 :activityDescription """Why you should join Newquay Foodbank:
Newquay Foodbank was founded in 2011 by the community and we work to distribute emergency food and essential items to people in Newquay, and surrounding areas, who are facing a financial crisis. We are a volunteer led organisation and rely on the skills that people from outside our organisation can bring. We are committed to ensuring that we have a sustainable operation both financially and by volunteer support and we must ensure our profile is raised in the community. 

This is a newly developing team and an exciting time to join us if you like to shape the future. By volunteering as a Press Officer, you will be responsible for engaging with the media to raise the profile of Newquay Foodbank, all while making a real difference to people’s lives providing vital help and support at a time when they need it most.

What you will be doing (including but not limited to):
• Developing a PR plan, alongside the Communications Lead, for Newquay Foodbank
• Preparing and send press releases for significant foodbank events to raise the profile of Newquay Foodbank
• Engaging with and building a network of contacts for local and regional media press outlets e.g. print, radio
and tv

The skills you need:
• Excellent written communication skills
• Experience of writing press releases and generating communications materials
• Ability to build relationships with media outlets and individuals
• Organised and able to complete tasks accurately with good attention to detail
• Ability to listen and engage with people from a diverse range of backgrounds and experiences
• Ability to get on with others and be part of a team as well as completing tasks independently
• A willingness to learn about our organisation and our place within the Trussell Trust and align to our
campaigns""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:673f751424929b6d293417d8;
                            :activityTitle "Press Officer - Newquay Foodbank";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67a3764bb264d55f76ce3166 :address "From Home";
