                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:67a7604af7b54fbdf6c61683 :activityDescription """Young Lives vs Cancer Fundraising Groups are special. Across the UK each year they run huge themed events, carol concerts, regular local bucket collections, raffles and stalls at fetes. The list goes on and on and the possibilities are endless.  

Groups organise their own activities and events with the support of a Young Lives vs Cancer Fundraising Engagement Manager. By joining, or creating a group you’ll be able to put your passion and creativity into a positive outlet and achieve some incredible things, personally and for Young Lives vs Cancer. 

Each group has a leader, a banker and members. We ask that each group run at least two events per year, with the support of our expert fundraisers. 

Whether you’d like to join an existing group in your area or create a group of your own, please apply and our team will be in touch to chat ideas! 

You need to be 18 or over to take part in this role.

At Young Lives vs Cancer, we recognise that opportunities for too many people remain a condition of their race, class, sex, disability, sexual orientation – or a combination. This has never been acceptable to us as an organisation. At Young Lives vs Cancer, we do not just accept difference — we value it, we celebrate it, we nurture it, and we thrive off it. 

We positively welcome your application irrespective of your background. We are on a journey, and if you join us, you will be part of a community that is committed make a difference to the lives of children and young people with cancer. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ceeaa0624f3ab9fb35fd;
                            :activityTitle "Join or Start a Voluntary Fundraising Group";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67a76adc83da3f24e4d696cf :activityDescription """Snapping pictures of special moments at events is so important to our volunteers and those taking part in the events. They’ve put so much into their training and having pictures of those moments will last a lifetime.

If you are an amateur, hobbyist, or professional photographer and want to join #TeamYoungLives then getting involved with one of our events might be the perfect opportunity for you.

The photos you create will be fully credited to you, shared with event participants and they may go on to be used in future advertising campaigns.

We do ask that you have your own equipment and we’ll make sure you have all of the support you need, including our brand guidance for photographs.

To apply to be a photographer at one of the events near you, please apply and one of our team will be in touch.

You need to be 18 or over to take part in this role.

At Young Lives vs Cancer, we recognise that opportunities for too many people remain a condition of their race, class, sex, disability, sexual orientation – or a combination. This has never been acceptable to us as an organisation. At Young Lives vs Cancer, we do not just accept difference — we value it, we celebrate it, we nurture it, and we thrive off it. 

We positively welcome your application irrespective of your background. We are on a journey, and if you join us, you will be part of a community that is committed make a difference to the lives of children and young people with cancer. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ceeaa0624f3ab9fb35fd;
                            :activityTitle "Photographer - all abilities welcome";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
