                            :longitude "-0.08574219999999999"^^xsd:double.
id:67ab7db550c7312ca908e5e9 :activityDescription """At Careers Carousel, students will hear from a range of business volunteers and learn about five different sectors. Volunteers will prepare a 45 minute presentation and interactive activity to introduce their sector and inspire the students to learn more. The activity will encourage the students to practise key transferable skills.

No experience is necessary and training will be provided - the only requirement is enthusiasm for working with young people. Where possible we will pair volunteers to deliver together - please let us know if you would not be happy delivering alone.

Once your attendance has been confirmed it is important you are commit to volunteering, as last-minute drop outs affect the quality of the programme and the experience of the young people we support.

Lunch and refreshments are also provided.

Volunteers can reach out to us on volunteer@inspire-ebp.org.uk!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425fe9cf2d4b77a6e167265;
                            :activityTitle "William Ellis School Y8 Careers Carousel";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67ab7db550c7312ca908e5ea :address "Highgate Road, London";
                            :latitude "51.5564279"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.1463202"^^xsd:double.
id:67ab7e54be1fbafc25d89bc5 :activityDescription """At Options Day, Year 8 students will hear from a range of business/education volunteers and learn about  different sectors. Volunteers will prepare a 45 minute presentation and interactive activity to introduce either university, further education/apprenticeships or a career sector. 

No experience is necessary and training will be provided - the only requirement is enthusiasm for working with young people. Where possible we will pair volunteers to deliver together - please let us know if you would not be happy delivering alone.

Once your attendance has been confirmed it is important you are commit to volunteering, as last-minute drop outs affect the quality of the programme and the experience of the young people we support.

Lunch and refreshments are also provided.

Volunteers can reach out to us on volunteer@inspire-ebp.org.uk!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425fe9cf2d4b77a6e167265;
                            :activityTitle "Plashet School Y8 Options Day";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
