id:67b1cdd72303737bef35f103 :activityDescription """Location: Remote
Commitment: Flexible, approximately 3-5 hours per week
Reports to: Faye Burgess, Community Support Coordinator

 

Role Summary:

Mast Cell Action is looking for a dedicated and detail-oriented Volunteer Newsletter Coordinator to manage our weekly newsletter for our Friends community. This role involves planning, compiling, and distributing engaging content that informs and supports our audience. The coordinator may also oversee additional newsletters for other key groups within Mast Cell Action. Full training will be provided with ongoing support.

 

Key Responsibilities:

Newsletter Management: Plan, source, and compile content for the weekly Friends newsletter, ensuring it is engaging, well-structured, and aligned with Mast Cell Action’s brand and tone.
Collaboration & Engagement: Work with internal teams to gather updates, distribute newsletters via email marketing platforms, and review audience feedback to improve engagement.
Expansion & Coordination: Support or manage additional newsletters as needed, maintaining consistency in messaging and formatting.
 

Skills & Experience:

Strong written communication and editing skills.
Experience with email marketing platforms (preferred but not essential).
Ability to organise content and manage deadlines.
Attention to detail and an understanding of audience engagement.
Passion for supporting people with MCAS and aligned with Mast Cell Action’s mission.
 

Outcomes

Community Engagement & Support

Deliver a well-structured, engaging weekly newsletter to keep our Friends community informed and connected.
Improve audience interaction by refining content based on feedback and analytics.
Consistent & Effective Communication

Ensure newsletters align with Mast Cell Action’s brand, tone, and messaging.
Collaborate with internal teams to share timely and relevant updates.
Growth & Development

Support or coordinate additional newsletters to reach wider audiences.
Enhance overall communication strategies through improved content and engagement.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65f3026f18277cf997bc34ad;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Digital Communications Coordinator";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67b1cdd72303737bef35f104 :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:67b31a71ee53864df7831b11 :activityDescription """What will you be doing?

Key Responsibilities:

Grant/Bid Writing:
Research and identify grant opportunities from government agencies, foundations, corporations, and other sources.
Write compelling grant proposals and bids that effectively communicate BKMs goals, programs, and impact to potential funders.
Collaborate with program staff to gather relevant data, statistics, and success stories to support grant proposals and bids.
Ensure timely submission of grant applications and bids, adhering to all requirements and deadlines.
Donor Stewardship:
Cultivate and maintain relationships with current and prospective donors, sponsors, and funding partners.
Acknowledge and recognise donors' contributions through personalised communications, thank-you letters, and donor recognition events.
Provide regular updates and reports to donors on the impact of their support and how their contributions are making a difference.
Collaboration and Coordination:
Collaborate with internal stakeholders, including program staff, finance team, and executive leadership, to align fundraising efforts with organisational priorities and goals.
Coordinate with external partners, consultants, and vendors as needed to support fundraising activities and initiatives.
Stay informed about trends, best practices, and regulations related to fundraising, grant writing, and philanthropy.

What are we looking for?

BKM is seeking a passionate and experienced Fundraising and Grant/Bid Writing Coordinator to join our team. The ideal candidate will be responsible for developing and implementing fundraising strategies, identifying funding opportunities, and writing grant proposals and bids to secure financial support for our organisation’s initiatives.

What difference will you make?

As Grant/Bid Writing Coordinator for BKM, you will have a profound impact on our organisation’s ability to fulfil its mission.

Through your strategic fundraising efforts and persuasive grant/bid writing skills, you will:

Secure Financial Support: Your ability to develop and execute comprehensive fundraising strategies will ensure that BKM has the financial resources needed to sustain and expand our programs, events, and initiatives.
Expand Programs and Services: With your expertise in identifying and securing grant opportunities, you will enable BKM to access additional funding sources to expand our programs and services. By writing compelling grant proposals and bids, you will successfully secure grants that support the development of new initiatives, the expansion of existing programs, and the implementation of innovative approaches.
Increase Awareness and Engagement: Your fundraising campaigns, events, and activities will raise awareness about BKMs mission and impact, engaging donors and supporters in our cause.
Commitment required:

Our roles are flexible and remote. For this role, we believe a commitment of at least 6 months is essential. 

Recruitment process:

Volunteers are asked to provide CV and a covering letter explaining their suitability for the role.

We welcome applications from individuals with diverse backgrounds and experiences who are passionate about supporting our cause. If you do not meet all of the criteria but are eager to learn, please reach out!
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6426134dde05bf8ae7ca09ec;
                            :activityTitle "Fundraising and Grant/Bid Writing Coordinator";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67b31c6793a3faa5247390bd :address "From Home";
