                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:67b4a2f913d2255f72866e6b :activityDescription """Volunteer Opportunity: Help Children Master Literacy with Real Action

Do you have 2-3 hours to spare on Saturdays? Are you a confident reader?
If so, you can make a real difference in the lives of children from diverse, disadvantaged backgrounds by helping them develop essential literacy skills through a structured, effective, and enjoyable reading programme.

Who We Are
Real Action is a London-based educational charity dedicated to transforming the lives of children through literacy. For over 25 years, our flagship Butterfly Programme has empowered children aged 5-12—from diverse backgrounds—to swiftly master reading, writing, and comprehension. The results? A lifelong love for learning and a pathway to higher education!

Why Volunteer With Us?
•	No prior teaching experience needed – just a passion for sharing your knowledge with others!
•	Gain valuable experience working with children in a classroom setting.
•	Make a tangible impact on young lives.
•	Build transferable skills useful for careers in education, social work, and community engagement

Your Role as a Volunteer
You’ll help children master literacy using our fast-acting phonics-based method. Depending on your comfort level, you can:
•	Start as a classroom assistant before taking on a more active lead role.
•	Work with small groups or individual students, guiding them through reading, writing, and comprehension exercises.
•	Support in managing classroom behaviours
•	Offering extra guidance and personalized support to children who might be struggling with reading, writing, or comprehension.

Location & Commitment
📍 Venture Community Association, 103a Wornington Rd, London W10 5YB 
OR
📍 The Learning Store, 3 Mozart St, London, W10 4LA
 
📅 Saturdays (term-time only), 10:00 AM – 12:00 PM

Make a Difference Today!
By volunteering with us, you will help bridge the literacy gap, providing children with the tools they need to succeed in school and beyond. Many of our students go on to university, thanks to the strong foundation they build in our programme.
If you're passionate about education and eager to inspire young minds, we would love to hear from you!

This opportunity is open to all skill levels, and no prior teaching experience is required. However, the following qualities would make you a great fit:
✅ Good communication skills – Ability to engage and support young learners.
✅ Patience and enthusiasm – A willingness to encourage and motivate children.
✅ A strong grasp of reading and literacy – You should feel comfortable helping children with phonics, reading, and comprehension.
✅ Reliability and commitment – Volunteers should be able to commit to at least two hours on Saturdays during term time.
✅ A passion for education and community work – A desire to make a real difference in the lives of children.

Applications to volunteer can be submitted through this link:
https://www.realaction.org.uk/pages/30-work-with-us 



""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6426107cde05bf8ae7c9af41;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer English Teaching Assistants for Real Action";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
