id:67d85419bfe2761c494ee20f :activityDescription """Started in 2011 by Central London Samaritans, Facing the Future is a program that offers support for people bereaved by suicide through free of charge online peer support groups across the UK and Ireland.

The branch is looking for a support volunteer to assist in the recruitment, communication with and coordination of applicants of the role of Facing the Future Facilitator, which at present is only open to current Samaritans listening volunteers.

Working mostly from home, with some infrequent in person meetings at our branch building in Marylebone with dates agreed ahead of time, the successful candidate will demonstrate good communication skills, an ability to work independently and ideally possess a background in administrative roles and knowledge of typical tools such as Office Suite and Outlook. 

An interest in the work of Samaritans and supporting those suffering grief and bereavement would also be very much sought after.  

Please apply through the platform if interested in order to receive the full role profile and further details.

Thank you. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:64132e2747ee134e99d35360;
                            :activityTitle "Facing the Future Recruitment Intern ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67d854bb65be084157ee59a8 :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:67d883e5c2667d5a2920e5a1 :activityDescription """Volunteer Position: Content Creator

Location: Remote or London-based (optional office collaboration)

Commitment: Flexible (Minimum 4 hours per week)



About Linguist Point



Linguist Point is a community interest company dedicated to breaking down language barriers in the UK. We provide professional interpreting and translation services for both the public and private sectors, ensuring communication is accessible for everyone.



Role Overview



We are seeking a creative and passionate Content Creator to join our team on a voluntary basis. This is an exciting opportunity for someone looking to build their portfolio, gain experience in the language services industry, and make a meaningful impact.



Key Responsibilities:

• Create engaging and informative content for our social media platforms (LinkedIn, Instagram, Facebook, Twitter, Pinterest, TikTok).

• Write compelling blog articles and website content related to interpreting, translation, and language accessibility.

• Design eye-catching visuals, infographics, and videos using Canva or Adobe tools.

• Assist in developing storytelling-based marketing campaigns to increase brand awareness.

• Repurpose existing content into different formats (e.g., turning a blog post into social media posts).

• Research industry trends and optimise content for SEO.

• Collaborate with the marketing team to improve audience engagement and lead generation.



What We’re Looking For:

• A strong passion for content creation, writing, and digital marketing.

• Experience in social media management, copywriting, or graphic design is a plus.

• Familiarity with tools like Canva, Adobe Photoshop, WordPress, or video editing software is beneficial.

• Knowledge of SEO, content marketing, or social media analytics is a bonus.

• Ability to work independently while meeting deadlines.



What’s in It for You?

• Gain hands-on experience in digital marketing and content creation.

• Build a strong portfolio to showcase your skills.

• Opportunity to network with industry professionals in the language services field.

• A chance to make a real impact in promoting language inclusivity.

• Reference letter and recommendation upon successful completion of the role.



How to Apply



If you’re interested in this volunteer role, please send your CV, portfolio (if available), and a short cover letter explaining why you’d be a great fit to info@linguistpoint.co.uk or Website: https://linguistpoint.co.uk/
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cce8a0624f3ab9fafdd4;
                            :activityTitle "Content creator";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67d8852d22cd572b0bbd75ee :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:67d955980ee84c60376db906 :activityDescription """🔹 What You’ll Do:

✅ Create engaging designs for social media, marketing materials, and campaigns
✅ Develop visually appealing branding assets
✅ Work closely with our team to enhance our digital presence
✅ Support a community-driven cause through impactful design

🔹 What We’re Looking For:

🎨 Proficiency in Canva, Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, or similar tools
💡 A creative and innovative mindset with a keen eye for detail
🌎 Passionate about language access, diversity, and inclusion
📅 Availability to contribute remotely a few hours per week

🔹 What You’ll Get:

🚀 Hands-on experience to build your portfolio
🌍 The chance to contribute to a meaningful community cause
🤝 Work alongside an inspiring and supportive team
📢 Recognition for your skills and contributions

💡 This is a volunteer role (unpaid) and can be done remotely. If you want to make an impact through design, we’d love to hear from you!

📩 Apply now! DM us or email info@linguistpoint.co.uk to get involved.

#VolunteerOpportunity #GraphicDesign #LinguistPoint #CreativeForACause #CommunityImpact #MakeADifference""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cce8a0624f3ab9fafdd4;
                            :activityTitle "🎨 Volunteer Opportunity: Graphic Design Volunteer at Linguist Point! 🌍✨";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67d955980ee84c60376db907 :address "From Home";
