id:67e671a7975b7d775bad26e3 :activityDescription """Working as a member of the Family Services team, you’ll be offering information, guidance and support to families and loved ones of those in prison.

Based in the prisons visitor's centre meeting and greeting visitors, you will provide practical and emotional support to families ensuring they are treated with dignity and respect and their voices are heard.

As well as supporting in the visitor's centre, you will also be required to support Pact's play and children’s services, including our family days, as well as our refreshment service in the prison visits hall.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64260874def19e4770803295;
                            :activityTitle "Family Services Volunteer ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67e671ef86df571a76a25271 :address "Bovingdon, Hemel Hempstead HP3 0NZ, UK";
                            :latitude "51.72486319999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.5412707999999999"^^xsd:double.
id:67e872ff43dc542a4bd7c771 :activityDescription """About the Role:

We are seeking compassionate and dedicated Volunteer Counsellors to provide emotional support and guidance to individuals in need. This role is ideal for those passionate about mental well-being and looking to make a meaningful difference in their community.

Key Responsibilities:

Provide one-on-one or group counselling support to individuals facing emotional or mental health challenges.
Listen actively and offer a safe, non-judgmental space for clients to share their concerns.
Use appropriate therapeutic techniques to support and empower individuals.
Maintain confidentiality and adhere to ethical counselling guidelines.
Work collaboratively with other volunteers and professionals to ensure the best outcomes for clients.
Keep accurate and confidential session records, following organizational policies.
Signpost individuals to additional support services where necessary.

Requirements:

Background in counselling, psychology, mental health, or a related field.
Relevant qualifications (or currently training towards one).
Strong active listening, empathy, and communication skills.
Ability to maintain boundaries and work within ethical guidelines.
A non-judgmental and supportive approach.
Experience working with diverse individuals and communities is a plus.
Membership with a professional body (e.g., BACP, UKCP, or equivalent) is desirable but not essential.

What We Offer:

A rewarding opportunity to make a difference in people's lives.
Experience in a supportive counselling environment.
A chance to develop counselling skills and gain practical experience.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65ce23f8fc240c9dd603de87;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Counsellor";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67e872ff43dc542a4bd7c772 :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:67e8742043dc542a4bd7ca72 :activityDescription """About the Role:

As a Volunteer Tender Writer, you will play a crucial role in researching, writing, and submitting high-quality funding applications. Your work will directly contribute to securing financial support, enabling Several Seats to expand its programs and reach more people.

Key Responsibilities:

Identify and research suitable funding opportunities, including grants and tenders.
Write compelling and well-structured funding applications, ensuring alignment with funder requirements.
Collaborate with the team to gather relevant information, impact data, and success stories.
Ensure applications meet submission deadlines and comply with guidelines.
Maintain a database of funding applications and track progress.
Assist in reporting on funding successes and areas for improvement.

Requirements:

Strong writing, editing, and proofreading skills.
Experience in bid writing, grant applications, or proposal writing (preferred but not essential).
Ability to research and interpret funding criteria.
Excellent attention to detail and ability to meet deadlines.
Understanding of nonprofit funding and social impact work is an advantage.
Passion for community development and social change.

What We Offer:

Experience in bid and grant writing for a purpose-driven organization.
Opportunity to develop valuable skills in fundraising and nonprofit development.
A collaborative and supportive team environment.
The chance to make a meaningful impact by helping secure funding for vital community projects.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65ce23f8fc240c9dd603de87;
                            :activityTitle "Tendor Writer (Commision post) ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67e8742043dc542a4bd7ca73 :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
