id:67ebb81ee40e13423e61b1d5 :activityDescription """Our shops help raise lots of money for us. It’s always lovely chatting to our customers about the fabulous items we sell and telling them about the fantastic work that we do. As a volunteer you will get the chance to meet new people and make friends, plus be part of an amazing team of volunteers.

On the shop floor, as well as welcoming and serving our customers with a smile, you will be using the till (don't worry, we will show you how) and handling money. When people come in to donate items you will also be completing the Gift Aid forms that let their donations help us even more. You will also be answering the telephone. The role would suit anyone with basic computer skills, and a clear phone voice.

We currently need volunteers Mondays and Saturdays all day and Wednesday afternoons.

It’s really easy to get your volunteering started, if you're over 16 years old, please apply now.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66324bcff384b9c7d01f7b92;
                            :activityTitle "Customer Service Volunteer - Eastbourne Warehouse";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67ebb89ff6223a08234469c6 :activityDescription """Our shops help raise lots of money for us. It’s always lovely chatting to our customers about the fabulous items we sell and telling them about the fantastic work that we do. As a volunteer you will get the chance to meet new people and make friends, plus be part of an amazing team of volunteers.
There’s so much for you to get stuck into when volunteering in our shops. We get lots of donations so you will be rolling up your sleeves in the back room where you will be receiving, sorting, steaming and pricing donations, it's always exciting when one of our volunteers spots a real gem. 
On the shop floor, as well as welcoming and serving our customers with a smile, you will be using the till (don't worry, we will show you how) and handling money. When people come in to donate items you will also be completing the Gift Aid forms that let their donations help us even more.
It’s really important that our window and shop displays look appealing so people keep visiting our shops, so you'll be wielding a duster and vacuum as well as your imagination to make the shop look its best.
It would be ideal if you could volunteer one shift a week, which is about four hours but we're also happy to have more flexible times. No special skills are needed as we will show you what to do and will provide all the training you need. But if you have any experience or particular interest tell us, it may come in useful. It’s really easy to get your volunteering started, if you're over 16 years old, please apply now. We currently need more volunteers, especially at weekends.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66324bcff384b9c7d01f7b92;
                            :activityTitle "Customer Service Volunteers - Hastings Shop";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67ebb915d6e4be0a93a6f062 :activityDescription """Our shops help raise lots of money for us. It’s always lovely chatting to our customers about the fabulous items we sell and telling them about the fantastic work that we do. As a volunteer you will get the chance to meet new people and make friends, plus be part of an amazing team of volunteers.
There’s so much for you to get stuck into when volunteering in our shops. We get lots of donations so you will be rolling up your sleeves in the back room where you will be receiving, sorting, steaming and pricing donations, it's always exciting when one of our volunteers spots a real gem. 
On the shop floor, as well as welcoming and serving our customers with a smile, you will be using the till (don't worry, we will show you how) and handling money. When people come in to donate items you will also be completing the Gift Aid forms that let their donations help us even more.
It’s really important that our window and shop displays look appealing so people keep visiting our shops, so you'll be wielding a duster and vacuum as well as your imagination to make the shop look its best.
It would be ideal if you could volunteer one shift a week, which is about four hours but we're also happy to have more flexible times. No special skills are needed as we will show you what to do and will provide all the training you need. But if you have any experience or particular interest tell us, it may come in useful. It’s really easy to get your volunteering started, if you're over 16 years old, please apply now.  

We are currently looking for volunteers on Wednesday and Thursday afternoons and all day Friday, Saturday and Sundays. Please get in touch if you would like to become part of our amazing Volunteer Team!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66324bcff384b9c7d01f7b92;
                            :activityTitle "Customer Service Volunteers - Lewes Shop";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67ebf6da094463dec2d9dd91 :activityDescription """Enjoy cooking? Looking for a fun way to make a difference in your community? 

Join FoodCycle as a Cooking Volunteer and help turn surplus food into delicious, three-course meals for your local community!

You’ll get involved in everything from prepping ingredients and cooking to coming up with recipe ideas and tidying up at the end. No experience? No problem! Our friendly FoodCycle Leaders will guide you through the session, making sure everything runs smoothly.

Why volunteer with FoodCycle?
- Make an impact – Help provide free, nutritious meals for those who need them.
- Learn new skills – Whether you're a kitchen pro or a total beginner, there’s always something to pick up.
- Meet great people – Be part of a welcoming, supportive team and connect with your local community.
- Flexible volunteering – No minimum commitment, just join when you can! Each cooking session lasts around four hours.

About FoodCycle:
FoodCycle is a national charity running 100+ community meals every week. We use food that would otherwise go to waste to create free, nutritious meals for anyone who needs them. But it’s more than just a meal—it’s a chance to chat, make friends, and feel part of your community.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65d604686123f8876966688d;
                            :activityTitle "FoodCycle Cooking Volunteer - help us cook community meals (North England)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
