id:67ecf532be2c93e354387dcd :activityDescription """Enjoy cooking? Looking for a fun way to make a difference in your community? 

Join FoodCycle as a Cooking Volunteer and help turn surplus food into delicious, three-course meals for your local community!

You’ll get involved in everything from prepping ingredients and cooking to coming up with recipe ideas and tidying up at the end. No experience? No problem! Our friendly FoodCycle Leaders will guide you through the session, making sure everything runs smoothly.

Why volunteer with FoodCycle?
- Make an impact – Help provide free, nutritious meals for those who need them.
- Learn new skills – Whether you're a kitchen pro or a total beginner, there’s always something to pick up.
- Meet great people – Be part of a welcoming, supportive team and connect with your local community.
- Flexible volunteering – No minimum commitment, just join when you can! Each cooking session lasts around four hours.

About FoodCycle:
FoodCycle is a national charity running 100+ community meals every week. We use food that would otherwise go to waste to create free, nutritious meals for anyone who needs them. But it’s more than just a meal—it’s a chance to chat, make friends, and feel part of your community.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65d604686123f8876966688d;
                            :activityTitle "FoodCycle Cooking Volunteer - help us cook community meals (North England)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:67ecf532be2c93e354387dce :address "Minstead Gardens, London SW15 4EB, UK";
                            :latitude "51.4518895"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.2499846"^^xsd:double.
