id:6812e3ea4c17e0959b94d54b :activityDescription """RSPB Lichfield Local Group is an active group with an exciting and varied programme of local walks, field trips and indoor meetings. We are a friendly bunch, and our more experienced birdwatchers are always happy to assist those just starting out on their bird-watching journey. It’s a great place to meet like-minded people if birds and nature are already your thing or if you’d simply like to learn more.

We also support the work of the RSPB in the local community, part of which is raising funds that can be used to make a difference for birds and wildlife. We’re looking for someone good with figures and a couple of hours a week spare to take on the role of treasurer.

What would I be doing?

Monitor Group finances regularly, ensuring all income is banked and both income and expenditure is appropriately recorded.

Pay occasional invoices and expenses claims, set up any authorised payments and retain a petty cash float.

Prepare an annual financial report for presentation at the group’s AGM.

Complete the annual financial return for the group with submission to RSPB Finance by the required date and ensure the accounts are independently reviewed.

Ensure surplus funds are donated to the RSPB, while retaining enough for group operating costs.

What skills do I need?

Comfortable handling and accounting for charity money and keeping simple accounts.

Computer savvy with internet and email access.

What’s in it for me?

This is an opportunity to use your skills to make a valuable contribution towards saving nature.

You’ll meet like-minded people and make new friends.

This role can be done mostly from home, so is flexible and can fit in around other commitments.

What support is available?

You’ll be asked to attend 'Managing Finances' training workshop (online) within your first year but will also have support from a dedicated Local Group Development Officer and the RSPB Finance department.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Local Group Treasurer ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:6812e3ea4c17e0959b94d54c :address "Lichfield & District Local Group, Bore Street, Lichfield, Staffordshire, WS13 6LU, England";
                            :latitude "52.683104"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.827013"^^xsd:double.
id:68133fc59e295624dba4cb31 :activityDescription "It’s vital for an older person’s wellbeing to have access to affordable leisure and recreational facilities. As a volunteer at the Polegate Healthy Living Club, you will be a welcoming face within the Polegate Community Centre. You will get a chance to meet new people and work with an excellent team of volunteers. It’s important to us that we provide a warm, affordable, and enjoyable place for our clients and visitors to learn something new, socialise, and keep fit. The club is open Tuesdays 2pm-4pm on alternative weeks. You will have a sociable attitude, be reliable and honest, empathic, a good listener, and have a love of meeting and greeting new people and an interest in health and wellbeing. No fitness skills, qualifications or background is required and you can learn many transferable skills which is ideal for a work experience! You will be presenting passion and interest in the health and wellbeing of clients, whilst, ensuring all visitors feel welcome and valued when they visit and are supported on their fitness journey. You will also be multi-tasking by assisting with set up of classes and getting involved with general fitness and a bit of administration. You will need to be willing to maintain a good working knowledge of services and facilities provided by the club and be comfortable with assisting the lead volunteer. We will provide all the training and support that you need.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66324bcff384b9c7d01f7b92;
                            :activityTitle "Polegate Healthy Living Club";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68133fc59e295624dba4cb32 :address "Windsor Way, Polegate BN26 6QF";
                            :latitude "50.8247842"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.2455372"^^xsd:double.
id:68134d4dc3ee39768fbe7753 :activityDescription """BOSS Day is a full day programme, led by volunteers, to prepare students for upcoming work experience placements and employment opportunities by practising professional skills and behaviour. The workshops are designed to develop transferrable skills, promote professional awareness and ultimately foster students' confidence.

What happens?
You will work with a class of up to 30 Year 9 (14-15 years old) students, with a teacher in the room. We have prepared PowerPoint presentations for you to deliver to students, these sessions include: First Impressions, CV Preparation, Interview Practice and Networking. The aim of the day is for you to work with the students on the sessions provided, speak to them about your career journey and share all your experiences and knowledge on the above sessions as well as delivering the tasks on the PowerPoint with the students.

Timings
8:30am to 3:00pm (TBC)

Requirements
No experience is necessary and training will be provided - the only requirement is enthusiasm for working with young people. Where possible we will pair volunteers to deliver together - please let us know if you would not be happy delivering alone.

Once your attendance has been confirmed it is important you are commit to volunteering, as last-minute drop outs affect the quality of the programme and the experience of the young people we support.

Lunch and refreshments are also provided.

Volunteers can reach out to us on volunteer@inspire-ebp.org.uk!
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425fe9cf2d4b77a6e167265;
                            :activityTitle "Greatfields BOSS Day";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68134d4dc3ee39768fbe7754 :address "Barking IG11 7QG";
                            :latitude "51.53307909999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.0839398"^^xsd:double.
id:6814e9fba7d343e2d64a31ac :activityDescription """Do you have a love of reading? 
Could you share that love with children in a local primary school?
