id:681acce7de9e7a636c6d986a :activityDescription """The RSPB manages a big network of nature reserves which are havens for wildlife, and importantly very special places for people of all ages and abilities to visit and experience a nature rich landscape.

Nature is in trouble, there aren't many places left where wildlife can thrive, that is why we want to welcome more people to these places.

We are looking for volunteers who can help with our visitor engagement activities, welcoming people on arrival, managing our simple catering offer, and talking to our visitors about membership. 

Full training and support will be provide for this role but you do need to be a ‘people person’ and have good communication skills.

This is a really rewarding and enjoyable role. You will be working with a friendly team on a beautiful nature reserve, you will have the opportunity to make new friends and spend time outdoors. You will get to meet loads of new people in this role, enjoying conversation and helping people have a wonderful visit.

There is always the opportunity to learn new things and gain skills through volunteering, by working on a reserve, you'll naturally learn all about how nature reserves are managed and the wildlife that is found there.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Centre Welcome (Strumpshaw Fen Welcome Team Member)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:681acce7de9e7a636c6d986b :address "Strumpshaw Fen, Low Road, Strumpshaw, Norwich, Norfolk, NR13 4HS, England";
                            :latitude "52.608734"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "1.457787"^^xsd:double.
id:681cb3b6f4691bab8e66f144 :activityDescription """🎃 Liverpool Spooky Welly Walk 👻

🗓Saturday 18th October 2025
🌳Sefton Park, Liverpool, L17 1AP
🕣09:00am – 16:30pm

The Spooky Welly Walk is creeping back into Sefton Park for another fang-tastic year! 🧙‍♀️🕷️ One of Merseyside’s most boo-tiful Halloween traditions, this ghostly gathering brings thousands of families together for a day of tricks, treats, and spooky surprises. 🦇🍬

Join us if you dare... 🧛 We’re summoning all volunteers, witches, werewolves, and wizards alike to help make this year's walk the most spooktacular yet! Even if you can't commit to the full hours, let us know and we’ll conjure up a shift that works for you. 🧹💀

💼 Roles Include: 
☑Manning frightfully fun activities like the Yucky Dip and Terrifying Tattoos
☑Creepy crowd control (aka stewarding)
☑Guiding families through the haunted happenings
☑Answering questions from curious creatures and goblins

The day zooms by faster than a broomstick ride 🧹—thanks to the endless parade of costumed kiddos and their families! Expect an atmosphere charged with giggles, ghouls, and giddy excitement.

🎁 What you get in return:
☑ A glowing reference for work or school🌟
☑ A certificate to show off your hard work🙏
☑The eternal gratitude of our spooky squad 🧡

Your helping hands ensure the Spooky Welly Walk is a screaming success! So, dust off your best costume and help us make this year’s event frightfully unforgettable! 🎃🕸️
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66ebff86941fcccf03075ca6;
                            :activityTitle "Spooky Welly Walk Family Event Volunteer ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:681cb3b6f4691bab8e66f145 :address "Sefton Park Road, Liverpool";
                            :latitude "53.38910240000001"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.9494691"^^xsd:double.
id:681d6fe949cf8a2c2d530584 :activityDescription """Do you enjoy meeting new people and spending time in beautiful surroundings? We are looking for people who can enjoy engaging with our visitors and help them to make the most out of their visit. 

Opportunity Details

Arne is such a beautiful, special place that we want our visitors to enjoy it too. We want them to have the best day possible when they visit and are looking for volunteers who can help them make the most of their visit.

You don't need to be an expert - it's more about showing them where they can get the best views of the amazing wildlife that lives here , or pointing them in the direction of the cafe  for a cup of tea or showing them the optics which could enhance their visit.
As one of our welcome volunteers you will undertake the following tasks 
 
- provide a friendly face wherever you are volunteering that day , out on the reserves, in a hide, or at the information hub by the shop,
- having conversations with our visitors and finding out how you can help them enjoy their visit and support the sales of optics at the shop
-helping with our events and activities
-talking to the public about the work of the RSPB
-being a guide in a hide using RSPB optics
- ensuring our information hub is kept clean and tidy

We are looking for volunteers who can help with all our visitor engagement activities, from speaking to Visitors when the arrive at the Information hub , to  leading events and activities and supporting optic sales through demonstrating the use of binoculars. Our events and activities are aimed at all age ranges from families, new to nature and those who are already nature lovers.  We have several large events in a year including Pull a Pine and Wild Sleep outs 

You can choose a half day or full day shift to fit around your commitments but we do expect as a minimum 2 booked shifts a month and currently we primarily need volunteers on a  or Saturday., Sunday and Wednesday.
This role will really suit you if you are a people person and can adapt your style to a diverse range of visitors and activities..
This is a really rewarding and enjoyable role and brings the following benefits;
-Working with a friendly team on a special nature reserve and spending  time outdoors in beautiful surroundings
-Meeting lots of people and enjoying conversations that make the most from their visit
-Being part of a Team and making new friends
-The opportunity to learn new things and gain skills through volunteering and learning about how nature reserves are managed and the wildlife, flora and fauna that are found there

-

Full training and support will be provided for this role and  everyone after initial training must attend an Induction session with our Senior Management team the first of which will take place  on Friday 11th July.

You  do need the following skills and experience: 


- You must be a ‘people person’, who enjoys meeting new people and is a confident communicator.  

- An ability to adapt your communication style to be able to talk to a diverse mix of visitors including families with children.
- Attention to detail.

-must be flexible and willing to do anything that management needs doing on any particular day 

- Organisational skills, to help ensure events and activities are carried out safely. 

This is a really rewarding and enjoyable role. You will be working with a friendly team on a beautiful nature reserve, you will have the opportunity to make new friends and spend time outdoors. You will get to meet loads of new people in this role, enjoying conversation and helping people have a wonderful visit. 

There is always the opportunity to learn new things and gain skills through volunteering, by working on a reserve, you will naturally learn all about how nature reserves are managed and the wildlife that is found there. 

Please note that we will be responding to any applications after 27 May.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Engagement Family and Children Events (RSPB Arne Dorset)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:681d6fe949cf8a2c2d530585 :address "Arne, Arne Road, Wareham, Dorset, BH20 5BJ, England";
                            :latitude "50.690273"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.042511"^^xsd:double.
id:681d6fea49cf8a2c2d5305a9 :activityDescription """The RSPB manages a big network of nature reserves which are havens for wildlife, and importantly very special places for people of all ages and abilities to visit and experience a nature rich landscape.

Nature is in trouble, there aren't many places left where wildlife can thrive, that is why we want to welcome more people to these places.

We are looking for volunteers who can help to support our membership recruiters at the arrival point. This will involve greeting visitors, checking membership cards, taking payments, hiring all terrain mobility scooters and directing visitors to our Information area and supporting car park management.

Full training and support will be provide for this role but you do need to be a ‘people person’ and have good communication skills.

This is a really rewarding and enjoyable role. You will be working with a friendly team on a beautiful nature reserve, you will have the opportunity to make new friends and spend time outdoors. You will get to meet loads of new people in this role, enjoying conversation and helping people have a wonderful visit.

There is always the opportunity to learn new things and gain skills through volunteering, by working on a reserve, you'll naturally learn all about how nature reserves are managed and the wildlife that is found there.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Centre Welcome (Membership Support)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:681d6fea49cf8a2c2d5305aa :address "Arne, Arne Road, Wareham, Dorset, BH20 5BJ, England";
                            :latitude "50.690273"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.042511"^^xsd:double.
id:681de4af987013b848509a05 :activityDescription """Volunteering at Memory Walk is an incredible experience. You and hundreds of others across the country will help us to run 12 inspiring walks that raise vital funds, providing help and hope to people affected by dementia.

Memory Walk simply couldn't happen without the incredible support of our volunteers.

Liverpool Memory Walk takes place at Aintree Racecourse, Ormskirk Road, Aintree, Liverpool, L9 5AS.

You can find out more about Liverpool Memory Walk here: https://www.alzheimers.org.uk/get-involved/events-and-fundraising/join-event/memory-walk/liverpool-memory-walk

You can find out more about volunteering at Memory Walk here: https://www.alzheimers.org.uk/get-involved/events-and-fundraising/join-event/memory-walk/volunteer
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65cb8060481c82abdf3842c6;
                            :activityTitle "Liverpool Memory Walk";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
