id:682a9ee595d3d213c8fed531 :activityDescription """Would you like to connect to your inner frog, fancy being a dinosaur or soaring about as a kestrel?

We are looking for enthusiastic people to puppeteer our giant illuminated wildlife sculptures at RSPB Old Moor’s WildLights Lantern Trail events and community events.  The puppets are a fantastic way to engage with the public, tell people about Old Moor Nature Reserve and have great fun.  To see the puppets in action head to the video section of our Facebook page: RSPB Old Moor | Facebook.
 You could have puppeteering skills already or come with bags of enthusiasm and willingness to learn/ give it a go!

We also have our Creative People role, which involves creating the illuminated puppets and leading lantern making workshops.  https://volunteer.rspb.org.uk/opportunities/44357-event-helper-creative-people-2023-03-02

This role would involve occasional volunteering at events, often in the evening and at weekends but flexible to fit around your life style.  You would be in a pool of events volunteers who between them cover our events programme.
We currently do art/ lantern trails twice a year, in March and October.  You would know at least a month in advance about events, would have an event plan, and could help with planning and ideas.

Our puppets are made from willow and tissue paper, fabric and waterproof PVA and carried on a back pack.  They are fairly light for their size but puppeteering is still quite physical, so please consider this when thinking of applying.  Full training will be given in how to use each puppet, before any public appearances.

This role would be suitable for 16-18 year olds, though Safeguarding would meet young people would need to work in a group.

The RSPB is committed to making our organisation diverse and inclusive, and, as such, are keen to encourage applications from everyone, of all ethnic backgrounds, as well as those with disabilities.

We believe volunteering shouldn’t leave you out of pocket, so will reimburse travel expenses.
We look forward to hearing from you!

(Please be aware that clicking 'More about this role' below brings up a more generic event volunteer role description)""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Event Helper (Puppeteer)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:682a9ee595d3d213c8fed532 :address "Dearne Valley - Old Moor, Old Moor Lane, Wombwell, South Yorkshire, S73 0YF, England";
                            :latitude "53.515519"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.364673"^^xsd:double.
id:682a9ee695d3d213c8fed556 :activityDescription """Are you creative, enthusiastic and love wildlife? We're looking for creative volunteers to design and make artwork for our WildLights Lantern Trail events, illuminated art trails which celebrate the wildlife and nature living in the Dearne Valley.
You could have willow sculpture making skills already or come with bags of enthusiasm and willingness to learn/ give it a go!

In the Creative Volunteer role, you might:

Help lead craft workshops for families/ at community groups

Design and create sculptures/ costumes/ pieces for art for events

Could help on the day, puppeteering sculptures or running crafts

Share your ideas for crafts/ artwork during events

Interact with visitors of all ages

The creative team meets twice a week (Weds and Sunday afternoons) to make artwork throughout the year and also volunteer at events. 
 How often you volunteer and when is up to you, and flexible around your other commitments, you might come every week, or just occasionally for events, or even get creative at home, taking materials from the site and staying in touch via the WhatsApp group.

This role would be suitable for 16-18 year olds and families (adults and children volunteering together).

The RSPB is committed to making our organisation diverse and inclusive, and, as such, are keen to encourage applications from everyone, of all ethnic backgrounds, as well as those with disabilities.
We believe volunteering shouldn’t leave you out of pocket, so will reimburse travel expenses.
We look forward to hearing from you!

(Please be aware that clicking 'More about this role' below brings up a more generic event volunteer role description)""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Event Helper (Creative People!)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
