                            :longitude "-4.1426565"^^xsd:double.
id:6836c9641e2e9ce639a3dcdc :activityDescription """📣 Mitie Colleagues—It’s Time to Go Back to School!

We’re thrilled to launch our Back to School Volunteering Campaign, a fantastic opportunity to make a lasting impact on the lives of young people in our communities. Whether you’ve volunteered before or are just getting started, there’s a role for everyone. 👧🏽👦🏾

💼 How You Can Get Involved:
Career Insight Days – Share your career journey and inspire the next generation.
School Challenge Days – Support students in developing teamwork, creativity, and problem-solving skills.
Campus Clean-ups – Help create safe, welcoming environments for learning.
Mentoring – Offer guidance and encouragement to students navigating their future.
School Kit Assembly – Help pack essential supplies for students in need.
📝 Already Volunteering?
If you’re already involved in any of these activities, don’t forget to log your hours on the Do-It platform. Every hour counts and helps us track the collective impact we’re making.

🤝 Want to Get Started?
If you’re interested but unsure where to begin, we’re here to help! Reach out to us at GivingBack@mitie.com and we’ll guide you through the options.

📬 Stay Connected
Keep an eye on MiNET and the Foundation newsletters for:

Inspiring volunteer stories
Campaign updates
Shout-outs to our amazing colleagues
Let’s come together to support education, build confidence, and open doors for young people
#BackToSchool #MitieVolunteers #PlanThrive #SocialValue #InspireTheNextGeneration""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65b7befedcc4366de5311230;
                            :activityTitle "🎒 Back to School: Inspire the Next Generation- Log your hours";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6836da88a15b60849ec243f2 :activityDescription """We’re looking for a volunteer Web Developer to help us redesign and reimagine our website and you’ll have a blank canvas to play with. This is a rare opportunity to shape the online presence of a mission-led organisation from the ground up.

What you'll do:

Redesign and restructure our current website
Make the site mobile-friendly, accessible, and engaging
Add new features such as blog pages, donation buttons, or contact forms
Work closely with our founder to bring the brand and mission to life online

What you’ll bring:

Experience with CMS platforms (e.g. WordPress, Webflow, Wix)
Basic HTML/CSS skills (or strong experience with no-code tools)
A collaborative, creative mindset and enthusiasm for our purpose
Proven experience building High Quality Landing pages
Experience with Mobile would be great
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66f4314f49ced32a707c085f;
                            :activityTitle "Web Developer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
