id:683fb6e32f40186884f4b1de :activityDescription """Want to make a real difference in Nature and people’s lives? Join our Belfast Window on Wildlife Reserve as a Volunteer Coordinator – Visitor Experience!

If you are a people person with a passion for wildlife and community, this is your chance to help shape unforgettable experiences for our visitors and support an incredible team of volunteers who make it all happen. Be at the heart of something meaningful – where nature and people thrive together. 

**Why we want you**

Our volunteers are the lifeblood of what we do. As our Volunteer Coordinator, you’ll help build a happy, motivated and well supported volunteer team that brings our Belfast Window on Wildlife Reserve to life. We are looking for someone that believes in the power of people, thrives in a team environment, and wants to help others feel valued and inspired while surrounded by nature. 

**What you will be doing**

- Managing the volunteer rota and ensuring everyone knows where they’re needed
- Organising volunteer training and induction sessions
- Helping to create induction packs for new starters
- Welcoming and inducting new volunteers so they feel supported from day one
- Being a friendly face on site a few days each week
- Communicating with the team through newsletters and updates 
- Helping to organise volunteer taster days and social events
- Working closely with the team to ensure volunteers feel heard, happy and recognised
- Supporting the team in enhancing the visitor experience 


**The Skills you will need**

You don’t need to be an expert – we’ll provide all the training! But you’ll be a great fit if you:

- Are warm, confident communicator who enjoys working with people
- Are organised and good at juggling multiple tasks 
- Love helping others grow and feel supported
- Are passionate about nature, conservation, and the community
- Can give a few days a week at the reserve to stay connected with the team 

**What’s in it for you**

Volunteering in this role is a great opportunity to:

- Be part of a passionate, friendly, and supportive team
- Gain hands-on experience in volunteer coordination and visitor engagement 
- Develop skills in leadership, communication, event planning and more
- Receive full training and ongoing support from RSPB NI staff
- Make a lasting impact on both people and wildlife in your local community
- Enjoy time in a beautiful natural setting

**Ready to take the next step?**

If you’re excited to help create a welcoming, positive environment for our volunteers and visitors – and want to be a part of something bigger – we’d love to hear from you. 
Apply now and start your journey as a Volunteer Coordinator at our Belfast Window on Wildlife Reserve!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Coordinator (Visitor Experience)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:683fb6e32f40186884f4b1df :address "Belfast's Window on Wildlife, 100 Airport Road West, Belfast, County Down, BT3 9ED, Northern Ireland";
                            :latitude "54.627811"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-5.873535"^^xsd:double.
id:684023ac16f329fe129c702c :activityDescription """Put your crafting skills to use and become an Art Group Volunteer at our fun social Thursday group!

We are looking for a ‘people person’ to assist at this weekly group: being a welcoming and encouraging presence; helping the facilitator to set up activities, and being alongside our clients while they learn new skills and have a go at different art and craft techniques.

You don’t need to be an expert – just enthusiastic to ‘have a go’ and a willingness to be creative.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66422f0e845341afe3f25e16;
                            :activityTitle "Social Art Group Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:684023ac16f329fe129c702d :address "2a Grosvenor Park, Tunbridge Wells";
                            :latitude "51.13700110000001"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.2627424"^^xsd:double.
id:684059665d271835a2253c9d :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899;
                            :organisationDescription """Under One Sky (UOS) is a volunteer-led initiative which supports people living on the streets of London through friendship, compassion, and the distribution of essential supplies. 

Founded in 2012 by Mikkel Juel Iversen and a small group of friends, the organisation has since grown organically to a community of more than 1,000 volunteers. By Winter 2019, we had reached more than 4,000 homeless people through our street outreach events called “Skywalks”. At the centre of Under One Sky’s work is the power of human connection.

In April 2020, in direct response to the Covid-19 crisis, our emergency volunteer teams, along with partner organisations, began going out in Central London every day, delivering hot food and drinks to the rough sleepers who had been left behind.

By the end of 2021 we’d served our homeless friends meals/clothing close to 100,000 times as part of this operation. With every interaction, a conversation, and a silent message of ' you have not been forgotten’.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/0c44bd8d-63bf-42b0-b4eb-0233c3414651_2025-06-04T14:34:12.497Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Under One Sky CIO";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://underoneskytogether.com/>.
id:68410893b4891b466c67eab1 :activityDescription """We are looking for volunteers to join our new weekend work party. RSPB nature reserves are special places for people and wildlife and we rely on volunteers to keeps these habitats thriving and in good shape. 

It might seem like these wild places have always just been there. But quite often we have to work really hard to maintain habitats to be in the best condition for wildlife. We have lost a lot of wild landscapes, so the small places that we do have, need a bit of extra care.  

As a Reserve Work Party Volunteer you will be joining a regular practical work party team to undertake practical habitat management tasks, including but not limited to: 
- Cutting and clearing vegetation.
- Maintaining and managing tools and equipment. 
- Creating and maintaining visitor infrastructure, such as paths and benches. 

If you enjoy being outdoors, meeting new people and hands on conservation work, then this role could be the perfect opportunity for you. This role does involve a reasonable amount of physical activity, so will enable you to keep your fitness levels high, as well as helping your mental health and wellbeing. You will have the satisfaction of knowing that you are making a genuine contribution to nature conservation, and you might find it rewarding to safeguard nature in the area you are working to protect. 

We are a friendly and supportive team. If you are volunteering to learn new skills and gain knowledge about wildlife conservation work, you will find that our team will be more than happy to help you on that journey.

The group meets every other Saturday morning for a few hours so is perfect for anyone looking to get out on reserve to do some work that aren't available in the week.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Practical Reserve Work (Rainham Marshes - Purfleet)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68410893b4891b466c67eab2 :address "Rainham Marshes, New Tank Hill Road, Purfleet, Essex, RM19 1SZ, England";
                            :latitude "51.486792"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.227471"^^xsd:double.
id:6841930e32ccfcea9fa33b8d :address "Esher KT10 8NA";
                            :latitude "51.36712929999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.3766291"^^xsd:double.
id:684259e6668ea80932fdb4eb :activityDescription """*Please scroll down for English*

Eisiau gwneud gwahaniaeth? Ydych chi eisiau llenwi ychydig o amser sbâr neu ddysgu sgiliau newydd a hefo diddordeb ym myd natur? Dewch i ymuno â'n tîm Manwerthu gwych yn [RSPB Conwy](https://www.rspb.org.uk/days-out/reserves/conwy)!!! 
Byddwch yn cael cwrdd â llawer o wahanol bobl a chael profiad mewn lleoliad manwerthu prysur. Byddai’r cyfle hwn yn berffaith ar gyfer CV, newid gyrfa neu her newydd!

Rydym yn chwilio am wirfoddolwyr cyfeillgar i helpu yn ein siop Gwarchodfa Natur [RSPB Conwy](https://www.rspb.org.uk/days-out/reserves/conwy) ar **prynhawn dydd Mawrth, prynhawn dydd Mercher, bore dydd Iau, prynhawn dydd Gwener a bore dydd Sul.**

**Beth sydd ynddo i chi?** Os ymunwch â'n tîm manwerthu, gallech ddisgwyl profiad gwirfoddoli amrywiol. Bydd eich rôl yn cynnwys: 

-  Gwisg a bathodyn enw RSPB.
-  Cyflwyniad am y RSPB.
-  Gellir ad-dalu costau teithio (hyd at radiws o 25 milltir).
-  Helpu i wasanaethu cwsmeriaid.
-  Hyfforddiant ar ddefnyddio'r holl offer yn ddiogel.
-  Bod yn wybodus am gynhyrchion a chynigion.
-  Stacio silffoedd.
-  Gwneud ein siop yn lle cyfeillgar i ymweld â hi.
-  Ateb ymholiadau cyffredinol.
-  Bod yn rhan o dîm cyfeillgar a chydweithredol.
-  Bydd hyfforddiant a chefnogaeth yn cael eu darparu.

Am ragor o wybodaeth, gwnewch gais isod neu e-bostiwch Meg, ein Cydlynydd Gwirfoddolwyr Manwerthu
E-bostiwch meg.ellisforrest@rspb.org.uk  
I ddarllen y disgrifiad rôl cyflawn, cliciwch ar 'mwy am y rôl hon' / **'more about this role'** isod.

---
  
Want to make a difference? Are you looking to fill some spare time or learn new skills & have an interest in nature? Then come join our fabulous Retail team at [RSPB Conwy](https://www.rspb.org.uk/days-out/reserves/conwy)!!! 

You’ll get to meet lots of different people & gain experience in a busy retail setting. This opportunity would be perfect for a CV, a change of career or a new challenge!

We are looking for friendly volunteers to help in our [RSPB Conwy](https://www.rspb.org.uk/days-out/reserves/conwy) Nature Reserve shop on a **Tuesday afternoon, Wednesday afternoon, Thursday morning, Friday afternoon and Sunday Mornings.**

**What’s in it for you?**
If you join our retail team, you could expect a varied volunteering experience. Your role will include: 

-  An RSPB uniform and name badge.
-  An induction about the RSPB.
-  Travel expenses can be reimbursed (up to a 25-mile radius).
-  Helping serve customers.
-  Training in the safe use of all equipment.
-  Being informative about products and offers.
-  stocking shelves.
-  Making our shop a friendly place to visit.
-  Answering general enquiries.
-  Being part of a friendly and co-operative team.
-  Training and support will be provided.

For more information apply below or email Meg our Retail Volunteer Coordinator
Email meg.ellisforrest@rspb.org.uk  

To read the complete role description, please click on '**more about this role**' right here below.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Retail Volunteer (Gwirfoddolwr Manwerthu (RSPB Conwy) / Retail Volunteer (RSPB Conwy)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:684259e6668ea80932fdb4ec :address "Conwy, Llandudno Junction, Caernarfonshire, LL31 9XZ, Wales";
                            :latitude "53.279348"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-3.805548"^^xsd:double.
id:684259e7668ea80932fdb510 :activityDescription """Why We Want You:
We are looking for enthusiastic residential volunteers to join our team, based at West Sedgemoor, for 6-12 months. RSPB Sedgemoor Reserves are special places with important habitats, including flower rich grassland and woodland. One of our priority habitats is lowland wet grassland which provides a home for a range of wetland species including lapwing, redshank, curlew, snipe and a variety of other species declining outside reserves.

We are looking for enthusiastic people to join the team, managing the internationally important Somerset levels reserves. You will play an essential part in delivering the reserve work programme and implementing the reserve management plan so that the reserve is managed to its full potential. You will undertake habitat management work on lowland wet-grassland and deciduous woodland.

 

What’s In It For You:
During your stay, you will become a full time integral member of the reserve management team. You will contribute to practical conservation work and learn about running and managing West Sedgemoor, Swell Wood and Greylake Reserves. Our residential volunteers have an excellent record at finding future employment in conservation and improving their skills and employability.

The work can vary from one day to the next, you may be looking after livestock, coppicing, hedge laying, repairing fences or carrying out other maintenance tasks depending on the time of year. Residential volunteers also assist with habitat and species management, research, survey and monitoring, estate management, species protection and engaging with visitors and assisting with guided walks.

Full training will be provided as appropriate and depending on the season may include work with, ATV, 4WD, tractors and livestock handling.

This is an excellent chance to make a genuine contribution to wildlife conservation and get on the ladder towards a career in conservation. You will gain a valuable insight into the workings of Europe's largest conservation charity.

Requirements:
Minimum age 18. We need someone who has an enthusiastic and friendly personality and is a good team player a keen interest in nature and conservation is also essential. An ability to work outside in all weathers and undertake strenuous manual labour, as work can be physically demanding especially in winter.

Driving licence essential.

Ornithological experience is an advantage though not essential.

The role is 7.5 hours with a 5 day working week. There may be some weekend working but time off in lieu is given.


Notes:
Accommodation (including bills) provided.

Appropriate training will be provided and pre-agreed expenses will be re-imbursed where necessary.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Residential on Reserve (More than 4 weeks) (Sedgemoor Reserves)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:684259e7668ea80932fdb511 :address "West Sedgemoor, Red Hill, Curry Rivel, Langport, Somerset, TA10 0PH, England";
