id:684aa9569ebddafce2efdb2a :activityDescription """We are currently looking for another volunteer to support our Serendipity Community Group in Eastleigh.

We need organised and passionate individuals who want to support and facilitate Community Groups for autistic adults in their local community. Our groups are designed to help autistic adults to meet in a welcoming and non-judgmental setting. We need friendly and caring volunteers to make this happen.

What you will be doing?

- Welcome new members to the group and help them settle in.
- Support members to participate in group activities.
- Help make suggestions about new group activities.
- Help send feedback about the group to Autism Hampshire staff.
- Keep an accurate record of attendance at the group.
- Report any concerns to Autism Hampshire staff.

The Eastleigh Serendipity Community Group runs twice a month on Fridays from 3pm to 5pm.

Full training for the role will be provided with regular quarterly training sessions.

Whilst we value regular commitment, you will be joining a team, so you do not need to be available for every session. Please make your availability known to Autism Hampshire staff when registering your interest.

Skills
- Interest in supporting autistic adults
- Good listener
- Reliable
- Can offer support in a non-judgmental way""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:667bd02c24b1dda7ed2c0e4b;
                            :activityTitle "Community Group Volunteer - Eastleigh";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:684aa9569ebddafce2efdb2b :address "Eastleigh";
                            :latitude "50.967182"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.374688"^^xsd:double.
id:684aacf68d7b986b2e4351b7 :activityDescription """We are currently looking for another volunteer to support our new running group in Portsmouth as part of our Serendipity Community Groups.

We need organised and passionate individuals who want to support and facilitate Community Groups for autistic adults in their local community. Our groups are designed to help autistic adults to meet in a welcoming and non-judgmental setting. We need friendly and caring volunteers to make this happen.

What you will be doing?

- Welcome new members to the group and help them settle in.
- Support members to participate in group activities.
- Help make suggestions about new group activities.
- Help send feedback about the group to Autism Hampshire staff.
- Keep an accurate record of attendance at the group.
- Report any concerns to Autism Hampshire staff.

The running group runs once a month on Mondays from 11am to 12pm.

Full training for the role will be provided with regular quarterly training sessions.

Whilst we value regular commitment, you will be joining a team, so you do not need to be available for every session. Please make your availability known to Autism Hampshire staff when registering your interest.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:667bd02c24b1dda7ed2c0e4b;
                            :activityTitle "Community Group Volunteer - Running, Portsmouth";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:684aacf68d7b986b2e4351b8 :address "Mountbatten Centre, Lawrence Road, Mount Batten, Plymouth";
                            :latitude "50.35995399999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-4.1277425"^^xsd:double.
id:684c02716a94de7921af061b :activityDescription """We're looking for a passionate and creative volunteer to lead our social media marketing efforts and help us grow our presence online. As Social Media Marketing Manager, you'll develop and schedule engaging content across platforms like Instagram, X (Twitter), LinkedIn, Threads & Facebook to raise awareness about our community energy projects, inspire local involvement, and attract new supporters. You’ll help tell the story of how community-owned renewable energy is tackling the climate crisis and supporting people in your area.

You’ll work closely with a small team of volunteers or community members to shape our messaging, promote upcoming events and share successes. Whether you’re experienced in marketing or just enthusiastic about climate action and storytelling, this is a fantastic opportunity to make a meaningful impact in your community while sharpening your digital skills.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:67aa00bb8e0715d8c0eefd61;
                            :activityTitle "Social Media Marketing Manager ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:684c0be2d13c48005729926e :activityDescription """As the Finance Director, you will be responsible for monitoring the finances of our community energy group (which is a Community Benefit Society regulated by the Financial Conduct Authority), providing accurate financial forecasting, and ensuring the financial stability and sustainability of our community energy projects. This voluntary position is ideal for someone with financial qualifications and a passion for renewable energy who wants to make a meaningful impact on the transition to clean energy within our community.

This role has the aim to establish a sub-group of volunteers to help manage the work, and you will be supported by the Board of Directors and CEO.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:67aa00bb8e0715d8c0eefd61;
                            :activityTitle "Finance Director ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:684ce5e46c271e643c36e7d9 :activityDescription """Are you keen to help save nature, would like to utilise your existing office-based skills and have up to 1 day a week to spare? 

We are looking for an administrative volunteer to support the Bowland Breeding Wader Survey and take on administrative tasks to support this important survey work. Tasks include data management, GIS mapping, volunteer coordination and other general admin. By opening up our work to more volunteers in this way, it means we can scale up what we can achieve and do more for nature. 

You will be a good all round 'people person', have a keen attention to detail and great organisational skills as well as a confident user of Microsoft Word, Outlook and Excel. Training will be provided on any specialist skills, including GIS mapping and using RSPB systems. 

This is a great opportunity to utilise your existing skills and learn new ones, whilst working as part of a small, friendly team. There is room for development within the role, and opportunities to volunteer for other field-based roles.

This opportunity is based in the RSPB Lancaster office. The time commitment is 2-4 days per month, with lots of flexibility.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Administrator (Wader Survey Administrator Lancaster)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:684ce5e46c271e643c36e7da :address ", LA1 4XF, United Kingdom";
                            :latitude "54.04508"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.796814"^^xsd:double.
id:684f88e18044fc05e23fb8af :activityDescription """We are offering volunteering placements! 

Blean Woods is part of a network of woodland surrounding Canterbury that comprises one of the largest blocks of continuous woodland in Kent.

Seasalter Levels is a newly restored wetland to the west of Whitstable that will develop into a key part of an internationally important landscape of lowland wet grassland habitat across North Kent.

We are seeking individuals who are just starting out or changing to a new career in conservation. You will be volunteering 3 days a week for six months. You will have a say in your own development, and we will do our best to accommodate if there are specific areas you would like to work on. 

The main emphasis of the placement is build your practical skills as well as your ecological knowledge. This will help you work towards a career in conservation through understanding nature reserve management. You will work alongside our experienced team to create and enhance habitats for key species, including nightingales, heath fritillaries and lapwings. You will engage in practical habitat tasks such as coppicing, glade and heathland management within Blean and scrub control and hydrological management at our Seasalter reserve. 

Are you looking to start a career in conservation, keen to play your part in helping conserve nature, and have skills and knowledge you can share? If so, apply for one of our volunteer placements today.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "RSPB Volunteering Placement (Blean Woods and Seasalter Levels)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:684f88e18044fc05e23fb8b0 :address "Blean Woods, Rough Common Road, Rough Common, Upper Harbledown, Canterbury, Kent, CT2 9DD, England";
