id:686440a1fd4651daed36e262 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription "To promote resilience, perseverance and positive mental health in disadvantaged populations in the UK. We do this by: A) Awarding educational institutions grants to establish awards for students who have shown extraordinary perseverance in the face of adversity. B) Raising awareness of resilience and its impact on maintaining positive wellbeing amongst the general public.";
                            :organisationName "The Goodluck and Melville Charity".
id:686442124b9a812603acf769 :activityDescription """The volunteer will raise awareness of mental health and wellbeing through various outreach activities. These include:
•	Delivering educational talks and workshops within disadvantaged communities.
•	Conducting field research and gathering testimonials from individuals who have demonstrated resilience.
•	Assisting in the creation and dissemination of awareness campaigns through social media and community events.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:686440a1fd4651daed36e262;
                            :activityTitle "Community Engagement Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:686442124b9a812603acf76a :address "Boston PE20 2HD";
                            :latitude "52.9060864"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.08877729999999999"^^xsd:double.
id:6864a0f06f32a71c38efe1ab :activityDescription """Do you enjoy meeting new people or would like to gain catering experience? We are looking for volunteers to help run the popular and friendly café on Old Moor nature reserve in Barnsley. This role is suitable for 16-18 year olds. 

As part of our café team you will help to ensure that visitors have an enjoyable and safe visit. When people visit our café, we want them to have a warm welcome, get served quickly and enjoy their food and drinks in relaxing and clean surroundings. All this work requires a team of friendly and supportive people to help out. We simple can't run our café without volunteers. 

As part of our café team, you will be serving customers hot and cold drinks, clearing tables, talking to customers about our food and drink options and any allergens, maintaining cleanliness standards and health and safety codes of practice.   

Café team volunteers work on a rota to cover the needs of the site, this could be from a few hours a week upwards, to suit you.

As part of your role you will learn new skills and gain experience working in the hospitality industry, including great transferable skills, such as customer service, diplomacy, people engagement, following health and safety protocols. The money raised through our retail and catering contributes to nature conservation, so you are also helping to save nature!

The RSPB is committed to making our organisation diverse and inclusive, and, as such, are keen to encourage applications from everyone, of all ethnic backgrounds, as well as those with disabilities. We believe volunteering shouldn’t leave you out of pocket, so will reimburse travel expenses. We look forward to hearing from you!
(Please be aware that clicking 'More about this role' below brings up a more generic event volunteer role description)""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Café Volunteer (RSPB Old Moor)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:6864a0f06f32a71c38efe1ac :address "Dearne Valley - Old Moor, Old Moor Lane, Wombwell, South Yorkshire, S73 0YF, England";
                            :latitude "53.515519"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.364673"^^xsd:double.
id:686512f57fc0590c5f2fe5f5 :activityDescription """Across the UK, our 270 local groups play a vital part in supporting people affected by MS. They provide sense of belonging, unity and friendship. And they deliver services and support for their local MS community.

We are looking to recruit a Fundraising Volunteer for the Maidstone and District Group. As our Fundraising Volunteer you’ll support your Group Coordinator to organise local fundraising activities and events throughout the year.

In this role you’ll be able to develop your organisation, communication and team working skills.Most importantly you’ll inspire your local community to raise funds that help make sure no one has to face MS alone.

Time Commitment

We estimate this role will need around 2 hours a week. Our roles are flexible and aim to fit around you. Time commitments for this role may vary depending on your activities. This is an ongoing role.

This is a great opportunity to gain experience within a large charity and develop your existing skills and learn new ones. We need you to get involved and help make positive changes to the lives of people affected by MS.

About you

You’ll have an interest in the MS Society and the work that we do, as well as the enthusiasm to represent both us and our values locally. You will understand the needs of people affected by MS in your area and be sympathetic to the needs and motivations of volunteers. You’ll be confident using Microsoft Office, the internet and email. You’ll be able to apply disability, equality and inclusion practices and understand and apply our risk management system. Ideally you’ll understand the local area and organisations that provide local services.

You will be reliable and easy to contact and you need to live in or near the area the group to carry out this role.

Apply 

1. Read through the role description carefully

2. Please apply online

The MS Society is committed to promoting diversity. We can only offer roles to over 18s.

 """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425eae8c794380477b70969;
                            :activityTitle "Fundraising Volunteer (Maidstone and District)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:686512f57fc0590c5f2fe5f6 :address "Maidstone ME14 1TF";
                            :latitude "51.2733153"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.5220384"^^xsd:double.
id:68651316ef4c53f0ee9eddeb :activityDescription """Finance Volunteer

We’re the MS Society – a community of people living with MS, scientists, campaigners, listeners, organisers, ambassadors and fundraisers. Our volunteers are a key part of achieving our goals and their support is vital. Join us.

About this opportunity
We are looking to recruit a Finance Volunteer for our Peterborough and District Group. As a Finance Volunteer, you would be joining a coordinating team of volunteers to plan and deliver services and activities to support people locally.

You will maintain and approve income and expenditure records and explain financial information clearly to other group members. You would ensure our financial requirements and policies are followed, and that money is spent in a cost effective manner.

This is a great opportunity to gain experience with a large charity, develop your existing skills and learn new ones. We need you to get involved and help make positive changes to the lives of people affected by MS.

About you
You’ll have an interest in the MS Society and the work that we do, as well as the enthusiasm to represent both us and our values locally. You will understand the needs of people affected by MS in your area and be sympathetic to the needs and motivations of volunteers. You’ll be comfortable with figures, preferably with an accounting or business background.

Apply 

Read through the role description carefully

Please apply online

The MS Society is committed to promoting diversity. We can only offer roles to over 18s.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425eae8c794380477b70969;
                            :activityTitle "Finance Volunteer (Peterborough and District)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68651316ef4c53f0ee9eddec :address "Peterborough PE1 1HG";
                            :latitude "52.5714592"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.2420084"^^xsd:double.
id:686513657fc0590c5f2fe637 :activityDescription """Across the UK, our 270 local groups play a vital part in supporting people affected by MS. They provide sense of belonging, unity and friendship. And they deliver services and support for their local MS community.

We are looking to recruit an Activities Volunteer for the Chesterfield and District Group. As our local group Activities Volunteer you’ll help us to set up activities in the area. Whether you’re serving refreshments, talking to people, registering attendees or collecting payments, you’ll be making sure everyone feel welcome.

In this role you’ll be able to develop your organisation, communication and team working skills. Most importantly you’ll be supporting your local group to run activities that bring friendship and fun to your local MS Community.

About you

You’ll have an interest in the MS Society and the work that we do, as well as the enthusiasm to represent both us and our values locally. You will understand the needs of people affected by MS in your area and be sympathetic to the needs and motivations of volunteers. You’ll be able to apply disability, equality and inclusion practices and understand and apply our risk management system. Ideally you’ll understand the local area and organisations that provide local services.

You will be reliable and easy to contact and you need to live in or near the area the group to carry out this role.

Time Commitment

We estimate this role will need up to two hours a week. Our roles are flexible and aim to fit around you. Time commitments for this role may vary depending on your activities. This is an ongoing role.

Apply 

1. Read through the role description carefully

2. Please apply online

The MS Society is committed to promoting diversity. We can only offer roles to over 18s.

 """;
