id:686553a50eda5b2df92e512c :activityDescription """We are looking to recriut a new governor for September 2025 who is currently or recently involved in or around the Education sector so that they can bring their knowledge, understanding and experience to add to our Board of 11 governors.

The term of office is for 4 years and involves contributing to the work of the Board in terms of monitoring and overseeing the educational and financial health of the school and holding the leadership to account as well as providing strategic lead and direction for the school as it grows and develops.

The commitment is for 3 meetings per term, ideally in person (but possible online) - these take place in the evenings from 6-8pm.  Regular visits to the school during working hours to obtain an overview and understanding of it's work and functioning and for monitoring visits around an area of responsibility.  Contributing proactively to the work of the Board and keeping up to date and relevant through webinars and training etc.....""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6865504c9579ef1d1a5d4f80;
                            :activityTitle "Hoe Valley School, Woking, Surrey";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:686553a50eda5b2df92e512d :address "Egley Road, Mayford, Woking, Surrey GU22 0NH";
                            :latitude "51.2983375"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.5720689"^^xsd:double.
id:686556982c3b77860e551a37 :activityDescription """As a County Lead of North Yorkshire & Teeside you will be part of the establishment of a County St John Council to oversee and guide volunteer Community Networks aims to create a structured and supportive framework that empowers volunteers to operate more effectively and efficiently. By providing strategic leadership, coordination, and oversight, the council ensures that volunteer efforts align with community needs and priorities while avoiding duplication of services.

St John has embarked on a journey to achieve the goal of ensuring that every community and young person across the country is first aid confident.

We are looking for a leader with a passion for local volunteering and helping communities to inspire and support volunteers on this journey across your county

The post will also interact with relevant Communities of Practice to share learning, advice and best practice

Within this role, there will be focus on the fundraising element, so we would want you to be passionate about supporting, inspiring, and working with networks to develop fundraising plans and activity.

We are seeking a dynamic and motivated individual to join our team as a Fundraising & Priory Lead. This role is a job share, where the post holder will focus primarily on the Fundraising aspect. You will work collaboratively with the Community Fundraising Manager and County President to craft and execute a comprehensive fundraising plan for the County.

The closing date for this vacancy is 1st August 2025

For more information on this vacancy, please contact sam.austin1@sja.org.uk

 """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "County Fundraising & Priory Lead";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:686556982c3b77860e551a38 :address "Marton Road, Middlesbrough TS4 2EZ";
                            :latitude "54.567065"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.223342"^^xsd:double.
id:6865f27947cebec60f5a26cb :activityDescription """RSPB Watford Local Group is an active group with an exciting and varied programme of local walks, field trips and indoor meetings. We are a friendly bunch, and our more experienced birdwatchers are always happy to assist those just starting out on their bird-watching journey. It’s a great place to meet like-minded people if birds and nature are already your thing or if you’d simply like to learn more.

We also support the work of the RSPB in the local community. This includes raising funds to support conservation projects. If you're good with figures and have a few hours to spare each month, then we'd love to hear from you. 

**What would I be doing?**

Monitor Group finances regularly, ensuring all income is banked and both income and expenditure is appropriately recorded.

Pay occasional invoices and expenses claims, set up any authorised payments and retain a petty cash float.

Prepare a simple, annual financial report for presentation at the group’s AGM.

Complete a simple, annual financial report for submission to RSPB finance department.

Donate surplus funds to the RSPB, whilst retaining enough for group operating costs.

**What skills do I need?**

Comfortable handling and accounting for charity money and keeping simple accounts.

Computer savvy with internet and email access.

**What’s in it for me?**

This is an opportunity to use your skills to make a valuable contribution towards saving nature.

You’ll meet like-minded people and make new friends.

Learn more about the scope of work the RSPB delivers.

This role can be done mostly from home, so is flexible and can fit in around other commitments. However the group would prefer a candidate who can attend in-person activities.

**What support is available?**

You’ll be asked to attend 'Managing Finances' training workshop (online) within your first year but will also have support from a dedicated Local Group Development Officer and the RSPB Finance department.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Local Group Treasurer (Watford)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:6865f27947cebec60f5a26cc :address "Watford Local Group, The Stanborough Centre, St. Albans Road, Watford, Hertfordshire, WD25 9JL, England";
                            :latitude "51.6835"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.392259"^^xsd:double.
id:68663b46b0330778c15191e6 :activityDescription """No one should die because they needed first aid and didn’t get it. St John Ambulance teaches people first aid so they can be the difference between life and death, and you can help us do this.

We are seeking Event Doctors to respond and manage emergency calls/incidents at events which may include venues such as stadia, concert halls, motorsports tracks, road races etc. Event doctors shall provide specialist, clinical, social and holistic care while undertaking clinical assessment and interventions in the pre-hospital environment. This will mainly involve working in mobile treatment centres or temporary event medical centres.

Successful candidates will be registered registered medical practitioners with the GMC, without cautions or restrictions, and hold a licence to practice outside of an approved practice setting.

Availability during early July is essential - flexible approach to events throughout the year

Join St John Ambulance to provide excellent level of clinical care for people attending events across London

For more information about this role please contact amanda.pestell@sja.org.uk

The closing date for this role is: 01/08/2025""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "Event Doctor";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68663b46b0330778c15191e7 :address "Meridian Way, Norwich NR7 0TA";
                            :latitude "52.6264603"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "1.3733428"^^xsd:double.
id:68663b68ec00ea2bb86b7e05 :activityDescription """At St John Ambulance, we are looking to develop our volunteering offer and become an even more integral part of our communities through delivering community first aid and education. 

We need people who have a passion for helping others, care about their communities and want to make a difference, supporting them to become safe and more resilient by sharing your first aid skills and knowledge. As a Community First Aider, you’ll deliver first aid to those in need through local events, as well as provide education to the public so that the ripple effect of First Aid grows.

Through supporting the growth of community partnerships, you will bring people along to our cause, growing our membership and fundraising base and spreading the message that First Aid Saves Lives. 

Through volunteering as a Community First Aider, you’ll get a huge sense of satisfaction and pride delivering an essential service. It’s great for you, great for your community and great for our nation, and it requires only a small commitment of your time. 

We will make sure you will have access to a proper induction to volunteering with SJA and the training you need for the role you take on. We will also provide you with a supportive environment while you are volunteering with us. Information about our volunteer roles are included in the role descriptions. What you can expect from SJA, and what we expect from those who volunteer with us, is included in the volunteer charter.

This is an excellent opportunity for people to learn First Aid skills to give help and support to others in their community. As a Community First Aider you will help deliver First Aid for those in need and and support local events with a focus on engagement and education and be an advocate for St John through talks and demonstrations.

You will need to be in attendance at Wells at least twice a month on a Wednesday evening for training. Also, attendance on duties in the Network - these events are largely at weekends including Bank holidays.

Interviews will be held in Wells from mid July onwards, with further details confirmed with candidates. 


If you are successful you will need to undertake induction & training for role at these dates:
Welcome Event (Induction) - These will be held in Wells from mid October.
Training for role -Some on line learning with links to be provided to successful candidates. Face to face training for role will be over 2 days and likely to be weekends.

Closing date for these opportunities is: 01/09/2025

If you’d like to know more about volunteering or would just like to chat to someone who does, get in touch. Please contact our the hiring manager,Lynne Alton, via emailing: lynne.alton1@sja.org.uk

To apply for this opportunity please follow the link below:""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "Community First Aider (Bristol, Avon & Somerset)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68663b68ec00ea2bb86b7e06 :address "Charter Way, Wells BA5 2FB";
                            :latitude "51.21013110000001"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.6614486"^^xsd:double.
id:68663e37b0330778c1519346 :activityDescription """Do you have a love of reading? 
Could you share that love with children in a local primary school?
Can you make a weekly afternoon commitment?

If you answered yes to these questions; we need you!

Coram Beanstalk has a long standing history of training volunteers to go into local primary schools and support children to grow a love of reading. 
You will be trained how to not just listen to children read, but also how to engage them in conversation about books and how to encourage them to find books they love. 

We provide training in small, online, interactive group sessions with one of our trainers as well as providing ongoing support once you are placed in school.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d5f5a0624f3ab9fbc763;
                            :activityTitle "Coram Beanstalk: In person reading help in school";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68663e37b0330778c1519347 :address "Elm Rd, Higher Tranmere, Birkenhead CH42 0PH, UK";
                            :latitude "53.3786928"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-3.0253083"^^xsd:double.
