id:686667367434fd6c81c0af32 :activityDescription """We’re looking for friendly and reliable volunteers to help create a welcoming and enjoyable shopping experience for visitors at Michelham Priory House & Gardens. As a Shop Volunteer, you’ll ensure the shop is well-stocked, tidy, and inviting, helping visitors find unique gifts and souvenirs that enhance their visit.

You’ll confidently handle sales, operate the till accurately, and complete cashing-up at the end of each day. Alongside this, you’ll respond positively to visitor enquiries, providing helpful information about the shop, the site, upcoming events, and venue hire options.

No previous experience is needed – training will be provided – but you should be comfortable working in a busy environment, either independently or as part of a team. If you enjoy engaging with people and contributing to a positive visitor experience, this role offers a great opportunity to get involved in a unique heritage setting.

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64260070f2d4b77a6e16a5a5;
                            :activityTitle "Shop Volunteer at Michelham Priory House & Gardens";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:686667367434fd6c81c0af33 :address "Upper Dicker, Hailsham BN27 3QS";
                            :latitude "50.8632388"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.211089"^^xsd:double.
id:6866681002acf20bcbefef5e :activityDescription """We’re looking for friendly and enthusiastic volunteers to help create a warm, inviting atmosphere for everyone who visits Michelham Priory House & Gardens. As a Visitor Welcome Volunteer, you’ll be the first point of contact, offering a friendly greeting, providing information, and helping visitors have the best possible experience.

This role is a fantastic opportunity to meet new people, share the unique story of the Priory, and play an important part in making every visit memorable. You’ll work in shifts – morning or afternoon – and have the chance to work independently as well as part of a team.

No previous experience is necessary, and full training will be provided. If you enjoy engaging with a diverse range of visitors and have a positive, approachable attitude, this role is for you.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64260070f2d4b77a6e16a5a5;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Welcome Volunteer at Michelham Priory House & Gardens";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6866681002acf20bcbefef5f :address "Upper Dicker, Hailsham BN27 3QS";
                            :latitude "50.8632388"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.211089"^^xsd:double.
id:68666932fa4eaa25f055c78f :activityDescription """We’re seeking volunteers with practical experience in property maintenance and one or more trades such as carpentry, plumbing, electrical work, or exterior decorating. As a Maintenance Volunteer, you’ll play a key role in delivering our maintenance programme, carrying out remedial repairs, and ensuring the property is kept to a high standard.

Please note that some tasks may involve manual lifting, working at heights, confined spaces, or exposure to chemicals, so a willingness to undertake physically demanding work is important.

If you have hands-on skills, a good eye for detail, and enjoy working in a practical role that helps preserve a unique historic site, this role offers a rewarding way to contribute your expertise.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64260070f2d4b77a6e16a5a5;
                            :activityTitle "Maintenance Volunteer at Michelham Priory House & Gardens";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68666932fa4eaa25f055c790 :address "Upper Dicker, Hailsham BN27 3QS";
                            :latitude "50.8632388"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.211089"^^xsd:double.
id:68666a0802acf20bcbefefc0 :activityDescription """Do you enjoy working with children, bringing history to life, and helping others have a great day out? Join our team as a Learning Assistant Volunteer and play a key role in creating memorable learning experiences for school groups visiting Fishbourne Roman Palace & Gardens?

Step into the past and help bring Roman history to life! Fishbourne Roman Palace offers a fascinating glimpse into Romano-British life, and we’re looking for enthusiastic volunteers to support our dynamic learning programme. From hands-on workshops about Roman daily life to Latin and Ancient Greek sessions for all ages, this role is perfect for anyone passionate about education, history, and inspiring others. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:64260070f2d4b77a6e16a5a5;
                            :activityTitle "Learning Assistant Volunteer at Fishbourne Roman Palace & Gardens";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68666a0802acf20bcbefefc1 :address "Chichester PO19 3QR";
                            :latitude "50.8366257"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.8093465999999999"^^xsd:double.
id:68666b14ee34575ac544e415 :activityDescription """Join us as a Visitor Welcome Volunteer and help bring the story of Fishbourne Roman Palace to life. You’ll play a key role in creating a memorable experience for our guests – from greeting visitors and processing admissions to sharing fascinating insights about the Palace’s discovery, its stunning mosaics, and its royal resident, Tiberius Claudius Togidubnus.

You might support tours, take part in special events (even in costume!), promote our gift shop, and contribute ideas to enhance the visitor experience.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64260070f2d4b77a6e16a5a5;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Welcome Volunteer at Fishbourne Roman Palace & Gardens";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68666b14ee34575ac544e416 :address "Chichester";
                            :latitude "50.83761000000001"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.774936"^^xsd:double.
id:68666c297434fd6c81c0afde :activityDescription """Help us preserve the historic buildings and grounds of Fishbourne Roman Palace by joining our hands-on maintenance volunteer team. Whether you’re a qualified tradesperson or just have a passion for DIY, your skills will help keep this remarkable site safe, functional, and looking its best.

From general repairs and equipment upkeep to painting, decorating, and supporting the gardening team, there’s a wide variety of tasks to get involved with. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:64260070f2d4b77a6e16a5a5;
                            :activityTitle "Maintenance Volunteer at Fishbourne Roman Palace & Gardens";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68666c297434fd6c81c0afdf :address "Chichester";
                            :latitude "50.83761000000001"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.774936"^^xsd:double.
id:68666cc602acf20bcbeff052 :activityDescription """Join our friendly volunteer team and help maintain the beautiful gardens at Fishbourne Roman Palace, an essential part of our historic site. Whether you’re an experienced horticulturist or just starting out with your own garden, if you love being outdoors, getting your hands dirty, and learning new gardening skills, we’d love to have you.

As a volunteer, you’ll assist with a range of tasks from planting and pruning to helping with special garden projects.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64260070f2d4b77a6e16a5a5;
                            :activityTitle "Gardens Volunteer at Fishbourne Roman Palace & Gardens";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68666cc602acf20bcbeff053 :address "Chichester";
                            :latitude "50.83761000000001"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.774936"^^xsd:double.
id:6866896b729c9ad71d895a38 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899;
                            :organisationDescription """FareShare East Anglia operates from its base in Ipswich and covers a wide geographical area. Our mission is to prevent good food from going to waste by redistributing it to charities and community groups across East Anglia.

Starting from scratch seven years ago, we have grown rapidly and last year distributed 685 tonnes of surplus food to 141 charities members – enough to provide 1.6 million meals to the people at risk of hunger. Currently we serve Suffolk, Norfolk, Essex, Cambridgeshire. We are developing and will be shortly starting to serve Hertfordshire and Huntingdonshire.

To handle increased demand, we have recently moved to a larger premises in Ipswich where we handle fresh, frozen, chilled, and ambient food including bulk catering packs.

We operate a delivery service or if preferred collections can be made from the Ipswich warehouse.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/1dea8486-9225-4f67-994b-d9add17ffb0e_2025-07-03T13:49:58.283Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "FareShare East Anglia";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://fareshare.org.uk/fareshare-centres/east-anglia/>.
id:68668c728d4edafd8afa8b46 :activityDescription """We stop good food from going to waste and give it to people who need it. Drivers deliver food to our Community Food Members which is vital to ensuring the food gets to people who need it.

What will I be doing?

Safely driving vans to deliver and collect food
Loading and unloading food orders, planning routes and completing paperwork
Responsibly driving the van, cleaning the van, reporting any issues or accidents
Representing FareShare in a courteous and professional manner and accompanied by a Volunteer Driver’s Assistant.

What you need to be:

Hold a full driving licence with low point
Over 21 with 3 years driving experience
Confidence to drive a medium-sized van
Ability to perform physical manual handling tasks safely including loading/unloading food from the van
Ability to complete paperwork and follow directions via Sat Nav system/map
Adaptable and flexible. Managing surplus food is unpredictable and tasks vary
Positive, friendly and personable
Work well in a team and on your own
Follow health and safety policies & procedures

Why volunteer as a Driver?

Gain skills such as route planning, manual handling, organisation, teamwork and communication skills
Meet new people, be part of a team and socialise with volunteers and Community Food Members
Be physically active, keep fit and help vulnerable people in your community
Click here for more benefits from volunteering with FareShare.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6866896b729c9ad71d895a38;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Driver";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68668c728d4edafd8afa8b47 :address "4 Bermuda Road, Ipswich";
                            :latitude "52.02819359999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "1.2048896"^^xsd:double.
id:68669360c35086b1a0eac3e7 :activityDescription """Migrant Help is a leading charity that was established in 1963 and delivers a range of support and advice services to migrants across the UK. Our vision is for a global society that protects migrants, treats them with respect and enables them to reach their full potential.

The Digital Inclusion Volunteer role:

As Digital Inclusion volunteer, you will provide support to people seeking asylum in Liverpool by distributing and activating SIM cards. SIM cards are a vital resource for our clients as they help them to stay connected and up to date. It enables them to make a call to a GP service, have their solicitor’s appointment booked or stay in touch with their loved ones.

You will help us manage the flow of people who need a SIM card and make sure that everything is happening in an orderly way. You will also help with issuing the SIM cards and explaining to clients how to do it correctly.

Key responsibilities of our Digital Inclusion Volunteer:

Volunteering every week at an agreed time in Liverpool.
Closely liaising and communicating with the staff to ensure that there are enough SIM cards, and any arising issues are addressed promptly.
Manage the flow of people coming in to get SIM cards.
Support and guide clients through SIM card set up.
Help issue cards and provide our clients with information on how to top up their SIM.
Record information on SIM card distribution in line with Migrant Help’s policies and procedures.
Overall provide a patient and kind environment for people we support.
Report any health and safety or safeguarding concerns to a member of staff.
The experience and skills you need to become our Digital Inclusion Volunteer:

Complete relevant induction and training provided by Migrant Help
Undergo a criminal conviction check (DBS, PVG or AccessNI).
Commit to volunteering for a minimum of 3 months, at agreed times.
Attend volunteer support sessions as required.
Complete feedback forms when required highlighting any growth opportunities and honestly communicating what is not working well
Adhere to confidentiality and safeguarding procedures
Uphold Migrant Help’s values.
Start volunteering at an agreed time and be punctual
Complete all relevant documentation as required by volunteer coordinator
Be open and understanding of different customs, values, and beliefs
​What you are not be able to do:

Volunteer with us if you are under 18.
Exchange contact information with clients
Buy gifts, food or lend or give/receive money to/from clients
Carry out casework tasks, such as, complete benefits applications, liaise with local authorities or refer to other services or provide immigration advice
You will be an excellent candidate for this role if you:

Have spare time to undertake volunteering.
Are willing to work with diverse range of people.
Are non-judgmental and inclusive.
Have a friendly and approachable nature.
Are reliable and punctual.
Are patient.
Have empathetic listening skills.
Are a keen learner.
Are comfortable using computer or laptop for typing and sending emails, video calls.
You will benefit from volunteering with us by:

Gaining experience useful for your future CVs and cover letters.
Being able to provide a volunteering reference to your future employer or educator.
Being a part of dedicated and inclusive service. 
Developing new skills. 
Being more aware of immigration and asylum systems in the UK. 
Having reasonable expenses reimbursed. 
Having regular check ins and supervision to support your volunteering experience and growth.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6426131fde05bf8ae7ca0394;
                            :activityTitle "Digital Inclusion Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68669360c35086b1a0eac3e8 :address "39 Percy Street, Liverpool";
