                            :longitude "-2.9690037"^^xsd:double.
id:686743f1e6e9eddc94428e18 :activityDescription """We are looking for work party volunteers to join us on our reserves. RSPB nature reserves are special places for people and wildlife and we rely on volunteers to keeps these habitats thriving and in good shape. This role is suitable for under 18’s. 

It might seem like these wild places have always just been there. But quite often we have to work really hard to maintain habitats to be in the best condition for wildlife. We have lost a lot of wild landscapes, so the small places that we do have, need a bit of extra care.  

As a Reserve Work Party Volunteer you will be joining a regular practical work party team to undertake practical habitat management tasks: 
- Cutting and clearing vegetation.
- Tree planting
- Drystone walling
- Hedge laying 
- Scything
- Nest Box checks
- Helping at our community Tree Nursery 
- Habitat restoration
- Species surveys 
- Woodwork (making nest boxes and other habitat boxes)
- Fencing and repairs
- Invasive species management (e.g. Himalayan Balsam)
- Creating and maintaining visitor infrastructure, such as paths and benches. 
- Following annual work plans. 
- Following Health and Safety protocols. 

If you enjoy being outdoors, meeting new people and hands on conservation work, then this role could be the perfect opportunity for you. We have a variety of roles to ensure to keep volunteering as varied and accessible as possible.

**Tuesday Work Party 10am-3pm** - This role does involve a reasonable amount of physical activity, so will enable you to keep your fitness levels high, as well as helping your mental health and wellbeing. You will have the satisfaction of knowing that you are making a genuine contribution to nature conservation, and you might find it rewarding to safeguard nature in the area you are working to protect. 

**Friday Women's Group 10am-2pm** - This opportunity is based at our community tree nursery. It's a much slower pace, and you can come for the whole day or just an hour or so. Tasks include tree care, planting, watering, seed collection, propagation, weeding, habitat creation, hedge laying, digging and more. 

We are a friendly and supportive team. If you are volunteering to learn new skills and gain knowledge about wildlife conservation work, you will find that our team will be more than happy to help you on that journey.

Please get in touch with any enquiries vibrantvyrnwy@rspb.org.uk""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Practical Reserve Work (Lake Vyrnwy Reserve - Gwaith Ymarferol ar Warchodfa (Gwarchodfa Llyn Efernwy)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
