                            :organisationDescription "Cancer Research UK (CRUK) exists to beat cancer through world-class research, prevention, and treatment. Its mission is to save lives by preventing, controlling, and curing cancer, working towards a future where all cancers are cured. It funds research, raises awareness, and ensures discoveries benefit everyone.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/5d26183d-b348-4214-bc73-e87f14c91a25_2025-07-04T08:49:30.986Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Cancer Research UK";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/>.
id:686798ffb187924019420150 :activityDescription """Volunteer Opportunity: Join the Fun and Make a Difference!
Looking for a rewarding way to give back to your community this summer? We’re looking for enthusiastic volunteers to support two exciting events taking place at Costello Stadium, Hull on the 26th and 27th of July 2025 — and we’d love for you to be part of it!
Hull Pretty Muddy 5K – Saturday 26th July 2025
This is a fun-filled 5K obstacle course where participants climb, crawl, and slide their way through mud in support of cancer research. It’s open to all fitness levels and designed to be more about fun than speed
Volunteer roles include:
	• Obstacle/Course marshalling
	• Cheering and motivating participants
Sign up and find out more HERE: https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/get-involved/volunteer/event-volunteer-hull-pretty-muddy-26th-july-2025
Hull Race for Life 3K/5K/10K – Sunday 27th July 2025
This inclusive event welcomes people of all ages and abilities to walk, jog, or run in solidarity against cancer. It’s a powerful day of community spirit and hope — and volunteers play a vital role in making it happen.
Volunteer roles include:
	• Marshalling and route guidance
	• Welcoming and supporting participants
	• Answering queries and providing information
Sign up and find out more HERE: https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/get-involved/volunteer/event-volunteer-hull-race-for-life-27th-july-2025
Together, participants across both events aim to raise over £240,000 for cancer research. Whether you can help on one day or both, your time and energy will make a huge difference.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6867959b70ac38148a12d5e1;
                            :activityTitle "Event Volunteer - Hull Pretty Muddy and Race for Life";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
