id:686bea0164f4f390b92a2f37 :activityDescription """The Royal Parks Half Marathon is London’s original half marathon! 

Join us at our charity cheer station to represent Breakthrough T1D on race day, and give the Team Breakthrough T1D runners the best experience possible.

Cheer Station Volunteers
What will I be doing?
-	Providing support for runners taking part in the Royal Parks Half Marathon. 
-	Looking out for runners wearing Breakthrough T1D tops and pointing them out to your fellow cheerers. 
-	Cheering and helping to make our cheer station the loudest on the event route! 
-	Helping to support families of our runners who may also come and use the cheer station as a point to see their loved ones.  

Please note, this role may require you to be outside and on your feet for a long time. We will not provide any seating, but you will be welcome to take breaks when you need to.

You will be part of a cheerful and friendly team, meet like-minded people, make a real difference to our amazing runners, and have lots of fun on the day.

 No experience is necessary. We are just looking for people who are enthusiastic about supporting the charity and who aren’t afraid to get stuck in and create a fun atmosphere for our runners and their supporters. 

When do you need me?
Date: Sunday 12 October 2025
Time: Our staff will be there from 8am to set up. You can arrive any time from this point, but we ask you to be there by 10am at the latest.  
The cheer station will be packed down when it is clear that all Breakthrough T1D runners have run past. We anticipate this will be approximately 2pm. However, if you’re not able to stay for the full day, any amount of time you are able to provide is greatly appreciated.

The cheer point is a 5 minute walk from Hyde Park Corner station (Piccadilly Line). Other nearby stations are Bond Street (Jubilee, Central, Elizabeth Lines) and Edgeware Road (Hammersmith & City, Circle and District Lines). There are also plenty of local bus routes, but some of these may not be running due to road closures.

The cheer station is located in Hyde Park, near the Band Stand.
Hyde Park, London W2 2UH 

If interested in volunteering for this event, call or email:
Telephone Number: 020 3410 6084
Email: volunteering@breakthrought1d.org.uk

Website: www.breakthrought1d.org.uk 

Facebook page: https://www.facebook.com/BreakthroughT1DUK 

Twitter page: https://x.com/BT1DUK 


""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6426107cde05bf8ae7c9af41;
                            :activityTitle "Royal Parks Half Marathon Cheer Station Volunteers - Sunday 12 October 2025";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:686bea0164f4f390b92a2f38 :address "London W2 2UH";
                            :latitude "51.5079994"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.1662518"^^xsd:double.
id:686bea22e7e01b73625bdf43 :activityDescription """Youth Helper work directly with young people in St John Ambulance Badger Setts and Cadet Units. By support our Youth Leaders to deliver a sessions across our range of programmes. In this role, you'll support the learning and development of young people into the next generation of health citizens. Youth Helpers also help young people develop their confidence, teamwork skills, self-discipline, and generally encourage them to strive to be the best they can be, as well as supervise and support other adult volunteers in their team.

You’ll get a huge sense of satisfaction and pride delivering an essential service. It’s great for you, great for your community and great for our nation, and it requires only a small commitment of your time. 

 

Pursuing the role
Closing date for these opportunities is: 30th August 2025

If you’d like to know more about volunteering or would just like to chat to someone who does, get in touch. Please contact our the hiring manager, via emailing viv.moore@sja.org.uk

To apply for this opportunity please follow the link below:""";
