id:686c89eff716445fa030fde8 :activityDescription """**Description**
**You will be sharing bedrooms with other people of the same gender. You will need to tick 'willing to share' for your application to be processed.**

**Why We Want You:** This is a unique chance to be part of one of the most ambitious projects to save seabirds across the UK.

Rathlin Island has the largest seabird breeding colony in Northern Ireland, including Puffins, Razorbills, and the largest population of Guillemots across the whole of the UK and Ireland. Their future is threatened, however, by invasive non-native species, namely rats and ferrets. Last year only one in three Puffin chicks survived long enough to leave the nest.

The LIFE Raft project aims to protect these seabirds by eradicating the rats and ferrets, and this volunteering opportunity is critical to making this project a success.

Last September we placed about 6,000 bait stations across the island. These were baited with rodenticide, which were then removed and baited again with wax blocks for monitoring until April this year.  The bait stations have remained in situ and volunteers will be working as part of a wider team that check and rebait each station every two weeks.
**
What’s In It For You**
As an RSPB volunteer you’ll be part of something big – a team of amazing and dedicated people who donate their time, energy, talent and skills to help birds and other wildlife.

Rathlin is a beautiful island with a close-knit community of about 150 people. There is a hotel, a cooperatively run store, shops with local products, a pub and café, and regular yoga and film nights and other community events.

There is also lots for the wildlife enthusiast. While the seabirds are a strong draw in the spring and the summer, there are oystercatchers, eider ducks and seals all year round, and dolphins are regularly seen from the ferries and harbours.

Rathlin’s dark skies also allow for stunning views of the stars. 2024 proved to be a particularly good year for the northern lights, it’s a great time to be spending time on island.

Accommodation is provided in a hostel just half a mile from the harbour, or in an old cottage about five kilometres inland. You will be sharing a room with members of the same gender, or if you apply as a couple you can share one of the smaller rooms.

**Requirements**
Minimum age 18. Enthusiasm and ability to work both on your own initiative and as part of a team are necessities – but perhaps most importantly, you must be good with people and physically fit and active.  

Please take into account that volunteers hike over rough and varied terrain in the winter, through all weathers. It also requires lots of working with your hands in the cold, and wearing gloves is not always possible due to the nature of the work. It is physically tough but incredibly rewarding.

There are about 150 people who live on Rathlin Island and volunteers get to know people well over the course of the programme. You will be informal ambassadors for the project, even while off-duty, and it is expected that you will be respectful and considerate of the community at all times.

**Notes**
There is no charge to take part in the scheme. All accommodation and a contribution to food (sufficient to cover three meals a day) will be provided, as well as initial travel to Rathlin from anywhere in the UK or Ireland. Travel on and off the island at the weekends is not covered, and as it is dependant on the weather and ferry availability, should be undertaken only occasionally. We are not able to cover the cost of off-island accommodation or other expenses should you be unable to return due to ferry cancellations.
Volunteers will be expected to work 5-day weeks - baiting starts mid September right through until 19th December 2025, minimum stay 4 weeks""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Residential on Reserve (More than 4 weeks) (Residential on Reserve (More than 4 weeks) (LIFE Raft Fieldworker Volunteer (Rathlin)))";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:686c89eff716445fa030fde9 :address "Rathlin Island, BT54 6RT, Rathlin Island, Ballycastle, County Londonderry, BT54 6RT, United Kingdom";
                            :latitude "55.293389"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-6.197745"^^xsd:double.
id:686c89f0f716445fa030fe0d :activityDescription """We are offering volunteering placements! From practical habitat management to communications, our placements help people gain the skills and experience needed to pursue a career in conservation. You will get to meet new people and help save nature too.

We are seeking individuals who are just starting out or changing to a new career in conservation. You will be volunteering up to 3 days a week for anything from one month to a year. We will work with you to arrange a placement at a time that is convenient to you and the RSPB. You will have a say in your own development, and we will do our best to accommodate if there are specific areas you would like to work on. 

What you will be doing on your volunteer placement will depend on the specific department you are working in, such as communications, fundraising, education, ecology, habitat management and volunteering development. The specific activities will vary based on the team’s requirements, but may include research, surveying, habitat management, stakeholder communication, project participation, meeting follow-ups, volunteer support, administration, or responding to enquiries.

We aim to help you build your skills and knowledge. You will learn all about how environmental charities work, with a special focus on your chosen department/business area. You will be working as part of a wider team and will have the opportunity to work with lots of different people.

Are you looking to start a career in conservation, keen to play your part in helping conserve nature, and have skills and knowledge you can share? If so, apply for one of our volunteer placements today.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "RSPB Volunteering Placement (Frampton Marsh)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:686c89f0f716445fa030fe0e :address "Frampton Marsh, Roads Farmhouse, Frampton Roads, Frampton, Boston, Lincolnshire, PE20 1AY, England";
                            :latitude "52.931387"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.018938"^^xsd:double.
id:686c89f1f716445fa030fe32 :activityDescription """**Where**: Old Moor, South Yorkshire
**When**: July 2025
**Commitment**: 6 months

Please Note: We are actively interviewing, if you are interested in this position please apply soon

**Why We Want You**: 
Old Moor is the centre of a busy and dynamic suite of reserves in the wonderful Dearne Valley. We are comprised of 8 wetland sites, allowing us to create essential habitats in an urban area. We want to share these wetland oases with enthusiastic people who share our passion for conservation. This is a great opportunity to see how a wetland reserve works, gaining experience and qualifications to progress onto a career in conservation. 

**What’s In It For You:**
During your stay you will be a key member of the wardening team and depending on the time of you year you will be carrying out tasks such as:

• Scrub clearance

• Livestock management (including konik ponies)

• Hedgerow maintenance

• Reedbed creation/ management

• Estate maintenance

• Wildlife surveys

• Predator fence management

• Using machinery

• Volunteer management

No two days are the same! There are many more aspects to the role, including supporting our large visitor team.

During your stay, you will be living on the reserve in a beautiful stone farm house, with Old Moor as your back yard! Professional training is provided including: brushcutter, 4x4 and more. In addition to gaining extensive and varied work experience.

This a full time residential position, it can be a four day a week position if the candidate requires a part time job alongside the scheme. Overall this is an excellent chance to make a genuine contribution to a leading conservation charity as well as gaining a valuable insight into the RSPB.

**Requirements**:

• 18+

• Driving licence essential

• Enthusiasm and interest in conservation

• Ability to work with part of a diverse team

• Able to walk long distances over rough terrain/ carry out strenuous manual tasks

• Comfortable working outside in all weather conditions

Note- this role requires some weekend work and will be discussed at interview.

Please get in touch if you are interested!

For more information on this role please contact **bryony.thiedeman@rspb.org.uk**""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Residential on Reserve (More than 4 weeks) (Residential Volunteer 6 Months at RSPB Old Moor)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:686c89f1f716445fa030fe33 :address "Dearne Valley - Old Moor, Old Moor Lane, Wombwell, South Yorkshire, S73 0YF, England";
                            :latitude "53.5155"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.364672"^^xsd:double.
