id:686d37339d2852e83360e38a :activityDescription """Volunteer Driver & Driver’s Mate – Food Rescue Team 

Pentecostal City Mission Church are looking for enthusiastic, reliable, and committed individuals to join our team as Volunteer Drivers or Drivers’ Mates to help collect surplus food from local suppliers.

As part of this vital role, you will:
•Collect waste/surplus food from partner suppliers and transport it safely back to our facility
•Help load and unload food items efficiently and with care
•Work as a team to ensure timely and consistent collections
•Represent our organisation in a friendly and professional manner

What we’re looking for:
•A positive attitude and willingness to get stuck in
•Reliability and punctuality
•Good teamwork and communication skills
•A full, clean UK driving licence (Driver role only)

This is a rewarding opportunity to help reduce food waste and support your local community. Whether you're behind the wheel or lending a hand, your time and energy will make a real difference.

Volunteer Driver & Driver’s Mate – Food Rescue Team
Days/Times: Flexible shifts available (weekday and weekend mornings/afternoons)

Are you passionate about reducing food waste and supporting your local community? Join our vibrant Food Rescue Team as a Volunteer Driver or Driver’s Mate and help make a real difference!

Every day, tonnes of perfectly good food go to waste — and we’re here to stop that. We collect surplus and short-dated food from local supermarkets, wholesalers, and food producers, and redistribute it to community organisations, food banks, and individuals in need. With your help, we can rescue more food, feed more people, and reduce environmental harm.

What You’ll Do:
As a Volunteer Driver, you will:
•Drive our van to local suppliers to collect surplus food donations
•Safely load and unload food crates with support from your mate
•Follow a planned route and schedule, ensuring collections run smoothly
•Maintain a clean, tidy, and respectful vehicle and appearance
•Represent the organisation positively when interacting with suppliers and recipients

As a Volunteer Driver’s Mate, you will:
•Accompany the driver on the collection route
•Help with loading/unloading crates and sorting food
•Assist with navigation and supplier communication
•Ensure safe handling of goods and help manage food logs or forms

What We’re Looking For:
•Enthusiastic, community-minded individuals with a can-do attitude
•Reliability and punctuality are a must – our partners rely on us!
•Physically able to lift and carry crates (with support)
•A friendly and respectful approach with teammates and food partners
•Drivers must hold a full, clean UK driving licence and be confident driving a van (we provide vehicle and fuel)

What You’ll Get Out of It:
•Make a real difference in your community by reducing food waste and supporting those in need
•Free access to quality surplus food at the end of your shift
•Be part of a friendly, welcoming team and meet like-minded people
•Boost your CV with experience in logistics, teamwork, and community service
•Training and ongoing support provided – no prior experience needed!
•A genuine sense of purpose and fulfilment

This is more than a driving or lifting job – it’s about community, care, and impact. Whether you're looking to give back, gain experience, or meet new people, we’d love to hear from you.

Volunteers are required for any of the following shifts:
Mondays from 1-6pm
Tuesdays 3-7pm
Wednesdays 3-6pm
Thursdays 10-6pm
Fridays 9-12 & 3-7pm
Saturdays 10-5pm

Apply today and become a Food Rescue Hero!

Interested, please contact J Hall:
Telephone Number: 07931 430725
or
Email: jhall@pcmc.org.uk""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6426107cde05bf8ae7c9af41;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Driver & Driver’s Mate – Food Rescue Team";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
