id:686f2ce8683ed80024e04a94 :activityDescription """The RSPB manages a big network of nature reserves which are havens for wildlife, and importantly very special places for people of all ages and abilities to visit and experience a nature rich landscape.  

Nature is in trouble, there aren't many places left where wildlife can thrive, that is why we want to welcome more people to these places like Minsmere.  

We are looking for volunteers who can help with all our visitor engagement activities, from welcoming people on arrival to showing them where to find amazing wildlife! We are looking for volunteers who could help us on weekdays and especially Saturday afternoons. 

As a Minsmere Welcome Volunteer the tasks you will undertake will include some of the following: 

- Providing a friendly welcome to visitors when they arrive and making them aware of entry requirements.
- Having conversations with visitors and finding out how you can help them enjoy their visit, whether that's pointing out where the café is or which trails they might like to explore. 
- Enthusing about and pointing out  the best places to spot Minsmere's spectacular wildlife.
- Talking to the public about the work of the RSPB, what we're all about and asking them if they would like to become members if the conversation takes you there.  
- Helping deliver events and activities, including setting up and clearing away afterwards.
- Ensuring the welcome area is clean and tidy, leaflets are replenished, and information boards are up to date.

Full training and support will be provide for this role but you do need to be a ‘people person’ and have good communication skills. 

This is a really rewarding and enjoyable role. You will be working with a friendly team on a beautiful nature reserve, you will have the opportunity to make new friends and spend time outdoors. You will get to meet loads of new people in this role, enjoying conversation and helping people have a wonderful visit. 

There is always the opportunity to learn new things and gain skills through volunteering, by working at Minsmere you'll naturally learn all about how nature reserves are managed and the wildlife that can be found here. 

This role is suitable for under 18’s.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Engagement Volunteer (On Reserves) (Minsmere Welcome Volunteer)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:686f2ce8683ed80024e04a95 :address "Minsmere, Sheepwash Lane, Saxmundham, Suffolk, IP17 3BY, England";
                            :latitude "52.248947"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "1.607202"^^xsd:double.
id:686f2ce9683ed80024e04ab9 :activityDescription """The RSPB manages a big network of nature reserves which are havens for wildlife, and importantly very special places for people of all ages and abilities to visit and experience a nature rich landscape.

Nature is in trouble, there aren't many places left where wildlife can thrive, that is why we want to welcome more people to these places.

We are looking for volunteers who can help greet visitors on arrival, take entry fee payments through the till and explain how to get the most out of their day. We're currently looking for support on a Sunday but we do have other timeslots available.

Full training and support will be provide for this role but you do need to be a ‘people person’ and have good communication skills.

This is a really rewarding and enjoyable role. You will be working with a friendly team on a beautiful nature reserve, you will have the opportunity to make new friends and spend time outdoors. You will get to meet loads of new people in this role, enjoying conversation and helping people have a wonderful visit.

There is always the opportunity to learn new things and gain skills through volunteering, by working on a reserve, you'll naturally learn all about how nature reserves are managed and the wildlife that is found there.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Centre Welcome ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:686f2ce9683ed80024e04aba :address "Saltholme, Seaton Carew Road, Stockton-On-Tees, Middlesbrough, Durham, TS2 1TU, England";
                            :latitude "54.600739"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.223351"^^xsd:double.
id:686f2cea683ed80024e04ade :activityDescription """The RSPB manages a big network of nature reserves which are havens for wildlife, and importantly very special places for people of all ages and abilities to visit and experience a nature rich landscape.  

Nature is in trouble, there aren't many places left where wildlife can thrive, that is why we want to welcome more people to these places. 

We are looking for volunteers who can help with all our visitor engagement activities, specifically hide and trail guides. 

As a Visitor Engagement Volunteer the tasks you will undertake will depend on which reserve you're working on, but will include some of the following: 

- Having conversations with visitors while out on the reserve and finding out how you can help them enjoy their visit, 
  whether that's pointing out where they can see wildlife, what and where specific sightings have been seen during 
  the day. As well advising where other amenities are situated on the reserve.
- Explaining to the public about the work of the RSPB, what we're all about and asking them if they would like to  
   become members if the conversation takes you there.  
- Ensuring the hides area is clean and tidy, leaflets are replenished, and information boards are up to date.

Full training and support will be provide for this role but you do need to be a ‘people person’ and have good communication skills. 

This is a really rewarding and enjoyable role. You will be working with a friendly team on a beautiful nature reserve, you will have the opportunity to make new friends and spend time outdoors. You will get to meet loads of new people in this role, enjoying conversation and helping people have a wonderful visit. 

There is always the opportunity to learn new things and gain skills through volunteering, by working on a reserve, you'll naturally learn all about how nature reserves are managed and the wildlife that is found there. 

This role is NOT suitable for under 18’s.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Engagement Volunteer (On Reserves) (Hide & Trail Guides)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:686f2cea683ed80024e04adf :address "Burton Mere Wetlands, Burton Mere Wetlands, Puddington Lane, Burton, Cheshire, CH64 5SF, England";
