id:687521cc2fdba65afe246c5a :activityDescription """No one should die because they needed first aid and didn’t get it. St John Ambulance teaches people first aid so they can be the difference between life and death, and you can help us do this.

We are seeking Event Nurses to respond to and manage emergency calls/incidents whilst attending events. Event nurses shall provide specialist, clinical, social and holistic care and undertake clinical assessment and interventions in the pre-hospital environment, which may include venues such as stadia, concert halls, motorsports tracks, road races etc. This will mainly involve working in treatment units or temporary event medical centres.

Successful candidates will be registered nurses with the NMC and be able to provide evidence of CPD activity within the previous 12 months.

For more information about this role, please contact daniel.jennings@sja.org.uk

The closing date for this role is: 31/10/2025

 

 """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "Event Nurse";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:687521cc2fdba65afe246c5b :address "Guildford GU1 1HA";
                            :latitude "51.24626370000001"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.576794"^^xsd:double.
id:687521ebb34d0e5e1381a28a :activityDescription """No one should die because they needed first aid and didn’t get it. St John Ambulance teaches people first aid so they can be the difference between life and death, and you can help us do this.

We are seeking Event Doctors to respond and manage emergency calls/incidents at events, which may include venues such as stadia, concert halls, motorsports tracks, road races etc. Event doctors shall provide specialist, clinical, social and holistic care while undertaking clinical assessment and interventions in the pre-hospital environment. This will mainly involve working in mobile treatment centres or temporary event medical centres

 Successful candidates will be registered medical practitioners with the GMC, without cautions or restrictions, and hold a licence to practice outside of an approved practice setting.

For more information about this role, please contact daniel.jennings@sja.org.uk

The closing date for this role is: 31/10/2025""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "Event Doctor";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:687521ebb34d0e5e1381a28b :address "Guildford GU1 1HA";
                            :latitude "51.24626370000001"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.576794"^^xsd:double.
id:6875c498b3de859a7d3bac3a :activityDescription """We are looking for enthusiastic volunteers aged 13 to 18 to join our young practical Conservation Crew at Ribble Reserves National Nature Reserve (NNR), including Marshside and Hesketh Out Marsh, RSPB. RSPB nature reserves are special places for people and wildlife and we rely on volunteers to keeps these habitats thriving and in good condition. 

It might seem like these wild places have always just been there. But quite often we have to work really hard to maintain habitats to be in the best condition for wildlife. We have lost a lot of wild landscapes, so the small places that we do have, need a bit of extra care.  

As a Youth Reserve Work Party Volunteer you will be joining a regular practical work party team to undertake practical habitat management tasks: 

- Cutting and clearing vegetation.
- Maintaining and managing tools and equipment. 
- Creating and maintaining visitor infrastructure, such as paths, benches and hides. 
- Following Health and Safety protocols. 

If you enjoy being outdoors, meeting new people and hands on conservation work, then this role could be the perfect opportunity for you. Working alongside experienced staff and volunteers who will guide and teach you the importance of our work and how we all can make a difference to wildlife and people. You will be part of Marshside and Hesketh Out Marsh, RSPB Conservation Crew with like minded, enthusiastic and passionate individuals who share a love for wildlife.  This role does involve a reasonable amount of physical activity, so will enable you to keep your fitness levels high, as well as helping your mental health and wellbeing. You will have the satisfaction of knowing that you are making a genuine contribution to nature conservation, and you might find it rewarding to safeguard nature in the area you are working to protect. 

The Conservation Crew programme is aimed at 13 to 18 year olds. Sessions will be delivered on the first Sunday of each month. The Aim of the sessions is to give young people an opportunity to gain experience to learn and understand practical conservation within a conservation organisation. Thus, being able to learn additional skills and knowledge about habitat management and why it is so important.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Practical Reserve Work (Conservation Crew)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:6875c498b3de859a7d3bac3b :address "Marshside, Marine Drive, Southport, Lancashire, PR9 9PJ, England";
                            :latitude "53.672473"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.974258"^^xsd:double.
id:6875c499b3de859a7d3bac5f :activityDescription """Do you enjoy meeting new people or would like to gain catering experience? We are looking for volunteers to help run the popular and friendly cafés on our nature reserves.

As part of our café team you will help to ensure that visitors have an enjoyable and safe visit. When people visit our cafes, we want them to have a warm welcome, get served quickly and enjoy their food and drinks in relaxing and clean surroundings. All this work requires a team of friendly and supportive people to help out. We simple can't run our cafes without volunteers. 

As part of our café team you will be serving customers hot and cold drinks, clearing tables, talking to customers about our food and drink options, maintaining cleanliness standards and health and safety codes of practice. You will be helping visitors find seating and answering questions.  

As part of your role you will learn new skills and gain experience working in the hospitality industry, including great transferable skills, such as customer service, diplomacy, people engagement, following health and safety protocols. The money raised through our retail and catering contributes to nature conservation, so you are also helping to save nature!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Café Volunteer ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:6875c499b3de859a7d3bac60 :address "Saltholme, Seaton Carew Road, Stockton-On-Tees, Middlesbrough, Durham, TS2 1TU, England";
                            :latitude "54.600739"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.223351"^^xsd:double.
id:6875c49ab3de859a7d3bac84 :activityDescription """We need Site Check and Maintenance Volunteers to help look after our reserve at Rainham Marshes. This role is about maintaining a site presence as much as possible with the emphasis being on unlocking or locking our hides. 

Site Check and Maintenance Volunteers, sometimes known as Rangers or Wardens, play an important role here at Rainham. This role is all about ensuring that we maintain a site presence on the ground as much as possible. Essentially, we like to have volunteers out on the reserve every day of the week. We are looking for people who can help us out by taking on a regular shift walking the reserve. The main task being to either unlock our hides first thing or to lock our hides late afternoon. 

Our nature reserves are very special places for people and wildlife. Right across the UK the RSPB manages woodlands and wetlands, heathlands and meadows. A real mosaic of different kinds of habitats for a wide range of wildlife. 

This role at Rainham Marshes will include the following: 

- Talking to members of the public about the reserve and the wildlife they might see.
- Unlocking/locking the hides 
- Checking paths, fences and benches and reporting any issues while walking the reserve 
- Litter picking.
- Checking signage.  
- Reporting back to the site team.

Training and support will be provided for this role. Good communication skills and enjoyment of nature is all you need to apply. 

Whether you can cover a regular slot of opening/unlocking the hides or whether you can help us on a variety of different days during the week, all applications will be welcome. 

This is a really rewarding role. You will enjoy doing your role in a beautiful wildlife rich setting, the great outdoors will be your place of work and you will be able to take it at your own pace. By talking to visitors as you go along, you'll have the pleasure of helping people learn more about the reserve and the work of the RSPB, or just be a familiar friendly face to our regulars.  

You will be making a genuine contribution to nature conservation, and you might find it rewarding to safeguard nature in the area you are working to protect. This role will involve a certain amount of physical activity, so it will enable you to keep your fitness levels high.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Site Checks and Maintenance Volunteer (Site Checks and Locking/Unlocking Hides)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:6875c49ab3de859a7d3bac85 :address "Rainham Marshes, New Tank Hill Road, Purfleet, Essex, RM19 1SZ, England";
                            :latitude "51.486792"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.227471"^^xsd:double.
id:6876152feee76415f5d153ed :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """
We have two hospices, one in Oswestry, Shropshire and another at Conwy in North Wales, providing professional care and improving the quality of life for every child with a life-threatening condition, and their family. 
WE aim to reach every local child with a life-threatening condition as soon as possible to give their families informed choices about accessing our services.
In order to achieve this we will raise the money we need and target those resources in the best way to make the biggest impact.
""";
                            :organisationName "Hope House Children's Hospices";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.hopehouse.org.uk/>.
id:6876154eeee76415f5d15451 :activityDescription """Are you a good listener? 

More than 150,000 people live with multiple sclerosis (MS) in the UK. Every one of them shares the uncertainty of life with MS.

People are most likely to find out they have MS in their thirties, forties and fifties; news that can be worrying and heart breaking. MS can get steadily worse, or symptoms can come and go unpredictably throughout someone’s life.

Could you spare one or two hours a week to provide support to those affected by MS? If so, the MS Helpline team would love to hear from you. 

We’re the UK charity for people with MS. We’re fighting for better treatment and care to help people with MS take control of their lives, and we’re funding research that we believe will stop MS for good. We’ve already made important breakthroughs, and big advances in MS treatments are possible within our lifetimes. With your support, we will stop MS. 

Time and Commitment

All of our MS Befriending Volunteers will carry out their volunteering from home. You will provide weekly friendly phone calls to people affected by MS, at a time convenient to you.

We are looking for volunteers who can offer one or two hours a week, providing one or two phone call sessions. There will also be an annual volunteer event and regular volunteer support sessions you will be asked to attend. 

You’ll receive role specific training and the training session will be delivered remotely on Teams.

About you

We do not ask for previous experience although we are looking for people with good listening skills and a clear, warm telephone voice. You will have good IT skills as the role will require use of Microsoft Office Outlook, and online call handling system which you will receive full training on.

We also ask that you have access to a confidential and comfortable working space, to carry out your phone call sessions.

What will you get from volunteering with us?

A chance to learn new skills
Meet new people
Be part of a supportive, caring team
Ongoing support for your development as a volunteer
A rewarding role supporting the MS community
Before applying please ensure you will be able to meet the following considerations: 

If you are shortlisted, there will be a 30 minute virtual interview on 30th July. Successful candidates will then need to attend a 2 hour virtual training session on 4th August.

Application closing date – 12pm 25th July

If you think you meet the criteria and would like to apply, please click here to find out more. If you would like to speak to someone for further information, please contact Ahra An, Helpline Services Volunteer Manager at ahra.an@mssociety.org.uk or on 020 8438 0704.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425eae8c794380477b70969;
                            :activityTitle "Befriending Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
