                            :longitude "-0.2486683"^^xsd:double.
id:68761b7d1e97e34b1ebd4ae8 :activityDescription """Make memories. Make a difference. One event at a time.

Fancy getting involved in something meaningful - but only have time now and then? Whether you’re looking to boost your CV, meet new people, or just do something worthwhile with your free time, joining us as an Events & Fundraising Volunteer could be the perfect fit.

We’re looking for friendly, enthusiastic volunteers to support Dragonfly Cancer Trust at fundraising events throughout the year. From community fairs and tombola stalls, your support will help us raise vital funds for children and young people with cancer.

What you'll be doing:
Volunteering at events is flexible - you choose the ones that work for you. Most take place on weekends and we’ll always make sure you’re supported and comfortable in your role.

You could help with:

Welcoming and chatting to guests at events

Supporting our tombola or raffle stalls

Bucket collecting at venues or events

Setting up gazebos, banners or tables

Representing Dragonfly and raising awareness

No experience is needed - just a big smile and a willingness to get stuck in!

Why volunteer with us?
It’s completely flexible - you pick what works for you

You’ll make a real difference to families going through incredibly tough times

You’ll gain confidence, new skills and experience

You’ll become part of the Dragonfly family 💛

Ready to help create magical memories?
We’d love to hear from you. Whether you can help at one event or ten, your time makes a lasting impact.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66b234fcd34458062210df35;
                            :activityTitle "Dragonfly Cancer Trust";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68761b7d1e97e34b1ebd4ae9 :address "2 Walesmoor Ave, Kiveton Park, Sheffield S26 5RG, UK";
                            :latitude "53.34029630000001"^^xsd:double;
