id:68761f3668e061e654c96e76 :activityDescription """Are you a crafter, maker, stitcher 
or creative thrifter?
Then we invite you to join our 
Repurposed Rag Challenge 
volunteer opportunity.

Promote the benefits of Regenerating, Repurposing and Re-wearing thrifted items. 
Call at your local Hope House Tŷ Gobaith shop and book a visit to select a kilo of clothing that we are not able to sell and which, as ‘rags’, would have a value to us of around 14p.
Take it away and use the fabrics to turn into something beautiful (clothing or artwork). 
Return the repurposed item to us and we will sell it in the new quirky and retro concession area in our Chester shop.
We will contact you to celebrate the vast increase in value that your upcycling/ mending/ recrafting has created!

#Fashion Reclaimed 		#Sustainable Fashion 
#Ethical Consumerism    #Handmade and unique

Feel great knowing you’re raising money to help local children 
with a life-limiting condition live their very best life.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6876152feee76415f5d153ed;
                            :activityTitle "Repurposed Rag Challenge ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
