                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:6877a902a245b21ba3fae966 :activityDescription """We are the Bassung Legacy Foundation, and we support Single Parent Families and their dependents through a variety of community-focused initiatives. One of our key efforts includes running a charity shop located at 90 Goldhawk Road in West London, which helps fund our work and serve the local community.

We are currently looking for reliable and enthusiastic volunteers to help with the day-to-day operations of our shop. Whether you can give a few hours a week or more, your time will make a big difference.

Volunteer responsibilities may include:
 - Sorting and organising donated items
 - Helping with recycling and waste reduction processes
 - Assisting customers on the shop floor with a warm and helpful attitude
 - Keeping the shop tidy and clean throughout the day
 - Helping price and display items in a visually appealing way
 - Contributing to social media content (Instagram, TikTok, Facebook, etc.)
 - Supporting behind-the-scenes tasks like tagging items or updating inventory
 - Occasionally assisting with charity events or pop-up sales

Volunteering with us comes with a range of personal and professional benefits:
 - Gain valuable retail and customer service experience
 - Boost your CV and improve job prospects
 - Practise and improve your English in a real-world setting
 - Make new friends and become part of a supportive community
 - Contribute to a meaningful cause supporting single-parent families
 - Build confidence and develop transferable skills
 - Flexible shifts to suit your availability

Whether you're looking to gain retail experience, meet new people, support a great cause, or give back to your community - we'd love to have you on board.

To get involved, pop into the shop for a quick chat or email us at [insert email]. Training is provided, and we’re happy to work around your availability.

Come join us and be part of something meaningful. 💜""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66a8f58f83e49e04268f3b2d;
                            :activityTitle "Charity Shop Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6877a902a245b21ba3fae967 :address "90 Goldhawk Road, London";
                            :latitude "51.50209510000001"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.2288441"^^xsd:double.
id:6877afd05f2f64ab87624f3f :activityDescription """Conservation Volunteer Celtic Harmony Camp, Brickendon, Hertfordshire SG13 8NY Mondays & Thursdays, 10:30am – 4:00pm
About the Role Support a purpose-driven charity dedicated to preserving Britain’s prehistoric heritage by helping conserve and restore the ancient woodland surrounding our Iron Age village. As a Conservation Volunteer, you’ll play a vital role in maintaining diverse habitats and supporting local biodiversity.
About Celtic Harmony We are an award-winning charity delivering immersive Prehistory and sustainability education since 1998. Based in a reconstructed ancient settlement in Hertfordshire woodland, we inspire future generations through a connection to nature and heritage.
Key Responsibilities
Assist with woodland management and habitat restoration
Clear invasive species and manage vegetation
Maintain natural footpaths and coppiced areas
Support wildlife-friendly projects such as dead-hedging and bug hotels
Help keep the site tidy and ecologically balanced
Contribute to conservation projects across the site
Support other tasks based on site needs
Person Profile We’re looking for someone who is:
Enthusiastic about nature and environmental conservation
Comfortable working outdoors in all seasons
Hands-on, practical, and eager to learn traditional skills
Reliable and team-minded
In possession of own transport due to the rural location
Volunteer Benefits
Make a tangible impact on local biodiversity and heritage
Learn woodland conservation and land management skills
Join a welcoming community in a peaceful outdoor setting
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68750ec9dcb895c13dcc6978;
                            :activityTitle "Conservation Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6877b04cb050f9641d4d997a :address "Brickendon Lane, Brickendon, Hertford";
                            :latitude "51.7553044"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.0836762"^^xsd:double.
id:6877b3f0c60ddeb9f3f12a2a :activityDescription """Visitor Experience Volunteer
Location: Prehistory Centre, Celtic Harmony Camp, Brickendon, Hertfordshire SG13 8NY 
Availability: Weekends and some weekdays from 24th July to 25th August. Flexible hours from between 9:30am to 5:30pm, for example a shift of 10am to 2pm or 1pm to 5pm.
About the Role Support the day-to-day running of the Prehistory Centre by welcoming visitors, sharing insights about our collection, and ensuring our visitors are engaged. As a Visitor Experience Volunteer, you'll play a vital role in bringing history to life for our guests.
About Celtic Harmony Celtic Harmony is an award-winning charity delivering immersive Prehistory and sustainability education since 1998. Based in a reconstructed Iron Age village within Hertfordshire woodland, we inspire future generations through connection to nature and heritage.
Key Responsibilities
Welcome and engage with visitors to create a memorable experience
Provide information about the Stone to Iron Age exhibition, Prehistory Centre layout, and educational purpose
Maintain a tidy, accessible, and welcoming environment within the Centre
Take money for shop purchases
Assist with events and activities hosted within the Prehistory Centre
Ensure the safety and security of our visitors and the collection
Support other duties in line with day-to-day visitor operations
Person Profile We’re looking for someone who is:
Passionate about history, education, and engaging with the public
Friendly, confident, and enjoys speaking with people from all walks of life
Organised and proactive in keeping spaces presentable
Reliable and adaptable to the needs of the day
Able to travel to our woodland site in Brickendon
Volunteer Benefits
Make a tangible impact on heritage education and visitor engagement
Gain experience in customer service, interpretation, and event support
Be part of a supportive and enthusiastic volunteer team
Enjoy a unique setting surrounded by woodland and historic reconstructions
Share your love of learning with future generations
All volunteers are required to be DBS checked and other tasks may be required.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68750ec9dcb895c13dcc6978;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Experience Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6877b3f0c60ddeb9f3f12a2b :address "Brickendon Lane, Brickendon, Hertford";
                            :latitude "51.7553044"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.0836762"^^xsd:double.
id:6877c3481a82be6bec4930c8 :activityDescription """Conservation Maintenance Volunteer Celtic Harmony Camp, Brickendon, Hertfordshire SG13 8NY Mondays & Thursdays, 10:30am – 4:00pm
About the Role Support a purpose-driven charity dedicated to preserving Britain’s prehistoric heritage. As a Maintenance Volunteer, you'll help care for the Iron Age village, ensuring it's safe, functional, and welcoming for schools and community groups.
About Celtic Harmony We are an award-winning charity delivering immersive Prehistory and sustainability education since 1998. Based in a reconstructed ancient settlement in Hertfordshire woodland, we inspire future generations through a connection to nature and heritage.
Key Responsibilities
Maintain footpaths, steps, and woodland trails
Repair shelters, fences, and learning spaces
Restore educational props and activity stations
Assist with habitat management and vegetation clearance
Keep the site clean and visitor-ready
Contribute to site improvement projects as needed
Support other tasks based on site needs
Person Profile We’re looking for someone who is:
Comfortable working outdoors year-round
Hands-on and eager to learn new practical skills
Experienced with tools (or open to training)
Reliable, punctual, and a team player
Able to travel to the rural location independently
Volunteer Benefits
Make a real impact in a sustainability-focused charity
Gain skills in site maintenance and traditional crafts
Join seasonal workshops and creative activities
Enjoy a peaceful woodland setting with a warm community
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68750ec9dcb895c13dcc6978;
                            :activityTitle "Conservation Maintenance Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6877c3481a82be6bec4930c9 :address "Brickendon Lane, Brickendon, Hertford";
                            :latitude "51.7553044"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.0836762"^^xsd:double.
id:6878bd8c928515222626b592 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription "Currently only 14% of England’s river catchments are in good health. We've set out to reverse this trend with the Riverlands project. Working with partners and communities we’re working to improve the health of the River Bure. The work will establish a diverse habitat for nature to thrive including water voles and eels. Improving access to the river will also create a natural space for everyone to visit and enjoy.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/e7ba242a-8079-4a3b-97d7-4440fc690b87_2025-07-17T09:08:25.603Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "National Trust, Upper Bure Riverlands Partnership";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.nationaltrust.org.uk/visit/norfolk/restoring-the-river-bure-in-norfolk>.
id:6878c4add1af7a3bc7ff4cfe :activityDescription """Join the Riverlands team to make some biological records using field guides and iNaturalist. Learn about freshwater habitat restoration and common species to find near rivers and on the Blickling estate. We recommend downloading iNaturalist beforehand. Walks are 2 hours with regular stopping.  There are no toilets nearby so we suggest visiting the main visitor reception before arriving.
Dress appropriately for the weather and for walking through tall vegetation.

Meeting at National Trust's Fisherman's Car Park""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6878bd8c928515222626b592;
                            :activityTitle "Biological Recording Walk";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6878c7111bf958130bc3e6ab :activityDescription """Learn about freshwater habitat restoration and common species to find near rivers and on the Blickling estate. We recommend downloading iNaturalist beforehand. Walks are 2 hours with regular stopping. There are no toilets at the meeting point so suggest visiting the main Blickling visitor reception before arriving. We recommend wearing appropriate clothing and footwear for the weather and walking through tall grass.

Parking is restricted to village roads, meeting point at the village bus stop""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6878bd8c928515222626b592;
                            :activityTitle "Freshwater Walk";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
