id:6878d11929486b650f0145cc :activityDescription """Family Friends carefully recruit, train, and match volunteers with families in Kensington & Chelsea, Hammersmith & Fulham and Brent. Volunteers offer practical and emotional support based on each family's unique needs and potential. 

Our Family Befrienders support parents and families; volunteers will aim to help families/single parents to discover their strengths, build confidence, and resolve difficulties. Volunteers meet with their family weekly or fortnightly for a period of 6 to 12 months.

Activities might include:

- Supporting a parent to take their children on days out.
- Helping to strengthen family relationships.
- Providing a listening ear.
- Helping family members build confidence in themselves.

Essential Criteria:
- Level of commitment mentioned above
- 18+
- Must have lived in the UK for the last 2 years

What we provide in return:
- Full induction training and ongoing training
- Weekly supervision and support
- The chance to learn new skills
- References provided after 6 months' commitment
- Reimbursement of travel and session expenses

We are an equal opportunities charity and value the principles of diversity and inclusion, which is central in providing successful support to our families. We welcome and encourage applications from people with a wide range of backgrounds and experiences, including people from Black, Asian or Minority Ethnic backgrounds, people who identify as LGBTQI+ and individuals from different socio-economic and educational backgrounds. 

In the first instance, please fill out our Volunteer Application Form at this link: https://airtable.com/appBRIjuDYUGNPr6x/pagnpvEckpBWBnSAu/form 

Once this has been done, someone from our organisation will be in touch soon!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d743a0624f3ab9fbe81a;
                            :activityTitle "Family Befriender";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6878d11929486b650f0145cd :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:6878d3b2d1af7a3bc7ff5054 :activityDescription """Learn about freshwater habitat restoration and common species to find near rivers and on the Blickling estate. We recommend downloading iNaturalist beforehand. Walks are 2 hours with regular stopping. There are no toilets at the meeting point so suggest visiting the main Blickling visitor reception before arriving. We recommend wearing appropriate clothing and footwear for the weather and walking through tall grass. 

Parking is restricted to village roads, meeting point at the village bus stop
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6878bd8c928515222626b592;
                            :activityTitle "Freshwater Walk";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6878d3b2d1af7a3bc7ff5055 :address "Wolterton Road, Itteringham, Norwich NR11 7AU, England, United Kingdom";
                            :latitude "52.8316832"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "1.1843857"^^xsd:double.
id:6878d957f79b3b4c92a9fe8a :activityDescription """Why we want you: This vital role supports local groups across the UK, which are volunteer-run, offering friendship and support to people living with Parkinson's, their families, and friends. As a pivotal part of the local volunteer team, you will help plan group spending for the benefit of people affected by Parkinson's in your community.

What you will be doing: Be an ambassador for Team Parkinson’s, engaging with local staff, volunteers, and your community to ensure the group has the greatest possible impact. Accurately record financial activity, keeping the group and the Parkinson's UK local networks finance team informed of the group's financial position. With local staff support, stay updated on Parkinson's UK's financial policies, sharing them with the group and ensuring compliance. Provide regular financial reports to the committee, including final accounts at the Annual General Meeting. Deal with financial administration, from annual reports to legacy spending, and ensure accurate volunteer expense payments per policy. Be a signatory on the group's bank accounts.

The skills you need: Previous experience in finance, accountancy, or bookkeeping can be valuable but is not essential. You must be confident with numbers and able to lead the group’s finances, possessing confident computer and email skills and openness to using new systems and digital tools. A commitment to the wider charity’s aims and values is essential, as is the ability to contribute to balanced, collaborative, open, and inclusive decisions with committee and local staff.

What's in it for you: Develop valuable leadership, teamwork, and people skills. Play a crucial role in the local Parkinson's community, Team Parkinson’s, and wider local planning, making new friends and building connections. Develop or maintain your accountancy or bookkeeping skills, along with administrative and communication skills; we are happy to provide references.

Disclaimer: As a Branch Treasurer handling personal or sensitive data, you must complete and maintain data protection and confidentiality training. To be a signatory on a local group account, banks will perform a credit check, and we will take up a reference. Volunteers cannot perform this role if they have been declared bankrupt.

For enquiries contact Zoe Sole on zsole@parkinsons.org.uk or call 07842449295

Apply online at: https://volunteer.parkinsons.org.uk/opportunities/76055-branch-treasurer-oxford-2024-11-05
​""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6688101e4435668103b1c65a;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Treasurer Parkinson's UK Oxford branch";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6878d957f79b3b4c92a9fe8b :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:6878da3701aef942fd7cf437 :activityDescription """Why we want you
Local groups across the UK are run by volunteers and offer friendship and
support to people living with Parkinson's and their families and friends. The
friendly faces and warm welcome provided by branch volunteers means
attendees get the most from the group, with the activities on offer running
smoothly.

What you will be doing
Core to group meetings, you'll help set up the venue, offering a warm
welcome to all attendees
Assist with fundraising events
Getting involved in the activities the group offers - joining in to get the most out of these for you too

The skills you need
Good communication skills
Supportive; able to listen to the needs of people with Parkinson's, and
reflect these to the group to shape the support provided
Honest; you'll know when to ask for help, or when tasks might be seen as
less important, and able to share that with Parkinson's UK and your group

What's in it for you
You'll make new friends and meet new people, both in the branch and in
the local community
You'll be making a real difference for people affected by Parkinson's in
your community
Developing valuable organisational and people skills
You'll be part of a movement of people improving the lives of people
affected by Parkinson's
You'll be able to take part in the activities of the group

For enquiries contact Zoe Sole on zsole@parkinsons.org.uk or call 07842449295
​
Apply Online at: https://volunteer.parkinsons.org.uk/opportunities/71330-branch-volunteer-oxford-2024-08-20
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6688101e4435668103b1c65a;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Parkinson's UK Oxford branch";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6878da3701aef942fd7cf438 :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:6878db70cb9160db05f23ff5 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription """You don’t have to join an existing community energy group or spend time creating one – you can just join the Big Solar Co-op and start looking for suitable solar sites. Many of our Volunteer Members work outside of any local group. Others prefer to work with us from within their community group, benefitting from each other’s local knowledge, connections and working together in person.

To make this decentralised approach possible, we use a custom built database of sites and an online messaging platform that can be accessed 24/7. We get together in person for an annual interactive conference – the Big Solar Gathering and run regular free training and collaborative discussion events over Zoom through the year. All our learning so far is available in a dedicated Volunteer Member area along with past recordings of our webinars, talks and training videos.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/de8852df-d569-4c1a-a5e5-5a4868af0bd7_2025-07-17T11:15:59.822Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "The Big Solar Co-op";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://bigsolar.coop/>.
id:6878f7b2548fc003af941ccb :activityDescription """Do you have a love of reading? 
Could you share that love with children in a local primary school?
Can you make a weekly afternoon commitment?

If you answered yes to these questions; we need you!

Coram Beanstalk has a long standing history of training volunteers to go into local primary schools and support children to grow a love of reading. 
You will be trained how to not just listen to children read, but also how to engage them in conversation about books and how to encourage them to find books they love. 

We provide training in small, online, interactive group sessions with one of our trainers as well as providing ongoing support once you are placed in school.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d5f5a0624f3ab9fbc763;
                            :activityTitle "Coram Beanstalk: In person reading support";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6878f7b2548fc003af941ccc :address "Thornhill Rd, London N1 1HX, UK";
