id:6878ff38e1bc2e9dcb6421ce :activityDescription """Do your friends and family comment that you make a lovely cup of tea?  Well, if so, then you are who we need! 

We are looking for a friendly cuppa volunteer (or two!) to join us at our Deansfield Court Saturday Social events, once a month, to help make refreshments for all our lovely attendees.

We need helpers between 1.30pm - 3pm, but you would be welcome to stay and enjoy the entertainment.

We would like someone that is passionate, friendly and willing to help out with serving refreshments. You just need to be able to talk to others and be a friendly face for those attending.

You will help set up by getting the cups ready and the kettle boiled. Make the all important brews and beverages, then at the end of the event you will ensure everything is washed, clean and tidy.

Due to the nature of the role, as you will be supporting vulnerable members of the community, you must be over the age of 18 if you are doing this on your own. However, we are happy to consider someone over 14 if they volunteer with a parent or guardian, who is over the age of 18.

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66223a743eee01aca4c93417;
                            :activityTitle "Cuppa Crew Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6878ffd3fd187d11f49bf275 :address "Furlongs Avenue, Norton, Malton YO17 9DJ";
