id:687a2816222bf98931125a15 :activityDescription """Summary
Marshalling opportunities at our fabulous fundraising event - the inclusive annual Sutton Park Challenge!


Who we are

Midland Mencap is a charity which works and campaigns for accessible and inclusive services and a better quality of life for everyone with experience of learning disabilities and additional needs.

 

Purpose of the role
 
Our fabulous annual Sutton Park Challenge Run takes place on Sunday 5th October.

 

We need friendly people for approximately 4 hours to marshal the routes, greet competitors and supporters, help us to set up and run the registration tent and runners village, man the music station or clear away at the end of the event! 
 

A marshal is one of the most important volunteer roles at any event, helping us achieve our fundraising goals, and making the day special, safe, and memorable for all.


We are passionate that it is a highly accessible and inclusive event. Whether someone wants to run, walk, or push someone else in a wheelchair, this is a great way for people to challenge themselves.

 

This is a small event with a huge heart, and to ensure everyone is included we will be hosting three races – a 10k, a 5k and a 1k.


Competitors are sponsored to run, and all funds raised will support the vital work Midland Mencap does for people with disabilities and their family carers. 

 
When and where

The race takes place within Sutton Park B74 2YT.


We’re looking for enthusiastic volunteers to join us between 8am and 12.00 noon (Sunday 5th October 2025)


What would I be doing?

·      Help with the setup of the course including positioning of any signage or equipment

·      Guide and cheer participants along the route

·      Providing a friendly face and assistance at key areas

·      Willingness to work as part of a team

·      To keep in contact with other marshals, the volunteer manager and safety officer and report any problems

·      To assist in event close down and return any signage and equipment

 

What do I need?

·      Bags of energy and enthusiasm

·      Great communication skills

·      Be reliable and punctual

·      Willingness to work as part of a team

·      You need to be practical and being willing to get involved where needed

·      Able to deal with problems in a cool and calm manner

·      You may need to wear warm footwear and clothes.



NB - 16-17yr olds can volunteer with parental consent, under 16s must be accompanied by a responsible adult!

A DBS is not required for this role.

 

What’s in it for me?

·      A full briefing in advance of the event and on the day

·      You’ll get a really great overview of what it takes to run an event

·      A fun time and the opportunity to work alongside a fantastic team of volunteers

·      Knowing that you have made a difference to people with a learning disability

·      Genuine appreciation for your help

·      A free hot drink from 'The Awesome Coffee Company'



What to do if you’re interested?

Register your interest via our form, or download and complete an application from our website.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:67ed34d0697c35c76953a1b9;
                            :activityTitle "Sutton Park Challenge - Volunteer Marshal";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:687a2816222bf98931125a16 :address "Sutton Park Road, Sutton";
                            :latitude "51.3606236"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.1951317"^^xsd:double.
