id:687a5bda7f3e3f771ef87c58 :activityDescription """Why We Want You
Local groups across the UK are run by volunteers and offer friendship and support to people living with Parkinson's, along with their families and friends. The friendly faces and warm welcome provided by branch volunteers mean attendees get the most from the group, with the activities on offer running smoothly.

What You Will Be Doing
Core to group meetings, you'll help set up the venue and offer a warm welcome to all attendees. You'll also assist with fundraising events and get involved in the activities the group offers, joining in to get the most out of these for yourself too.

The Skills You Need
You'll need good communication skills and be supportive, able to listen to the needs of people with Parkinson's and reflect these to the group to shape the support provided. Honesty is key; you'll know when to ask for help or when tasks might be seen as less important, and be able to share that with Parkinson's UK and your group.

What's In It For You
You'll make new friends and meet new people, both within the branch and in the local community. You'll also be making a real difference for people affected by Parkinson's in your community, developing valuable organisational and people skills. Finally, you'll be part of a movement of people improving the lives of people affected by Parkinson's and will be able to take part in the activities of the group.

For enquiries contact Zoe Sole on zsole@parkinsons.org.uk or call 07842449295
​
Apply Online at: https://volunteer.parkinsons.org.uk/opportunities/86966-branch-volunteer-bandbury-2025-04-04""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6688101e4435668103b1c65a;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Parkinson's UK Banbury Branch";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:687a5bda7f3e3f771ef87c59 :address "Banbury, UK";
                            :latitude "52.0629009"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.339775"^^xsd:double.
