id:687e354e0ced8a70b353a668 :activityDescription """Are you passionate about making a real impact? Kent Community Energy is launching an ambitious Share Offer from August 1st to October 31st, 2025, aiming to raise £400,000 to install 400kW of rooftop solar on community buildings across Kent. It’s a chance to grow our community business, grow our investor community, expand our social media following and get positive media attention. We're looking for enthusiastic volunteers to help us achieve this vital goal!

What we need
We're seeking self-starting, adaptable \"doers\" with skills in any of the following:
Social Media & Writing: Craft engaging posts for Facebook, WhatsApp, and newsletters.
Basic Design (eg. Canva): Create eye-catching infographics, flyers, and banners.
Content Creation: Collect inspiring stories, photos, and videos from our solar sites and grantees, especially in East and South Kent.
Media & Press Liaison: Help us secure positive coverage and interviews.

When & where
Ideally, you're available from mid-July to end of August, though any help is valued! Most tasks can be done remotely across the UK, with story collection focused on Kent (particularly East and South).

Why volunteer with Kent Community Energy?
KCE will provide a clear induction, concise task briefs, stakeholder introductions, and cover pre-agreed expenses. You'll gain valuable experience, see your work directly contribute to tangible renewable energy projects, and be credited for your efforts.

Interested? Get in touch:
Contact us with a brief note about yourself and your experience.   """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:687e3223f7b7526062455601;
                            :activityTitle "Social media, design or press volunteer for Kent Community Energy";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:687e354e0ced8a70b353a669 :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:687efeea9e45ed3b31f610df :activityDescription """**When:** Flexible but placements available from September 2025 lasting for 6+ months. Closing date for applications 20 August 2025.

Interviews will be held in late August 2025

**Commitment:** 26 weeks

**Duration:** Flexible but typically 6 month placement

**Why We Want You:**

We are looking for an enthusiastic residential volunteer with some prior practical experience to join our wardening team for six months, starting in September 2025.  Help us to deliver nature conservation on the ground as part of the team carrying out the day-to-day management of the reserve, and ensuring that it is maintained to the high standard expected of RSPB.
Winter work is likely to involve reed cutting, coppicing, path maintenance and bird surveys around Morecambe Bay.

**What’s In It For You:**
 
This is a chance to spend 6 months volunteering and living in the stunning surroundings of Leighton Moss and Morecambe Bay, home to key species such as otter, bearded tit, marsh harrier, bittern and a host of rare plants and invertebrates.  The reserve has a flagship visitor centre, receiving 110,000 visitors a year! In addition you will gain:

• Excellent practical experience of working on a flagship nature reserve and managing different habitats for wildlife.

• Experience  of wildlife monitoring techniques such as wetland bird surveys and moth trapping. 

• Appropriate training in the use of machinery and power tools. 

• Experience of working in a team and supervising other volunteers

• A working knowledge of the RSPB and conservation issues   

• Free accommodation in stunning surroundings on the reserve.

**Requirements:**
 
Essential criteria are

• Enthusiasm for the role

• An interest in conservation

• Some experience of practical conservation work

• Ability to work as part of a team 

• A full driving licence is also required for this role 


You will need to be at least 18 yrs old. You must be prepared to undertake strenuous manual labour outside in all weathers, walking long distances and you must have a flexible approach, as some tasks may take place early in the morning, late at night or at weekends.


**Notes:**
 
Accommodation is provided on site in the main visitor centre building. There are two bedrooms and a shared living room, kitchen and bathroom.

Appropriate training will be provided and pre-agreed expenses will be re-imbursed where necessary. 
 
For more information please contact **Nick Godden** on 01524 703014 or email nick.godden@RSPB.org.uk. Nick spends most of his time working out on the reserve but will respond to your application or e-mail ASAP. If you are interested in applying for this placement, please fill in the residential volunteer application on assemble.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Residential on Reserve (More than 4 weeks) (Leighton Moss)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:687efeea9e45ed3b31f610e0 :address "Leighton Moss, Storrs Lane, Silverdale, Carnforth, Lancashire, LA5 0SW, England";
                            :latitude "54.168246"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.802461"^^xsd:double.
