id:687fa24bb11cc1f052e7f376 :activityDescription """•	To provide a welcoming environment for visitors to the Chelsea History Festival.
•	To help visitors enjoy a unique experience at the Chelsea History Festival
•	To offer volunteers a fantastic opportunity to play a vital role in the Festival, while gaining experience volunteering at a National institution and for a large- scale annual history Festival.  

Minimum commitment: Half day of the festival
Thursday 25th – Sunday 28th September 2025
4-8 hour shifts, between 09:30 and 21:00 

•	Greeting and welcoming visitors to the Festival as a first point of contact as they enter the Festival site. 

•	Pro-actively engaging with visitors and providing information about the Festival and its events to help visitors get the most out of their visit. 

•	Helping visitors with wayfinding and giving directions to events.

•	Assisting with checking visitors’ tickets and ushering at events, crowd control, queue management and guiding visitors to seats.

•	Ensuring event spaces are kept, tidy, clean and presentable and set up correctly ahead of forthcoming events.

•	To be a hands-on, friendly and an approachable presence during events, as and when needed.

•	Answer other Festival attendee related enquiries, watching over and assisting the smooth running of events, talks and/or workshops.

•	Maintain a good knowledge of the Chelsea History Festival programme and keep informed about operational changes and timings.

•	Distribute flyers and collect evaluation as required.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cceba0624f3ab9fafe1a;
                            :activityTitle "Chelsea History Festival 2025";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:687fa24bb11cc1f052e7f377 :address "Royal Hospital Road, London";
                            :latitude "51.4865866"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.1603089"^^xsd:double.
id:687fa4723425e41734ffb35f :activityDescription """Are you creative? Would you like to support others to express their emotions through arts and crafting?

We are looking for a passionate and creative volunteer to assist in leading our Acrylic Painting sessions. This role is perfect for someone who enjoys art, has a keen interest in acrylic painting, and is enthusiastic about supporting others in their creative journey.

This group will run on Monday between 11am and 1pm!

About the service.. Hestia provides mental health support across 17 London boroughs and in Kent. Last year, Hestia supported more than 6,000 people across our mental health services.

1 in 4 people will experience a mental health issue of some kind in England.

We have a range of services providing short to long term support for people at times of crisis. People receive support to access and sustain their accommodation, support with their physical and mental health, maximise their finances, engage in the community and develop their social skills.

What you will be doing
Assist the session leader in setting up and organizing art materials before the session.
Support participants with basic acrylic painting techniques, color mixing, and brushwork.
Provide encouragement and guidance to attendees, helping them feel comfortable and inspired. independent activities
Help maintain a clean and safe workspace by managing supplies and cleaning up after sessions.
Assist with any administrative tasks, such as attendance tracking or taking photographs of completed artwork (if permitted).
Ensure all health and safety guidelines are followed.

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cec6a0624f3ab9fb3209;
                            :activityTitle "Acrylic Painting Group Volunteer (Kingston)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:687fa4723425e41734ffb360 :address "Kingston upon Thames";
                            :latitude "51.41233"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.300689"^^xsd:double.
id:687fa5251a9a8eb09a486dfc :activityDescription """Become a Buddy with BuddyUp!

Are you passionate about making a positive impact in the lives of young people with disabilities? Join BuddyUp, a rewarding volunteering opportunity where you can help a young person (aged 14-17) in Richmond or Kingston gain independence and confidence.

What You'll Do: As a Buddy (volunteers aged 16+), you'll be matched with a young person with disabilities, helping them navigate public transport, explore their community, and most importantly—have fun! Whether it’s going to the cinema, painting pottery or bowling, you’ll spend time together twice a month, building a meaningful friendship.

About Richmond AID: Richmond AID is a local charity dedicated to empowering people with disabilities across all ages and needs. Our mission is to support independent living and ensure everyone has equal opportunities to thrive.

Why Volunteer?
Impact Lives: Help young people grow in confidence and independence.
Flexible Commitment: Just 2 hours, twice a month, on your schedule.
No Cost: Enjoy outings with your Buddy at no expense to you—we cover it all!
Group Outings: We have optional opportunities to join us for group outings, they happen every 2 months and are tailored to various interests.

Requirements:
A fun, positive attitude
Availability to volunteer twice a month for at least 6 months (flexible to your schedule as we know life can get busy)
Ability to travel to Richmond or Kingston for your outings
DBS check (we’ll help with this)
Ready to get started? Join BuddyUp and be the change in a young person’s life. Express your interest today, and we’ll guide you through the next steps!

Please get in touch if you are interested in supporting a young person and we will guide you through the next steps.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:687f9df80ce3f9e2e65e8232;
                            :activityTitle "Become a Buddy to a young person with BuddyUp!";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:687fa5251a9a8eb09a486dfd :address "Kingston, ON, Canada";
                            :latitude "44.2334401"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-76.49302949999999"^^xsd:double.
