id:687fa798b11cc1f052e7f4c9 :activityDescription """Are looking to give back to the local community? By joining our team of befrienders, you will support us to reach some of the most isolated adults in the community to reduce their feelings of loneliness, build friendships and provide support for mental wellbeing. You will support to relight a spark in a hobby, interest or encourage individuals to explore and participate in new social activities.

Loneliness and isolation can affect anyone in life, whatever their age or family situation.

About Our Service... Hestia provides mental health support across 17 London boroughs and in Kent. Last year, Hestia supported more than 6,000 people across our mental health services.

1 in 4 people will experience a mental health issue of some kind in England.

We have a range of services providing short to long term support for people at times of crisis. People receive support to access and sustain their accommodation, support with their physical and mental health, maximise their finances, engage in the community and develop their social skills.

What you will be doing
Agree a mutual time and frequency to meet in the local community
To develop and promote a positive relationship with your befriendee
To encourage your befriendee to engage in social activities and support them in doing so whilst building their confidence
To support your befriendee in developing their goals and social skills
Encourage your befriended to make links with community services, based on their identified goals



""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cec6a0624f3ab9fb3209;
                            :activityTitle "Befriender Volunteer (Ealing)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:687fa798b11cc1f052e7f4ca :address "Ealing, London";
                            :latitude "51.5132537"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.3043136"^^xsd:double.
id:687fb357a795103f8ef662a7 :activityDescription """Are you committed to driving excellence and innovation? Do you have experience working within practitioners of Volunteer Education Programmes?

As a Community of Practice Officer, you will play a vital role in supporting and enhancing a national community of practice. You will focus on specific activities or areas within the community, ensuring that efforts align with national standards and priorities while avoiding duplication.

As a Community of Practice Officer, you will:

Support the Community of Practice Lead in coordinating the community.
Focus on specific activities or areas within the community of practice.
Assist in delivering impactful initiatives and projects.
Foster collaboration and strengthen professional engagement.
Champion inclusivity and provide support to community members.
Contribute to the overall success and development of the community.
For more information about this role, please see the role description.

The closing date for this vacancy is 25/07/2025

For more information on this vacancy, please contact katie.goodale@sja.org.uk""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "Clinical Education Community Of Practice- Geographical Officer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:687fb357a795103f8ef662a8 :address "Nightingale Close, Bury Saint Edmunds IP33 3SY";
