id:6880a8f7ce97bcfd418350ce :activityDescription """Finance Volunteer

We’re the MS Society – a community of people living with MS, scientists, campaigners, listeners, organisers, ambassadors and fundraisers. Our volunteers are a key part of achieving our goals and their support is vital. Join us.

About this opportunity
We are looking to recruit a Finance Volunteer for our Preston Group. As a Finance Volunteer, you would be joining a coordinating team of volunteers to plan and deliver services and activities to support people locally.

You will maintain and approve income and expenditure records and explain financial information clearly to other group members. You would ensure our financial requirements and policies are followed, and that money is spent in a cost effective manner.

This is a great opportunity to gain experience with a large charity, develop your existing skills and learn new ones. We need you to get involved and help make positive changes to the lives of people affected by MS.

About you
You’ll have an interest in the MS Society and the work that we do, as well as the enthusiasm to represent both us and our values locally. You will understand the needs of people affected by MS in your area and be sympathetic to the needs and motivations of volunteers. You’ll be comfortable with figures, preferably with an accounting or business background. You will live in the immediate area of the Group, allowing you to meet with other volunteers from the Group.

Apply 

Read through the role description carefully

Please apply online

The MS Society is committed to promoting diversity. We can only offer roles to over 18s.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425eae8c794380477b70969;
                            :activityTitle "Finance Volunteer (Preston)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6880a8f7ce97bcfd418350cf :address "Preston PR1 2RL";
                            :latitude "53.7598883"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.6986986"^^xsd:double.
id:6880aef7e5d2bcf73d7a91d9 :activityDescription """This month we’re inviting your team to get involved in a simple, flexible and impactful micro volunteering activity: delivering postcards to inspire even more people to host a Macmillan Coffee Morning. 
 
It’s easy to take part – and even easier to make a difference.
Whether during your lunch break, your commute, or a walk around your local area, you can help spread the word by popping your postcards through letterboxes, pinning them to community boards, or sharing them with local shops and cafes.
Why join in?
•	Do it anytime, anywhere – totally flexible to your schedule
•	A great way to get those lunchtime steps in- whether you’re working from home or the office!
•	Perfect for individuals or small teams looking to make a quick impact
•	A fantastic way to support one of the UK’s biggest fundraising events
This year we’re aiming to raise an incredible £17 million during Coffee Morning, and we need your help to make it happen.
Together, your steps can help us take a big step forward for people affected by cancer. Join us in spreading the word.
Interested in taking part?
Please register to receive your postcard pack and help us make Coffee Morning 2025 our most successful yet.  
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:665de4919155fda1cf3f31d9;
                            :activityTitle "Micro volunteering- delivering postcards to inspire even more people to host a Macmillan Coffee Morning";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6880b233c58eb82c9ec945d5 :activityDescription """We’re challenging you to walk 100 miles over the 31 days of August. You can split the miles up however you like throughout the month, but it works out as just over three miles each day. 

Walk the streets. Head for the hills. Stroll in the park. However you do it - do it for people living with cancer.

Once registered, you can activate the fundraising page we’ve built for you. We recommend setting your fundraising pledge at £160, but the goal is to raise what you can. We’ll provide you with lots of fundraising tips along the way to help you make the biggest impact for people living with cancer. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:665de4919155fda1cf3f31d9;
                            :activityTitle "Walk 100 Miles in August Challenge";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:6880b7d72cf19e872ae1835e :address "High Street, Croydon CR0 1QD";
