id:6880ea62216b8fe9220470f4 :activityDescription """Would you like to make a difference to the life of a veteran living with sight loss? 

We have veteran's living across York who would welcome a volunteer to visit them at home on a weekly or fortnightly basis for companionship and chat to reduce their social isolation.

By popping by once a week or fortnight to see a veteran in their area, home visitors are a friendly face that can make all the difference to our veterans. A visit could be a simple chat and a cup of tea, helping out with odd jobs around the home that can otherwise be a struggle for our veterans to complete or getting out and about in the local area and visiting local attractions.

You will never be asked to do any personal care. Although you will be working in the community independently, your manager is only a phone call away and there is a network of other volunteers for you to link in with too.
Volunteers need to be able to travel independently to and from our veteran’s home. Our veterans live across the York area, willingness to drive and access to a car would be of an advantage. All agreed out of pocket expenses such as travel costs will be met by Blind Veterans UK.

Volunteers must understand the importance of confidentiality and relationship boundaries. The role can be flexible around your other commitments, but we ask that you are reliable and punctual for our veterans. You will be fully trained and supported so you feel comfortable and confident in your volunteering.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ea9ac794380477b70039;
                            :activityTitle "Home Visitor Volunteer York";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6880ea62216b8fe9220470f5 :address "York";
                            :latitude "53.9614205"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.0739108"^^xsd:double.
