                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:68810623cf539d1bfedb084c :activityDescription """Are you looking for a Fundraising role that makes a real difference to a local charity? 

 At Acorns we provide care and support for life limited or life threatened children and their families. We are a charity, and our fundraising is vital to enable us to continue providing care and support to the children: it costs around £11 million a year to run our care services. 

Shelsley Walsh Hill Climb on Saturday 9th August 2025 9.00am – 5.00pm 

The 2025 British Hillclimb Championship returns to Shelsley Walsh for a great weekend of non-stop action. With an Inter Club meeting taking place on Saturday showcasing more of the well contested interclub championships.

Am I right for the role? 

We’re looking for volunteers who are

Approachable and happy to raise awareness about Acorns
Versatile and willing to adapt and help out 
  Why volunteer at Acorns? 

To help a local charity and make a difference in your community
Connect with likeminded people and make new friends
Learn new skills to boost your CV
Opportunities to progress to other roles
Volunteers will receive wristbands for the day

We can only accept volunteers who are 18 years of age or older. If you are under 18, a parent or guardian must also apply as they need to accompany you for the duration of your volunteer activities.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641096af1097b43af15de362;
                            :activityTitle "Community Giving Event - (Shelsley Walsh Hill Climb)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68810623cf539d1bfedb084d :address "Walsh Cottages, Shelsley Walsh, Worcester WR6 6RP";
                            :latitude "52.270262"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.4146173"^^xsd:double.
id:6881a204da4e4ef37a433d58 :activityDescription """Do you enjoy meeting new people and want to make a positive impact for nature? Do you remember those fun days out as a child, exploring the wonders of the outdoors and nature? If YES, come and be part of our Visitor Engagement team and help inspire visitors, young and old, about the amazing wildlife we have here at Rainham Marshes.

We're looking for enthusiastic volunteers who are keen to get involved with all aspects of visitor engagement. 
Following a short period of training and working alongside experienced team members, we will ask you to:

• Provide our visitors with a warm welcome. Engage in conversation with them and find out how you can help them enjoy their visit. Offer information on recent sightings, the best places to view our wildlife and make them aware of parking/entry requirements. 

• Talk to the public about the work of the RSPB, what we're all about and ask them if they would like to become members if the conversation takes you there. 

• Help deliver events and activities, including on weekends and school holiday for under 18’s, including setting up and clearing away afterwards. Typical holiday activities include pond dipping and minibeast hunting.

• Assist with running events at Halloween, Christmas and Easter such as fetes and workshops.

• Ensure the welcome area is clean and tidy.

There is also an opportunity to be part of the rota to open and close the hides. This gives you a chance to walk around the reserve before any visitors arrive or at the end of the day; times when wildlife can be very active. 

We are looking for volunteers who are:

• Confident and enjoy meeting and chatting to new people of all ages.

• Enthusiastic about nature and wildlife and keen to engage and inspire visitors no matter their age or level of knowledge.

• Able to adapt their communication style to be able to talk to families with children

• Willing to learn new skills.

This is a rewarding and enjoyable role. You will be working with a friendly team on a beautiful nature reserve; you will have the opportunity to make new friends and spend time outdoors. Volunteering with us can fit around a part time job, higher education courses and family life. We do ask for a minimum of 1 day every month, but you are welcome to commit to as many days as you can for as long as you can. 
 
We supply a uniform and reimburse your travel expenses, up to 25 miles each way.

We’re now the largest nature conservation charity in the country, consistently delivering successful conservation, forging powerful new partnerships with other organisations and inspiring others to stand up and give nature the home it deserves. We rely on the support and generosity of our volunteers to make a difference Our work stretches far beyond the UK. Wherever wildlife is in threat, we'll work with partners across the globe to help save it and give it a home.

Thank you for reading this role description. Clicking on 'more about this role' and the downloadable pdf will give you just the generic role profile for this opportunity. A role profile is the family to which an opportunity belongs and informs vetting and training requirements and may not be an exact fit to the role described above.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Engagement Volunteer (On Reserves) (Rainham Marshes)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:6881a204da4e4ef37a433d59 :address "Rainham Marshes, New Tank Hill Road, Purfleet, Essex, RM19 1SZ, England";
                            :latitude "51.486792"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.227471"^^xsd:double.
id:6881fae729060d90160fff65 :activityDescription """Join our Event Crew at our fun, family-friendly One Walk at Roundhay Park on Saturday 13 September. Help us make sure the event runs like clockwork and create a fun, welcoming atmosphere as the T1D community comes together to take on a scenic 5km walk, to raise awareness and vital funds for type 1 diabetes research.

What will I be doing?
There are various roles available on the day, including:
- Helping us set up the registration desk and merchandise stall in the Event Village before walkers arrive.
- Welcoming walkers as they arrive, making sure they’ve registered and have their Breakthrough T1D t-shirts and One Walk route maps.
- Looking after the merchandise stall and sharing information about Breakthrough T1D.
- Helping walkers find their way around the Event Village before the walk begins.
- Directing walkers along the route to make sure they go the right way and cheering them on to keep them motivated.
- Handing out One Walk medals to the walkers when they finish their walk.
- Helping us to pack everything away after the walk has finished.

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:67f6582f914c997ed111942c;
                            :activityTitle "One Walk Leeds Event Crew";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6881fbcf5835f0faf257771a :address "Roundhay Park, Roundhay, Leeds LS8 2HH";
