                            :longitude "-3.1632079"^^xsd:double.
id:6884a493d8295b120ad4e8b5 :activityDescription """About the Role:
Are you passionate about mental health and want to make a real difference in your community? Join our busy, energetic Fundraising Team at Counselling in the Community and be part of something truly life-changing!
As a Volunteer Fundraiser, you’ll play a key role in raising vital funds and spreading awareness of our work. You’ll get involved in a variety of exciting activities – from attending local events and exhibitions to supporting street collections, raffles, and community stalls. No two days are ever the same!
What You'll Be Doing:
•	Representing CITC at events, festivals, and exhibitions
•	Collecting donations and engaging with the public
•	Helping set up and run fundraising stalls and community displays
•	Spreading awareness of our services and how people can support us
•	Sharing ideas to boost fundraising impact
What We're Looking For:
•	A friendly, positive attitude and good communication skills
•	Enthusiasm for mental health and community wellbeing
•	Reliability and a willingness to get stuck in
•	Happy working solo or as part of a team
What You’ll Gain:
•	A chance to meet new people and make a tangible impact
•	Experience in community fundraising and events
•	Full support and guidance from our fundraising lead
•	A role that’s flexible, rewarding, and fun!
Ready to Join Us?
Whether you’re outgoing or just want to help behind the scenes, we’d love to hear from you. You’ll be part of a supportive team making a real difference to people’s lives.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6720b4fd25befcb723b95a33;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Fundraiser ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6884a493d8295b120ad4e8b6 :address "9-11 Crescent W, Blackpool, Thornton-Cleveleys FY5 1AD, UK";
