                            :longitude "-3.041335"^^xsd:double.
id:6884ac392fc041aca99346e5 :activityDescription """About the Role:
We’re looking for a friendly, practical volunteer to help keep our counselling hubs safe, welcoming, and well-maintained for the hundreds of people who walk through our doors each week. This role is perfect for a retired or trainee tradesperson with a few hours to spare and a heart for the community.

Tasks May Include:

Small repairs (door handles, shelving, fixtures, etc.)

Painting and touch-ups

Assembling or moving furniture

General DIY and safety checks

Keeping therapy rooms looking fresh and cared for

What We’re Looking For:

Basic DIY or trades experience

A can-do attitude and attention to detail

Respect for the calm, confidential environment of our hubs

Someone reliable, friendly, and happy to work independently or with others

What You’ll Gain:

The joy of helping others in a tangible way

A chance to use your practical skills for a great cause

Plenty of tea, biscuits, and community spirit

Flexible hours to suit your schedule""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6720b4fd25befcb723b95a33;
                            :activityTitle "Maintenance/Caretaker";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6884ac392fc041aca99346e6 :address "Waterloo Rd, Blackpool FY4 1AD, UK";
