id:6884af63b9a80af1c213f593 :activityDescription """About the Role:
We’re looking for a talented and enthusiastic volunteer writer to help us tell our story and secure vital funding. This is a fantastic opportunity to gain hands-on experience in grant writing, copywriting, and fundraising communications – all from the comfort of your own home.

You’ll work closely with our CEO and fundraising team to research funding opportunities, draft compelling grant applications, and craft clear, emotive copy that reflects the heart of what we do at Counselling in the Community.

Key Responsibilities:

Researching trusts, foundations, and grant opportunities

Drafting and editing funding applications

Writing powerful copy for impact reports, donor communications, and social media

Helping shape our voice across written materials

Supporting our mission to provide accessible mental health support to all

What We’re Looking For:

Strong writing and editing skills

A passion for mental health, community work, or social impact

Attention to detail and the ability to meet deadlines

Self-motivation and good communication (we’re a friendly team!)

Any prior writing, grant, or fundraising experience is a bonus – but not essential

What You’ll Gain:

Real-world experience writing for a busy, respected charity

Portfolio-worthy work and the potential for references

Flexible remote volunteering that fits your lifestyle

The chance to make a genuine impact through your words""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6720b4fd25befcb723b95a33;
                            :activityTitle "Grant - Bid Writer ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
