                            :organisationDescription """At Commissioned Generation (CIC), we aim to be a supportive force in the community, offering young people a sense of security, belonging, and opportunity. By fostering interpersonal connections, providing skill-building programs, and creating a supportive network, we strive to empower young individuals to become agents of positive change.

Our programs provide training in diverse skill sets while offering a supportive environment for personal and professional growth. Beyond skill development, we actively encourage young people to give back to their local communities through structured service initiatives throughout the year.

Through these efforts, we aim to instill a sense of social responsibility, cultivate strong character, and strengthen community ties. We believe that when young people engage in meaningful service, they develop a deeper sense of purpose and fulfillment. Research has also shown that contributing to one's community can reduce stress, boost self-esteem, and foster a sense of achievement.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/87d11fd5-76f8-422f-bfd4-bc109b9ef709_2025-08-02T14:50:05.319Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Commissioned Generation".
id:688e27c9cada85fb3e466a12 :activityDescription """Help steward a Spirit-led media project focused on truth, unity, and creative collaboration.

We’re looking for a reliable and organised volunteer to support the day-to-day running of a Christ-centered production. This behind-the-scenes role is perfect for someone who enjoys planning, communication, and helping teams thrive.

Key Responsibilities:

Schedule filming days, meetings, and creative deadlines
Manage applications and contracts for volunteers and participants
Track episode workflow, guest releases, and logistical needs
Support communication across the team and help maintain a clear, Spirit-led vision
Coordinate sponsorships, collaborations, and promotional ideas (e.g. community screenings, emails, partnerships)
Ensure on-the-day details like lanyards, registration forms, and guest management are in place
Assist in planning a live final episode with videographers and support crew
Ideal for someone who:

Has strong admin or coordination skills
Can commit time weekly and work with a team of creatives
Feels called to support a biblically grounded, ecumenical vision behind the scenes""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:688e259dcada85fb3e46691c;
                            :activityTitle "Administration and project support for series";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
