id:6890b08c338cf04062dd1115 :activityDescription """Volunteer opportunity-DV advisor 

Volunteer opportunity @MEWSO: Domestic Violence Advisor
Organisation: MEWSo (Middle Eastern Women and Society Organisation)
Location: Hybrid-London-based community work
Hours: Depend on availability
Salary: Competitive, based on experience and qualifications
Closing date: Rolling applications accepted
MEWSo is recruiting a committed and experienced volunteer Domestic Violence Advisor to support women from migrant, refugee, and minoritised backgrounds (particularly from Middle Eastern and South Asian communities) who are impacted by domestic abuse.
This is a “By and For” position, meaning the advisor must bring both lived or deep professional understanding of the community they serve. The successful candidate will join a small, dedicated team working to offer culturally sensitive, trauma-informed, and rights-based support to women navigating abuse, exclusion, and systemic barriers.
Key Responsibilities:
Provide direct advice, safety planning and support to women experiencing domestic abuse
Advocate for women navigating complex issues including No Recourse to Public Funds (NRPF), housing, and legal challenges
Work closely with local authorities, legal services, and housing teams
Maintain accurate case records and contribute to reports and impact evaluation
Support outreach and community education activities
 
Essential Criteria:
Formal qualification/certificate in domestic abuse support (e.g., IDVA or equivalent)
At least 2 years’ experience in supporting women affected by domestic abuse
Deep understanding of the experiences of migrant and refugee women, including barriers related to immigration status, language, and cultural pressure
Knowledge of NRPF policy and its implications for survivors
Strong engagement skills with Middle Eastern and/or South Asian communities
Ability to work confidentially and uphold safeguarding best practice
Excellent communication, organisational, and teamwork skills
Ideally recommend speak Arabic language 
Desirable:
Experience in multi-agency working or partnership settings
Understanding of trauma-informed approaches
If you believe in empowering women and want to make a difference in your community, we’d love to hear from you. To apply, please email your CV and a short cover letter explaining why you are a good fit for this role to: office@mewso.org 
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64260fe2de05bf8ae7c99f64;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer opportunity-DV advisor ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:6890cd088d1953be4dd47ae9 :activityDescription """Registration support help us welcome and register our students for their classes, using our CRM Software (Salesforce). They are key in ensuring attendance is registered and making sure students know which classroom they need to go to. Registration support volunteers are provided with a short training on registering students on our system and can request to become digital fellows. Digital fellows complete a Salesforce online, self-paced course (in 27 languages) leading to a qualification, access fortnightly digital mentorship by our digital instructor, are provided with a tablet to practice, a CV review.

Time Commitment in Newcastle: 2 hours per week from Monday to Thursday, between 9:30 and 16:00. 
Tasks & Responsibilities: 
The following points are a guide, rather than a definitive list, to help with role definition. 

Registration support volunteer are expected to: 
•	Be punctual; 
•	Carefully register all students for their classes;
•	Signpost students to relevant events and opportunities (shared with you be staff)
•	Attend appropriate training sessions or meetings (with the Project Manager or Officer), including online;
•	Respect the privacy of the students;
•	Maintain appropriate professional relationships and boundaries with staff, volunteers, and students; (do not swap phone number with the student)
•	Treat all students equally and be sensitive to cultural and religious differences;
•	Report any concerns/difficulties regarding students directly to the Officer or Project Manager as early as possible;
•	Treat all information about students as confidential (except for safeguarding concerns which should be reported to a staff member / Safeguarding Lead); 
•	Abide by the values and ethos of Action Foundation.

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:688f774977d87e464e071764;
                            :activityTitle "Registration Support";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6890cd088d1953be4dd47aea :address "The CastleGate, Melbourne Street, Newcastle upon Tyne";
                            :latitude "54.9720926"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.6051341"^^xsd:double.
id:6890cd9ec9ce0a7f76d4045a :activityDescription "set up classrooms with tea, coffee, and refreshments, creating a welcoming and warm atmosphere, and to help moving things back to the kitchen. To communicate to the Project Manager when it is time to buy new supplies. Timely communication with the Project Manager will be necessary in order to access ingredients and ensure Health and Safety rules are followed.";
