id:68910c37039052113e8b6b6f :activityDescription """Join us in making the Green Meadows Festival, an annual celebration of green living and climate action, a success!
 
We're gearing up for our annual celebration on September 6th, 2025 at Queens Walk Recreation Ground (12-4pm) and we’d love YOUR help to make it another unforgettable one.
 
Event Date: September 6th, 2025
Location: Queens Walk Recreation Ground
Time: 12:00 PM – 4:00 PM
 
Whether you can volunteer for a few hours on the day or lend a hand behind the scenes beforehand, your support makes all the difference. Free refreshments and food will be provided.
 
Ways you can support:
In the run up:
 * Marketing/social media support, content creation
 * Sign painting & making
 
On the day:
 * Setting up, packing away & tidying up
 * Greeting attendees on the Welcome Desk
 * Content creation
 * Stewarding & advising attendees
 * Serving food and drinks and helping with the tea/coffee station
 * Supporting stalls, activities, live talks & more
 
We will do our best to honour your preferences—no matter what you're interested in helping with, we’ll try to accommodate you. Every contribution makes a difference, and your support is truly appreciated.
 
Have an impact in the community:
Your support ensures the success of the Green Meadows Festival, an annual outdoor event free to the community that aims to inspire positive action on climate change. Join us to make a difference in your community and help make this event a success - so more people in Nottingham can access green initiatives and learn about climate change.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68764a5c8e328c6f50449046;
                            :activityTitle "Festival volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68910c37039052113e8b6b70 :address "Queens Walk, Nottingham";
                            :latitude "52.9422795"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.1505976"^^xsd:double.
id:689173f58351bd66ca0784bb :activityDescription """We are looking for volunteers to support our Visitor Experience Team  at Fairburn Ings, in ensuring that all our outdoor visitor areas are always looking fabulous and to help us to maintain the highest quality of visitor experience. This will include car park areas, paths to and from our visitor facilities and the surrounding areas, as well as some trails on the reserve. You will be alongside other volunteers, ensuring that in maintaining these areas we also protect the natural environment. You will be out and about on the reserve in this varied practical role, part of a team of Quality Control and Maintenance volunteers.
The role can be undertaken on any weekday and we are especially looking for people who can volunteer on Fridays.

**Main Tasks:**
- Checking: paths, around the car park area, to and from visitor facilities, some trails, visitor areas such as picnic areas and around the Fairburn Visitor Centre for any issues. 
- Maintaining these areas to ensure that grass and wild flowers are not impeding use or presenting a risk to visitors, that there are no branches overhanging paths and presenting a hazard, and that paths are not blocked in any way.  
- Keeping information boards looking clean and presentable. 
- Generally ensuring that areas that visors use around the entrances, car parks and facilities look and feel well maintained and hazard free, but keeping a natural informal feel to these areas. 

**You will:** 
- Have some experience of garden maintenance. 
- Have some experience using garden tools, including power tools such as petrol mower, strimmer, hedge cutter etc. would be desirable, however full training in their use will be provided. 
- Be enthusiastic about maintaining a high standard of facilities and understanding of why this is needed. 
- Be flexible and happy to take the initiative to maintain a quality environment for visitors. 
- Have a friendly approach and able to interact with the public.
- Be able to work independently and as part of a team. 

You will be working with a great, friendly team on a beautiful nature reserve. You will get to meet lots of new people all committed to nature. You can claim your travel expenses when volunteering, and you will be provided with a uniform and all the resources, equipment and training you need to undertake your role. You will have opportunities to learn new things and gain new skills and to learn about our reserves and the wildlife that is found here. You will need to undertake some essential training and you will be supported by a line manager and have opportunities to discuss your role with them.

This role is not suitable for under 18's. 

*Clicking on ‘More about this role’ will take you to the generic ‘role profile’ for this opportunity. A role profile is the family to which an opportunity belongs and informs the vetting and training requirements, but may differ from the role described.*""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Practical Reserve Work (Aire Valley Quality Control and Maintenance Volunteer)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:689173f58351bd66ca0784bc :address "Fairburn Ings, Newton Lane, Castleford, Yorkshire West Riding, WF10 2BH, England";
                            :latitude "53.745685"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.324136"^^xsd:double.
id:689173fe6d04b947275e8545 :activityDescription """The RSPB manages a big network of nature reserves which are havens for wildlife, and importantly very special places for people of all ages and abilities to visit and experience a nature rich landscape.

Nature is in trouble, there aren't many places left where wildlife can thrive, that is why we want to welcome more people to these places.

We are looking for volunteers who can help with all our visitor engagement activities. Can you provide a warm welcome to visitors and share knowledge & enthusiasm about the species on our reserves? The Lookout Welcome Centre is a family focussed, educational space welcoming a variety of people from complete beginners to those who are already nature lovers.

We are looking for a ‘people person’ with good communication skills and enthusiasm for nature. Full training and support will be provide for this role.

This is a really rewarding and enjoyable role, as you will be working with a friendly team on a beautiful nature reserve, and you will have the opportunity to make new friends, learn, and spend time outdoors. You will get to meet loads of new people in this role, enjoying conversation and helping people have a wonderful visit.

This role is not suitable for under 18’s.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Engagement Volunteer (On Reserves) (Bowling Green Marsh Lookout Team)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:689173fe6d04b947275e8546 :address "Bowling Green Marsh, Bowling Green Rd, Topsham, Exeter, Devon, EX3 0BG, England";
                            :latitude "50.6793"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-3.45715"^^xsd:double.
id:6891e2303086f01dc0c0911e :activityDescription """Available from 20/09/2025

Location: Donard Park, Newcastle, Northern Ireland Date: Saturday, 20th September 2025

We’re looking for friendly and enthusiastic volunteers to help us make this event unforgettable.

About the Event

The Slieve Donard Trek is a fully guided 11km hike, climbing 840 metres over 5–8 hours. Participants will challenge themselves on forest trails and steep ground to reach the summit — and we’ll be there to cheer them on every step of the way.

Volunteer Roles

Before the Trek:

-Welcome participants as they arrive
-Help with check-in and registration
-Cheer them off as they begin their trek

After the Trek:

-Help set up the post-trek reception
-Welcome participants back and congratulate them
-Hand out medals and thank them for supporting Mencap
-Create a fun and celebratory atmosphere with clappers, whistles and big smiles

Why Volunteer? By giving just a few hours of your time, you will:

-Support Mencap’s vital work for people with a learning disability
-Be part of a warm, inclusive team
-Help raise awareness and celebrate our amazing fundraisers
-Receive a full briefing and support on the day
-Have your travel expenses covered (in line with our policy)

Who Can Volunteer?

Anyone aged 18+ who is:

-Friendly and approachable
-Reliable, kind and patient
-A good communicator
-Willing to follow guidance and work as part of a team
-Inclusive and accepting of others
-No experience needed — just bring your energy and enthusiasm. 

About Mencap
 Mencap is the leading learning disability charity in England, Wales and Northern Ireland. We support people to live happy and healthy lives, challenge prejudice, and campaign for change.
Our events help fund services like Mencap Direct, advocacy programmes, and national campaigns such as Treat Me Well. We couldn’t do it without our volunteers.

Interested? Email us at volunteering@mencap.org.uk to sign up or ask any questions.

Let’s make this trek one to remember.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cceca0624f3ab9fafe38;
                            :activityTitle "Events Volunteer (Volunteer at the Slieve Donard Trek – Be Part of Something Special!)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6891e2313086f01dc0c0911f :address "5 Donard Park, Newcastle";
                            :latitude "54.20597799999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-5.894234700000001"^^xsd:double.
id:6891eaa88ed46e45caa9c664 :activityDescription """Mentors sought, able to provide 1-2 hours support per week to disadvantaged young people, either within the care system or who are at risk of going into care.

Opportunities available across Kent, full training and support is provided.

Please help us change lives and help young people to thrive.

All training provided, and all expenses are covered.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ce71a0624f3ab9fb27d1;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Mentoring";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6892064e1e863d873b8f906b :activityDescription """6 months
Are you keen to help save nature, would like to utilise your existing office-based skills and have up to 1 day a week to spare?

We are looking for a volunteer who can help assist with developing and updating our projects database. This is part of our efforts to improve knowledge management on RSPB's operation in the Greater Gola Landscape in West Africa. By opening up our work to volunteers in this way, it means we can scale up what we can achieve and do more for nature.

You will be a good all round 'people person', have a keen attention to detail and great organisational skills as well as a confident user of Microsoft SharePoint.

This is a great opportunity to utilise your existing skills and learn new ones, whilst working as part of a small, friendly team. There is room for development within the role, an opportunity to volunteer for additional days or role-share.

This opportunity is remote-based.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Administrator (Gola Landscape)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68920788d34b7a1dbdae3289 :address "United Kingdom";
