                            :longitude "-3.435973"^^xsd:double.
id:68920db31e863d873b8f92df :activityDescription """Role Purpose: To support FARE Scotland’s main site by helping with practical tasks, repairs, and general upkeep. Whether you're a DIY enthusiast, a retired tradesperson, or just someone handy with a toolbox — this flexible role lets you lend your skills when you're available.

What You Can Get Involved In:

·       Light repairs and general upkeep (e.g. fixing shelves, tightening fixtures)

·       Painting and touch-ups around the site

·       Basic plumbing or electrical checks (if qualified)

·       Moving furniture or equipment

·       Supporting staff with site improvement projects

Skills and Qualities Needed

Volunteers will come from a wide range of backgrounds and will have many different qualities and skills. Essential qualities for this role are:

Practical skills in DIY, maintenance, or repairs
Ability to work safely and follow instructions
Reliability and good timekeeping
Friendly and respectful approach
Commitment:

This can be a flexible on-call volunteer role, we’ll contact you when we have a project that we need help with. Or this can be a weekly commitment of 1-5 hours per week. Whatever is best for you!

What’s in it for you?

·       Use your practical skills to improve a valued community space

·       Gain experience in site maintenance and facilities support

·       Be part of a friendly, hands-on team

·       Enhance your CV

·       Make a visible and lasting impact in your local area

Support and Training

·       Induction and guidance from staff""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:686b9bb4cf3b950b85a90188;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Handyperson / Maintenance Support";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68920db31e863d873b8f92e0 :address "31 Drumlanrig Avenue, Glasgow";
                            :latitude "55.8689292"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-4.0984676"^^xsd:double.
id:68920e0bdf6bd09b7ae069a2 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """About Us:
We are a new Black-led Community Interest Company (CIC) dedicated to supporting survivors of childhood trauma in the Black British Caribbean community through radical storytelling, podcasting, and community healing. Our flagship platform is a podcast that gives survivors a safe space to speak their truth freely and powerfully.

Our goal is to build a digital and social media presence that informs, uplifts, and activates our community—all while remaining free at the point of access.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/e3734263-2deb-4f90-a937-04b28d90947a_2025-08-05T13:58:34.642Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "tell my truth and shame the devil";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.tellshame.com/>.
id:68920e45df6bd09b7ae06a02 :activityDescription """We're looking for friendly, enthusiastic volunteers to help run our Stepford Café — a welcoming social hub where players, families, and locals can enjoy a hot drink, a tasty bite, and a warm atmosphere while the games are on. Whether you're great with people, love being part of a team, or just want to give back to your community, your support will help keep the café buzzing and make a real difference.

What you can get involved in:

·       Serving teas, coffees, and light snacks

·       Chatting with customers and making them feel welcome

·       Helping with basic cleaning and tidying

·       Restocking supplies and keeping the café organised

·       Supporting events or match days with extra hands on deck

Volunteers will come from a wide range of background and will have many different qualities and skills. We are looking for:

·       A friendly, approachable attitude

·       Willingness to muck in and help out wherever needed

·       Reliability

·       It would be great if you had experience in a café or service industry setting however, experience isn’t essential —a positive spirit and a willingness to get involved will do just fine!

Commitment:

We’re ideally looking for volunteers who can help out once or twice a week for a couple of hours — but we’re totally flexible. Whether you can commit weekly or just want to pop in when you can manage, we’d love to hear from you.

What’s in it for you?

·       Build confidence and customer service skills

·       Meet new people and be part of a supportive team

·       Gain experience in a service setting

·       Make a real difference in your local community

·       Boost your CV

·       Enjoy free hot drinks and good chat while you help out!

Support and Training

We’ll provide all the guidance you need, including a warm welcome, on-the-job training, and ongoing support from our friendly team.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:686b9bb4cf3b950b85a90188;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Café Helper";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68920e45df6bd09b7ae06a03 :address "1514 Edinburgh Road, Glasgow";
                            :latitude "55.858478"^^xsd:double;
