id:6894783749913f41c34f2a79 :activityDescription """From factories to schools, leisure centres to steelworks, golf clubs to community centres — we’ve got over 40 sites across the UK signed up and ready to build over the next two years. Together, we already own 12 large solar rooftops, and this is just the beginning!

We’re looking to apply for a variety of awards — from general sustainability ones to specialised community energy awards — and we need your help with the applications!

If you’re up for helping us, the next step would be to hop on a call with one of our team members to talk through some of the key areas we want to focus on. We’ll even share some of our old submissions that you can use for reference.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6878db70cb9160db05f23ff5;
                            :activityTitle "Help us to write an award nomination";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6894804dc1877e5f3f4923d4 :activityDescription """
Our volunteers play an important part in the services we provide and the people we support. If you are looking for a rewarding role where you will making a big difference, then join us here at RJ4ALL

About The Community Fridge Service

The RJ4All Community Fridge provides quality food to communities in South East London while simultaneously preventing food waste. Our Community Fridge is a social space that does not only meet the food needs of community members but also provide a space to connect with others

What will you be doing as a Food Waste Hero ?

Collect surplus food from Rotherhithe Community Kitchen at Peter Hills C of E Primary School, 2 Beatson Walk, London SE16 5ED on Sundays 11-12pm and Thursdays from 12-1pm to Rotherhithe Community Centre, 30 Plough Way, London SE16 2LJ
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6602c279a3a5c888847ede82;
                            :activityTitle "Food Waste Heroe";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6894804dc1877e5f3f4923d5 :address "Peter Hills C of E Primary School, 2 Beatson Walk, London SE16 5ED, UK";
