                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:6894a98e5a72ff4721813969 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription "Home-Start Exeter, East & Mid Devon recruits and trains volunteers to visit families in their own home, usually once a week, to provide emotional and practical support.  All of the families we support must have at least one child aged five or under.   Families tell us what a huge difference it makes to their lives to have that support at a time of need, often describing our volunteers as “a ray of sunshine” or a “life-line”.  The best part of our work is to see the children start to thrive again as the volunteer helps the parents work through their difficulties.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/cdee0c36-b325-4c06-9c51-a2e7f67e4077_2025-08-07T13:26:38.254Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Home-Start Exeter, East and Mid Devon";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://homestarteemd.org.uk/>.
id:6894b4041ee35ec926dd5268 :activityDescription """Volunteers needed in Exeter, East Devon and Mid Devon
At the heart of Home-Start’s work is home visiting volunteer support. Home-Start works because our volunteers understand how hard it can be. They work alongside parents, in the family's own home, to help them cope with the stresses and strains of life and make sure they have the skills, confidence and strength they need to nurture their children.

Our volunteers are usually parents themselves or have parenting experience and bring with them personal experience, parenting skills, and knowledge of the resources available within their local area. They are friendly and approachable and can be relied on and trusted by parents to listen without being judgemental, and to respect the needs of each individual family.

Home-visiting volunteers...
Undertake a training course which fully prepares volunteers for their role. 
Receive lots of support both during training, and after, when they are supporting Home-Start families from a designated volunteer co-ordinator.
Can access additional training and social events throughout the year.
Receive all out of pocket expenses incurred whilst volunteering for Home-Start.

If you are interested in joining us as a volunteer please call 01395 542298 and ask for an application pack or go to our website and download an application pack. We will contact you and arrange an initial interview with one of our volunteer co-ordinators.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6894a98e5a72ff4721813969;
                            :activityTitle "Home-Start Home-Visiting Volunteers - Exeter, East and Mid Devon";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6894b45f2437784209be223d :address "From Home";
