id:6894bdb07d1ad9af720d6e3e :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription "There is currently no care pathway for Autistic people in North Staffs. Lifeworks North Staffs is a charity that supports marginalised, isolated people 14+ in North Staffordshire with Autistic conditions including ADHD, Dyspraxia, Tourette's Syndrome, mostly with mental ill health, and their carers to find a sustainable lifestyle. We do this through helping with social interpretation (advocacy), one-to-one appointments, befriending, lifecoaching, client activities and drop-ins, carer’s groups and befriending. Established in 2006 we now have over 850 clients and 330 carer’s that we are supporting.";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/19dca285-df0b-456b-8b37-92b1df4177b9_2025-08-19T13:53:39.689Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Lifeworks North Staffs";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.lifeworksnorthstaffs.org.uk/>.
id:6894c227ef931b079d4c697f :activityDescription """Are you passionate about local community life? Do you want to use your skills or lived experience to support a small charity making a big difference in Hackney? We’re looking for new Trustees to join the Board at Clapton Commons. 
Clapton Commons is a small, grassroots charity based in north Hackney. We run warm, welcoming community spaces like Liberty Hall and the Common Room, and we support people to organise and act on what matters most in their local area, from tenant rights to food justice and community celebrations. 
This is a brilliant opportunity to:
• Support community-led change in your local area
• Help a small, values-led charity thrive
• Learn more about charity strategy, finance and leadership
• Share your insights and skills in a collaborative way
• Be part of something joyful, grassroots and important
We are especially keen to hear from people who reflect the diversity of Clapton and Hackney and from people who haven’t been trustees before.
We’d love to hear from you. If you’re interested please arrange a chat with Aaron Barbour, our Interim-Director, at: aaronbarbour1@gmail.com and/or with William Taylor, our Chair of Trustees at: fatherwilliamtaylor@hotmail.com """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6849aa6de700cdd86eb2e252;
                            :activityTitle "Trustee";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6894c227ef931b079d4c6980 :address "1 Clapton Terrace, London";
                            :latitude "51.56982"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.0642473"^^xsd:double.
id:6894f6cc74c2a5ffa010f8be :activityDescription """Whether you're an experienced filmmaker or an enthusiastic beginner who's never picked up a camera, this is your chance  to explore video production for public benefit. The charity WORLDwrite is offering an exclusive, hands-on volunteer opportunity to train with professional equipment and film the Battle of Ideas Festival, held in the heart of Westminster, London.
This dynamic opportunity combines training, teamwork, and the thrill of capturing a fast-paced, intellectually stimulating festival on film. Over an action-packed weekend, you'll help produce high-quality video content from more than 100 challenging debates and discussions on everything from politics, economics, and education to science, technology, and the arts. The festival is renowned for its dedication to thought-provoking, public conversations. Since its inception in 2005, WORLDwrite has proudly served as media partner for this prestigious event, and we want you to be part of our 2025 crew.
As a Festival TV Maker, you'll be trained in every aspect of live debate filming. Your efforts will contribute to the production of over 50 high-quality debate videos—shared online for a global audience. And yes, every volunteer receives a credit, a powerful asset for any aspiring media professional. You’ll also receive a full festival pass and local travel expenses, lunches and references are provided.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cf80a0624f3ab9fb3ffe;
                            :activityTitle "Festival TV makers with free training provided";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6894f6cc74c2a5ffa010f8bf :address "Millfields Rd, Lower Clapton, London E5 0AL, UK";
