                            :longitude "-4.618736"^^xsd:double.
id:6899591b4f2e150c30bb3d49 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """hi, I'm a 17 year old student passionate about supporting other students. Our mission is to empower young ESL girls in STEM to unleash their full potential and inspire them to become the next generation of women leaders in science and technology. We are building an online platform to support GCSE and A-level students in Maths, Further Maths, and Science by providing high-quality resources — including translated versions in multiple languages to help students overcome their language barriers. To deepen our impact, we will run weekly mentoring sessions for each subject, supporting students every step of the way. Beyond exam subjects, we also offer coding resources and mentoring designed to teach practical, real-world skills that prepare students for the future. Recognizing the importance of language, we provide simple English conversation guides tailored for both students and their parents, helping bridge communication gaps and support their educational journey while boosting their confidence. To inspire and motivate, we are excited to host talks from women in STEM, sharing their stories and showing our students the incredible
possibilities that lie ahead.

""";
                            :organisationName "stem girls hub";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://stemgirlshub.my.canva.site/>.
id:6899ea37e1f77e32cb5b2b47 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "Make a Smile is a charity built on the principle that all children deserve a childhood. We believe that through no fault of their own, often children under-going hardship can miss vital play opportunities or lose out on opportunities to interact with their idols. Through visits to hospitals, schools, libraries, other children charities (and more!), we bring their favourite characters to life, whether that be a Disney princess or a Marvel superhero.";
                            :organisationName "Make a Smile";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://makeasmile.org.uk/>.
id:6899f6cdce7c945a5bfa49df :activityDescription """What is Make a Smile? 

Make a Smile is a charity that visits disabled, neurodivergent, and disadvantaged children as beloved fictional characters, such as princesses and superheroes, to bring some magic to their day. Learn more about us on our website: https://makeasmile.org.uk/



Why join Make a Smile?

- To put giant smiles on wholesome childrens' faces! (need I say more?) 

- Make a difference in the community and be a part of something bigger than yourself 

- Meet new people and befriend very cool people 

- Enhance your CV, show employers you have a heart! 

- Refine your teamwork, communication and leadership skills



Tasks: 

Imagineers are perfect if you are short on time, so cannot commit to a committee role, or do not want to attend events. Imagineers are a key pillar to Make a Smile as they help with the general running of the charity. They can help with organising events, admin, getting feedback from volunteers, helping with costumes...etc. 

Join our Whatsapp to find out more: https://chat.whatsapp.com/H5zrhuXbaV482BtTvy9eWJ?fbclid=PAZXh0bgNhZW0CMTEAAacqSmjFXpKD7wV7MbGWGUGxG8U0oezzy523fGeaQTKvpzZ2Fjen95pQ8Eww0w_aem_tBgux5dJhzjwZI9PSUD_Dw""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6899ea37e1f77e32cb5b2b47;
                            :activityTitle "Make a Smile Imagineer - help us behind the scenes to run events where other volunteers dress up as disadvantaged children's characters";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6899f7e499bfa9a99c8da140 :activityDescription """What is Make a Smile? 

Make a Smile is a charity that visits disabled, neurodivergent, and disadvantaged children as beloved fictional characters, such as princesses and superheroes, to bring some magic to their day. Learn more about us on our website: https://makeasmile.org.uk/



Why join Make a Smile?

- To put giant smiles on wholesome childrens' faces! (need I say more?) 

- Make a difference in the community and be a part of something bigger than yourself 

- Meet new people and befriend very cool people 

- Enhance your CV, show employers you have a heart! 

- Refine your teamwork, communication and leadership skills

- Have fun at the events!



Tasks: 

As a registered volunteer, you will get information on upcoming events you can attend. Your job will be to attend events out of character and act as a supporting staff. This can involve playing games with the children, chatting with children, assisting characters at events, taking photos...etc. If you are nervous about dressing up as a character, this can also be a good jumping pad to that and get you introduced to what events look like. 

Join our Whatsapp chat to find out more: https://chat.whatsapp.com/H5zrhuXbaV482BtTvy9eWJ?fbclid=PAZXh0bgNhZW0CMTEAAacqSmjFXpKD7wV7MbGWGUGxG8U0oezzy523fGeaQTKvpzZ2Fjen95pQ8Eww0w_aem_tBgux5dJhzjwZI9PSUD_Dw""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6899ea37e1f77e32cb5b2b47;
                            :activityTitle "Make a Smile Magic Maker - help out events where other volunteers are dressing up as disadvantaged children's characters";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:6899f9a599bfa9a99c8da1a7 :activityDescription """What is Make a Smile? 

Make a Smile is a charity that visits disabled, neurodivergent, and disadvantaged children as beloved fictional characters, such as princesses and superheroes, to bring some magic to their day. Learn more about us on our website: https://makeasmile.org.uk/



Why join Make a Smile?

- To put giant smiles on wholesome childrens' faces! (need I say more?) 

- Make a difference in the community and be a part of something bigger than yourself 

- Meet new people and befriend very cool people 

- Enhance your CV, show employers you have a heart! 

- Refine your teamwork, communication and leadership skills

- Have fun at the events you helped organise and keep running!


Tasks: 

It is the role of the Wellbeing Officer to ensure that the voice of the members is heard on committee. It is recommended that the Wellbeing Officer implement a wellbeing programme and a widening access policy. The Wellbeing Officer should ensure that there is a way for the members to voice concerns to them and proactively provide support and wellbeing. Finally, the Wellbeing Officer will be expected to assist the President and Vice President with committee responsibilities.

Time commitment:

We ask our committee members to commit 2 hours a week (excluding attending events). This can be in the form of contacting societies for collaboration, creating social media posts, organising events...etc. However, in general, our committee roles are very flexible - we are all busy students, so communication is key! Let the team know when you have a particularly busy week, and we can help each other out. Also, with some roles, you can choose when in the term to perform the bulk of your responsibilities. Thus, once we get the ball rolling, it really should not take up too much time. 


Requirements:

Nice and pleasant person to work with, can work and effectively communicate in a team, problem solver, passionate about our cause - no volunteering experience required 

Benefits and perks:

Certificates can be produced. Full committee training is provided before you start, and additional training sessions are provided throughout the year to elevate your skillset. You will feel very supported in this role by your training officer, president, regional manager, and corresponding trustee. 

More info and sign up here: https://forms.office.com/r/YzLR2HHJKA if you have any questions, feel free to DM us on Insta""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6899ea37e1f77e32cb5b2b47;
                            :activityTitle "Make a Smile Wellbeing Officer - Children's charity involving dressing up as childrens' favourite characters needs a Wellbeing Officer for the 25/26 year";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
