Tasks: 

 A Recruitment Officer is selected by the committee and focuses on encouraging members to join. In terms of member recruitment, they will need to help organise and run training sessions, organise and seek recruitment opportunities such as hosting stalls at the Volunteering Fayre and Open Days. Finally, they will need to encourage trainees to complete the essential training and attend their first event.

Time commitment:

We ask our committee members to commit 2 hours a week (excluding attending events). This can be in the form of contacting societies for collaboration, creating social media posts, organising events...etc. However, in general, our committee roles are very flexible - we are all busy students, so communication is key! Let the team know when you have a particularly busy week, and we can help each other out. Also, with some roles, you can choose when in the term to perform the bulk of your responsibilities. Thus, once we get the ball rolling, it really should not take up too much time. 


Requirements:

Nice and pleasant person to work with, can work and effectively communicate in a team, problem solver, passionate about our cause - no volunteering experience required 

Benefits and perks:

Certificates can be produced. Full committee training is provided before you start, and additional training sessions are provided throughout the year to elevate your skillset. You will feel very supported in this role by your training officer, president, regional manager, and corresponding trustee. 

More info and sign up here: https://forms.office.com/r/YzLR2HHJKA if you have any questions, feel free to DM us on Insta
""";
