                            :organisationDescription """Unseen Expeditions pioneers long-term, self-supported global expeditions that combine physical endurance, deep immersion in nature, and authentic storytelling. Each project is partnered with an aligned charity, providing a real-world beneficiary impact. Our mission is to advance mental health awareness, foster connection to nature, and inspire resilience and personal growth.

Flagship Project – The Unseen Mile:
A 4.5-year, 25,000-mile walking expedition across 37 countries and four continents. The expedition is designed to demonstrate the mental health benefits of endurance exploration while sharing authentic stories to inspire others.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/4d3551f4-ab22-4bf1-9f3b-d38f6a62f163_2025-08-14T15:05:33.976Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Unseen Expeditions";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://unseenexpeditions.carrd.co/>.
id:689e066369e34133d063e052 :activityDescription """Chair / Trustee – Unseen Expeditions CIO

Location: Flexible / Remote (UK-based)

Time Commitment: Approx. 3–5 hours per month (may be more during start-up and registration phase)

About Us:
Unseen Expeditions is a Charitable Incorporated Organisation (CIO) supporting aligned UK-registered mental health charities, and other mission-led expedition projects. Our flagship expedition, The Unseen Mile, is a 4.5-year journey covering 25,000 miles across 37 countries. We aim to inspire, raise awareness of mental health, and share unique storytelling and learning experiences from the field.

As a new CIO, we are in the process of recruiting our initial trustee board to enable registration and formally launch the charity.

Role Overview:
We are seeking a Chair / Trustee to lead the board of Unseen Expeditions CIO. The Chair is a key governance role, ensuring that the charity operates effectively, meets its legal and regulatory responsibilities, and supports the delivery of its mission.

Key Responsibilities:
-Provide leadership to the board and ensure effective governance
-Chair trustee meetings and ensure decisions are properly recorded
-Support trustee recruitment, induction, and development
-Act as a main point of contact for stakeholders and regulators
-Oversee compliance with charity law and CIO regulations
-Assist with reporting to the Charity Commission
-Help guide the initial registration and start-up processes

Person Specification:
-Strong leadership, organisational, and strategic skills
-Familiarity with charity governance and trustee responsibilities (training can be provided)
-Commitment to the mission and values of Unseen Expeditions and Adventure Therapy
-Ability to work collaboratively with a small trustee team
-UK-based (for legal trustee requirements)

Benefits:
-Play a pivotal role in shaping a new charity and its high-profile expedition projects
-Contribute to mental health awareness and adventure-led impact projects
-Flexible, supportive role within a passionate team
-Opportunity to influence the governance and strategic direction from the outset

How to Apply:
Please submit a CV and a short cover letter outlining your interest in the role to: rednallthomas@gmail.com""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:689dfb1693a21cebe388e73f;
                            :activityTitle "Chair / Trustee - Unseen Expeditions CIO";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:689e0dc24e0d5cc47eeb178e :activityDescription """Location: Fully flexible / Remote – open to applicants anywhere in the UK
Time Commitment: Approx. 2–4 hours per month (may be more during start-up and registration phase)

About Us
Unseen Expeditions UK is a newly forming Charitable Incorporated Organisation (CIO) supporting mission-led charities and expedition projects across the UK and internationally. Our flagship initiative, The Unseen Mile, is a 4.5-year journey covering 25,000 miles across 37 countries. Through this and future projects, we aim to inspire, raise awareness for important causes, and share unique storytelling and learning experiences from the field.

We are currently recruiting our initial trustee board to help launch and register the charity.

Role Overview
We are seeking a Secretary / Trustee to join our board and ensure strong governance. The Secretary will help the charity meet its legal and regulatory responsibilities while supporting the delivery of its mission.

Key Responsibilities
-Maintain accurate records of trustee meetings and decisions
-Ensure compliance with charity law and CIO regulations
-Support trustee recruitment, induction, and governance processes
-Act as a point of contact for official communications
-Assist with reporting to the Charity Commission
-Help guide the charity through its registration and initial set-up

Person Specification & Requirements
Strong organisational and administrative skills
-Familiarity with charity governance and trustee responsibilities (training can be provided)
-Commitment to the mission and values of Unseen Expeditions and its partnered charities
-Ability to work collaboratively with a small, remote trustee team
-Comfortable working remotely and communicating online with a UK-wide board
-UK-based (required for legal trustee responsibilities)
-2–4 hours per month commitment (more during start-up if possible)
-Basic tools for communication (email, phone, video calls)

What You’ll Gain
-Opportunity to shape and govern a new, high-profile charity from launch
-Hands-on experience in charity leadership and governance
-Contribution to awareness-raising and adventure-led impact projects
-Recognition for your role in mission-driven initiatives, including The Unseen Mile and future projects
-Flexible, fully remote role within a passionate, purpose-driven team

How to Apply
Please submit a CV and a short cover letter outlining your interest in the role to: rednallthomas@gmail.com""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:689dfb1693a21cebe388e73f;
                            :activityTitle "Secretary Trustee - Unseen Expeditions UK CIO";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
