id:689f68cc4419b9682572ffd6 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "OmWana is a grassroots charity working to give Ugandan children in need a brighter future by helping them access education, with a special focus on girls who are often less likely to be enrolled in school. Every pound we raise goes directly towards covering school fees, uniforms, menstrual pads, and school supplies for the 12 children we sponsor. Alongside this, we empower Ugandan women by buying their handmade baskets and tote bags, which we then sell in Scottish markets, providing them with a sustainable income to support their own families. ";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/034a5653-69e8-4b88-8bdf-4a6fbb058f5a_2025-08-15T17:05:15.624Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "OmWana";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.omwana.org/en>.
id:689f6c0786e768eddf326fed :activityDescription """About Omwana
Omwana is a small, dedicated charity that supports children’s education in Uganda by providing scholarships, school supplies, and other essential resources. We believe every child deserves the chance to learn, grow, and build a brighter future.

The Role
We are looking for a motivated and creative volunteer to help us strengthen our communication and fundraising efforts. You will play a key role in raising awareness of our work, engaging our supporters, and helping us secure the funds needed to keep children in school.

What You’ll Do
-Assist with creating and posting engaging content on our social media platforms.
-Support the organisation of online or community fundraising campaigns.
-Reach out to potential donors, partners, and local media.
-Share ideas to grow our audience and donor base.

What We’re Looking For
-Good written communication skills (French is a +++).
-Creative mindset and enthusiasm for storytelling.
-Basic knowledge of social media (Facebook, Instagram, etc.).
-Interest in fundraising, marketing, or non-profit work.
-Reliability and ability to work independently.

Time Commitment
Flexible – a few hours per week, remote volunteering. We’re happy to work around your availability.

What You’ll Gain
-Experience in charity communications and fundraising.
-The chance to make a real difference in children’s lives.
-References and recognition for your contribution.

How to Apply
If you’re passionate about education and want to use your skills to help children in Uganda, we’d love to hear from you! Please email us at with a short introduction and why you’d like to volunteer.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:689f68cc4419b9682572ffd6;
                            :activityTitle "📢 Volunteer Opportunity – Communication & Fundraising Assistant for Omwana";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:689f6c3868f3ba8e88648587 :address "From Home";
