id:68a489b04ff744a4731dcdd0 :activityDescription """The Edible Classroom is Earth Trust’s newest outdoor learning resource! Within this 1.5-acre plot, close to 
the Earth Trust centre, we have built 80 no-dig market garden beds, and a ‘camp’ with three beautiful 
weatherproof bell tents. We’ve also created outdoor cooking areas to turn super fresh produce into delicious 
food, and a large, shaded area for eating it whilst socialising and developing friendships. 
A huge amount of activity will take place here. This will be centred around our Earth Skills learning 
programme for young people, and new volunteering opportunities for young people and adults. Secondary 
school aged students will attend weekly with their school or supporting charity to learn valuable skills for 
life and employment. 
We are recruiting volunteers to support this work. If you are interested in small scale commercial production 
of fruit, vegetables and herbs, this is for you. There is also the opportunity to engage with children and young 
people in the space as part of our education programme, but that is very much an optional extra!
Time required: Wednesdays and/or Thursdays each week. Flexible according to your schedule once 
you have received full training. 
Tasks: Sowing seed, propagation, weeding, harvesting, sorting produce for sale 
(no previous experience required)""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ed04c794380477b73fa1;
                            :activityTitle "Earth Trust Edibles Grower";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68a489b04ff744a4731dcdd1 :address "Little Wittenham, Abingdon OX14 4QZ";
