id:68a4910abe65366a8e6934da :activityDescription """Join Us as a Trustee!
Are you passionate about making a difference in your community and changing lives ? 
We are seeking dedicated and enthusiastic individuals to join our Board of Trustees.
About the Role:
As a trustee, you will play a vital role in shaping the future of our organisation. You’ll help guide our strategy, ensure good governance, and support our vision of A resilient, truly inclusive Neurodiverse society, where all are enabled to achieve their potential with the acceptance, timely support, and opportunity they need to be recognised and celebrated for who they are. 
Working under 4 core themes of the support to ENABLE success, the opportunities to ENJOY, the information and advocacy to EMPOWER and the skills to EMBRACE this life less ordinary, we aim to ensure that everyone has an equitable opportunity to live their best lives, lifelong. With the New Inclusion Hub now providing a safe space of belonging and acceptance for all and offering the opportunity to extend the hand of friendship, our skills, experience and expertise to any member of the community experiencing loneliness and isolation, this new chapter promises to be an exciting and fulfilling one for all. 
. .
What We’re Looking For:
•	Commitment to our values and mission
•	Strategic thinkers who can see the bigger picture and help set our direction
•	Good communicators who can share ideas clearly and work well with others
•	Willingness to attend regular board meetings; usually monthly or quarterly, depending on the role you choose. 
•	Ability to work collaboratively and contribute ideas
•	We have several roles within the board, from fundraising and marketing to finance and admin whatever your skill base, we have a role to suit you. 
What You’ll Gain:
•	The chance to make a real difference
•	Experience in governance and leadership
•	Opportunities for personal and professional development
•	The satisfaction of supporting a cause you care about


Please note this is an enhanced DBS checked role  
This is a voluntary position, but your contribution will have a lasting impact.
We welcome applications from all backgrounds and experiences.
How to Apply:
If you’re interested in joining us as a trustee please 

email chair@empathyforspecialchildren.org for a chat or to set up a video call 

or fill in the expression of interest form on the website https://www.empathyforspecialchildren.org/volunteers
To join our board today ! changes lives today, tomorrow and forever.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425fb2ef2d4b77a6e161cf4;
                            :activityTitle "Trustee";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68a4910abe65366a8e6934db :address "Corvedale Road, Craven Arms";
                            :latitude "52.4405876"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.8324316"^^xsd:double.
