id:68a49add114d6a6b4f682b81 :activityDescription """About the 'Include Me' Project
\"Lonely is not being alone, it is feeling that no one cares.\"
The 'Include Me' project, based at the new Empathy Inclusion Hub in Craven Arms, is dedicated to combating loneliness and isolation. While building on our 15 years of experience supporting the neurodiverse, this project extends the warm arms of friendship to any member of the community who feels isolated. We believe that life's journey, age, health, or simply feeling different can make anyone feel out of step. The Inclusion Hub and the Include Me project are here to create a safe place for everyone to belong and find their tribe.
We achieve this through a variety of fun and welcoming sessions, including drop-in coffee mornings, lunch clubs, intergenerational skill-sharing, and even afternoon silent discos for those who still like to \"throw some shapes.\" The 'Include Me' project is all about ensuring Fun, Friendship, Support, and Inclusion is available to all.
This role requires an Enhanced DBS (Disclosure and Barring Service) check. We will guide you through the process, and there will be no cost to you.
The Opportunity
We are looking for friendly and enthusiastic volunteers to join us as 'Include Me' Project Buddies. Your role will be to create a welcoming atmosphere at our sessions, acting as a friendly face and a point of contact for our community. You'll be a vital part of making sure every person who walks through our doors feels comfortable, supported, and included.
What You'll Do
•	Meet and Greet: Welcome people as they arrive, helping them feel at ease from the moment they enter the hub.
•	Be a Friendly Face: Circulate among guests, initiating conversations and making introductions to help new connections form.
•	Support the Empathy Team: Work alongside our staff to ensure the smooth running of each session, from setting up to tidying up and signposting visitors to the relevant member of staff for additional support. 
•	Serve Refreshments: Help set up and serve snacks and drinks, ensuring everyone has what they need.
•	General Support: Lend a hand with any light tasks to keep the events running smoothly.
What's in it for You?
•	Make a Real Difference: Your time and friendly presence will directly help people in your community feel less isolated and more connected.
•	Gain Valuable Experience: This is a chance to develop your communication and interpersonal skills in a supportive, community-focused environment.
•	Be Part of a Team: You'll join a warm and welcoming group of staff and fellow volunteers who are all passionate about our mission.
•	Training and Support: We provide full induction training and ongoing support from the project coordinator.
We're Looking For Someone Who Is...
•	Approachable and warm. You have a natural ability to put people at ease and are genuinely happy to chat.
•	A great listener. You're patient and attentive, ready to listen to what people have to say.
•	Reliable and committed. You'll be a dependable part of our team, showing up with a positive attitude.
•	A team player. You're happy to work collaboratively with our staff and other volunteers.
•	Passionate about our mission. You believe in the importance of combating loneliness and creating a truly inclusive community.
Time Commitment
This role involves a commitment to our scheduled 'Include Me' events, which typically run for a few hours. We will provide a schedule in advance so you can sign up for the events that work for you.

________________________________________
Ready to Help Us Include Everyone?
If you're interested in being a friendly face for our community, we would love to hear from you.
Please contact Sam Goddard at sam@empathyforspecialchildren.org or 01588 671357 to learn more 
Or complete the expression of interest form on the website https://www.empathyforspecialchildren.org/volunteers
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425fb2ef2d4b77a6e161cf4;
                            :activityTitle "Include Me Buddy";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
