                            :longitude "-0.1125002"^^xsd:double.
id:68a5d0dace6e627395d4f335 :activityDescription """Purpose of the Role: 
To support the Into School Programme Coordinator in delivering a comprehensive educational programme for newly arrived and refugee girls aged 11–18, helping them develop their English and Maths skills, confidence, and community bonds. 

Main Responsibilities: 
- Provide classroom and administrative support. 
- Reinforce positive behaviour and engagement. 
- Build supportive relationships with students. 
- Assist in planning and running activities and community events. 
- Help source materials and run errands.
- Prepare and share lunch with students twice a week. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and complete evaluations as required. 
 
Skills and Qualities Required:
- Strong interpersonal and written communication skills. 
- Comfortable working with diverse cultural backgrounds. 
- Computer literacy (Outlook, Excel). 
- Reliable, punctual, and well-organised. 
- Able to work independently and in a team.
- Interest in charity, education, or community development. 
- Flexible and willing to support varied tasks. 
 
Desirable: 
- Community or education experience (including ESOL). 
- Volunteering or youth work background. 
- Knowledge of a second language (e.g. Spanish, Portuguese, Arabic, French). 
- Research or reporting experience. 
 
Commitment: 
- 2–4 days per week (Monday–Thursday), 10:00 am – 5:00 pm. 
- 4 to 6 months during term time, with flexibility to extend. 

Benefits: We reimburse up to £7 for travel and £5 for lunch expenses for each full day of internship. 
- Gain practical experience working in youth services and the charity sector. 
- Develop skills in group facilitation, data management, and community engagement. 
- Contribute to positive outcomes for young people and families. 
- Opportunity to attend volunteer social events and network. 
- Valuable insight into alternative educational and community support settings. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female Into School Intern";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68a5d0dace6e627395d4f336 :address "300-302 Brixton Road, London";
                            :latitude "51.4700721"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.1125002"^^xsd:double.
id:68a5d1a57ab4a459dc3a5eb7 :activityDescription """Purpose of the role: 
Your role is to support the Mentoring Coordinator at the Baytree Centre in delivering a high-quality mentoring programme for around 100 mentoring pairs across the academic year. The programme focuses on academic support (including GCSE preparation), character development, and creating an empowering environment for mentees and mentors. 
 
Main responsibilities: 
- Work closely with the Mentoring Coordinator to plan and deliver academic workshops and activities (e.g., GCSE-focused sessions). 
- Support the creation, updating, and organisation of mentoring toolkits and academic resources. 
- Develop new academic exercises and tools for volunteer mentors to use in their sessions. 
- Accurately input and maintain attendance records, session notes, and other data on Baytree’s internal database. 
- Conduct focus groups and surveys with mentors and mentees to gather feedback and improve the programme. 
- Provide administrative support, including ticking attendance, updating session logs, and following up with mentors or mentees when required. 
- Assist in designing simple promotional or informational materials for the programme (e.g., timetables, resource sheets). 
- Run errands and source resources needed for mentoring activities. 
- Engage positively and respectfully with mentors, mentees, and families accessing the centre. 

Skills and qualities required: 
- Good interpersonal skills, able to work well within a diverse team. 
- Computer literate, with proficiency in Microsoft Outlook and Excel. 
- Ability to work independently with minimal supervision. 
- Good time management and organisational skills. 
- Reliable, punctual, and committed. 
- Interest in mentoring, education, youth development, or community engagement. 
- Flexibility and willingness to assist with a variety of tasks as needed. 
- Experience working with young people, education, or volunteering is desirable. 
 
Commitment:
- 2 to 4 days per week, Monday to Thursday. 
- Hours: 10:30 am – 6:15 pm. 
- Duration: 4 to 6 months, with flexibility to extend if required. 

Benefits: We reimburse up to £7 for travel and £5 for lunch expenses for each full day of internship. 
- Gain practical experience working in youth mentoring and the charity sector. 
- Develop skills in academic resource creation, group facilitation, and data management. 
- Contribute to positive outcomes for young people and volunteers. 
- Valuable insight into mentoring, education, and community support work. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older.

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female Mentoring Intern";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68a5d1a57ab4a459dc3a5eb8 :address "300-302 Brixton Road, London";
                            :latitude "51.4700721"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.1125002"^^xsd:double.
id:68a5d300ce6e627395d4f39c :activityDescription """Youth Service Intern 

Purpose of the role: 
Your role is to support the Youth Team at the Baytree Centre in delivering high-quality programmes and activities for young people and their families. You will assist the team to ensure smooth running of sessions, engage positively with the youth, and contribute to the development of a safe, welcoming, and empowering environment. 

Main responsibilities: 
- Work closely with the programme coordinator to plan, support, and sometimes lead group activities and workshops. 
- Accurately input and maintain data and records on Baytree’s internal database. 
- Provide cover and support for after-school club activities when required. 
- Assist in designing promotional materials such as posters, leaflets, and timetables. 
- Conduct focus groups and surveys to gather feedback from the girls and young people using the service. 
- Run errands and source resources needed for activities. 
- Engage positively and respectfully with the young people and families accessing the centre. 
- Support the Youth Team with any additional tasks necessary to ensure smooth service delivery. 
- Follow all Baytree Centre policies and procedures. 
- Complete volunteer questionnaires and evaluations as requested. 
 
Skills and qualities required:
- Good interpersonal skills, able to work well within a diverse team. 
- Computer literate, with proficiency in Microsoft Outlook and Excel. 
- Ability to work independently with minimal supervision. 
- Good time management and organisational skills. 
- Reliable, punctual, and committed. 
- Interest in working with children, young people, community development, or social care. 
- Flexibility and willingness to assist with a variety of tasks as needed. 
- Experience working with young people or volunteering is desirable. 
- Knowledge of a second language (e.g. Spanish, Portuguese, French, Arabic) is a plus. 

Commitment: 
- 2 to 4 days per week, Monday to Thursday. 
- Hours: 10:30 am – 6:00 pm. 
- Duration: 4 to 6 months, with flexibility to extend if required. 
 
Benefits: We reimburse up to £7 for travel and £5 for lunch expenses for each full day of internship. 
- Gain practical experience working in youth services and the charity sector. 
- Develop skills in group facilitation, data management, and community engagement. 
- Contribute to positive outcomes for young people and families. 
- Opportunity to attend volunteer social events and network. 
- Valuable insight into alternative educational and community support settings. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female Youth Service Intern";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68a5d300ce6e627395d4f39d :address "300-302 Brixton Road, London";
                            :latitude "51.4700721"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.1125002"^^xsd:double.
id:68a5d596f363c8812cb3ab0f :activityDescription """Purpose of the role: 
Your role is to support the Monitoring and Evaluation (M&E) Officer at the Baytree Centre in assessing the Centre’s programmes and monitoring their impact on service users. This includes assisting with data collection and analysis, organising focus groups and interviews, and supporting the creation of reports that inform service improvement and highlight outcomes. 

Main responsibilities: 
- Support the enhancement of M&E processes across all Baytree services. 
- Conduct research into innovative methods for data collection and analysis. 
- Organise and facilitate focus groups and conduct interviews with service users. 

- Assist service users in completing questionnaires.
- Prepare case studies based on collected data. 
- Compile and analyse findings to create clear, accurate reports. 
- Adhere to the policies and procedures of the Baytree Centre. 
- Complete volunteer questionnaires and evaluations as required. 
 
Skills and qualities required: 
- Strong interpersonal skills; able to work collaboratively in a diverse team. 
- Good written and verbal communication skills. 
- Proficiency in Microsoft Outlook and Excel. 
- Strong organisational skills with the ability to work independently. 
- Good time management and attention to detail. 
- Reliable, punctual, and committed to the role. 
- Interest in working with children, young people, and community services. 
- Willingness to support various tasks and contribute flexibly as needed. 
 
Commitment: 
- 2 to 4 days per week (Monday–Thursday). 
- Hours: 10:00 am – 6:00 pm. 
- Duration: 4 to 6 months, with flexibility to extend if required. 
 
Benefits: We reimburse up to £7 for travel and £5 for lunch expenses for each full day of internship. 
- Hands-on experience in monitoring and evaluation within the charity sector. 
- Opportunity to develop practical research, analysis, and reporting skills. 
- Insight into the impact of educational and community programmes. 
- Inclusion in volunteer social events. 
- Personal fulfilment from supporting meaningful community development work. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female Monitoring and Evaluation Intern";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68a5d596f363c8812cb3ab10 :address "300-302 Brixton Road, London";
