id:68a5d9f70db68cbea4fca774 :activityDescription """Purpose of the Role: 
To support the delivery of engaging and inclusive English conversation sessions at the Baytree Centre, helping participants practise speaking English in a relaxed group setting. By offering encouragement, guidance, and a welcoming environment, the role empowers participants to improve their language skills, build confidence, and make meaningful social connections. 

Main Responsibilities: 
- Assist in preparing and setting up for English conversation sessions.
- Facilitate group discussions, encouraging participation and peer interaction. 
- Provide one-to-one support to participants, helping with pronunciation, vocabulary, and conversational skills. 
- Ensure all materials and resources are available and organised for each session. 
- Create a supportive and inclusive environment where participants feel comfortable practising English and -asking questions. 
- Encourage connections and engagement between participants. 
- Collect feedback to help improve future sessions. 
 
Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Fluency in English with the ability to model correct pronunciation and usage. 
- Patience, empathy, and cultural sensitivity. 
- Good organisational skills to ensure smooth preparation and delivery of sessions. 
- Strong interpersonal skills to create a positive and inclusive atmosphere. 
- Effective communication skills to give clear instructions and constructive feedback. 
- Interest in language learning, community support, or adult education. 
 
Commitment: 
- Assist in weekly English conversation sessions, (day and time subject to the timetable). 
- Minimum commitment of 2 terms for continuity and effectiveness. 
- Location: The Baytree Centre. 
 
Benefits: 
- Gain experience in facilitating group learning and language practice. 
- Develop skills in cross-cultural communication and group engagement. 
- Contribute to the confidence and integration of adult ESOL learners. 
- Be part of a supportive and welcoming volunteer community. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea""";
