id:68a5db33f363c8812cb3ac7f :activityDescription """Purpose of the role: 
Your role is to support the Life Skills and Employability Programme Lead at the Baytree Centre in delivering one of the programmes within the Life Skills Project. The programmes include Her Space (Spark) for girls in school year 10 and above, Future Me (Jr Spark) for girls in school years 8–9, and Step into Secondary (Sparklers) for girls in school year 7. This includes co-facilitating weekly workshops that focus on essential life and leadership skills such as self-confidence, mental health and wellbeing, relationships, online safety, and conflict resolution. You will help create a welcoming, inclusive environment where girls can explore important topics and develop the skills they need to thrive. 

Main responsibilities: 
- Co-deliver weekly life skills workshops alongside the Programme Lead. 
- Encourage active participation and ensure sessions reflect the girls' interests. 
- Promote inclusion and representation of the diverse local community. 
- Occasionally support trips or outings (e.g. theatre visits). 
- Build positive, respectful relationships with participants. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre’s policies and procedures, including safeguarding, health & safety, and equality, diversity & inclusion. 
- Complete volunteer evaluations and other tasks as required. 
 
Skills and qualities required: 
- Good interpersonal skills and ability to build strong relationships. 
- Positive, friendly, and proactive approach. 
- Reliable, punctual, and committed. 
- Ability to work as part of a diverse team. 
- Understanding of safeguarding and child protection. 
- Experience working with young people (desirable). 
- Experience planning or delivering workshops (desirable). 
- Knowledge of a second language (e.g. Spanish, Portuguese, French, Arabic) is an advantage. 
 
Commitment: 
- One afternoon per week (Monday to Thursday), for approximately 1 hour and 30 minutes between 4:00 pm and 6:30 pm. 
- Specific times will be assigned according to the termly programme timetable. 
- Minimum commitment of two terms (approximately 6 months). 
 
Benefits: 
- Gain experience in youth facilitation and life skills education. 
- Develop transferable skills in communication, leadership, and inclusivity. 
- Make a meaningful impact in the lives of young girls. 
- Join a vibrant and diverse volunteer community. 
- Professional development and insight into the charity and education sectors. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female Youth Life Skills Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68a5db33f363c8812cb3ac80 :address "300-302 Brixton Road, London";
