                            :longitude "-0.1125002"^^xsd:double.
id:68a5dbba8f59737f7c667136 :activityDescription """Purpose of the Role: 
To provide administrative support for the school application process for participants in the Baytree Centre’s Into School programme. The role focuses on preparing, organising, and processing application paperwork, maintaining accurate records, and supporting staff to ensure smooth and timely submissions. By assisting with the administrative tasks behind the admissions process, the volunteer will help newly arrived girls aged 11–19 transition successfully into the UK education system. 
 
Main Responsibilities: 
- Assist Baytree staff with preparing and organising school and college application forms. 
- Input and update application data accurately in relevant tracking systems. 
- Prepare and organise supporting documentation for submission. 
- File and maintain records in line with Baytree’s data protection policies. 
- Assist in producing reports and summaries for internal monitoring purposes. 
- Support with general administrative tasks related to the Into School programme. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and safeguarding procedures. 
 
Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Good written English and attention to detail when reviewing and entering information. 
- Strong organisational skills to manage paperwork and digital files efficiently. 
- Ability to follow processes and work accurately to meet deadlines. 
- Proficiency in using Microsoft Office and/or Google Workspace (training can be provided). 
- Discretion and reliability when handling sensitive information. 
- Ability to work as part of a team and follow instructions from staff. 
 
Commitment: 
- One day per week (Monday to Thursday). 
- Final day and time to be confirmed based on the programme timetable. 
- Minimum commitment of two terms (approximately 6 months). 
 
Benefits: 
- Gain experience in administrative processes within an educational support programme. 
- Develop skills in data management, organisation, and reporting. 
- Contribute to the smooth running of the Into School programme and the successful integration of participants into formal education. 
- Be part of a supportive and welcoming volunteer community. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea


 """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female School Application Support Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68a5dbba8f59737f7c667137 :address "300-302 Brixton Road, London";
                            :latitude "51.4700721"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.1125002"^^xsd:double.
id:68a5dc458f59737f7c6671b0 :activityDescription """Purpose of the Role: 
To support the delivery of engaging and age-appropriate wellbeing and enrichment activities for newly arrived migrant girls aged 11–19 at the Baytree Centre. These activities form part of the Into School programme and may include cookery, wellbeing/fitness sessions, and creative workshops. The role helps girls to build confidence, develop personal and social skills, and form positive relationships while waiting for a place in formal education. By offering encouragement, guidance, and a welcoming environment, the volunteer will help participants integrate, express themselves, and explore new interests. 
 
Main Responsibilities: 
- Assist in planning and delivering enrichment sessions (e.g., cookery, wellbeing/fitness) for girls, or accompany Baytree staff to off-site workshops. 
- Support Baytree staff in ensuring the smooth delivery of off-site activities by assisting facilitators and guiding girls through planned activities. 
- Create engaging activities that encourage creativity, learning, and personal development. 
- Foster a supportive and inclusive environment where girls feel comfortable expressing themselves, trying new skills, and building confidence. 
- Support positive relationship building and teamwork among participants. 
- Assist with administrative tasks such as recording attendance, activity planning, and organising materials for sessions. 
- Adhere to Baytree Centre policies and safeguarding procedures. 
 
Skills and Qualities Required: 
- Patience, empathy, and understanding when working with girls from different cultural backgrounds, ages, and abilities. 
- Strong communication skills to interact positively with participants, volunteers, and Baytree staff. 
- Creativity and enthusiasm for developing and delivering engaging activities that capture the girls’ interests. 
- Reliability and commitment to attend scheduled sessions consistently. 
- Ability to work as part of a team and follow instructions from facilitators or staff. 
 
Commitment: 
- One session per week for at least one term (usually 10–12 weeks). 
- Please refer to the Into School timetable for exact session times. 
- Final day and time will be confirmed following review of the programme timetable. 
- Meeting location: The Baytree Centre. 
 
Benefits: 
- Gain experience in delivering creative and wellbeing-focused enrichment activities. 
- Develop skills in youth engagement, activity facilitation, and cross-cultural communication. 
- Contribute to the confidence, wellbeing, and personal growth of newly arrived young people. 
- Be part of a supportive and welcoming volunteer community. 

This role is open to female applicants only (Equality Act 2010: Schedule 9: Occupational Requirements). Applicants must be 18 years or older. 

Apply now via The Baytree Centre's Volunteer Application form: https://thebaytreecentre.beaconforms.com/form/745669ea
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d646a0624f3ab9fbcd71;
                            :activityTitle "Female Into School Teaching Support Volunteer (Well-being and Enrichment Focused)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68a5dc458f59737f7c6671b1 :address "300-302 Brixton Road, London";
