id:68a5ebb867821c6570f0e1ae :activityDescription """Role title: Collection volunteer Braehead Shopping Centre, Renfrewshire 

Time commitment: 2 -4 hours a day

 

What we're looking for

 

We're looking for enthusiastic, creative and organised people to be an NSPCC Collection Volunteer in your local community. Around 90 per cent of our income comes from our supporters and we couldn't continue doing what we do without them. That means, our collection volunteers play a important part in rallying people together to raise vital funds which help to protect children and prevent abuse.

 

What you'll do

 

You'll be working together with the rest of the team to raise awareness and funds. you'll be collecting for the vital work the NSPCC does, engaging with the public- promoting a positive image for the NSPCC!

We appreciate that work, family and friends come first and, with that in mind, this role offers flexibility to fit in with your lifestyle.

Distribute collection boxes to locations such as cafes, shops, bars, restaurants and small businesses in your local area
Replace full boxes, counting and banking funds, liaising with your local community team and organising receipts and thank you cards for supporters
Represent NSPCC in a professional manner
Share news about our work in the local community and help promote fundraising events and initiatives

 

What you'll get

 

We'll support you with advice, skills and tools to help you fundraise and spread the word about the NSPCC. You'll be given a designated point of contact and we'll cover reasonable mileage expenses. You'll learn more about how you're helping to protect children in your local area and across the UK. 

It's also a chance to spend time with like-minded people and make new friends.

 

Who's right for the role?

 

While we think this role is suitable for a whole range of people, we are particularly looking for those with the following qualities and experience.

 

passionate about helping young people and children
enthusiastic and personable
strong organisational skills
you work well within a team
great communication and social skills

 

 

We are currently unable to accept applications from under 18's to this role, please view our other volunteering opportunities or get in touch with the Volunteer Recruitment team on volunteerrecruitment@nspcc.org.uk

 

 

Interested in getting involved? Volunteer today and join our fight for every childhood

 """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:64135259bab6b2821fb75dee;
                            :activityTitle "Collection Box Co-Ordinator Braehead";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68a5ebb867821c6570f0e1af :address "Renfrewshire";
                            :latitude "55.8298581"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-4.5428385"^^xsd:double.
id:68a5ec8a81adcefbafa7a7a8 :activityDescription """Collection Box Volunteer

Every childhood is worth fighting for. This is our belief. We all share it. And it drives us to get out there and bring in the funds we need to protect children and prevent abuse.  

Do you…. 

… have a few hours a month to spare?
… enjoy building relationships with your local community?
… have a passion for helping children and young people? 

If so, you could be exactly who we need to raise vital funds to support the work of NSPCC Cymru, as a collection box volunteer.

Work in your local community to provide collection tins, record and monitor and thank businesses for their support.

What you'll get…

A designated point of contact in our community team
We will support you with the right information, tools, and training
Be part of NSPCC Cymru and our mission to end child cruelty
Meet like-minded people and enjoy new experiences
Access to the Volunteer Portal with training and learning opportunities
Volunteer Newsletter

Around 80% of our income comes from the public and we couldn't do what we do without them. Your role as a fundraising volunteer would help us raise money and awareness of our vital work in supporting communities and protecting children and young people across Wales.

This is a fantastic opportunity to join the UK's leading children's charity and work alongside a friendly, passionate and dedicated team. If you share our passion about the impact you can create for children, we'd love to hear from you. 

We are currently unable to accept applications from under 18's to this role, please view our other volunteering opportunities or get in touch with the Volunteer Recruitment team on volunteerrecruitment@nspcc.org.uk  

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Mae pob plentyndod yn werth brwydro drosto. Rydyn ni'n credu hynny'n gryf. Bob un ohonom. Ac mae hynny'n ein hannog ni i fynd allan i gymunedau i godi'r arian sydd ei angen arnom i amddiffyn plant ac atal camdriniaeth.  

Ydych chi... 

… yn gallu sbario ychydig oriau bob mis?
… yn mwynhau meithrin perthynas â'ch cymuned leol?
… yn frwd dros helpu plant a phobl ifanc? 

Os felly, efallai mai chi yw'r union berson sydd ei angen arnom i godi arian hanfodol i gefnogi gwaith NSPCC Cymru, fel gwirfoddolwr blychau casglu.

Cewch weithio yn eich cymuned leol i ddarparu blychau casglu, cofnodi a monitro cyfraniadau, a diolch i fusnesau am eu cefnogaeth.

Beth fyddwch chi'n ei gael…

Pwynt cyswllt dynodedig yn ein tîm cymunedol
Cefnogaeth gennym ni – gyda'r wybodaeth, yr adnoddau a'r hyfforddiant iawn
Bod yn rhan o NSPCC Cymru a'n cenhadaeth i roi terfyn ar greulondeb at blant
Cwrdd â phobl o'r un anian a mwynhau profiadau newydd
Mynediad i'r Porth Gwirfoddolwyr gyda chyfleoedd hyfforddi a dysgu
Cylchlythyr Gwirfoddolwyr

Daw tua 80% o'n hincwm gan y cyhoedd a fydden ni ddim yn gallu gwneud ein gwaith hebddyn nhw. Byddech chi fel gwirfoddolwr codi arian yn ein helpu i godi arian ac i godi ymwybyddiaeth o'n gwaith hollbwysig yn cefnogi cymunedau ac yn amddiffyn plant a phobl ifanc ar hyd a lled Cymru.

Dyma gyfle gwych i ymuno â phrif elusen blant y DU a gweithio ochr yn ochr â thîm cyfeillgar, angerddol ac ymroddedig. Os ydych chi'n rhannu ein hangerdd am yr effaith y gallwch chi ei chael ar blant, byddem wrth ein bodd yn clywed gennych chi. 

 

Ar hyn o bryd, nid ydym yn gallu derbyn ceisiadau gan bobl ifanc o dan 18 oed ar gyfer y rôl hon. Edrychwch ar ein cyfleoedd gwirfoddoli eraill neu cysylltwch â'r tîm Recriwtio Gwirfoddolwyr yn volunteerrecruitment@nspcc.org.uk""";
