id:68a5f3c22ef6471c76341701 :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089d,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """We believe in the creative power of the individual, and that everyone should have the opportunity to contribute to the creative life of their local community. This richness in sharing stories and experiences of those who can often feel underrepresented, encourages stronger communities, changes perceptions, and ultimately helps people live healthier, happier and more connected lives.

We produce vibrant and important cultural programmes, created by and for the communities we work with, namely isolated older people, those living with profound and multiple disabilities, and those living in care home environments, enabling them to play an active and visible role in the creative life of their community.

Our programmes are often developed in partnership with organisations from across the arts, health and care industries on a local and national level.

We work with a pioneering and diverse range of artists across all art forms, who collaborate with our communities to meet, celebrate, and experience each other and the world.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/55fcc554-02be-4e27-a0e1-1bdf9b597454_2025-08-20T16:11:45.195Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Entelechy Arts";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://entelechyarts.org/>.
id:68a5fbdca64d25608140a99a :activityDescription """We are looking for new volunteers to join the Meet Me team to support Meet Me at the Albany in person and remote activities. 

⭐️ What is Meet Me at the Albany? ⭐️
In 2013 Entelechy Arts and the Albany, in partnership with Lewisham Council, established Meet Me at the Albany – an arts and social club for over 65s. Meet Me… is led by a vibrant and diverse community of previously isolated older people alongside incredible artists. Members come together weekly for a cross-art form social and creative programme to make friends, be creative, advocate for themselves, and contribute to the vibrant cultural life of Lewisham. 

⭐️Who we are looking for? ⭐️
Our volunteers are a huge part of the smooth running of all of our weekly and monthly sessions! We are looking for people who have the following skills and experience: 
📌Personable and Friendly 
📌Listening skills: these are really important to connect and work with our members and ensure their safety 
📌Experience working with older people or interest in supporting older people and their creativity – however previous experience is not essential 
📌Adaptable and Flexible: sometimes the activities might need to change and our volunteers need to be open to some different ways of approaching things in the sessions 
📌Some of our volunteers like to share their own creativity with Meet Me members, however there is no expectation that volunteers have any creative experience.  

🚩🤳This term we are also looking for people who can work with our members to create dynamic and fun social media content
 
🎨If you have a creative practice, from visual arts to dance, from film and photography to poetry, and would like to share this as part of a skills exchange with our members please let us know! 🎨

⭐️What to expect  ⭐️
Our team of volunteers get involved in all or some of the following activities, according to personal interest and skills: 
📌 empowering participants to make choices regarding art and creative activities and listening to their feedback 
📌 supporting participants as they engage in arts and creative activities which are run by professional artists 
📌 engaging participants in additional activities, such as gardening 
📌 meeting, greeting and welcoming people as they arrive 
📌 helping participants socialise by befriending 
📌 helping serve lunch and refreshments 
📌 helping people to their transport. 

⭐️ What’s next? ⭐️
Get in touch for a chance to discuss our opportunities. We will then invite you to complete a registration form and book you on to our next available training session. Training will cover safeguarding, setting boundaries and we will explore the programme. It is a chance to work through possible scenarios and ensure you feel confident joining us for one of the in person, over the phone or online sessions. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:68a5f3c22ef6471c76341701;
                            :activityTitle "Join us! Come and volunteer at Meet Me, an older peoples's arts and social club at the Albany in Deptford";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
