id:68a68bf204c36588ab18cd44 :activityDescription """The Orkney Native Wildlife Project is a partnership project between NatureScot, RSPB, Orkney Island Council, EULife and the National Lottery Heritage Fund. Our purpose is to remove the non-native invasive stoat from Orkney and protect its native wildlife. You can find more information about who we are and what we do at www.orkneynativewildlife.org.uk.

 We are looking for volunteers to join some of our key functional teams to help grow our capacity. This role is all about taking on a few tasks as part of an existing team at the Orkney Native Wildlife Project. The tasks will vary depending on which team is looking for support, but this can range from undertaking research, working alongside trappers to monitoring our native species. By working together we can achieve and do more for nature. 

Volunteer tasks will vary greatly depending on the specific role, but it may include some of the following: 

- Taking on a few stoat traps that you check every 2-3 weeks.
- Monitoring local wildlife during our set seasons.
- Office work inputting data.

This role will require some key general skills, but please note that we will offer full training and induction into this particular area. You **may** need some experience in the area depending on what it is. The list below is just a suggestion and obviously this will be dependent on the role that you decide to undertake.

- IT skills, creating documents, managing spreadsheets.
- Be physically active and able to walk across difficult terrain.  
- Organisational skills. 

This is a rewarding role that offers the opportunity to support the ONWP in a big way. You'll find satisfaction in making a genuine contribution to nature conservation. You will learn all about how the ONWP works and gain experience working for an environmental charity.  

We like to think we're a friendly and welcoming team, so you'll have the opportunity to make new friends too.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "RSPB Team Member (Orkney Native Wildlife Project Volunteer)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68a68bf204c36588ab18cd45 :address "ONWP, Garrison Road, Hatston Industrial Estate, Kirkwall, KW15 1GN, United Kingdom";
                            :latitude "58.987351"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.971905"^^xsd:double.
id:68a68bfc742e948790e1cf9c :activityDescription """An exciting opportunity to join our Biosecurity Team, making a direct impact for nature. The Incursion Response Team are responsible for protecting Orkney's stoat free islands by reacting to, and removing, reported invasion of stoats.

You will be completing regular training ‘drills’ on incursion response including how to place and monitor camera traps as well as DOC200 spring traps. You will be deployed at short notice on islands where an incursion has occurred to survey the land, collect data work with the Incursion Leader to respond to the incursion appropriately. You will be working alongside ONWP staff and other volunteers, as well as working with the island communities. 

You will need a range of skills and experience for this role including:  

- Be able to follow the procedures required for the removal of stoats and learn the necessary monitoring skills required.   
- Be able to attend training.  
- Have general administration and IT skills to enable rota management and communication with the ONWP Biosecurity Officer.  
- Ability to identify the Health and Safety requirements of the project. 
- Work as part of a team of people to carry out the main tasks.    
- Be flexible and adaptable to change.  
- Have a friendly disposition and be able to communicate effectively with islanders.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Biosecurity Team Leader (Orkney Native Wildlife Project)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68a68bfc742e948790e1cf9d :address "Orkney Islands";
                            :latitude "58.987099"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.971288"^^xsd:double.
id:68a6d3e364dcb3b40ca5025c :activityDescription """Support Over-55s with Digital Skills – Become a Volunteer Digital Champion

Join us in making a real difference in your community by helping people aged 55 and over build confidence with digital technology. As a Volunteer Digital Champion, you’ll provide friendly, one-to-one support to residents at Haven Court in Erdington, helping them learn how to use smartphones, tablets, computers, and smart speakers.

You’ll assist with everyday digital tasks like:

Using Google and browsing the internet
Setting up and using email
Finding reliable health information online
Making video calls to stay in touch with loved ones
Accessing job search websites
Exploring hobbies and interests online
You don’t need to be a tech expert—just someone with basic digital skills, patience, and a passion for helping others. In return, you’ll receive free accredited training, ongoing support, and the satisfaction of knowing you’ve made a real impact.

Sessions run fortnightly on Wednesdays from 10AM to 1PM, and we welcome volunteers who can commit weekly, fortnightly, or monthly.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:67a0ea3698a9ee042f595843;
                            :activityTitle "Digital Skills Support";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68a6d9fb0d7ba8eb61640e17 :address "The Gardens, Erdington, Birmingham B23 6AG";
