id:68a99acf695233afeea70fe5 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """At Hearts in Healing, our mission is to transform pain into purpose.
Born from lived experience, we exist to stand beside those who have faced trauma, hardship, or life in care. We provide a safe space for people to express their emotions, find strength through creativity, and rediscover their voice.

Through our workshops, courses, and community projects, we aim to break cycles of silence and isolationempowering people to heal, grow, and move forward with hope.

We are more than an organisation; we are a movement of compassion, resilience, and restoration.""";
                            :organisationName "Hearts In Healing ".
id:68a99cc31b086fd7cad6a5bc :activityDescription """Content Creator
Hearts in Healing CIC – Hybrid Role (Remote & In-Person Meetings)

We are a brand-new charity dedicated to supporting mental health and healing through creativity, storytelling, and community connection. To help us grow our impact and reach, we are looking for a passionate Content Creator to join our volunteer team.

In this role, you will be at the heart of bringing our mission to life through engaging and meaningful content. You’ll work closely with our Social Media Manager and wider team to create visuals, videos, and written content that inspire, connect, and raise awareness.

Responsibilities

Develop creative content (graphics, videos, photos, reels, blogs, etc.) that aligns with our mission and values.
Support campaigns, workshops, and book promotions with tailored content.
Collaborate with the Social Media Manager to plan content calendars.
Capture highlights from events (when attending in person).
Contribute fresh ideas to strengthen our online presence and engagement.
What We’re Looking For

A creative eye with experience in content creation (can be personal, educational, or professional).
Familiarity with tools such as Canva, CapCut, Adobe, or other design/video platforms.
Strong communication skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with a team.
Passion for mental health, healing, and making a difference.
Ability to commit to around 3–4 hours per week (flexible).

What You’ll Gain

Hands-on experience growing a charity’s digital presence.
A chance to expand your portfolio and showcase your creative skills.
Flexible hybrid volunteering (mainly remote via Teams, occasional in-person catch-ups).
The opportunity to be part of something meaningful and impactful from the ground up.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68a99acf695233afeea70fe5;
                            :activityTitle "Content Creator ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
