id:68adbc333040a0afb276be07 :activityDescription """Day Centre Volunteers Needed

Are you looking for a rewarding way to give back to your community? Homelink Day Respite Centre is seeking friendly and enthusiastic volunteers to help make a positive difference in the lives of our elderly clients.

What you’ll be doing:

Serving teas, coffees, and meals, and helping with table setting

Engaging with clients through conversation, dancing, or simply being present

Supporting a variety of fun and stimulating activities such as board games, arts and crafts, music sessions, quizzes, bingo, and more

Assisting staff with day-to-day tasks to ensure the centre runs smoothly

When: Weekdays between 9:45 am and 3:30 pm

Why volunteer with us:

Make a real difference to people’s lives in your local community

Meet new people and develop friendships

Gain experience in care and support roles

Enjoy a fun, friendly, and welcoming environment

No prior experience is required – just a kind heart, a smile, and a willingness to help! Full training and support will be provided.

Join us and help bring joy, companionship, and fun to our clients every day.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64106006814bf5829d62a68e;
                            :activityTitle "Day Centre Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68adbc333040a0afb276be08 :address "Hospital Bridge Road, Whitton, Twickenham TW2 6DE";
                            :latitude "51.4431255"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.365051"^^xsd:double.
id:68adbee2a43612afb7b4728a :activityDescription """Volunteer Drivers Needed

Are you looking for a meaningful way to make a difference in your community? We are seeking reliable and friendly volunteer drivers to help transport our clients safely to and from our Day Centre in Whitton.

What you’ll be doing:

Picking up clients from their homes in the morning (between 9:30–9:45 am)

Driving them safely to the Day Centre

Returning clients to their homes in the afternoon (between 3:00–3:30 pm)

Providing a friendly and welcoming presence during the journey

When:

Weekdays on a regular basis

Why volunteer with us:

Make a real difference to people’s lives by helping them attend our centre

Be part of a supportive and friendly volunteer team

No special qualifications are needed, just a valid driving license, a reliable vehicle, and a willingness to help. Full support and guidance will be provided to all our volunteer drivers.

Join us and help ensure our clients can safely access the services and activities they enjoy every day!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64106006814bf5829d62a68e;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Driver";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68adbee2a43612afb7b4728b :address "Hospital Bridge Road, Twickenham";
                            :latitude "51.4447366"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.3654963"^^xsd:double.
id:68adbf77dc39da3ad0ddba0a :activityDescription """Volunteer Gardener Needed for Sensory Garden

Are you passionate about gardening and looking to make a positive impact in your community? We are seeking a dedicated volunteer gardener to assist with the upkeep of our sensory garden.

Responsibilities: Pruning and tidying plants, planting, watering during the summer months, general garden maintenance

Requirements:

A love for gardening and the outdoors

Willingness to commit to regular volunteering hours

Ability to work independently

If you have a green fingers and a heart for helping others, we would love to hear from you!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64106006814bf5829d62a68e;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Gardener";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68adbf77dc39da3ad0ddba0b :address "Hospital Bridge Road, Whitton, Twickenham TW2 6DE";
                            :latitude "51.4431255"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.365051"^^xsd:double.
id:68adc0afdc39da3ad0ddba43 :activityDescription """Volunteer Kitchen Assistant

We’re looking for friendly and reliable volunteers to assist in our kitchen and help support the smooth running of our Day Centre.

Responsibilities:

Assist our Cook with general kitchen duties

Serve meals, wash up, and load the dishwasher

We’re looking for someone who:

Enjoys working with older adults with patience and support

Communicates well and works effectively as part of a team

Is caring, dependable, and flexible

Understands the importance of health, safety, and confidentiality

Brings a positive, enthusiastic attitude

Join us and help create a welcoming, safe, and enjoyable environment for our clients!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64106006814bf5829d62a68e;
                            :activityTitle "Kitchen Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68adc0afdc39da3ad0ddba44 :address "Hospital Bridge Road, Whitton, Twickenham TW2 6DE";
