id:68adc6387c4bb0b32cc7bdb6 :activityDescription """This role is about bringing together people who enjoy making, crafting, and being creative to support Earth
Trust’s events, education sessions, and seasonal festivals. Volunteers will work as part of a friendly group
to create handmade and sustainable items that help bring our work to life—from bunting and signage to
props, decorations, and creative touches for our celebrations and learning spaces. You’ll get to use your
creative skills to support Earth Trust in inspiring people to care for nature, all while working in a relaxed,
social setting.
Time required: Frequency: Approx 3 hours per session
Fortnightly (proposed day: Tuesday mornings, 9:30am-12:30pm) come when you
are available
Tasks may include:
Creating event decorations (e.g. bunting, wreaths, display items)
Painting signs, drawing illustrations, or making visual props
Stitching, knitting or crafting items for educational use
Whittling or woodworking for handmade games or nature-based activities
Upcycling or repurposing materials in creative ways
Contributing ideas to group projects and seasonal themes""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ed04c794380477b73fa1;
                            :activityTitle "Earth Trust Creative Hub Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68adc6387c4bb0b32cc7bdb7 :address "Little Wittenham, Abingdon OX14 4QZ";
                            :latitude "51.62924779999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.1873423"^^xsd:double.
id:68adc88e071f7c0c647dba4c :activityDescription """The role will vary depending on the survey(s) you decide to help with including: walking set transect
routes, checking reptile mats, FIT counts, visual soil assessments, grassland rapid assessments & checking
mammals prints.
The role will offer an opportunity to develop species identification skills and spend time outdoors with a
purpose whilst enjoying our beautiful green spaces. You’ll contribute data towards the Thames Valley
Environmental Records Centre (TVERC) which is dedicated to maintaining a comprehensive ecological
information hub. You’ll also be contributing valuable data for a greater understanding of what impact the
changes we are making in a farming practises are having on biodiversity. You’ll also gain valuable
volunteering and surveying experience which is helpful for pursuing a career in conservation.
Flexible hours between April – September annually
Visiting our sites regularly from April to September as part of a rota system.
Following a set route and methodology.
Reporting data to TVERC (Thames Valley Environmental Records Centre) and UKBMS
(United Kingdom Butterfly Monitoring Scheme)""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ed04c794380477b73fa1;
                            :activityTitle "Earth Trust - Surveyor Volunteers";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68adc88e071f7c0c647dba4d :address "Little Wittenham, Abingdon OX14 4QZ";
                            :latitude "51.62924779999999"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.1873423"^^xsd:double.
id:68adcda83e908a601402283f :activityDescription """Butterflies are a valuable indicator species which means that their numbers can often tell us about the
state of their habitats. By collecting more data on butterfly population we are hoping to understand more
about how the habitats we manage are changing over time and in response to factors such as climate
change, pollution and urban development.

Tasks:
Walking a set transect route and recording the number and species of butterflies you
see.
Visiting our sites regularly from April to September as part of a rota system.
Following set route and methodology.
Reporting data to UKBMS (United Kingdom Butterfly Monitoring Scheme) website
after each visit and to Earth Trust at the end of the season.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ed04c794380477b73fa1;
                            :activityTitle "Earth Trust - Butterfly Surveyor";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
