id:68adcde7b533f22d6e870bdc :address "Tuckmill Meadows, Shrivenham, Swindon SN6 8EX, UK";
                            :latitude "51.6055084"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.6569018"^^xsd:double.
id:68add18ba26f088ea58845b9 :activityDescription """Tuckmill Meadows have cattle to help with the management of the site. We are looking for volunteer
stock-watchers to keep an eye on them. We want to ensure that they are happy, healthy and have
everything they need, each and every day.
The role involves visiting Tuckmill Meadows and finding the three Dexter cattle which reside there (this
should be quite easy with a smartphone as they are wearing GPS collars), checking that they happy grazing
or resting, have no visible injuries and have access to water and letting us know if there are any concerns.
This role does not involve getting up close and personal with the cows, it’s a visual check from a distance.
Time required: A walk around the site to look for the cattle and check them could take between 15-45 minutes.
Frequency: Ideally one day a week but can be flexible.
Tasks: Find the cattle, check behaviour and for injuries, check water supply.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ed04c794380477b73fa1;
                            :activityTitle "Stock Watcher Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68add18ba26f088ea58845ba :address "Shrivenham, Swindon SN6 8EX";
                            :latitude "51.6082444"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.6635771"^^xsd:double.
id:68add416a3178ad39987ca03 :activityDescription """With so many exciting things happening at the Earth Trust Centre, we welcome many visitors to the site on
a daily basis and the gardens around the Earth Trust offices and barns offer the first impression for our
visitors. We currently have a small team of experienced volunteer gardeners who come on a Thursday and
do a fantastic job of keeping the site looking at its very best, all year round. We are looking to expand the
team.
Tasks include:
o Maintaining and enhancing the garden
areas around the Earth Trust Centre.
o Ensuring that Fison Barn courtyard is well
presented for weddings and meetings.
o Weeding, pruning, watering and other
general gardening duties.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ed04c794380477b73fa1;
                            :activityTitle "Centre Gardener";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68add416a3178ad39987ca04 :address "Little Wittenham, Abingdon OX14 4QZ";
