id:68aed66e9b30a48d069714ab :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089d;
                            :organisationDescription "Access All Areas is a company of 22 professional associate artists who identify as learning disabled and autistic. Their productions, board of trustees, consultancy, participatory and educational work are all co-led and co-created by the associate artists. Access All Areas are known for making disruptive theatre by learning disabled and autistic artists. The company also train and support partners across film, TV, and theatre to make their work and workplaces more accessible, and have ongoing relationships and collaborations with Netflix UK, Sky Studios, National Theatre, Royal Court Theatre, Battersea Arts Centre, The Lowry, and many others. www.accessallareasproductions.org";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/d1330aa1-626c-4844-9056-07fc58c13c20_2025-08-27T10:14:06.025Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Access All Areas";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://accessallareasproductions.org/>.
id:68aed94d6890e68e01bf4a28 :activityDescription """NCT is a registered tax-exempt organization. NCT is supporting poor children's education in Andhra Pradesh. NCT is verified and vetted for corporate giving and employee workplace giving by Benevity Causes Portal, YourCause portal, and Charities Aid Foundation, America!
We are looking for volunteers, probably corporate employees, who can help us promote corporate giving. Your volunteering ensures that poor children get continuous education. Girl children escape child marriage and get continuous education. 

This project will prevent and protect children from becoming victims of child marriage, human trafficking, school dropouts, and child labour. Your support and contribution will not only save lives but also ensure a bright future for the beneficiaries. 
Appreciating your efforts and hard work, NCT will award a 'Certificate of Appreciation' to each volunteer.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68aebc90330528cfb780308c;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer to promote/Liasson corporate employee giving in EU countries";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68aee732a81db1abaf2489ba :activityDescription """Youth Leaders work directly with young people in St John Ambulance Badger Setts and Cadet Units. By organising a mixed weekly programme, this role will support the learning and development of young people into the next generation of health citizens. Youth Leaders also help young people develop their confidence, teamwork skills, self-discipline, and generally encourage them to strive to be the best they can be, as well as supervise and support other adult volunteers in their team.

You’ll get a huge sense of satisfaction and pride delivering an essential service. It’s great for you, great for your community and great for our nation, and it requires only a small commitment of your time. 

This role is subject to a DBS check and the applicant undertakings some online course. They must be prepared to undertake Safeguarding qualification and Youth Leader Qualification

Pursuing the role
 

Welcome Event (Induction) - 01/09/2025
Closing date for these opportunities is: 30/09/2025

If you’d like to know more about volunteering or would just like to chat to someone who does, get in touch. Please contact our the hiring manager- Catherine.pearce@sja.org.uk

 """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "Youth Leader";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68aee732a81db1abaf2489bb :address "North Rd, Ripon HG4 1JR";
                            :latitude "54.1423476"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.52035"^^xsd:double.
id:68aee750f901dd7567752e52 :activityDescription """At St John Ambulance, we are looking to develop our volunteering offer and become an even more integral part of our communities through delivering community first aid and education. 

We need people who have a passion for helping others, care about their communities and want to make a difference, supporting them to become safe and more resilient by sharing your first aid skills and knowledge. As a Community First Aider, you’ll deliver first aid to those in need through local events, as well as provide education to the public so that the ripple effect of First Aid grows.

Through supporting the growth of community partnerships, you will bring people along to our cause, growing our membership and fundraising base and spreading the message that First Aid Saves Lives. 

Through volunteering as a Community First Aider, you’ll get a huge sense of satisfaction and pride delivering an essential service. It’s great for you, great for your community and great for our nation, and it requires only a small commitment of your time. 

We will make sure you will have access to a proper induction to volunteering with SJA and the training you need for the role you take on. We will also provide you with a supportive environment while you are volunteering with us. Information about our volunteer roles are included in the role descriptions. What you can expect from SJA, and what we expect from those who volunteer with us, is included in the volunteer charter.


If you are successful you will need to undertake induction & training for role at these dates:
Welcome Event (Induction) - It will take place in late August/Early September
Training for role - Training dates to be confirmed at interview

Closing date for these opportunities is: 12/09/2025

If you’d like to know more about volunteering or would just like to chat to someone who does, get in touch. Please contact our the hiring manager, Joanne Russell, via emailing: Joanne.Russell@sja.org.uk

To apply for this opportunity please follow the link below:""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "Community First Aider (Central Hampshire - Andover, Alton and Winchester)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
