id:68b0423227ddbc10b3daab6b :activityDescription """Youth Leaders work directly with young people in St John Ambulance Badger Setts and Cadet Units. By organising a mixed weekly programme, this role will support the learning and development of young people into the next generation of health citizens. Youth Leaders also help young people develop their confidence, teamwork skills, self-discipline, and generally encourage them to strive to be the best they can be, as well as supervise and support other adult volunteers in their team.

You’ll get a huge sense of satisfaction and pride delivering an essential service. It’s great for you, great for your community and great for our nation, and it requires only a small commitment of your time. 

 

If there are specific commitments a volunteer would be expected to undertake in this role, such as attending specific meetings or training, please include this below so that this information can be included in the advert.

Penkridge cadets (term time only) Monday evenings 19:00-20:30 Rugeley cadets (term time only) Wednesday 19:30-21:00 Cannock (term time only) Tuesdays 18:30-20:00 for badgers and Thursdays 18:30-20:00 cadets

 

Additional Selection, Interview or Enrolment Event Details: Face to Face interview, ID check and DBS documents

Training For Role Information - Incorporated into youth leader training programme

Training For Role Course Details: Youth leader fundamentals and youth leader principles safeguarding level 2 and first aid for youth leaders/community first aider

Closing date for these opportunities is: 31/12/2025

If you’d like to know more about volunteering or would just like to chat to someone who does, get in touch. Please contact our the hiring manager,  Kathryn Safrany - kathry.safrany@sja.org.uk

To apply for this opportunity please follow the link below:""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "Youth Leader - Penkridge cadets, Rugeley cadets, Cannock cadets or Cannock badgers.";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
