id:68b6da8da2ff751e48e2e442 :activityDescription """🌺 Be Part of the 2025 Poppy Appeal – Make a Meaningful Impact This November
This Remembrance season, we invite you to honour the Armed Forces community by volunteering for the Royal British Legion’s Poppy Appeal. Whether you're based in London, Birmingham, Glasgow, Cardiff, Leeds, Bristol, Aberdeen, or Edinburgh, your time and energy can help raise vital funds for veterans, serving personnel, and their families.
💡 Why Volunteer?

Support essential services including rehabilitation, mental health, housing, and financial assistance for those who’ve served.
Join a nationwide movement of remembrance and gratitude.
Use your Giving Back Day to collect donations in exchange for poppy merchandise at local events.

📌 How to Get Involved

Sign up using the link provided
Join us at flagship events such as London Waterloo Station on Thursday 30 October, or support regional hubs across the UK.

💬 Hear from Our Volunteers

“It was a cathartic, inspiring experience I’d recommend to anyone. Thanks to RBL and Mitie for making it possible.” – Mitie Volunteer

Let’s come together this Remembrance season to support the Royal British Legion and show our appreciation for the Armed Forces community.

📍 Premier Event: London Waterloo Station – Thursday 30 October
Mitie colleagues who wish to support the flagship RBL Poppy Appeal 2025 event at London Waterloo are encouraged to register now.
🕢 Volunteering runs from 07:30 to 19:00. While there’s no strict time requirement, we kindly ask for a minimum commitment of 2 hours to help with coordination.
👉 Click here to register https://forms.office.com/e/CmyzEAsueT
Just ask Mervin Thomas (Security Area Manager) – his smile says it all! It’s a rewarding day full of opportunities to network, volunteer, and boost your Contract volunteering hours. Best of all, the admin is taken care of for you.

💬 Questions or Accessibility Needs at Waterloo London?
Please contact:
📧 Adrian Hopwood – Adrian.Hopwood@mitie.com""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65b7befedcc4366de5311230;
                            :activityTitle "🌺 Be Part of the 2025 Poppy Appeal – Make a Meaningful Impact This November";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68b701ebc1876a16d792ae06 :activityDescription """We are looking for new volunteers from all over the North East and Yorkshire to be Speak out. Stay Safe Volunteers. You would visit primary schools local to you to help us protect a generation of children from abuse and neglect. - Applicants must have access to their own transport due to the rural nature of the county. 

We are currently not recruiting for the following areas: Leeds

In 2022 the NSPCC's Speak out. Stay safe volunteers returned to primary schools. As a Speak out. Stay safe. volunteer, you will visit primary schools to deliver Speak out. Stay safe. workshops that teach children about the different types of abuse and how they can speak out and stay safe. Our Speak out. Stay safe. workshops are age-appropriate and memorable and need an energetic and enthusiastic person to deliver them. You'll work alongside other Speak out. Stay safe. volunteers to make sure at the end of each session the children feel empowered and know who they can speak out to if they are worried.



If you are interested in volunteering as a Speak out. Stay safe. volunteer and want to find out more about the role, the next step is to attend a Volunteer Information Meeting, which is a fantastic opportunity to:



• Meet with staff as well as volunteers to ask any questions you may have
• Learn more about the application process and your volunteer journey



Our meetings are designed to help you decide whether you want to apply – there's no obligation or expectation that you'll apply if you attend one. At the meeting, you'll also receive information on other ways you can become a supporter of the NSPCC.


If you have any questions or experience any issues, please contact the Volunteer Recruitment Team at VolunteerRecruitment@NSPCC.org.uk 

 

For this role, we can only accept people over the age of 16. 

 

Interested in getting involved? Volunteer today and join our fight for every childhood.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64135259bab6b2821fb75dee;
                            :activityTitle "Speak out. Stay safe. Volunteer Information Meeting - North East ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68b701ebc1876a16d792ae07 :address "North East";
                            :latitude "54.9456129"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.9479664"^^xsd:double.
id:68b707ce01a1e0c9b0a7b083 :activityDescription """Enjoy cooking? Looking for a fun way to make a difference in your community? 

Join FoodCycle as a Cooking Volunteer and help turn surplus food into delicious, three-course meals for your local community!

You’ll get involved in everything from prepping ingredients and cooking to coming up with recipe ideas and tidying up at the end. No experience? No problem! Our friendly FoodCycle Leaders will guide you through the session, making sure everything runs smoothly.

Why volunteer with FoodCycle?
- Make an impact – Help provide free, nutritious meals for those who need them.
- Learn new skills – Whether you're a kitchen pro or a total beginner, there’s always something to pick up.
- Meet great people – Be part of a welcoming, supportive team and connect with your local community.
- Flexible volunteering – No minimum commitment, just join when you can! Each cooking session lasts around four hours.

About FoodCycle:
FoodCycle is a national charity running 100+ community meals every week. We use food that would otherwise go to waste to create free, nutritious meals for anyone who needs them. But it’s more than just a meal—it’s a chance to chat, make friends, and feel part of your community.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65d604686123f8876966688d;
                            :activityTitle "FoodCycle Cooking Volunteer - help us cook community meals (North England)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68b707ce01a1e0c9b0a7b084 :address "Galway Rd, Grindon, Sunderland SR4 8JZ, UK";
                            :latitude "54.8898432"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4408935"^^xsd:double.
