id:68b80d9644bb7b8a0ee17af8 :activityDescription """Passionate about making a difference to children and families? 

As a schools volunteer you will have the chance to be part of a cooking or hosting team that produce a hearty two-course vegetarian meal using surplus food for children and their families to enjoy! 

You’ll get involved in everything from prepping ingredients, coming up with recipe ideas, serving meals and tidying up at the end. No experience? No problem! Our friendly FoodCycle Leaders will guide you through the session, making sure everything runs smoothly.

Why volunteer with FoodCycle?
- Make an impact – Help provide free, nutritious meals for those who need them.
- Learn new skills – Whether you're a kitchen pro or a total beginner, there’s always something to pick up.
- Meet great people – Be part of a welcoming, supportive team and connect with your local community.
- Flexible volunteering – No minimum commitment, just join when you can! Each session lasts between 3-4 hours.

About FoodCycle:
FoodCycle is a national charity running community meals every week in multiple locations across England and Wales. 
We’ve partnered with schools  to run free, after-school meals for children and their families. These school community meals help build stronger relationships between families and the schools, promote social interaction and a sense of belonging, plus they help kids discover new, healthy foods.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:65d604686123f8876966688d;
                            :activityTitle "FoodCycle School Volunteer - help us serve free school meals";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68b80d9644bb7b8a0ee17af9 :address "Tindal St, Balsall Heath, Birmingham B12 9QS, UK";
                            :latitude "52.4555532"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.8894346"^^xsd:double.
