id:68b9b141a92f86548b1e7cf3 :activityDescription """For women affected by domestic abuse, walking into court can feel overwhelming.

Your presence will make a difference. 

We’re looking for Court Support Volunteers to accompany women through family court proceedings. 

In this role, you’ll step in where it matters most and sit beside her as a calm and steady voice, taking notes, offering reassurance, and ensuring no woman has to face court alone.

Too often, abusers try to use the court system to maintain control. With you there, you show her that she’s not alone. 

-Commitment: just 2 days per month
-No experience needed as full training will be delivered 
-Guidance from the Support2Court team 
-Reasonable travel expenses to court paid 
-Access to your own vehicle is required 
-DBS check needed

Apply today if you’re ready to dedicate your time to something that matters. 

Training will take place on 2nd October, and you must be available for this training session. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:68b9ae7f59b6a9c0b26bb23b;
                            :activityTitle "Court Support Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68b9b141a92f86548b1e7cf4 :address "Kent, UK";
