id:68bae8d54613c17731c6554d :activityDescription """On Saturday 20th September, we will be hosting our first ever Mad Hatter's Dog Day at Elmtree Canine Retreat in Waltham Abbey. All money raised will go to our charity, Underdog International - this is a a family and dog friendly community event combining dogs, hats, and fun and will feature: 

Fun dog show with categories such as Best Rescue, Best Trick, Waggiest Tail, Best Puppy, Golden Oldie and more.
Hat Parade – where dogs and their owners showcase their best hats.
Dog demonstrations including agility, scent work, and gundog training.
Family zone with hat-making, crafts, bouncy castle, and stalls.
Food and market stalls featuring local businesses and artisan makers.

The event is jointly presented by Haute Dogs, Underdog International, and Elmtree Canine Retreat. Elmtree is providing the venue free of charge, ensuring that all proceeds go directly to Underdog International.

About Underdog International
Underdog International is a UK charity with a mission of “children helping dogs, and dogs helping children.” The organisation rescues and rehomes dogs, runs therapy dog programmes in schools, and delivers kindness education to children. By 2030, it aims to positively impact two million children and dogs worldwide.
Mad Hatter’s Dog Day directly supports this mission, with all proceeds going to Underdog International.

We are looking for support over the weekend and next week with handing out flyers and posters in the local area, including Waltham Abbey, Chingford, Epping Forest, Broxbourne, and the surrounding locations. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:68bae379a148fb4342df393d;
                            :activityTitle "Mad Hatter's Dog Day - Flyer distribution and raising awareness";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
