id:68c01531ad62983ef551a4fb :activityDescription """What we're looking for

We need enthusiastic volunteers to share the messages of the NSPCC School service and opportunities available in Bristol. 
This role can be done virtually or in person.

What you'll do

Through conversations with local groups, businesses and individuals you'll be a champion for the NSPCC Schools' service; engaging with community members to raise awareness of the service and promote volunteering opportunities. 
You'll use your existing local knowledge and contacts to help guide us on how best to inspire others to take action for NSPCC in your area.
This could include:
•    Sharing social media posts
•    Contributing to online networks and groups
•    Attending events

What you'll get

•    Training specific to the role and support with the information and tools you need
•    learn more about how you're helping to protect children in your local area and across the UK
•    the opportunity to meet and work with other volunteers and staff
•    spend time with like-minded people and make new friends
•    free access to our in-house training platform
•    travel expenses reimbursed


Who's right for the role?

We are particularly looking for those who are active within their region and have the following qualities and experience: 
•    passionate about helping young people and children 
•    comfortable talking about the NSPCC's work

If you would like any further information about the role please e-mail Michelle Green at michelle.green@nspcc.org.uk for more details or an informal chat.

Interested in getting involved? Volunteer today and join our fight for every childhood. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:64135259bab6b2821fb75dee;
                            :activityTitle "Conversation Starter";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68c01531ad62983ef551a4fc :address "Bristol";
                            :latitude "51.454513"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.58791"^^xsd:double.
id:68c0191d1a368d610ac13e97 :activityDescription """Warminster branch member

Time commitment: Flexible (at least 2-4 hours a month during busy period)

What we are looking for:

We are looking for enthusiastic, approachable and out going people to join the established branch in Warminster. Around 90% of our income comes from our supporters and we couldn't continue doing what we do without them. 

Our branch and district members will play an important part in raising vital funds so together we can keep children safe. 

What you will do:

You'll kindly volunteer your time to help support and organise fundraising events to help raise vital funds for the NSPCC. 

The ladies arrange a Christmas market with stalls, a raffle and refreshments and in 2024 they arranged a concert as well. Aside from that they arrange a supper club that normally happens in September with local restaurants. The group need new members to help with these events!

The group doesn't typically meeting much during the school holidays as a few of them have childcare responsibilities. 

What you'll get:

We will support you with guidance, advice, and tools to help you fundraise and spread the word for the NSPCC. 

You'll learn more about how you are helping to protect children across the UK. It is a chance to take on new challenges and make new friends with the lovely group.

 

Whos right for the role:

you would be right for this role if you

-are passionate about helping young people and children.

-are enthusiastic and personable

-strong organisational skills

-able to think on your feet

-you work well in a group""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64135259bab6b2821fb75dee;
                            :activityTitle "Warminster District Member ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68c01c55364ddf268e4955a8 :activityDescription """🎨✨ Craft Volunteer – Get Creative for a Cause! 

Location: Your cosy craft corner (aka home!) 
Time Commitment: Totally flexible – whenever inspiration strikes! 
 

🌟 What's the Gig? 

Love getting crafty? Whether you're a knitting ninja, a papercraft pro, or a DIY dynamo, we'd love your help! As a Craft Volunteer, you'll create beautiful handmade items that we can sell, raffle, or gift at NSPCC events – all to help keep children safe and supported. 

 

🧶 What You'll Be Doing 

Making magical things like: 
Cute crochet teddies 🧸 
Cosy knitted hats 🧢 
Gorgeous greeting cards 💌 
Festive decorations 🎄 
Or anything else your crafty heart desires! 
Donating your creations to the NSPCC to help raise funds. 
(Optional!) Joining us at local events to show off your masterpieces. 
(Optional!) Give it a go selling your work yourself to raise money for the NSPCC. 
Spreading the word and inspiring others to get involved by posting about your creations and volunteering online. 

 

🎯 What You Bring 

A love for crafting and a creative spark. 
A big heart and a passion for helping children. 
Your own materials (or the ability to source them). 
A sprinkle of imagination and a dash of dedication. 

 

🎁 What You'll Get 

That warm fuzzy feeling of doing something amazing 💚 
Shout-outs and thanks from our team and community 🙌 
A chance to show off your creations at NSPCC events 🎉 
Flexible volunteering that fits around your life 🕒 
Opportunities to connect with other crafty changemakers 🧵 

 

🧵 We'll Support You With 

Friendly guidance from our fundraising team. 
NSPCC logos and materials to jazz up your crafts. 
Ideas and inspiration for seasonal or themed makes. 

 

💌 Ready to Craft for a Cause? 

We'd love to hear from you! Whether you're a solo stitcher or part of a crafty crew, your creativity can help change children's lives. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:64135259bab6b2821fb75dee;
                            :activityTitle "Craft Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
