                            :longitude "-1.2167669"^^xsd:double.
id:68c0e9ea1e809021bc0b7dda :activityDescription """Imagine a day without coffee and cake! Or a refreshing cup of tea.
Our café volunteers understand the importance of a little break and help visitors to relax and refuel during their visit to RSPB Arne. We have different roles available, so you're bound to find something to suit.
The café at Arne is focused on delivering healthy, organic snacks and if not baked in house are sourced locally from trusted organic suppliers. 

BAKER/FOOD PREPARATION
You will be behind the scenes in the kitchen however with our open  style kitchen you'll still be able to see what is going on whilst preparing food. One day you could be baking as many scones as you can (think Bake-off without Paul and Pru judging) and another day cookies, or general food preparation . You will need to follow food hygiene, allergen and quality control procedures, but full training will be given in these. This role will really suit you if you love to cook.

SERVER/BARISTA
You will be warmly welcoming people/taking orders /making teas and coffee and serving 'Grab and Go ' counter items eg tray bakes, scones, cakes and various types of savoury pasties and sausage rolls. And all with a smile. The barista role is great for someone who likes the smell of fresh coffee and it is also a great way to get training and experience that can help with a career in hospitality. It will particularly suit you if you like being around people as you will meet a lot of them in this role.

WHAT'S IN IT FOR YOU?
By joining us you will
- join an enthusiastic team and make new friends
-develop your hospitality skills and put them into practice 
-help us to raise funds towards saving nature
If these roles really suit you could be trained as a Volunteer Front of House Supervisor 

Food hygiene level 2 and Allergen awareness training is mandatory for all those working in the café.
You will be provided with the necessary induction, training, and equipment to do this role well and safely and we can cover the travel costs between home and Arne. 
You can choose which shifts suit you , but the key service shift and peak time is 1100-1500 but other shifts may be available 0900-1300 and 1300-1700
DISCLAIMER
Suitable for under 18's, The RSPB will reimburse you for out of pocket expenses, we will provide the equipment, training and any uniform needed for you to complete the role. We are now the largest nature conservation charity in the country, consistently delivering successful conservation, forging powerful new partnerships with other organisations and inspiring others to stand up and give nature the home it deserves. We rely on the support and generosity of our volunteers to make a difference.
Please note our vacancies are currently on FRiday, Saturday and Sunday""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Café Volunteer (RSPB Arne)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68c0e9ea1e809021bc0b7ddb :address "Arne, Arne Road, Wareham, Dorset, BH20 5BJ, England";
                            :latitude "50.690273"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.042511"^^xsd:double.
id:68c1500917c44b9986795af3 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """The Sapphire Employability and Wellbeing Academy - (Formally The Sapphire Community Group) was established to help young people access work and accredited training. Aiming to increase young people's independence, abilities and freedom to thrive, all while reducing unemployment, mental health issues, crime rates and homelessness. 

OUR AIM
Empowering, Equipping, Inspiring, Training, Mentoring, Motivating and Educating young people aged 5 to 30 years old through Employability, Wellbeing and Enrichment Support. 

OUR OBJECTIVES
1. Reducing mental health issues 
2. Reducing homelessness
3. Reducing crime rates
4. Reducing unemployment
5. Increasing young people in education or training 
6. Increasing skills development

Montra: We are an organisation that aims to reconstruct a broken culture.
We represent hope. We represent love. But most of all life.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/52332f83-53c3-430c-b79a-fa8ccca0fecc_2025-09-10T10:16:40.228Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "The Sapphire Employability and Wellbeing Academy";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.sapphirecommunity.org/>.
id:68c152ee17a83fc952f60f96 :activityDescription """Youth Helper work directly with young people in St John Ambulance Badger Setts and Cadet Units, By supporting our Youth Leaders to deliver a sessions across our range of programmes. In this role, you'll support the learning and development of young people into the next generation of health citizens. Youth Helpers also help young people develop their confidence, teamwork skills, self-discipline, and generally encourage them to strive to be the best they can be, as well as supervise and support other adult volunteers in their team.

You’ll get a huge sense of satisfaction and pride delivering an essential service. It’s great for you, great for your community and great for our nation, and it requires only a small commitment of your time. 

 

Pursuing the role
 

Closing date for these opportunities is: 20/11/2025

If you’d like to know more about volunteering or would just like to chat to someone who does, get in touch. Please contact our the hiring manager, Adam Powell via email: adam.powell@sja.org.uk

 """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "Youth Helper - Derbyshire";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68c152ee17a83fc952f60f97 :address "Trinity Street, Derby DE1 2RE";
                            :latitude "52.9168187"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4679616"^^xsd:double.
id:68c155092d6af1329bb2e447 :activityDescription """🌟 Become a Sapphire Trustee! 🌟

Do you want to make a real impact in your community? Sapphire is seeking passionate professionals to join our Board of Trustees in roles such as:
💼 Fundraising & Events | 💰 Finance | ⚖️ HR & Legal | 📈 Business Development | 📣 PR & Media

✅ Attend monthly meetings
✅ Help guide Sapphire’s growth and impact
✅ Hold leadership accountable

Together, we can support underserved communities with employment, housing, food, and clothing.

✨ What you bring: Passion. Expertise. Team Spirit. Commitment to Change.

📩 Ready to make a difference? Send your CV & short statement to: Volunteer@sapphirecommunity.org

👉 Learn more about our mission at sapphirecommunity.org

""";
