id:68c15b8f07445c3236b4209f :activityDescription """Volunteers play a vital role in the management of our sites which cover 530 hectares around Little 
Wittenham, plus seven other green spaces in and around Wallingford, Abingdon, Didcot, Besselsleigh and
Shrivenham. 
As part of this varied and diverse role, you could be doing any of the following: 
• Seasonal land management tasks 
• Woodland management, including coppicing 
• Grassland management, including scything 
• Create and manage wildlife habitats using a range of techniques and activities 
• Maintain and improve access e.g. step building, footpath management, gates and 
fencing""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425ed04c794380477b73fa1;
                            :activityTitle "Earth Trust - Land Management Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
