id:68c418137aa5ac94bda57a88 :activityDescription """We’re looking for Pool Spotter Volunteers to support our children, young people and families at our Birmingham Hospice.

At Acorns we provide care and support for life limited or life threatened children and their families.  We have three hospices in the West Midlands, which provide a happy homely environment where children can experience all kinds of great activities, meet new friends or relax and enjoy some quiet time.

Pool Spotter Volunteers need to be lifeguard trained and we provide this training free for our volunteers. Training takes 6 hours over a 1 day period and volunteers are required to retrain every 2 years.

Volunteering with us is flexible. Once sessions are planned, you choose the sessions you help with. We ask that you offer a minimum of two sessions (1-3 hours) per month. You may be asked to attend occasional meetings and additional training sessions

Volunteers are required to complete an Enhanced DBS (Disclosure and Barring Service) Check, which we will pay for and process for you.

Am I right for the role?

Pool Spotter Volunteers need to:

Be welcoming and friendly
Have good communication skills
Be physically fit and a confident swimmer
Be willing to undertake lifeguard training
Be reliable
Be sensitive to the needs of our children, young people and families

What we offer:
 
Meet new people everyday
Access to free online courses
Learn new skills to boost your CV
We’ll give you a reference for future work or volunteering
We are committed to safeguarding children and vulnerable adults and therefore any successful candidate will be subject to an enhanced DBS check for children and will be asked to provide two satisfactory references.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641096af1097b43af15de362;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Pool Spotter (Birmingham Hospice)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68c418137aa5ac94bda57a89 :address "Oak Tree Lane, Selly Oak, Birmingham B29 6HZ";
                            :latitude "52.4350952"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.9382659"^^xsd:double.
id:68c41880b4be497284f5aef9 :activityDescription """Replenishment and Merchandising Volunteer  - We have multiple Volunteer Opportunities in Acorns Children's Hospice Superstore in Harborne

The Role 

To help us to continue to provide the care that we do, we are looking for fun and enthusiastic volunteers to join us in our Harborne Superstore. Our shops are exciting and dynamic, with no two days being the same. From our walk-in customers, to receiving donations, and everything in between.

How much time will it take? 

Our shop is open Monday to Saturday 9am to 6pm and Sundays 10am to 4pm. You can volunteer the hours that suit you, but it would be great if you could support in the shop for at least 3 hours a week.

Why volunteer at Acorns? 

To help a local charity
To make a difference in your local community
To connect with like minded people and make new friends
Boost your CV
Opportunities to progress to other roles
All training will be provided
Am I right for the job?

For this role, you'll need to:

Be welcoming and friendly
Have a good eye for merchandising
Be a team player that thinks of others
Be sensitive to the needs of our customers/donators

Full training will be provided""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641096af1097b43af15de362;
                            :activityTitle "Replenishment and Merchandising Volunteer (Harborne Superstore)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68c41880b4be497284f5aefa :address "High Street, Harborne, Birmingham B17 9NJ";
                            :latitude "52.4596508"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.9461496"^^xsd:double.
id:68c4230e1ea205373227f131 :activityDescription """Volunteering for Sense

Sense is a leading disability charity with extensive knowledge and expertise in delivering personalised, creative and flexible support for disabled people with complex needs. Our tailored approach ensures that every person is empowered to live fully at every stage of life.

Due to the nature of the role, we require all applicants to be aged 16 or over. You must have a UK address to volunteer with Sense.

 

What your role will involve

You’ll get the opportunity to get involved in a wide range of activities, including:

Welcoming and assisting customers, providing great customer service, helping create a wonderful shopping experience.
Receiving donated items from the public, thanking them for their support.
Sorting, steaming and preparing donations for sale.
Helping to display stock in eye-catching and exciting ways.
Keeping the shop floor clean, safe and tidy.
Talking to customers about Sense and the work we do. 
When you’re ready, we’ll provide you with additional training to:

Serve customers on the till in a warm and friendly way.
Put sales through the till, packing them and thanking the customer for shopping with us.
Talk to customers about Gift Aid and other fundraising initiatives.
If you’re interested in taking on additional responsibilities, you can train to become a Key Volunteer, helping the shop manager by:

Helping supervise the shop and other volunteers.
Supporting the shop manager to make sure customers have a great experience.
Opening and closing the shop when needed.
Cashing up at the end of the day. 
 

Will the role suit me? Yes, if you are:

Passionate about Sense’s work to support disabled people with complex needs.
Calm, kind and have a friendly personality.
A team player who enjoys working with others.
Enthusiastic, motivated and someone with a positive attitude.
Respectful of others. 
 

What can Sense offer me as a volunteer?

Full training with ongoing support and guidance from your team.
A chance to meet new people.
A great way to develop new skills and share your existing skills.
The feeling you get knowing you’re making a difference to the lives of disabled people with complex needs.
A reference to support future applications for paid or voluntary roles.
Support from our Mental Health First Aiders, should you need it. 
 

About Sense

For everyone living with complex disabilities. For everyone who is deafblind. Sense is here to offer personalised support to help people communicate and experience the world. We believe that no one, no matter how complex their disabilities, should be isolated, left out, or unable to fulfil their potential. Our experts offer support that’s tailored to the individual needs of each person, whether that’s at our centres, through our holidays and short breaks, or in people’s own homes. In addition to practical support, we also provide information to families, and campaign for the rights of people with complex disabilities to take part in life.

Volunteers add real value to Sense, bringing their passion, enthusiasm and fresh perspectives to the work that we do. We believe that volunteers enable us to bring people together, and provide opportunities for people with complex disabilities to communicate and experience the world.

We include. We collaborate. We find a way. We challenge. We celebrate.

 """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cd68a0624f3ab9fb0c4b;
                            :activityTitle "Charity Shop Volunteer - Huddersfield Shop";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68c4230e1ea205373227f132 :address "New Street, Huddersfield HD1 2TW";
                            :latitude "53.6440309"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.7831851"^^xsd:double.
id:68c4de62007c3361fc650119 :activityDescription """We're looking for enthusiastic and creative wildlife lovers to support our busy programme of family events at [RSPB Conwy](https://www.rspb.org.uk/days-out/reserves/conwy), and inspire the next generation to love nature. From pond dipping, bug hunting and bird watching, to hands-on crafts, storytelling and sleepouts - you'll have the opportunity to get involved in a wide variety of exciting events on our brilliant nature reserve!

We'd love to hear from people with a sense of adventure and fun, experience with children and good wildlife knowledge (although this can certainly be learnt 'on the job'). We're especially looking for people who are available at weekends and during school holidays, when the majority of our family events take place.

You'll need to be a friendly and approachable people person to initiate a conversation with anyone and everyone, and share the reserve's wildlife with them. Good communication skills are key, as is an ability to enthuse and inspire children and young people. Some basic wildlife knowledge is desirable, but with regular attendance you are guaranteed to build on this very quickly. Aside from the events themselves, we are very happy to explore training opportunities for our volunteers in any areas that they wish to develop. And we'd love to hear your own ideas for events and activities to engage families too!

Does this sound like you? Then apply via the link, or get in touch for more details!

[RSPB Conwy](https://www.rspb.org.uk/days-out/reserves/conwy) has over 100 fantastic volunteers in various roles on the reserve, without whom, we simply couldn't operate! By enrolling as a volunteer, you will be joining a huge family of like-minded people dedicated to giving nature a home. We recognise our volunteer's commitment with regular social evenings and get-togethers, as well as long-service awards and discounts too.

The RSPB is committed to making our organisation diverse and inclusive, and, as such, are keen to encourage applications from everyone, of all ethnic backgrounds, as well as those with disabilities.

We look forward to hearing from you!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Engagement Family and Children Events (Visitor Engagement - Events / Ymgysylltu ag Ymwelwyr - Digwyddiadau (RSPB Conwy))";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68c4de62007c3361fc65011a :address "Conwy, Llandudno Junction, Caernarfonshire, LL31 9XZ, Wales";
                            :latitude "53.279365"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-3.805552"^^xsd:double.
id:68c4de63007c3361fc650144 :activityDescription """We are looking for work party volunteers to join us on our reserves. RSPB nature reserves are special places for people and wildlife and we rely on volunteers to keeps these habitats thriving and in good shape. This role is suitable for under 18’s. 

It might seem like these wild places have always just been there. But quite often we have to work really hard to maintain habitats to be in the best condition for wildlife. We have lost a lot of wild landscapes, so the small places that we do have, need a bit of extra care.  

As a Reserve Work Party Volunteer you will be joining a regular practical work party team to undertake practical habitat management tasks: 
- Cutting and clearing vegetation.
- Maintaining and managing tools and equipment. 
- Creating and maintaining visitor infrastructure, such as paths and benches. 
- Following annual work plans. 
- Following Health and Safety protocols. 

If you enjoy being outdoors, meeting new people and hands on conservation work, then this role could be the perfect opportunity for you. This role does involve a reasonable amount of physical activity, so will enable you to keep your fitness levels high, as well as helping your mental health and wellbeing. You will have the satisfaction of knowing that you are making a genuine contribution to nature conservation, and you might find it rewarding to safeguard nature in the area you are working to protect. 

We are a friendly and supportive team. If you are volunteering to learn new skills and gain knowledge about wildlife conservation work, you will find that our team will be more than happy to help you on that journey.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Practical Reserve Work (Culbin Sands, Nigg Bay, Udale Bay, Fairy Glen, Loch Ruthven)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68c4de63007c3361fc650145 :address "Etive House, IV2 3BW, Etive House, Beechwood Park, Inverness, Highland, IV2 3BW, United Kingdom";
                            :latitude "57.472161"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-4.187902"^^xsd:double.
id:68c4de64007c3361fc65016f :activityDescription """At the RSPB we are passionate about young people and about nature.  Our youth groups have the potential to play a really important role in local communities, offering young people regular opportunities to get to know the wild places close to them and to be supported by enthusiastic adult volunteers.

Our Liverpool Wildlife Explorers are looking for a Treasurer to support them with managing their money.

**What will you be doing?**

Collecting and banking income from group monthly activities

Monitoring group finances regularly, ensuring that all income and expenditure for the group is recorded.

Completing a financial return at the end of the financial year

**The skills you need**

Comfortable keeping simple accounts

Comfortable handling and accounting for charity money

Well organised and conscientious

Effective communication skills, to liaise with other volunteers in the group

Computer literate with internet and email access

Passionate about wildlife and nature

**What's in it for you?**

An opportunity to learn new skills and gain knowledge

Being part of a team that is making a difference to young people and helping wildlife and nature in your area.



The RSPB is the UK's largest nature conservation charity! Join our fantastic volunteers who are helping to inspire everyone to give nature a home and secure a healthy environment for wildlife. We will help you gain skills and give you an invaluable insight into our essential work.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Local Group Treasurer (Youth Group Treasurer (Liverpool Wildlife Explorers))";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68c4de64007c3361fc650170 :address "Liverpool, Merseyside, England, United Kingdom, Liverpool, United Kingdom";
                            :latitude "53.408371"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.991573"^^xsd:double.
id:68c62fee428086a728b8138a :activityDescription """We are looking for volunteers with an interest and skills in photography to run a series of events at the reserve throughout the year. The aim of the events would be to improve the participants photography skills. Courses can be run partly on the reserve, and partly in the cosy visitor centre.

As event leader you would be responsible for:

Developing the course, with the aim to make it relevant to as many potential customers as possible.
Managing the pre-booked participants list, and dealing with any walk-ups
Leading the course, giving an enjoyable and informative experience
Providing post-course notes to all participants

This is very much a face-to-face role, so good interpersonal skills are essential, as is a knowledge of cameras and modern photography.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Engagement Volunteer (On Reserves) (Photography Event Leader at RSPB Frampton)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68c62fee428086a728b8138b :address "Frampton Marsh, Roads Farmhouse, Frampton Roads, Frampton, Boston, Lincolnshire, PE20 1AY, England";
                            :latitude "52.931387"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.018938"^^xsd:double.
id:68c62fef428086a728b813b5 :activityDescription """We are looking for volunteers who can help lead our events here at Frampton Marsh and Freiston Shore. Specifically we are looking for someone with a knowledge of dragonflies and damselflies to lead scheduled dragonfly events, running between May and September.

As the event leader you will responsible for: 
Managing the list of pre-booked event participants, and potentially taking money from any walk-ups. 
Providing an enjoyable and inspirational experience to all participants. 
Running the event in a safe manner

Full training and support will be provide for this role but you do need to be a ‘people person’ and have good communication skills. You will also need good knowledge of dragonflies and damselflies.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Engagement Volunteer (On Reserves) (Dragonfly Event Leader at RSPB Frampton)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68c62fef428086a728b813b6 :address "Frampton Marsh, Roads Farmhouse, Frampton Roads, Frampton, Boston, Lincolnshire, PE20 1AY, England";
                            :latitude "52.931387"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.018938"^^xsd:double.
id:68c62ff67b16865081c27200 :activityDescription """We are looking for volunteers with an interest in astronomy to lead stargazing events, potentially both at RSPB Frampton Marsh and RSPB Freiston Shore.

The event leader would be responsible for:

Researching what is likely to be seen on the night, and advising reserve staff on how to best run the event.
Managing the prebooked participants list, and dealing with any walk-ups.
Providing an enjoyable and informative experience for all attendees at the event.
Keeping an eye on the weather, and advising RSPB staff in good time if the event needs to be cancelled.

The reserve has a variety of binoculars and telescopes for birdwatching. Possessing your own astronomical telescope that others could also use would be a huge advantage.

This is very much a face-to-face role, so good interpersonal skills are essential, as is a knowledge of astronomy.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Engagement Volunteer (On Reserves) (Astronomy Event Leader, at RSPB Frampton Marsh)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68c62ff67b16865081c27201 :address "Frampton Marsh, Roads Farmhouse, Frampton Roads, Frampton, Boston, Lincolnshire, PE20 1AY, England";
                            :latitude "52.931387"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.018938"^^xsd:double.
id:68c62ff87b16865081c27237 :activityDescription """We are looking for volunteers with specialist skills in making and editing videos, to help create a suite of promotional materials for the reserve.

Potential projects include:
- Creating videoguides about the reserve and its trails, to be featured on its website and social media.
- Recording specific events at the reserve for posterity
- Conducting interviews with reserve staff, volunteers and visitors to help promote the reserve via social media.
- Getting footage of wildlife at the reserve, for promotional use on the website and social media.

 This role provides an excellent opportunity to donate your time and skills to have real impact on our work. You will learn all about how the RSPB works and gain experience working for an environmental charity. We like to think we're a friendly and welcoming team, so you'll have the opportunity to make new friends too.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Specialist/Expert Volunteer (Videographer at RSPB Frampton Marsh)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68c62ff87b16865081c27238 :address "Frampton Marsh, Roads Farmhouse, Frampton Roads, Frampton, Boston, Lincolnshire, PE20 1AY, England";
                            :latitude "52.931387"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.018938"^^xsd:double.
id:68c62ff87b16865081c27262 :activityDescription """Imagine a day out without a coffee and cake, or a refreshing cup of tea! Our café volunteers understand the importance of a little break and help visitors to relax and refuel during their visit to Frampton. We have different roles available, so you’re bound to find something to suit.

Barista -  You’ll be making coffees and hot chocolates to order on our Barista machine. This role is great for someone who loves the smell of freshly ground coffee and a bit of theatre! And it’s also a great way to get training and experience that can help you in a career in hospitality.

Server - You’ll be warmly welcoming people, taking orders, making teas and coffees and serving counter items like scones and cake, all with a smile. This role will particularly suit you if you are someone that likes being around people. You’ll meet a lot of them in this role!

Pot washer & tidy upperer - You’ll be mainly back of house but a vital cog in the smooth running of the café. Pot washing is a priority to ensure there’s no build up as well as ensuring equipment and stock is readily available to the servers. As a break from the sink, you’ll also be keeping an eye on the tables, ensuring that they are cleared and clean!

What's in it for you? By joining us in any of the roles our café you can:

Join an enthusiastic team and make new friends
Develop your hospitality skills and put them into practice
Help us raise funds towards saving nature

Food Hygiene Level 2 and Allergen Awareness training is mandatory for all working in the café. You’ll be provided with the necessary induction, training, and equipment do this role well and safely, and we can cover the travel costs between home and your place of volunteering.

You can choose which shifts to do to fit round your other commitments.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Café Volunteer ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68c62ff97b16865081c27263 :address "Frampton Marsh, Roads Farmhouse, Frampton Roads, Frampton, Boston, Lincolnshire, PE20 1AY, England";
