id:68c62ff97b16865081c2728d :activityDescription """We are looking for volunteers who can help lead our events here at Frampton Marsh and Freiston Shore. Specifically we are looking for someone with a knowledge of bats to co-lead our Bat and Moth Evenings, running between May and September.

As the co-lead you will responsible for:
Managing the list of pre-booked event participants, and potentially taking money from any walk-ups.
Providing an enjoyable and inspirational experience to all participants.
Running the event in a safe manner

Full training and support will be provide for this role but you do need to be a ‘people person’ and have good communication skills. You will also need reasonable knowledge of bats, and how to use bat detectors to distinguish between species. Five species of bat use the reserve (Noctule, Daubenton, Common Pipistrelle, Soprano Pipistelle and Nathusius' Pipstrelle) and you will need to know how to tell which is which.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Engagement Volunteer (On Reserves) (Bat Event Leader at RSPB Frampton)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68c62ff97b16865081c2728e :address "Frampton Marsh, Roads Farmhouse, Frampton Roads, Frampton, Boston, Lincolnshire, PE20 1AY, England";
                            :latitude "52.931387"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.018938"^^xsd:double.
id:68c62ffa7b16865081c272b8 :activityDescription """We are looking for an active person with an eye for detail to help keep the reserve looking clean, tidy and litter free. As part of this role you will clean the three hides at the reserve, making it so they are comfortable and easy to use with clean windows and no litter. You will also remove litter from the two car parks at the reserve, and from the reserve paths and picnic area.

This role does involve a moderate amount of physical activity, so will enable you to keep your fitness levels high, as well as helping your mental health and wellbeing.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Practical Reserve Work (Hide cleaner and litter picker - weekends at Frampton Marsh)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68c62ffa7b16865081c272b9 :address "Frampton Marsh, Roads Farmhouse, Frampton Roads, Frampton, Boston, Lincolnshire, PE20 1AY, England";
