id:68c92f0dfadd9de6df4692c6 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a1;
                            :organisationDescription """LW was established in 1985 in Blackburn by a group of women who were concerned by the high child mortality rates and the poor maternal health outcomes for women in the city.  A house was bought by the group and set up as Lancashire Women’s Centre. 

Over the next 30 years LW continued to develop and grow its work and support for women to what it is today, celebrating our 40th birthday in 2025. 

What We Do:
We offer a whole person approach to supporting women which is trauma informed and can be accessed directly by women themselves and / or through a referral: 

We can help with : 

- Mental health issues and general health and well-being 
- Money Advice / Debt and wider welfare support issues 
- Getting into employment with coaching, skills development and confidence building 
- We also work in the prevention and rehabilitation of women connected to the criminal justice system with expertise in addressing multiple and complex unmet needs of women who have been moved from pillar to post across services and agencies.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/a9cf8e39-02c2-4e08-b051-86e62c4f5aba_2025-09-16T09:34:04.524Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Lancashire Women ";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://lancashirewomen.org/>.
id:68c9340404c4d5d5ef902d79 :activityDescription """Are you looking for a fun and rewarding way to get involved in your community? Our Active Ageing Clubs bring older members of Haringey’s Irish community together for music, dancing, bingo and plenty of laughter. We’re looking for enthusiastic and reliable volunteers to help make these gatherings welcoming, lively and full of energy!

As a volunteer, you might welcome guests, serve refreshments, help with activities like bingo or dancing, or assist with special events and celebrations. Your support helps our members stay active, social and connected while building friendships.

This role is flexible and supported by our friendly team, so if you can give a few hours a week, your time will make a real difference! Volunteering with the Active Ageing Clubs is a chance to meet new people, be part of a vibrant community, and enjoy the fun, music and laughter that make these clubs so special.

Join us and help create a welcoming, energetic space where older people can thrive and enjoy every moment!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6821cf3390eb0574a3e401d8;
                            :activityTitle "Join our Active Ageing Clubs! ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
