id:68c9393e5d474a746343819a :activityDescription """Collaborative Shop Lead (Accrington Charity Shop)
Are you a retail whizz with a passion for people and purpose?

Or someone with great organisational skills who loves helping others thrive?

We’re looking for one or more friendly, proactive volunteers to help lead our charity shop in Accrington. This is a fantastic opportunity to use your retail or leadership experience to make a real difference — and help guide a team of volunteers who are enthusiastic but new to retail.

Our shop is open Monday to Friday, 9am–5pm, and we’re flexible about how you get involved — whether that’s a regular shift or a few hours a week.

What You’ll Be Doing (with support):

- Helping oversee the shop floor and backroom operations
- Supporting and guiding volunteers with little or no retail experience
- Managing donations, pricing, and creating eye-catching displays
- Delivering excellent customer service
- Helping boost shop income to support Lancashire Women’s vital work

What We’re Looking For:

- Experience in retail, shop management, or team leadership
- A positive, can-do attitude and good organisational skills
- Confidence working independently and collaboratively
- Friendly and professional approach
- Willingness to undertake a DBS check
- Respect for confidentiality and safeguarding
- A genuine desire to get stuck in and make a difference

Why Volunteer With Us?

- Flexible hours and shared responsibilities
- A supportive environment with other staff on-site
- A chance to build community and develop skills
- The satisfaction of helping a great cause""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68c92f0dfadd9de6df4692c6;
                            :activityTitle "Collaborative Shop Lead (Accrington Charity Shop)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68c9393e5d474a746343819b :address "21-23 Blackburn Road, Accrington";
                            :latitude "53.752598"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.36296"^^xsd:double.
id:68c93c5d5d474a74634385b7 :activityDescription """We are recruiting Youth Helpers to assist at our various Cadet and Badger groups in Tamworth.

Youth Helpers work directly with young people in St John Ambulance Badger Setts and Cadet Units by supporting our Youth Leaders to deliver a sessions across our range of programmes. In this role, you'll support the learning and development of young people into the next generation of health citizens. Youth Helpers also help young people develop their confidence, teamwork skills, self-discipline, and generally encourage them to strive to be the best they can be, as well as supervise and support other adult volunteers in their team.

You’ll get a huge sense of satisfaction and pride delivering an essential service. It’s great for you, great for your community and great for our nation, and it requires only a small commitment of your time. 

Pursuing the role

If you are successful you will need to undertake induction & training for role at these dates:

Welcome Event (Induction) - 08/10/2025
Closing date for these opportunities is: Thursday 9th October 2025

If you’d like to know more about volunteering or would just like to chat to someone who does, get in touch. Please contact our the hiring manager Paul Rook via emailing: paul.rook@live.co.uk

To apply for this opportunity please follow the link below:""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "Youth Helper";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
