                            :longitude "-0.06918189999999999"^^xsd:double.
id:68ca842de9ba7914675cf0bf :cause id:66982ffbbf338eca22aa267d;
                            :organisationDescription """CharityComms is the go-to membership organisation for those working in communications in the charity sector. Our expanding network shares their expertise and experience, through our wide range of events, on-demand and digital content, reports, our mentoring scheme and more.

Our aim is to connect, inform, empower, and inspire, working with our members and the wider communications community to enable them to deliver their world-changing missions more effectively. 

Our members come from charities of all sizes and across all sectors, as well as those working as freelancers and agencies who offer products and services to support the third sector. Across everything that we do our focus is always to listen and respond to our members to deliver the support and resources that they most need.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/82aa6d5a-dcdd-4cc7-9c97-60373ce7f939_2025-09-17T09:49:33.121Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "CharityComms";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.charitycomms.org.uk/>.
id:68ca949908b37ddf7b710bac :activityDescription """Are you passionate about the power of communications to drive change and make a positive impact? Do you want to help shape the future of a vibrant, values-driven organisation at the heart of the UK charity sector? 

CharityComms is looking for two brilliant new Trustees to join our board – one with expertise in HR / legal and the other in digital marketing / AI. These are voluntary roles where you can make a real difference.  """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:68ca842de9ba7914675cf0bf;
                            :activityTitle "Trustee at CharityComms";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68ca949908b37ddf7b710bad :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:68cabb82a87987cda3b64b5f :activityDescription """We’re solarising commercial and community buildings all over the UK, from doctors' surgeries to factories and everything in between, and we’re powered by support from volunteers and members of the public. 

For this opportunity, we are especially looking for volunteers who already know of a site in their community and have contact details for the building's legal owner (...even better if you know they are interested in having solar) or are prepared to go out and find such sites.

Your role could simply be putting us in touch with these sites, or if you would like to stay involved, you could join us as a full member and help us develop and maintain a good relationship with the owner or with further training, also learn to design, help us evaluate sites and the businesses that own them.

We are looking for sites with:

1. Large roofs (tennis court-sized and up) in good condition, 
2. High electricity usage (bills over £1k/month) 
3. That are owner occupied (freehold).
4. Are not listed buildings.

If this sounds like something you could do, please apply or get in touch with Jo, the Project Lead at Big Solar Co-op, who`s coordinating all our exciting projects

Joanna@sharenergy.coop""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6878db70cb9160db05f23ff5;
