id:68cc28eb3caf422400a86435 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """Governors for Schools is a charity dedicated to supporting education through effective governance. We do this by sourcing skilled volunteers to serve on governing boards across England and Wales. For over 25 years, we’ve played a vital role in helping schools and trusts build exceptional boards, helping pupils benefit from the best possible education. 

We know that good governance is essential to school and academy trust success. That’s why we focus on building diverse, knowledgeable, and committed boards that drive positive change and enhance pupil outcomes. Our services are designed to help schools and trusts access the governance expertise they need to thrive. """;
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/e1b703e0-5521-4744-bc85-e02c511ec95c_2025-09-18T16:13:17.663Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "FE Governor Recruitment Service by GfS (Governors for Schools )";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.governorsforschools.org.uk/>.
id:68cc2aa5b918e52f8979c315 :activityDescription "Grantham College is a vibrant rural Further Education (FE) provider with over 3,000 learners, a strong focus on disadvantaged students, and unique features like a four-day week and a national Table Tennis Academy. The Board is seeking two new governors, including a Vice-Chair to support the Chair and a governor with audit, finance, or risk expertise. With a proud history in engineering and membership of the Lincolnshire Institute of Technology, the College is ambitious about growth and innovation. This is a chance to shape strategy, champion learners, and make a real impact on education in the region.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68cc28eb3caf422400a86435;
                            :activityTitle "Governor - Further Education College Corporation";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
