id:68d3e54222bcfa3adec808ee :activityDescription """3x Trustees & 1x Treasurer opportunities with Sobus 

Local charity Sobus is looking for talented, passionate individuals to join its Board of Trustees and help guide the charity through a time of exciting opportunity and development.  Ideally, be a resident or familiar with the borough of Hammersmith & Fulham and even better, experience of volunteering or working in the community and voluntary sector.  

At this time, we’re also seeking a Treasurer, who has a good understanding of charity finance issues.

At Sobus, Hammersmith & Fulham Our role is to strengthen the voice, capacity and effectiveness of the local voluntary and community sector.  With a small but dedicated team, we provide capacity building and organisational development support to local groups and organisations, support their direct engagement or represent the sector in local strategic forums and developments.  We also provide office space and meeting rooms at our hubs in Fulham and North Kensington.

The environment for the VCSE sector is challenging – with more demand for fewer resources, increasing needs and an ever changing economic and social landscape – we aim to be flexible, responsive and effective at supporting the local VCSE to rise to the challenges of the day.

Our work is focussed on five main areas: 
•	Capacity building and organisational development
•	Voice and representation – championing the voice and engagement of the VCSE sector
•	Promoting collaboration, coordination and cooperation with and between VCSE groups
•	Providing low cost office and meeting room space from our hubs
•	Supporting residents to shape local services and challenge local power dynamics

We are seeking committed individuals from diverse backgrounds and with a range of skills and experience.  Lived experience of using, working or volunteering with a community, voluntary or social enterprise organisation is a definite advantage – but just as importantly, we’re looking for people who have: 

•	A passion and commitment to the role of the VCSE sector 
•	good, independent judgement, impartiality, fairness and the ability to respect confidences
•	The ability to think strategically and creatively
•	an understanding and acceptance of the legal duties, responsibilities and liabilities of Trusteeship
•	Integrity and the ability to work effectively as a member of a team
•	a strong commitment to equalities and diversity principles and practices

Individuals might also have other skills and experiences to bring to this role, such as: 
•	fundraising and income generation and enterprise
•	Lived experience of the issues are clients/organisations face
•	Business acumen
•	Communications, promotion and marketing
•	Legal services
•	Human resources management
•	Volunteering and brokerage
•	Property management
•	Corporate Social Responsibility 
•	Social investment and impact

However, most important is your commitment to supporting the development of a strong, sustainable and vibrant voluntary, community and social enterprise sector!

Board meetings are usually held on Monday evenings from 6-8 (every 6-8 weeks).  Some input may be requested at other times, but these are subject to your availability.  

We would welcome individuals who represent the diversity of the population of Hammersmith & Fulham, particularly individuals from less heard communities, disabled people and those with lived experience.

To apply:
Email for recruitment pack to Sue Spiller
Email: sue.spiller@sobus.org.uk
Website:   http://sobus.org.uk
Telephone Number: 020 7952 1230 """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6426107cde05bf8ae7c9af41;
                            :activityTitle "Trustees & Treasurer roles for Sobus ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68d4130fc04ae2ccac4481b0 :activityDescription """At St John Ambulance, we are looking to develop our volunteering offer and become an even more integral part of our communities through delivering community first aid and education. 

We need people who have a passion for helping others, care about their communities and want to make a difference, supporting them to become safe and more resilient by sharing your first aid skills and knowledge. As a Community First Aider, you’ll deliver first aid to those in need through local events, as well as provide education to the public so that the ripple effect of First Aid grows.

Through supporting the growth of community partnerships, you will bring people along to our cause, growing our membership and fundraising base and spreading the message that First Aid Saves Lives. 

Through volunteering as a Community First Aider, you’ll get a huge sense of satisfaction and pride delivering an essential service. It’s great for you, great for your community and great for our nation, and it requires only a small commitment of your time. 

We will make sure you will have access to a proper induction to volunteering with SJA and the training you need for the role you take on. We will also provide you with a supportive environment while you are volunteering with us. Information about our volunteer roles are included in the role descriptions. What you can expect from SJA, and what we expect from those who volunteer with us, is included in the volunteer charter.

Interviews will take place at the end of November/beginning of December and Welcome Events will take place during January. 

Closing date for these opportunities is: 28/11/2025

If you’d like to know more about volunteering or would just like to chat to someone who does, get in touch. Please contact our the hiring manager, Clare Hamilton, via emailing: clare.hamilton@sja.org.uk

To apply for this opportunity please follow the link below:""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "Community First Aider (West Anglia)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68d4130fc04ae2ccac4481b1 :address "Berry Lane, Rickmansworth WD3 7HQ";
