id:68d431a411b01f859337c78d :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription "Cambs Dining Club is a community-led initiative bringing people together through elegant dining and social events in support of the NSPCC. Our flagship gatherings combine fine food, conversation, and fundraising to create memorable experiences that make a difference";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/c59248b2-b00d-4e2d-9010-dac12078a296_2025-09-24T18:00:03.396Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "NSPCC Cambridge Dining Club".
id:68d4344e11b01f859337c83a :activityDescription """About Us
Cambs Dining Club is a community-led initiative hosting elegant dining and social events across Cambridgeshire, raising funds for the NSPCC. We’re relaunching with a brand-new programme and are looking for enthusiastic volunteers to join our team.

Volunteer Roles Available
We’re building a team to make our events truly special. You don’t need to be experienced — if you have a talent, skill, or just enthusiasm in one of these areas, we’d love to hear from you:

Event Coordinators – organised, detail-focused, good at planning and bringing people together.

Partnerships & Sponsorships Volunteers – confident communicators who enjoy building relationships with local businesses and community partners.

Marketing & PR Volunteers – creative individuals with skills in social media, writing, or publicity to help us spread the word.

Membership & Community Liaison – welcoming personalities who enjoy connecting with people, supporting members, and keeping everyone informed.

Logistics & Operations Volunteers – practical, hands-on people who can help with set-up, smooth running of events, and troubleshooting on the day.

Safeguarding & Welfare Officer – someone with awareness of safeguarding best practice (training can be provided) to make sure all activities, especially family-friendly ones, are safe.

What You’ll Gain

Be part of an exciting flagship community dining initiative.

Support the NSPCC through meaningful volunteering.

Develop new skills in event management, PR, fundraising, and partnerships.

Meet new people and make a difference locally.

Time Commitment
Flexible — from occasional event-day support to more regular planning involvement.

Next Steps
If you have any one of these skills, or just enthusiasm to get involved, please get in touch. Every contribution counts, and together we can make Cambs Dining Club a success.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68d431a411b01f859337c78d;
                            :activityTitle "Be Part of Cambs Dining Club’s Volunteer Team";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68d4344e11b01f859337c83b :address "From Home";
