id:68d5487e087a45d0b6902fea :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription """We recently formed in order to save the deconsecrated, 13th century church of St Andrew the Less in Cambridge for community use.

Our aim is to preserve the church of St Andrew the Less, now on the Heritage at Risk Register, as both part of the historic landscape of Cambridge and as a contribution to the contemporary life of the area. 

We want to make the church a space for learning, connection, inspiration and support for our community and beyond. """;
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/bfd5c7e6-9d38-462f-a329-ddb9bc1e9979_2025-09-25T13:49:49.679Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "The St Andrew the Less Community Project";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.standrewtheless.org/>.
id:68d54b02c0a36d7fb9a8537f :activityDescription """We are looking for an enthusiastic and committed individual, with a keen interest in financial matters, to become a trustee with Age UK East Sussex. You will play an important role in a local charity that provides a number of valuable services helping older people meet the many challenges they face in later life.

You will provide scrutiny and oversight of the work of the charity, with a particular focus on financial issues. This will include providing the Board with the reassurance that the finances and the related processes are operating effectively, ensuring best use of the charity’s resources. You will use your financial knowledge and experience to undertake a monthly review of the Charity’s management accounts, assisting the Management Team in achieving the charity’s financial targets, as well as providing the necessary oversight of the annual audited accounts process.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66324bcff384b9c7d01f7b92;
                            :activityTitle "Charity Finance Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68d54b02c0a36d7fb9a85380 :address "Faraday Close, Eastbourne BN22 9BH";
                            :latitude "50.7960325"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.281807"^^xsd:double.
id:68d54b47087a45d0b6903237 :activityDescription """We need an expert to help us design leaflets and postcards including a few survey questions as part of a consultation exercise to find out what they want to see happen to the 13th century church of St Andrew the Less once it is restored.

We have won a grant from the Cambridge Community Grant for events and printing. We are preparing for the events at which she shall reach out to the community.

We need someone expert in design to create something eye catching and engaging.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68d5487e087a45d0b6902fea;
                            :activityTitle "Community Engagement ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68d54bcc087a45d0b6903289 :activityDescription """Age UK East Sussex is a dynamic local charity and social enterprise, providing information, advice and services to older people across the county, and influencing to improve later life. We celebrate the fact that the proportion of the county's population over pensionable age is 26% of the total population. Moreover, the relative size of the population aged over 75 years is higher than in any other county in England and Wales.

As part of our ongoing programme of Board development, we are seeking new Trustees to join us to shape our future strategy and direction, overseeing and supporting those that run the organisation on a day-to-day basis.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:66324bcff384b9c7d01f7b92;
                            :activityTitle "Charity Trustee";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68d54bcc087a45d0b690328a :address "Faraday Close, Eastbourne BN22 9BH";
                            :latitude "50.7960325"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.281807"^^xsd:double.
id:68d54cecdae4f2bdae4ddc3e :activityDescription "We are looking for someone who really enjoys using social media to create our presence online and share the exciting story of us turning and old, dilapidated church into a thriving heritage and community centre.  They need to be excited about using social media and help shape our social media strategy.  ";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68d5487e087a45d0b6902fea;
                            :activityTitle "Social Media";
