id:68d6b402553e58bdf03c7c30 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897;
                            :organisationDescription """Quilombo UK is a community-driven, non-profit organisation that exists to empower professionals and communities through cultural, educational, and professional development programmes. Its purpose is to:

Provide meaningful volunteering and professional development opportunities that help individuals build skills, gain experience, and transition into employment.

Create pathways for professionals from diverse backgrounds — including those new to the UK labour market — to access training, mentoring, and real-world experience.

Support social justice, equality, and diversity by building networks that strengthen both individuals and communities.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/447ac527-4873-4a6f-a936-eb7b4d37d0d1_2025-09-26T15:40:50.176Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "QuilomboUk";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://httpsquilomboukcom/>.
id:68d6bab822c5c958c1c99b39 :activityDescription """We Are Explorers CIC supports Neurodivergent LGBTQ+ young people and adults, offering safe, engaging, and person-led spaces for connection, learning, and self-expression. Our mission is to create a better, more inclusive world for Neurodivergent LGBTQ+ communities. Now, we want to take our impact to the next level—and we need your ideas, skills, and energy!

As a volunteer, you could:

Generate creative ideas for projects, services, and community initiatives

Help us find sponsors, donors, or new funding opportunities

Assist in creating a sustainable business plan or social enterprise strategy

Contribute skills in marketing, finance, or operations to make our CIC more self-sufficient

Support events, campaigns, or initiatives that raise awareness of our work

Who we’re looking for:

Enthusiastic, proactive people who want to make a real difference

Experience in business planning, fundraising, marketing, or event planning is a bonus—but passion matters most!

Creative thinkers ready to brainstorm and problem-solve

Time commitment: Flexible—one-off sessions or ongoing involvement welcome.

Location: We're based in Leigh, Greater Manchester, but are open to remote volunteering from people across the country!

Benefits:

Make a meaningful impact on an inclusive, growing organisation

Build skills in business development, social enterprise, and non-profit management

Join a supportive, creative team and expand your network

How to get involved:

Sign up through this platform or contact us at jam@weareexplorers.org. Let’s build something sustainable together!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6807c51be1f731a9de22a5ed;
                            :activityTitle "Improve We Are Explorers CIC's Self-Sustainability";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
