id:68d7020aaa134ce7a21cf203 :activityDescription """Could you be a Befriending Volunteer for Sheffcare?

Sheffcare is seeking compassionate and reliable Befriending Volunteers to help tackle loneliness and social isolation among older people in our residential homes.

As a befriending volunteer, you'll be a friendly face and a listening ear. You'll spend quality time with a resident, providing companionship and conversation. This is an incredibly impactful role that can make a massive difference to someone’s day and their overall well-being.

What does the role involve?

Committing to regular visits (e.g., weekly or fortnightly) to one of our residential homes.
Spending time with a resident, either one-on-one or in a small group.
Engaging in conversations, sharing stories, and listening to their experiences.
Participating in activities like reading, playing cards, or simply enjoying a cup of tea together.
Bringing warmth and companionship to someone who may not have many visitors.

Who are we looking for?

You don't need any special qualifications to be a befriending volunteer—just a few key qualities:
Friendly and approachable: A warm smile and a kind word go a long way.

A good listener: Someone who is patient and genuinely interested in what others have to say.
Reliable: Someone who can commit to regular visits so a trusted relationship can grow.
Respectful: Someone who is respectful of our residents' privacy and dignity.

This is a fantastic opportunity to give back to your community, gain experience in the care sector, and build meaningful relationships. You'll also receive ongoing support from our team at Sheffcare.
If you have a few hours to spare and a big heart, we'd love to hear from you.

Our Commitment to Inclusion 
 
Sheffcare is an equal opportunity employer and values diversity in our staff and volunteers. 
We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, experiences, and identities. 
We believe that different perspectives enrich the lives of both our residents and our teams.

This is a voluntary position and is subject to a DBS check (which will be paid for by Sheffcare).

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68d6844e9de1efdd3bbc90c6;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Befriender";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68d7020aaa134ce7a21cf204 :address "Richmond Park Grove, Sheffield S13 8HX";
                            :latitude "53.3723928"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.3996884"^^xsd:double.
id:68d7038702ae2d6d2f080b53 :activityDescription """Are you a compassionate and meticulous individual with a knack for creating a clean and comfortable environment? Sheffcare is looking for a dedicated Voluntary Housekeeper to join our team! We run various care homes across Sheffield, providing high-quality care to our residents. Your help will directly contribute to their well-being and happiness.

What you'll be doing
As a Voluntary Housekeeper, you'll be a vital part of our team, helping us maintain a high standard of cleanliness and hygiene in our care homes. Your tasks will include:
Tidying communal areas like lounges and dining rooms.
Wiping down surfaces and keeping common spaces spotless.
Dusting and vacuuming to ensure a fresh and clean atmosphere.
Assisting with laundry duties, such as folding and organising linens.
Creating a warm and welcoming environment for our residents.

Who we're looking for

We're seeking someone who is:
Reliable and trustworthy with a strong work ethic.
Friendly and compassionate, with a genuine interest in helping others.
Able to work independently and as part of a team.
Meticulous with a keen eye for detail.
Respectful of our residents' privacy and dignity.
No prior experience is necessary, as complete training will be provided. The most important qualities are a caring attitude and a willingness to help.

Why volunteer with us?

Volunteering with Sheffcare is a rewarding experience. You'll have the chance to:
Make a real difference in the lives of elderly people.
Gain new skills and experience in a care setting.
Meet new people and join a supportive team.
Enhance your CV and gain valuable experience for future roles.
We value our volunteers greatly and will provide you with a full induction and ongoing support.
Our Commitment to Inclusion 
 
Sheffcare is an equal opportunity employer and values diversity in our staff and volunteers. 
We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, experiences, and identities. 
We believe that different perspectives enrich the lives of both our residents and our teams.

This is a voluntary position and is subject to a DBS check (which will be paid for by Sheffcare).
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68d6844e9de1efdd3bbc90c6;
                            :activityTitle "Volunteer Care Home Housekeeper";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68d7038702ae2d6d2f080b54 :address "Richmond Park Grove, Sheffield S13 8HX";
                            :latitude "53.3723928"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.3996884"^^xsd:double.
id:68d704026e6781abbec58861 :activityDescription """Are you a green-fingered enthusiast with a passion for plants and people?

Sheffcare is a not-for-profit organisation providing quality care for older people in our residential homes across Sheffield. We believe that beautiful, well-maintained gardens are a vital part of creating a positive and nurturing environment for our residents. They offer a space for relaxation, socialising, and reminiscence, and can even be a source of therapeutic activity.

We are looking for enthusiastic and dedicated Volunteer Gardeners to help us maintain and enhance the outdoor spaces at our homes. Whether you have a lot of experience or are just starting out, your time and effort will make a huge difference to the lives of our residents.

What you will do:

General garden maintenance, including weeding, pruning, and watering.
Planting flowers, shrubs, and vegetables to create vibrant and engaging spaces.
Helping to keep paths and communal areas tidy and safe.
Working with staff and other volunteers to plan and develop garden projects.
Potentially supporting residents to get involved in simple gardening activities, if you feel comfortable doing so.

What we are looking for:

A passion for gardening and the outdoors.
Reliability and a commitment to helping others.
A friendly and compassionate nature.
The ability to work independently or as part of a team.
No specific qualifications are needed, just a willingness to get your hands dirty!

What we offer:

The chance to make a real, tangible difference to the lives of older people.
The opportunity to meet new people and become part of the Sheffcare team.
Flexible volunteering hours to fit around your schedule.
The satisfaction of seeing your hard work flourish and bring joy to our residents.
Relevant training and ongoing support from our staff.
Our Commitment to Inclusion 
 
Sheffcare is an equal opportunity employer and values diversity in our staff and volunteers. 
We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, experiences, and identities. 
We believe that different perspectives enrich the lives of both our residents and our teams.

This is a voluntary position and is subject to a DBS check (which will be paid for by Sheffcare).
""";
