id:68da9e57fa883e8f3d5e3ba6 :activityDescription """Two Temple Place is a magnificent neo-Tudor gem in central London, built in 1895 for William Waldorf Astor. In 2011 we opened our first annual free exhibition, and since then exhibitions have welcomed 460,000 visitors. We run a growing programme of cultural and community events designed to open our doors more often, to more people. We rely on our friendly and enthusiastic team of more than 180 volunteers to make our free exhibitions possible. We are recruiting volunteers for our 2026 exhibition, The Weight of Being, which will explore the profound ways in which external pressures shape artistic expression, mental health, and resilience, highlighting the power of art as a means of expression, resistance, and survival.
Volunteers provide support in a front of house role by:
•Welcoming and engaging with visitors
•Ensuring the safety of visitors and exhibition objects
•Providing information about the building, the exhibitions, and events
•Looking after the gallery spaces
•Helping us run the exhibition shop (optional)

We look to recruit volunteers who are:
•Friendly & polite
•Helpful & proactive
•Punctual & reliable
•Keen to learn & enthusiastic

We welcome people of all abilities and offer a supportive environment for those with additional needs. We provide all training for the role; no prior volunteering or gallery experience is needed, just enthusiasm and commitment!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6426134bde05bf8ae7ca09b6;
                            :activityTitle "Gallery Steward Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68da9e57fa883e8f3d5e3ba7 :address "London WC2R 3BD";
                            :latitude "51.51160120000001"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.112247"^^xsd:double.
id:68db47ee58eba38c4a0a36a6 :activityDescription """We are looking for volunteers to help in our shops on reserves. Volunteers serve customers, stock shelves and make our shops a friendly place to visit. Profits made from our shops mean that we can continue to protect wildlife. 

In order to ensure that visitors have an enjoyable and safe visit, we need a team of volunteers to help everything run smoothly. When people visit our shops, we want them to have a warm welcome and to be able to talk to the team about the products, such as bird food and feeders. We also need to ensure that shelves are stocked, and the retail space is clean and tidy. All this work requires a team of friendly and supportive people to help out. We simply can't run our shops without volunteers. Profits made from our shops mean that we can continue to protect wildlife, so they're an important part of our work. 

Support and training will be provided but having the following skills or experience would be good: 
 
- Have good communication skills and enjoy talking to new people.
- Enjoy working as part of a team.
- Willing to be flexible and take on different tasks as and when needed. 
- Prior retail experience.

This is a rewarding role with a friendly team during which you will learn new skills and gain experience working in the hospitality industry. The money raised through our retail and catering contributes to nature conservation, through the so you’ll get satisfaction from making a difference.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
