id:68dd2b7e22fc21f829eee90e :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription """With a diverse range of experience, from charity governance to communications, land stewarding and education, our trustees and executive team are passionate about transforming lives.

Through our charitable giving, estate and collaborative partnerships, we help communities across east Dorset to live well.

Our Board of Trustees review grant applications and ensure that our funds and resources go to support a broad range of local causes, securing prosperity and opportunity for existing and future generations. United by a common goal to transform lives for the better, each Trustee gives their time free of charge, without financial benefit.

""";
                            :organisationName "Talbot Village Trust";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://talbotvillagetrust.org/about-us/who-we-are/>.
id:68dd362a5c3c01d7fc4c3441 :activityDescription """Talbot Village Trust is recruiting volunteers to help us maintain our historic woodland over Winter! 

This will include a variety of practical tasks such as bramble bashing, path maintenance and the removal of invasive species. Volunteers will have the opportunity to learn many employable skills relating to the Conservation industry. 

These sessions will also be a great opportunity to spend some time outdoors, and get involved with your local community!

Sessions will be roughly 2 hours long, including a full tool talk and briefing. They will initially take place on Tuesdays and Fridays, with refreshments included as standard!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68dd2b7e22fc21f829eee90e;
                            :activityTitle "Woodland Conservation Vounteering";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68de14dbb3a8f9794c262702 :activityDescription "Characters are responsible for dressing up as popular childhood heroes, such as Ariel or Spiderman, to bring magic to children we visit in a variety of environments. This could be at an activity centre, a hospital ward, or somewhere else entirely. If you live in the Oxfordshire area, have a passion for dressing up, and want to put some smiles on children's faces, this is perfect for you!";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6899ea37e1f77e32cb5b2b47;
                            :activityTitle "Make a Smile character";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68de14dbb3a8f9794c262703 :address "Oxfordshire, UK";
                            :latitude "51.7612056"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.2464674"^^xsd:double.
id:68de27635322f0a9a2e38235 :activityDescription """We are looking for work party volunteers to join us on our reserves. RSPB nature reserves are special places for people and wildlife and we rely on volunteers to keeps these habitats thriving and in good shape. This role is NOT suitable for under 18’s. 

It might seem like these wild places have always just been there. But quite often we have to work really hard to maintain habitats to be in the best condition for wildlife. We have lost a lot of wild landscapes, so the small places that we do have, need a bit of extra care.  

As a Reserve Work Party Volunteer you will be joining a regular practical work party team to undertake practical habitat management tasks: 
- Cutting and clearing vegetation.
- Maintaining visitor infrastructure, such as paths and benches. 
- Following annual work plans. 
- Following Health and Safety protocols. 

If you enjoy being outdoors, meeting new people and hands on conservation work, then this role could be the perfect opportunity for you. This role does involve a reasonable amount of physical activity, so will enable you to keep your fitness levels high, as well as helping your mental health and wellbeing. You will have the satisfaction of knowing that you are making a genuine contribution to nature conservation, and you might find it rewarding to safeguard nature in the area you are working to protect.  

Note work parties meet mainly on Thursday at 10am, finishing at 2pm. Note during this time you will often be over a 15 minute walk from toilets.

We are a friendly and supportive team. If you are volunteering to learn new skills and gain knowledge about wildlife conservation work, you will find that our team will be more than happy to help you on that journey.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Practical Reserve Work (Woolston Eyes SSSI Thelwall Lane, Warrington)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68de27635322f0a9a2e38236 :address "Woolston Eyes, Thelwall Lane, Woolston, Warrington, Lancashire, WA4 1PD, England";
                            :latitude "53.387007"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.523526"^^xsd:double.
id:68de349d27079b81e0578411 :activityDescription """At St John Ambulance, we are looking to develop our volunteering offer and become an even more integral part of our communities through delivering community first aid and education. 

We need people who have a passion for helping others, care about their communities and want to make a difference. Through volunteering as an Emergency Responder, you’ll get a huge sense of satisfaction and pride delivering essential first aid and lifesaving clinical care at community and major events in your areas, including at sporting events, concerts, community festivals.

We will make sure you will have access to a proper induction to volunteering with SJA and the training you need for the role you take on. We will also provide you with a supportive environment while you are volunteering with us. Information about our volunteer roles are included in the role descriptions. What you can expect from SJA, and what we expect from those who volunteer with us, is included in the volunteer charter.

Interviews available for booking after application on evenings throughout October, November & December

Welcome Evenings: 25th November 16th December, New Year Dates TBC


6 day in-person training course with mandatory pre-course learning.

Closing date for these opportunities is: 31/10/2025

If you’d like to know more about volunteering or would just like to chat to someone who does, get in touch. Please contact our the hiring manager, Sam Austin, via emailing: c-nyt-volunteers@sja.org.uk

To apply for this opportunity please follow the link below:""";
