id:68de893de0aa13d8441ef816 :activityDescription """In 2013, Entelechy Arts and the Albany, in partnership with Lewisham Council, established Meet Me at the Albany—an arts and social club for over-65s.

Led by a vibrant and diverse community of previously isolated older people, Meet Me is more than just a club. Every Tuesday, members gather at the Albany Theatre in Deptford to take part in a cross-artform programme where they can make friends, be creative, advocate for themselves, and contribute to the rich cultural life of Lewisham.

From singing to painting, drumming to dance, crafting to gardening—every week is different, and every week is full of warmth, energy, and creativity.

This is a space for joy, connection, and creativity—and our volunteers are at the heart of it all.

As a volunteer, you’ll help us create the warm, friendly environment that makes Meet Me at the Albany so special. Tasks include:
* Greeting members and making them feel at home
* Helping set up and tidy away activities
* Making teas and coffees
* Chatting with participants and building connections
* Supporting artists to ensure everyone can take part

You don’t need any special skills—just kindness, patience, and a willingness to get involved.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68a5f3c22ef6471c76341701;
                            :activityTitle "Meet Me at the Albany";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
