id:68dfe88ab32a4fbdd7dc3a61 :activityDescription """Volunteer with us!  Volunteer Opportunities in Acorn's Children's Hospice Superstore.

At Acorns we provide care and support for life limited or life threatened children and their families. We are a charity, so most of the care that we provide is funded through fundraising and through our shops.

To help us to continue to provide the care that we do, we are looking for fun and enthusiastic volunteers to join us in our Harborne Superstore shop. Our shops are exciting and dynamic, with no two days being the same. From our walk-in customers, to receiving donations, and everything in between.

Our shop is open Monday to Thursday 9am to 6pm and Friday's & Saturdays 9am to 7pm & Sundays 10am to 4pm. You can volunteer the hours that suit you, but it would be great if you could support in the shop for at least 3 hours a week.

As a Shop Volunteer with us, you will be:

Engaging with customers
Accepting and sorting donated stock
Pricing donations for sale
Working on the till
Why Volunteer at Acorns?

To help a local charity and make a difference in your local community
Connect with likeminded people and make new friends
Enhance your CV by learning new skills and gaining experience
Opportunities to progress to other roles
Access to free online courses
Retail discounts
Invites to social events and participation in our volunteer recognition schemes and rewards
Full training will be provided""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641096af1097b43af15de362;
                            :activityTitle "Retail Volunteers ( Harborne Superstore)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68dfe88ab32a4fbdd7dc3a62 :address "High Street, Harborne, Birmingham B17 9NJ";
                            :latitude "52.4596508"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.9461496"^^xsd:double.
id:68e08ddf4037602aab298bf2 :activityDescription """Available 6th July 2026

Commitment:  6-12 months, must include July and August

**Why We Want You**

The Lincolnshire reserve of Frampton Marsh has quickly become one of the best loved of all RSPB nature reserves. With a stunning array of wildlife offering close-up views, a reputation for helpful staff and an impressive record of rare species, this reserve has been making waves, regularly being mentioned as one of the best birdwatching sites in the country. It is popular with local families too, with popular events in the school holidays. Set against the stunning backdrop of The Wash, the reserve is prime destinations for birders, nature lovers and families.

We are looking for a residential volunteer to help us deliver the first class visitor experience that the Lincolnshire reserve is famous for. As a visitor engagement volunteer you will be instrumental in liaising with our visitors, delivering the events programme and assisting with promotional work through social media and other means.

If you want to spend your day with people who are passionate about nature and conservation, who are excited to share their knowledge and enthusiasm with others and who love their work then Frampton Marsh is the place for you!

We are a dynamic, forward thinking and customer based team which offers visitors a friendly welcome, a wealth of knowledge and an overall amazing experience which brings them back year after year. We are committed to protecting our wildlife and environments through innovative projects and proactive management of our diverse habitats. If you can engage with people, share our vision and inspire them to support our campaigns then we want to hear from you.

**What’s In It For You**

This is an ideal opportunity for anyone wanting to pursue a career or interest in visitor engagement, hospitality or tourism. You will gain practical experience in supporting a range of activities both on and off site, learn how to market and promote a leading tourist attraction, look after aspects of our quality assurance and take a key role in managing our social media.

Our staff and volunteers will offer you the support and training you need to have a worthwhile and productive experience. Development of skills, proficiencies and aptitudes are all on your agenda as you work with our knowledgeable and enthusiastic team.

In addition, you will benefit from free accommodation in our grade II listed Georgian farmhouse just a short walk from the reserve.

**Requirements**

Are you methodical, innovative and able to communicate with people at all levels? Can you work alone without supervision, plan ahead and be flexible in your work experience? (our volunteering week usually runs from Monday to Friday but you may be asked to help out on occasional weekends, early mornings or evenings).

You must be over 18 years old, confident using a computer and have strong social media skills (some administrative experience would be a bonus). You will need to be a team player who is willing to turn their hand to any one of a number of tasks, come rain or shine. A full clean driving licence is highly desirable.

If you are excited to work with us and share our commitment to save nature, you could be the person we are looking for!

**Notes**

For information on the role, the reserve and the accommodation offered, please contact Chris Andrews on 01205725143 or email chris.andrews@RSPB.org.uk

Interviews will be conducted for this placement, date and time to be arranged.

Please note that this role does not offer experience in habitat management, wildlife surveys or reserve maintenance.

Appropriate training will be provided and expenses will be re-imbursed where necessary.

The RSPB is the UK charity working to secure a healthy environment for birds and wildlife, helping to create a better world for all of us. We belong to BirdLife International, the global partnership of bird conservation organisations. Your time and skills could make a real difference to the work of the RSPB and it would be great if you could join us.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Residential on Reserve (More than 4 weeks) (Visitor Experience, at RSPB Frampton)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68e08ddf4037602aab298bf3 :address "Frampton Marsh, Roads Farmhouse, Frampton Roads, Frampton, Boston, Lincolnshire, PE20 1AY, England";
                            :latitude "52.931387"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.018938"^^xsd:double.
id:68e08de04037602aab298c1d :activityDescription """Description
Where: Lincolnshire. RSPB Lincolnshire Wash Reserves: Frampton Marsh and Freiston Shore
When: From November 2025
Commitment: From one month to one year depending on availability
Duration: From November 2025

**Why we want you**
We are looking for an enthusiastic Residential Volunteer to help us deliver all aspects of our reserve management programme. We have a real desire to continue to develop and improve the reserves, making them better for wildlife  and visitors all year round.  You will be a central part of our ambitious reserve team, helping us deliver our species targets while providing a wonderful visitor experience.

**What’s in it for you**
Frampton Marsh and Freiston Shore are at the forefront of innovative habitat and visitor management techniques. You will get the chance to be part of developing these processes and influence how we view reserve management for years to come, both for wildlife and visitors. We are offering you the chance to learn and develop your skills on managing wetlands, maintaining infrastructure, conducting research, survey and monitoring. Our team are all very keen to help you start your career in conservation and so far we have a high success rate of our residential volunteers finding paid employment. The accommodation provided is a large Georgian Grade II listed farmhouse  which is a one minute walk from the Frampton reserve boundary. 

**Requirements**
You will be able to work both as part of a team and undertake tasks yourself. You should have a keen interest in conservation, good interpersonal skills, a desire to learn and develop your identification skills of birds and other wetland wildlife. You must be prepared to undertake outdoor practical work in a variety of weather conditions. You must also be aged 18 or over and have a full driving licence.

**Notes**
For information on the role, the reserve and the accommodation offered, please contact Simon Wilson: simon.wilson@rspb.org.uk  
Interviews will be conducted for this placement, date and time to be arranged.
Accommodation and appropriate training will be provided and expenses will be re-imbursed where necessary.

The RSPB is the UK charity working to secure a healthy environment for birds and wildlife, helping to create a better world for all of us. We belong to BirdLife International, the global partnership of bird conservation organisations. Your time and skills could make a real difference to the work of the RSPB and it would be great if you could join us.

**More about this role**

**Volunteer role**: Residential on Reserve (More than 4 weeks)
**Where you will be based**: Roads Farmhouse, RSPB Frampton Marsh

**Why we want you**
Our residential volunteering opportunities are essential for keeping our reserves going. We are looking for volunteers to stay at one of our residential reserves for between 4 weeks to 1 year, which means our residential volunteers provide support that is integral.

The RSPB is the UK's largest nature conservation charity! Join our fantastic volunteers who are helping to inspire everyone to give nature a home and secure a healthy environment for wildlife. We will help you gain skills and give you an invaluable insight into our essential work.

**What you will be doing**
• Tasks vary greatly depending on which reserve you volunteer for, but it will be vital work and is likely to include some of the following:
• Practical conservation/management tasks.
• Undertaking wildlife monitoring and surveying.
• Reserve checks and general reserve maintenance.
• Visitor operations e.g. welcoming visitors and directing them to points of interest.
• Running or helping out at public events.

**The skills you need**
• We will provide all the training and information needed to carry out the role. Depending on which residential opportunity you apply for, you might need some more specific experience in a key area. We are looking for:
• Enthusiasm.
• Willingness to learn and work as part of a team.
• An interest in wildlife conservation.
• Driving licence.

**What's in it for you**
• Since you will be living on the reserve, this is a truly immersive volunteering experience.
• You will have the opportunity to work in a beautiful wildlife-rich setting and will get the satisfaction of doing something to help nature and see the direct results of your action.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Residential on Reserve (More than 4 weeks) (RSPB Frampton Marsh)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68e08de04037602aab298c1e :address "Frampton Marsh, Roads Farmhouse, Frampton Roads, Frampton, Boston, Lincolnshire, PE20 1AY, England";
                            :latitude "52.931387"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.018938"^^xsd:double.
id:68e34e8ec8a1346ff1642c2d :activityDescription """Are you passionate about making a difference? 
Are you good at communication skills?
Are you skilled in convincing others?
Then, this volunteer opportunity is for you!

We’re looking for a few committed and energetic volunteers to serve as HR Liaisons—helping us build meaningful partnerships with Corporate HR teams to promote workplace giving.

As an HR Liaison, you’ll play a key role in connecting NCT’s mission with companies that care. Your goal will be to:

Establish clear and consistent communication with HR departments.
Align NCT’s programs with corporate values and CSR goals.
Engage leadership and HR teams to foster a culture of giving.
Leverage HR’s role in employee engagement to make giving easy, meaningful, and sustainable.
What You’ll Do
Build strong relationships with HR professionals.
Craft and share a compelling narrative about NCT’s impact.
Encourage companies to include NCT in their workplace giving platforms.
Help employees feel a sense of ownership and pride in supporting NCT.
Why NCT?
NCT is already vetted and verified for workplace giving through:

Benevity Causes
YourCause + Blackbaud Fund
Charities Aid Foundation (CAF) America
This means companies can easily support NCT through payroll giving, matching grants, and donor-advised funds—making donations seamless and impactful.

Who Can Volunteer?
This opportunity is perfect for:
-Students
-Retirees
-Stay-at-home parents
-Professionals looking to expand their network
-Anyone with a compassionate heart and a desire to uplift vulnerable communities

What You’ll Gain
A chance to make a real difference in the lives of women and children from the poorest communities.
Opportunities to grow as a communicator and relationship-builder.
A Volunteer Appreciation Certificate and a Reference Letter upon request.
Join Us Today
Your time and skills can help build a brighter future. Be a part of something meaningful. Help us make the world a better place—one partnership at a time.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68aebc90330528cfb780308c;
                            :activityTitle "HR Liaison for Workplace Giving Partnerships";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68e34e8ec8a1346ff1642c2e :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:68e375f9fc8c7774abbfe787 :activityDescription """At St John Ambulance, we are looking to develop our volunteering offer and become an even more integral part of our communities through delivering community first aid and education. 

We need people who have a passion for helping others, care about their communities and want to make a difference. Through volunteering as an Emergency Responder, you’ll get a huge sense of satisfaction and pride delivering essential first aid and lifesaving clinical care at community and major events in your areas, including at sporting events, concerts, community festivals.

We will make sure you will have access to a proper induction to volunteering with SJA and the training you need for the role you take on. We will also provide you with a supportive environment while you are volunteering with us. Information about our volunteer roles are included in the role descriptions. What you can expect from SJA, and what we expect from those who volunteer with us, is included in the volunteer charter.

Are you a current Keele student looking to make a difference during your time at university? 

The Keele University Group is part of the Stoke and Keele Network, offering you the best of both worlds: student-led sessions on campus and access to a wide range of training and public event medical cover across the wider area. 

There will be a six-day Emergency Responder Course and associated e-learning to be completed for the role. 

There is a minimum requirement of 100 hours of volunteering per year. 

Keele students meet on Monday evenings (7 pm) during term time on the Keele Campus (Dorothy Hodgkin Building). You’re also welcome to join Wednesday sessions at our partner hub located in Stoke, or the Tuesday sessions run by our neighbouring network at either Hanley or Cheadle. 

You must be able to complete a minimum of 100 clinical volunteering hours each year at events to keep your skills up to date. 

This vacancy is also open to prospective volunteers looking to join the North Staffordshire Network. We have meetings on Tuesday evening from 7:30 pm at the following locations: 

Hanley meetings -> St John Ambulance, Sheaf Street, Hanley, Stoke-on-Trent, ST1 4LW 

Cheadle meetings -> Thorley Drive Pitches, Cheadle, Stoke-on-Trent, ST10 1SA 

We also have meetings on a Wednesday Evening from 8 pm at: Stoke-on-Trent meetings -> West End Community Centre, 405 London Road, Stoke-on-Trent, ST4 5AW

Any Questions Contact: Sophia.Khas@sja.org.uk (Keele University Students) Emma.Powell@sja.org.uk (All locations)

To apply for this opportunity please follow the link below:""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641096af1097b43af15de362;
                            :activityTitle "Emergency Responder (Keele & Stoke Network)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68e375f9fc8c7774abbfe788 :address "Keele, Newcastle ST5 5BG";
                            :latitude "53.0030727"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.2737135"^^xsd:double.
id:68e37bbd21516a6fc1e1dfeb :activityDescription """At St John Ambulance, we are looking to develop our volunteering offer and become an even more integral part of our communities through delivering community first aid and education. 

We need people who have a passion for helping others, care about their communities and want to make a difference, supporting them to become safe and more resilient by sharing your first aid skills and knowledge. As a Community First Aider, you’ll deliver first aid to those in need through local events, as well as provide education to the public so that the ripple effect of First Aid grows.

Through supporting the growth of community partnerships, you will bring people along to our cause, growing our membership and fundraising base and spreading the message that First Aid Saves Lives. 

Through volunteering as a Community First Aider, you’ll get a huge sense of satisfaction and pride delivering an essential service. It’s great for you, great for your community and great for our nation, and it requires only a small commitment of your time. 

We will make sure you will have access to a proper induction to volunteering with SJA and the training you need for the role you take on. We will also provide you with a supportive environment while you are volunteering with us. Information about our volunteer roles are included in the role descriptions. What you can expect from SJA, and what we expect from those who volunteer with us, is included in the volunteer charter.

Interviews will begin from the week commencing 3rd November at St John Ambulance, Sheaf Street, Hanley, Stoke-on-Trent, ST1 4LW

There will be a two-day Community First Aid Course and associated e-learning to be completed for the role. There is a minimum requirement of 80 hours of volunteering per year. Meetings held on a Tuesday evening from 7:30pm at St John Ambulance, Sheaf Street, Hanley, Stoke-on-Trent, ST1 4LW Alternative meeting place at held on a Tuesday evening from 7:30pm at Thorley Drive Pitches, Cheadle, Stoke-on-Trent, ST10 1SA
 

Closing date for these opportunities is: 03/11/2025

If you’d like to know more about volunteering or would just like to chat to someone who does, get in touch. Please contact our the hiring manager, Emma Powell, via emailing: Emma.Powell@sja.org.uk

To apply for this opportunity please follow the link below:""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "Community First Aider (Staffordshire, Shropshire & Wolverhampton)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68e37bbd21516a6fc1e1dfec :address "33 Sheaf St, Hanley, Stoke-on-Trent";
                            :latitude "53.0197864"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.1830804"^^xsd:double.
id:68e37be351719734cd1cc7d8 :activityDescription """At St John Ambulance, we are looking to develop our volunteering offer and become an even more integral part of our communities through delivering community first aid and education. 

We need people who have a passion for helping others, care about their communities and want to make a difference, supporting them to become safe and more resilient by sharing your first aid skills and knowledge. As a Community First Aider, you’ll deliver first aid to those in need through local events, as well as provide education to the public so that the ripple effect of First Aid grows.

Through supporting the growth of community partnerships, you will bring people along to our cause, growing our membership and fundraising base and spreading the message that First Aid Saves Lives. 

Through volunteering as a Community First Aider, you’ll get a huge sense of satisfaction and pride delivering an essential service. It’s great for you, great for your community and great for our nation, and it requires only a small commitment of your time. 

We will make sure you will have access to a proper induction to volunteering with SJA and the training you need for the role you take on. We will also provide you with a supportive environment while you are volunteering with us. Information about our volunteer roles are included in the role descriptions. What you can expect from SJA, and what we expect from those who volunteer with us, is included in the volunteer charter.

In-person interviews in Kidlington or Oxford will be arranged in the second half of November and in-person training for role will take place on 24th and 25th January. If this is not possible, we would still love to hear from you! Please do email jamie.wilmore@sja.org.uk to discuss alternative options.


In-person interviews in Kidlington or Oxford will be arranged in the second half of November


Induction will take place in person in the second half of November. You will be assigned an existing volunteer as an Induction Buddy to help you begin your volunteering journey.

Closing date for these opportunities is: 07/11/2025

If you’d like to know more about volunteering or would just like to chat to someone who does, get in touch. Please contact our the hiring manager, Jamie Wilmore, via emailing: jamie.wilmore@sja.org.uk.

To apply for this opportunity please follow the link below:""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "Community First Aider (Oxfordshire)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68e37be351719734cd1cc7d9 :address "High Street, Kidlington OX5 2DN";
