                            :longitude "-3.805548"^^xsd:double.
id:68e72586749a31cc2d4e138f :activityDescription """*Scroll down for English*

Dychmygwch ddiwrnod heb goffi na chacen!
 
Ydych chi'n mwynhau cwrdd â phobl newydd ac yn chwilio am her newydd? Neu hoffech chi roi rhywbeth yn ôl i'r gymuned leol? Rydyn ni’n chwilio am wirfoddolwyr i gefnogi ein tîm i redeg y caffi poblogaidd a chyfeillgar yma yn [RSPB Conwy](https://www.rspb.org.uk/days-out/reserves/conwy). Rydyn ni’n chwilio am wirfoddolwyr i helpu yn ystod yr wythnos ar **ddydd Llun, dydd Mawrth, dydd Mercher neu dydd Gwener**

Fel rhan o dîm ein caffi, byddwch yn helpu i sicrhau bod ymwelwyr yn cael ymweliad pleserus a diogel. Pan fydd pobl yn ymweld â'n caffis, rydyn ni am iddyn nhw gael croeso cynnes, a mwynhau eu bwyd a'u diodydd mewn amgylchedd ymlaciol a glân. Ac mae angen tîm o bobl gyfeillgar a chefnogol ar gyfer y gwaith hwn.
Fel rhan o dîm ein caffi, byddwch yn gweini diodydd poeth ac oer i gwsmeriaid, yn clirio byrddau, yn siarad â chwsmeriaid am ein dewisiadau bwyd a diod, a hefyd yn cynnal safonau glendid a chodau ymarfer iechyd a diogelwch. Byddwch chi'n helpu ymwelwyr i ddod o hyd i seddi ac yn ateb cwestiynau. 
 
Fel rhan o'ch rôl, byddwch yn dysgu sgiliau newydd ac yn ennill profiad o weithio yn y diwydiant lletygarwch. Fe gewch chi sgiliau trosglwyddadwy gwych, fel gwasanaeth cwsmeriaid, ymwneud â phobl, a dilyn protocolau iechyd a diogelwch. 

Mae'r arian a godir trwy ein siopau manwerthu ac arlwyo yn cyfrannu at gadwraeth natur, felly rydych chi hefyd yn helpu i achub byd natur!

---

If  you enjoy meeting new people and looking for a new challenge? Or would like to give something back to the local community? We are looking for volunteers to support our team to run the popular and friendly café here at [RSPB Conwy](https://www.rspb.org.uk/days-out/reserves/conwy). We are looking for volunteers to help in the week on a **Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Friday**

As part of our café team you will help to ensure that visitors have an enjoyable and safe visit. When people visit our cafes, we want them to have a warm welcome, and enjoy their food and drinks in relaxing and clean surroundings. All this work requires a team of friendly and supportive people to help out. 
As part of our café team you will be serving customers hot and cold drinks, clearing tables, talking to customers about our food and drink options, maintaining cleanliness standards and health and safety codes of practice. You will be helping visitors find seating and answering questions.  

As part of your role you will learn new skills and gain experience working in the hospitality industry, including great transferable skills, such as customer service, people engagement, following health and safety protocols. 

The money raised through our retail and catering contributes to nature conservation, so you are also helping to save nature!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Café Volunteer (RSPB Conwy) / Gwirfoddolwr Caffi (RSPB Conwy)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68e72586749a31cc2d4e1390 :address "R S P B Nature Reserve LLANDUDNO JUNCTION LL31 9XZ UNITED KINGDOM, Llandudno Junction, Conwy, LL31 9XZ, United Kingdom";
                            :latitude "53.279348"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-3.805548"^^xsd:double.
id:68e773d8119ad5920b480b6c :activityDescription """Are you thinking of pursuing a career in healthcare and want to gain experience in the field? Would you like to gain some hands-on experience working with patients? Do you want to know what it’s like to work on a ward with multi-disciplinary teams? Are you curious to see compassionate care in action?

If yes to all of the above (and you are aged between 17-19 years by March 2026), this could be the programme for you! In exchange for a few hours every week, we can help support your career ambitions by providing you with meaningful and valuable experience volunteering directly with patients in our In-Patient Unit (IPU). Our Ward Support Volunteers get amazing opportunities on every shift to care for patients and support our nurses and healthcare assistants.

Over the course of this 6 month programme, you will interact with patients and staff on a weekly basis, gain invaluable insights into compassionate healthcare and expand your skill set, knowledge, and confidence. You’ll also meet other Ward Support Volunteers with interests similar to yours. At the end of the programme, we recognise and celebrate your volunteering journey with a certificate of your achievement.

You must be able to commit to volunteering one evening every week, from 8 March 2026, for six months with minimal absence. The mandatory training day will be Saturday 7 March 2025.

Closing date for applications is 23 November 2025. Interviews will take place in December.

Find out more here: https://www.pah.org.uk/volunteer-roles/ward-support-volunteer/ 
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425d5fca0624f3ab9fbc83b;
                            :activityTitle "Ward Support Volunteer";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68e773d8119ad5920b480b6d :address "Esher KT10 8NA";
