id:68e793d5bebfd220e4aec748 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription """Launched in 2016 by a committed group of people determined to deliver locally owned community energy. Award-winning Grimsby Community Energy is a community benefit society (CBS), a form of not-for-profit cooperative owned and run by local people that works for the benefit of the community.

Over the last eight years we have raised over £894,000 of investment to deliver renewable energy across Grimsby, Cleethorpes and North East Lincolnshire, installing 697kW of solar PV (photovoltaic) panels for community organisations, generating 1.14GWh of clean electricity and saving 279t of CO2.

This place-based approach to energy generation means local community organisations pay less for their energy and everyone who invests in Grimsby Community Energy has a vote in the running of our society. We are proud to have kept our promises to our investors and our community, ensuring we pay members a fair rate of return and creating wider community benefits, including creating jobs and establishing a community fund.

Our team have worked hard to develop our business but there is so much more we can do with your support. We appreciate grant funding from Co-operatives UK Booster Fund, NELC’s UK Shared Prosperity Fund, and the REACH Fund.

Our vision is to reach one megawatt of community owned solar PV by the end of 2025, and we won’t stop there, adding a second megawatt by 2030. So far, we have identified three new sites and one existing site, with more in the pipeline, that could join our solar community with your help.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/1a1efb40-9361-466b-a2a8-c3e155afb333_2025-10-09T10:52:04.860Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Grimsby Community Energy - cooperative";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://grimsbycommunityenergy.coop/>.
id:68e793e956f105f6c513c411 :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50897,
                                   id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899;
                            :organisationDescription """Sufra NW London is a local charity established in 2013 to address both the causes and consequences of impoverishment in the community.

With the help of our volunteers and partners, we coordinate a network of food banks, kitchens, a community shop and café. These act as a gateway for guests to access more holistic support – including welfare advice, asylum support and our award-winning community garden.

We aim to work with our guests to find solutions to their challenges together, whilst campaigning against the causes of hunger and poverty.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/5f84e291-0024-4458-9c96-24003ed0a35b_2025-10-09T10:52:24.658Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Sufra NW London";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.sufra-nwlondon.org.uk/>.
id:68e795ce73bc9d1daed53691 :activityDescription """The Community Wellbeing Service offers relief from the rising cost of living for local families. For just £4/week, service members have access to a range of support including a Community Shop, Community Café and Advice and Guidance through an extensive timetable of partners in the space. The service provides preventative support for local families and enables members to access a wide range of support under one roof, in order to build financial and personal resilience.

Community Cafe Volunteers are at the heart of this service. This role involves welcoming guests, and serving warm drinks, pastries and lunches at our café. 

We're looking for volunteers with great communication skills, who like working in busy environment and motivated to ensure food safety measures are respected. Training for the role will be provided.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68e793e956f105f6c513c411;
                            :activityTitle "Community Cafe Volunteering";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68e795ce73bc9d1daed53692 :address "1 Robson Avenue, London NW10 3SG";
                            :latitude "51.5410875"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.2369161"^^xsd:double.
id:68e7975cafd4f4e0fe5e1e9e :activityDescription """About the Project – “Solta o Jogo” 
“Solta o Jogo” is a vibrant cultural competition and festival celebrating Brazilian heritage through Capoeira, music, dance, acrobatics, and a Brazilian arts & crafts fair. Hosted at Kingston University Townhouse, the event invites the community to participate in free performances, workshops, and exhibitions promoting cross-cultural understanding.
We are preparing to host the third edition of our International Collective Capoeira Competition and Afro-Brazilian Fayre at Kingston University Town House on 18th and 19th October 2025.
This highly anticipated event draws local residents, students, families, dignitaries including the Mayor of Kingston, the Consul General of Brazil, Kingston Council Officers, University Officers, and Local Councillors, alongside international participants from France, Spain, Germany, and across the UK. The event features live music, performances, martial arts competitions, and an Afro-Brazilian Fayre, with global reach through live broadcasts in both Portuguese and English. 

Position Overview:
We are seeking enthusiastic and reliable Event Volunteers to join our team for this exciting international cultural event. You’ll play a key part in coordinating logistics, supporting attendees, and ensuring a memorable experience for all participants.
This is a fully on-site role for one week — ideal for anyone looking to gain hands-on experience in event management, cultural coordination, and community engagement.


Key Responsibilities:

Support event setup, coordination, and smooth operations before, during, and after the event.
Take part in pre-event dry runs starting from 13th October.
Provide on-site support during event days (18th–19th October, 9 AM–6 PM).
Engage with visitors, participants, and community partners, ensuring everyone feels welcome.
Help manage logistics, registration, and attendee flow.
Assist in event documentation through photos, videos, or brief write-ups.
Collaborate with performers, vendors, and volunteers to create a vibrant atmosphere.
Contribute to post-event reports and feedback summaries.

Required Skills:
Previous experience in event coordination or customer service
Basic skills in photography, videography, or social media
Based in or near Kingston/London (preferred, due to on-site attendance)

Benefits:
All travel and food expenses reimbursed
Opportunity to gain hands-on event experience with an international cultural organisation
Work alongside creative professionals and community leaders
Certificate of Participation upon completion
Develop valuable skills in teamwork, logistics, and public engagement

Availability & Commitment
Start Date: 13th October 2025 (for pre-event dry runs and setup)
Event Days: 18th & 19th October 2025 (9 AM – 6 PM)
Commitment: One-week engagement (13th – 19th October 2025)
Location: On-site at Kingston University Town House, Kingston upon Thames
Preference: Candidates based in or near Kingston/London to reduce travel time.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68d6b402553e58bdf03c7c30;
                            :activityTitle "Event Volunteer  ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68e7975cafd4f4e0fe5e1e9f :address "Kingston University (KIngston Hill), Kingston upon Thames";
