id:68e7af64af9cdbf26bd9ec5f :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3,
                                   id:66982ffbbf338eca22aa267d;
                            :organisationDescription """SE24 has installed 9 solar projects and 3000 LED bulbs across Southwark and nearby areas leading to savings of Over 280 tonnes of CO2 avoided per year and £1.6 mln of lifetime savings. We primarily work with Academy Trusts to bring energy savings to the schools, thus freeing up funds for the primary purposes of education

For 2026/27, we have aim to deliver the following 
1)  8 solar PV installation projects at schools belonging to London South East Academy Trust (LSEAT) in Bexley, Bromley and Lambeth;
2) one solar PV project at a school belonging to United Learning Trust (ULT) in Southwark.
3) 4 LED projects
With an aggregate of c.£1.7m in site savings and 1,500 tCO 2 abatement identified over the lifetime of these projects, they will deliver benefits at scale across the two Academy Trusts.  We raise funds through a mix of Grants, community investments via share offer or community bond issuance. SE24 has a successful history of share offers, most recently raising £400,000 in 2024 and with a strong foundation of community engagement.
SE24 will continue to use surplus revenue from these and previous projects to maintain a Community Fund through which it will support projects to alleviate fuel poverty and educate on energy efficiency in the schools’ local communities.""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/759c74bc-e590-4c7e-8434-ca28f8c22e2a_2025-10-09T13:08:06.798Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "Sustainable Energy 24 Limited SE24";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://se24.co.uk/>.
id:68e7b0aedfe746c63c4261e8 :activityDescription """SE24 Sustainable Energy is seeking a volunteer with legal experience to assist with the preparation and coordination of lease and Power Purchase Agreement (PPA) documentation for our upcoming solar and LED installation programme.

For 2026/27, SE24 will be delivering 8 solar PV installations and 4 LED lighting projects across schools within the London South East Academies Trust (LSEAT) and the United Learning Trust (ULT). Each site will require individual lease agreements and PPAs to be finalised between SE24 and the respective schools.

We aim to complete all legal documentation by Q4 2025, ahead of the installation phase beginning in 2026. The role will primarily involve:
1) Reviewing and coordinating lease and PPA documents with school representatives and local authorities.
2) Supporting the preparation of supporting documentation for the Department for Education (DfE) a

This role would suit a volunteer solicitor, legal executive, or experienced paralegal interested in community energy, sustainability, or education-sector projects. We estimate a time commitment of around two days per month, offering flexibility around your schedule.

Your support will help us deliver a major expansion of community-owned renewable energy across South East London — bringing financial, environmental, and social benefits to local schools and their communities.

If you are interested or would like to learn more, please contact upasnaagarwal@gmail.com""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68e7af64af9cdbf26bd9ec5f;
                            :activityTitle "Solar Installation in Schools";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68e7bb90d40c150b46d8e57e :activityDescription """As a Friends of Moorfields volunteer, you'll be at the front-line of providing emotional and physical support to patients with visual impairment and to ensure Moorfields provide an excellent service. 

Some of the tasks we'll need you to complete at Moorfields Brent Cross can include leading and guiding patients around the clinics, providing advice and guidance about services etc. and administrative tasks under guidance from our admin team. 

Volunteering with us will give you a great sense of purpose and transferable skills and experience that can be used for job/university applications amongst other things.
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425f94df2d4b77a6e15e679;
