id:68e7fa9dca3587f6ae86786c :cause id:64093b542eed5dcadba50899;
                            :organisationDescription "Crawley Open House provides vital support and services for those suffering the effects of homelessness, unemployment, loneliness, discrimination, or other forms of social exclusion in Crawley and neighbouring areas.";
                            :organisationName "Crawley Open House";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.crawleyopenhouse.co.uk/key-information>.
id:68e7fc8677f4c7bc0b1edc4c :activityDescription """Trustee Volunteer Role Description
About Crawley Open House
Crawley Open House provides vital support and services for those suffering the effects of homelessness, unemployment, loneliness, discrimination, or other forms of social exclusion in Crawley and neighbouring areas.
 
Trustee Opportunities
We are now seeking dedicated, passionate, and skilled individuals to join our Board of Trustees. As a Trustee, you will play a key role in shaping our future — sharing your expertise, guiding our strategy, and helping us continue to deliver life-changing support to some of the most vulnerable people in our community.
If you want to make a real difference and be part of an organisation that truly transforms lives, we’d love to hear from you.
 
Ideal candidates will have a strong interest in adult education, benefits systems and fundraising and a genuine commitment to contributing to social change.
 
We are looking to appoint more than one Trustee and welcomes expressions of interest from individuals with experience in one or more of the following areas:
Adult Education
Benefits System
Fundraising
IT infrastructure
Local/Central Government
Social Housing
Immigration
Trustees are responsible for a full range of Trustee duties including strategic oversight of Crawley Open House, financial accountable (we have a dedicated treasurer), planning and monitoring, transparency and accountability and we would ask you to volunteer within the charity at least once a year.
 
In line with its commitment to inclusion, Crawley Open House actively welcomes applications from individuals of all backgrounds, including underrepresented groups across age, ethnicity, geography, physical ability, and socio-economic experience.
 
For further information and details on how to apply, please visit the Crawley Open House website.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68e7fa9dca3587f6ae86786c;
                            :activityTitle "Trustee Opportunity";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68e7fc8677f4c7bc0b1edc4d :address "Stephenson Way, Three Bridges, Crawley";
                            :latitude "51.1158768"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.1638315"^^xsd:double.
id:68e876eff7721db4ca260cff :activityDescription """We believe that RSPB Aire Valley, Fairburn Ings Nature Reserve and St Aidan's Nature Park are brilliant places to visit, whatever your age or level of wildlife knowledge. We are looking for volunteers to support us with social media and help us to keep our online activity up to date and looking great. You will be helping to spread the word, via social media posts, press releases and communications. Social media is widely used by the public who are planning trips out, or just for keeping up to date with events and activities at favourite destinations. Increasingly people use social media as a way of asking questions before their visit, so you will be helping people plan their brilliant day out too. Keeping our social media pages up to date is important.

**Main tasks**
- At an allocated time, check our social media for comments and messages and respond in a timely and appropriate manner
- Help to write and edit posts about activities, events and seasonal interest on the reserve for use on Social Media. 
- Work closely with the Visitor Experience Manager to ensure posts are current, timely and accurate etc. 
- Keep up to date with wildlife news, events and activities in the Aire Valley by talking to the staff and volunteers at both sites for ideas.
- Work to agreed standards and ensure our social media maintains expected quality. 

**What you need:**
- Good knowledge and experience of using social media platforms 
- Excellent written communication skills 
- Diplomacy and tact.
- Ability to work independently and use own initiative. 
- Interest in nature, the Aire Valley, or both!
- Able to make a commitment to at least one shift per week and work flexibly.

As a social media volunteer you will get to find out and influence how visitors feel about the Aire Valley and their visit. You will be given full training and support around how to respond to comments and questions on social media and will need to undertake some online training. You will also be able to access our learning and development programme to enhance your knowledge and skills. and will have regular meetings with and support from your line manager. 
You will be working in one of our office bases, and may be able to undertake some of the role from home. We believe volunteering shouldn’t leave you out of pocket, so will reimburse travel expenses.
You will be allocated a line manager and will have support and regular opportunities to discuss your role with this person. 

The RSPB is committed to making our organisation diverse and inclusive, and, as such, are keen to encourage applications from everyone, however unfortunately this role is not suitable for anyone under 18.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "RSPB Team Member (Aire Valley Social Media Assistant)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68e876eff7721db4ca260d00 :address "St Aidan's, Astley Lane, Leeds, Yorkshire West Riding, LS26 8AL, England";
                            :latitude "53.761592"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.416229"^^xsd:double.
id:68e8c413e1942f00dce44075 :activityDescription """No one should die because they needed first aid and didn’t get it. St John Ambulance teaches people first aid so they can be the difference between life and death, and you can help us do this.

We are looking for people with excellent interpersonal skills to join our Safeguarding team. Safeguarding is central to the work of St John Ambulance because it ensures that the diverse range of services we provide to children and adults at risk of harm, are delivered safely. Safeguarding Team Members do this in a number of ways e.g. by monitoring the implementation of the safeguarding policy, by responding to questions regarding and giving guidance etc.

 Learning is at the heart of St John Ambulance and we offer a very large range of learning and developmental opportunities to our volunteers, including the full professional training that is essential for our Safeguarding Team Members:

·         Safeguarding Awareness

·         Safeguarding in Practice

·         Working safely with Children and Adults at Risk of Harm

This role is exempt from the provisions of the Rehabilitations Offenders Act.

Closing date for this vacancy is the 9th January 2026

For more information please contact lyn.cavill@sja.org.uk""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425cee7a0624f3ab9fb35be;
                            :activityTitle "Safeguarding Team Member";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68e8c413e1942f00dce44076 :address "Stroud Road, Gloucester GL1 5JR";
                            :latitude "51.8532299"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.2430974"^^xsd:double.
id:68e8df196e3078d52245934b :activityDescription """We’re looking for Volunteer Befrienders to provide support to our children, young people and families at our Birmingham Hospice

At Acorns we provide care and support for life limited or life threatened children and their families.  We have three hospices in the West Midlands, which provide a happy homely environment where children can experience all kinds of great activities, meet new friends or relax and enjoy some quiet time.

Our Hospice Volunteer Befrienders engage with children, young people and families during their stay in the hospice.  Befrienders get involved in play and activities in the hospice, allowing children and young people to access and enjoy the play facilities.   

This is a particularly sensitive role, so to be a Volunteer Befriender you’ll:

Have an understanding and awareness of the care that we provide
Have some experience of caring for others or have natural empathy
Have good communication skills – able to listen to and understand
Be sensitive to the needs of our children, young people, and families
What we offer:

Meet new people everyday
Access to free online courses
Learn new skills to boost your CV
Retail discounts
Volunteer recognition scheme to show our appreciation
Full training will be provided

We are committed to safeguarding children and vulnerable adults and therefore any successful candidate will be subject to an enhanced DBS check for children and will be asked to provide two satisfactory references.

 

Words 

Help us to save the Children's Hospice Grant: Click here to find out more""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:641096af1097b43af15de362;
                            :activityTitle "Befriending Volunteer (Birmingham)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68e8df196e3078d52245934c :address "Oak Tree Lane, Selly Oak, Birmingham B29 6HZ";
                            :latitude "52.4350952"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.9382659"^^xsd:double.
id:68e8ef99581938222204722a :activityDescription """
SE24 Sustainable Energy is seeking a volunteer with legal experience to assist with the preparation and coordination of lease and Power Purchase Agreement (PPA) documentation for our upcoming solar and LED installation programme.

For 2026/27, SE24 will be delivering 8 solar PV installations and 4 LED lighting projects across schools within the London South East Academies Trust (LSEAT) and the United Learning Trust (ULT). Each site will require individual lease agreements and PPAs to be finalised between SE24 and the respective schools.

We aim to complete all legal documentation by Q4 2025, ahead of the installation phase beginning in 2026. The role will primarily involve:
1) Reviewing and coordinating lease and PPA documents with school representatives and local authorities.
2) Supporting the preparation of supporting documentation for the Department for Education (DfE) a

This role would suit a volunteer solicitor, legal executive, or experienced paralegal interested in community energy, sustainability, or education-sector projects. We estimate a time commitment of around two days per month, offering flexibility around your schedule.

Your support will help us deliver a major expansion of community-owned renewable energy across South East London — bringing financial, environmental, and social benefits to local schools and their communities.

If you are interested or would like to learn more, please contact upasnaagarwal@gmail.com""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68e7af64af9cdbf26bd9ec5f;
                            :activityTitle "Solar Installation and Funding";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68e9c8636f7d60198b11206a :activityDescription """RSPB Saltholme is one of the RSPB’s visitor havens with over 50,000 visitors each year and is a triple Visit England Gold Award winner. We have high standards of customer care to ensure every visitor has a memorial and engaging visit from start to finish whilst being able to experience a nature rich landscape.

Nature is in trouble, there aren't many places left where wildlife can thrive, that is why we want to welcome more people to these places. We are looking for volunteers who can help engage visitors with the wildlife that calls Saltholme its home, from the avocets to the wigeon or the seals and dragonflies. 

You'll need the following skills:
- Approachable and friendly demeanour
- Ability to communicate with visitors from different backgrounds and ages, with differing levels of knowledge
- Ability to listen to the needs of the customer
- Desire to help visitors and deliver excellent customer service
- Enthusiasm for wildlife, nature and conservation
- Confidence to communicate RSPB messages
- Willingness to undertake RSPB training
- Awareness of Health and Safety
- Ability to make a regular commitment

Full training and support will be provide for this role but you do need to be a ‘people person’ and have good communication skills.

This is a really rewarding and enjoyable role. You will be working with a friendly team on a beautiful nature reserve, you will have the opportunity to make new friends and spend time outdoors. You will get to meet loads of new people in this role, enjoying conversation and helping people have a wonderful visit.

There is always the opportunity to learn new things and gain skills through volunteering, by working on a reserve, you'll learn all about how nature reserves are managed and the wildlife that is found there.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Engagement Volunteer (On Reserves) (Saltholme Guide)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68e9c8636f7d60198b11206b :address "Saltholme, Seaton Carew Road, Stockton-On-Tees, Middlesbrough, Durham, TS2 1TU, England";
                            :latitude "54.600739"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.223351"^^xsd:double.
id:68e9c8646f7d60198b112095 :activityDescription """The RSPB manages a big network of nature reserves which are havens for wildlife, and importantly very special places for people of all ages and abilities to visit and experience a nature rich landscape.

Nature is in trouble, there aren't many places left where wildlife can thrive, that is why we want to welcome more people to these places.

We are looking for volunteers who can help greet visitors on arrival, take entry fee payments through the till and explain how to get the most out of their day. We're currently looking for support on a Sunday but we do have other timeslots available.

Full training and support will be provide for this role but you do need to be a ‘people person’ and have good communication skills.

This is a really rewarding and enjoyable role. You will be working with a friendly team on a beautiful nature reserve, you will have the opportunity to make new friends and spend time outdoors. You will get to meet loads of new people in this role, enjoying conversation and helping people have a wonderful visit.

There is always the opportunity to learn new things and gain skills through volunteering, by working on a reserve, you'll naturally learn all about how nature reserves are managed and the wildlife that is found there.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Visitor Centre Welcome ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68e9c8646f7d60198b112096 :address "Saltholme, Seaton Carew Road, Stockton-On-Tees, Middlesbrough, Durham, TS2 1TU, England";
                            :latitude "54.600739"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.223351"^^xsd:double.
id:68ecc5a248daa052a003b8f8 :activityDescription """Across the UK, our 270 local groups play a vital part in supporting people affected by MS. They provide sense of belonging, unity and friendship. And they deliver services and support for their local MS community.

We are looking to recruit a Support Volunteer for the North Staffordshire Group. As our local group Support Volunteer you’ll help people affected by MS find information about local and national services. That could be helping someone access local information about the care or benefits they need or giving them a hand with a grant application. See a video about one of our Support Volunteers here.

In this role you’ll be able to develop your listening and communication skills, as well as your knowledge of local services. Most importantly you’ll help people affected by MS to access the help they need.

Time commitment

We estimate this role will need around 2 hours a week. Our roles are flexible and aim to fit around you. Time commitments for this role may vary depending on your activities. This is an ongoing role.

This is a great opportunity to gain experience within a large charity and develop your existing skills and learn new ones. We need you to get involved and help make positive changes to the lives of people affected by MS.

About you

You’ll have an interest in the MS Society and the work that we do, as well as the enthusiasm to represent both us and our values locally. You will understand the needs of people affected by MS in your area and be sympathetic to the needs and motivations of volunteers. You’ll be confident using Microsoft Office, the internet and email. You’ll be able to apply disability, equality and inclusion practices and understand and apply our risk management system. Ideally you’ll understand the local area and organisations that provide local services.

You will be reliable and easy to contact and you need to live in or near the local area the group to carry out this role.

Apply 

1. Read through the role description carefully

2. Please apply online

The MS Society is committed to promoting diversity. We can only offer roles to over 18s.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425eae8c794380477b70969;
                            :activityTitle "Support Volunteer (North Staffordshire)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68ecc5a248daa052a003b8f9 :address "Bridge Street, Newcastle-under-Lyme, Newcastle ST5 2RY";
                            :latitude "53.0125409"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.2301026"^^xsd:double.
id:68ecce62e2605d3145c0f680 :activityDescription """Across the UK, our 270 local groups play a vital part in supporting people affected by MS. They provide sense of belonging, unity and friendship. And they deliver services and support for their local MS community.

We are looking to recruit a Group Coordinator for our Vale Royal and West Cheshire group. As our local Group Coordinator you’ll take the lead in making sure your local group works as effectively as possible. You’ll recruit, induct and support other group volunteers to make sure your group’s activities meet the needs of your local MS community.

In this role you’ll be able to develop your leadership, management, communication, organisation and motivation skills. To find out more about what services this group currently offer please go to https://volunteers.mssociety.org.uk/group-coordinator

Time Commitment

We estimate this role will need around 5 hours a week. Our roles are flexible and aim to fit around you. Time commitments for this role may vary depending on your activities. This is an ongoing role.

This is a great opportunity to gain experience within a large charity and develop your existing skills and learn new ones. We need you to get involved and help make positive changes to the lives of people affected by MS.

About you

You’ll have an interest in the MS Society and the work that we do, as well as the enthusiasm to represent both us and our values locally. You will understand the needs of people affected by MS in your area and be sympathetic to the needs and motivations of volunteers. You’ll be confident using Microsoft Office, the internet and email. You’ll be able to apply disability, equality and inclusion practices and understand and apply our risk management system. Ideally you’ll understand the local area and organisations that provide local services.

You will be reliable and easy to contact and you need to live in or near the Vale Royal and West Cheshire area to carry out this role.

Apply online or for further information contact simon.moran@mssociety.org.uk

The MS Society is committed to promoting diversity. We can only offer roles to over 18s.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425eae8c794380477b70969;
                            :activityTitle "Group Coordinator (Vale Royal and West Cheshire)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68ecce62e2605d3145c0f681 :address "Alexandra Street, Shotton, Deeside CH5 1DL";
                            :latitude "53.2132651"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-3.0386965"^^xsd:double.
id:68ecce8cae34348517de3134 :activityDescription """Finance Volunteer

We’re the MS Society – a community of people living with MS, scientists, campaigners, listeners, organisers, ambassadors and fundraisers. Our volunteers are a key part of achieving our goals and their support is vital. Join us.

About this opportunity
We are looking to recruit a Finance Volunteer for our North Staffordshire Group. As a Finance Volunteer, you would be joining a coordinating team of volunteers to plan and deliver services and activities to support people locally.

You will maintain and approve income and expenditure records and explain financial information clearly to other group members. You would ensure our financial requirements and policies are followed, and that money is spent in a cost effective manner.

This is a great opportunity to gain experience with a large charity, develop your existing skills and learn new ones. We need you to get involved and help make positive changes to the lives of people affected by MS.

About you
You’ll have an interest in the MS Society and the work that we do, as well as the enthusiasm to represent both us and our values locally. You will understand the needs of people affected by MS in your area and be sympathetic to the needs and motivations of volunteers. You’ll be comfortable with figures, preferably with an accounting or business background.

Apply 

Read through the role description carefully

Please apply online

The MS Society is committed to promoting diversity. We can only offer roles to over 18s.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425eae8c794380477b70969;
                            :activityTitle "Finance Volunteer (North Staffordshire)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68ecce8cae34348517de3135 :address "Bridge Street, Newcastle-under-Lyme, Newcastle ST5 2RY";
                            :latitude "53.0125409"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.2301026"^^xsd:double.
id:68ecceb7c59917b746b86cb1 :activityDescription """Across the UK, our 270 local groups play a vital part in supporting people affected by MS. They provide sense of belonging, unity and friendship. And they deliver services and support for their local MS community.

We are looking to recruit an Administration Volunteer for the North Staffordshire Group. Our Administration Volunteers are the linchpin for our local groups’ activities. They act as the first point of contact and they make sure all relevant information is circulated to other volunteers and members. And they play an important role in keeping our data and details up to date to comply with data protection legislation.

In this role you’ll develop your administration and organisation skills. Most importantly you’ll be help your local group run efficiently, so they can keep providing valuable services to our MS community. To find out more about what services this group currently offer please go to https://volunteers.mssociety.org.uk/administration-volunteer   

Time Commitment

We estimate this role will need around 2 hours a week. Our roles are flexible and aim to fit around you. Time commitments for this role may vary depending on your activities. This is an ongoing role.

This is a great opportunity to gain experience within a large charity and develop your existing skills and learn new ones. We need you to get involved and help make positive changes to the lives of people affected by MS.

About you

You’ll have an interest in the MS Society and the work that we do, as well as the enthusiasm to represent both us and our values locally. You will understand the needs of people affected by MS in your area and be sympathetic to the needs and motivations of volunteers. You’ll be confident using Microsoft Office, the internet and email. You’ll be able to apply disability, equality and inclusion practices and understand and apply our risk management system. Ideally you’ll understand the local area and organisations that provide local services.

You will be reliable and easy to contact and you need to live in or near the area the group to carry out this role.

Please apply online 

The MS Society is committed to promoting diversity. We can only offer roles to over 18s.

 """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:6425eae8c794380477b70969;
                            :activityTitle "Administration Volunteer (North Staffordshire)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68ecceb7c59917b746b86cb2 :address "Bridge Street, Newcastle-under-Lyme, Newcastle ST5 2RY";
