id:68ee73613643ab2066bc1971 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """Haven House Children’s Hospice cares for seriously ill babies and children (up to the age of 18) by creating a loving and warm environment for them and their families while they go through the toughest of times.

No family should have to face alone the difficulties of looking after a child with a serious illness. Haven House provides round the clock care at our hospice, surrounded in beautiful grounds and woodland, in Woodford Green and through our outreach services in the home and local community. We provide; day care, over-night stays, end of life care, bereavement support, as well as life enriching activities such as sensory play, music therapy and physiotherapy.

We provide care and support where and when our families need us. Hospice care does not mean that a child is near to the end of their life, we are here from the time a devastating diagnosis is made to help our families have choice, quality of life and to make the most of the precious time they have together.""";
                            :organisationName "Haven House Children's Hospice ";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.havenhouse.org.uk/>.
id:68ef0e6bea1549dcd93842b0 :activityDescription """Join Our Conservation Volunteer Team!
Opportunities between Barrow and Kendal

Do you love being outdoors, care about wildlife, and want to make a positive difference in your local area? We’re looking for volunteers to help with a range of conservation and community projects across the beautiful parks and green spaces between Barrow and Kendal.

Whether you can give a few hours a month or more regularly, your time will help nature thrive — and you’ll pick up some great skills along the way!

What You Could Get Involved In:
- Litter picks to keep our parks clean and welcoming
- Removing old tree tubes to help young woodlands flourish
- Building bird nest boxes and bee banks to support wildlife
- Meadow raking and summer surveys (birds, invertebrates, meadows)
- Assisting with or leading guided walks — including popular bat walks!
- Helping engage school groups and local communities with nature
- Contributing ideas for future projects like a community orchard or improving lake water quality

Why Volunteer?
- Enjoy time outdoors and boost your wellbeing
- Learn new conservation skills and gain valuable experience
- Meet friendly, like-minded people
- Make a real difference to local wildlife and your community
- Flexible opportunities — you choose when and how you help
- No experience needed — just enthusiasm and a willingness to get involved!

If this sounds like something you’d enjoy, we’d love to hear from you. Together, we can create healthier habitats and greener communities across South Cumbria.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Practical Reserve Work (South Lakes Conservation Volunteer)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68ef0e6bea1549dcd93842b1 :address "Abbey Road, Barrow-in-Furness, Westmorland and Furness, England, United Kingdom, Abbey Road, Barrow-in-Furness, Cumbria, LA14 5QS, United Kingdom";
