id:68ef7c9fb239d50f07154216 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba5089f;
                            :organisationDescription """At STEM On Track, we provide go-kart kits and online modules to schools, giving students hands-on experience in engineering, motorsport, and STEM subjects. Our programme bridges classroom learning with real-world application, helping students develop skills, confidence, and creativity.
""";
                            :organisationImage <https://s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/doit2.0-production-uploads/OrganizationPicture/a308ef50-7d7f-487a-bb98-4b70d2baa860_2025-10-15T10:51:10.757Z.jpeg>;
                            :organisationName "STEM On Track";
                            :organisationWebsite <https://www.stemontrack.com/>.
id:68ef81b80a306d0e59da38f9 :activityDescription """If you're looking to take your first step into a Motorsport career, we need YOU! 🏁
If you’ve ever wanted to be part of something fast-paced, inspiring, and full of future innovators, this is your moment. Whether you’re a teacher, student, motorsport fan, or simply passionate about STEM, volunteering at the National Finals is a chance to get behind the scenes of an unforgettable event. At STEM On Track, we help schools bring STEM to life through hands-on go-kart kits and online modules, giving students a real taste of engineering, motorsport, and marketing.
We’re looking for enthusiastic volunteers to help with:
⚙️ Event Marshals – keep the day running smoothly and safely
🏎️ Track & Team Support – assist teams and see innovation in action up close
🎤 Stage & Registration Helpers – welcome participants and keep the energy high
💡 All-Round STEM Champions – help wherever you’re needed and be part of the action!
Volunteering isn’t just about giving your time, it’s about making a real impact. You’ll meet like-minded people, see the next generation of STEM talent in action, and gain hands-on experience in events, teamwork, and STEM education. Plus, you’ll have a front-row seat to all the excitement on and off the track!
Join us and help power the next generation of STEM leaders. Your support makes the National Finals possible, and your enthusiasm inspires tomorrow’s engineers, innovators, and problem-solvers.
📅 National Finals: 20th of June
Test Days: 7th of May
📍 Location: Whilton Mill 
🔗 Sign up:info@espireeducation.co.uk
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68ef7c9fb239d50f07154216;
                            :activityTitle "STEM On Track National Finals";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68ef85b71a198af2bc6cfa97 :activityDescription "We are The Vench, a much-loved adventure playground and community centre in Lockleaze, Bristol. For over 45 years, we’ve been inspiring imaginative play in a supportive and fun environment to help Lockleaze children and young people live happy and healthy lives. We believe in the importance of providing our local young people and their families with a safe place to play, learn and create the change they want to see in the world.";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68e66f1161e4748e07083424;
                            :activityTitle "Kitchen Assistant Volunteers ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68ef85b71a198af2bc6cfa98 :address "Romney Avenue, Bristol BS7 9TD";
                            :latitude "51.4912432"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.5605479"^^xsd:double.
id:68ef90a61a198af2bc6cfbdd :activityDescription """The hospice is set in a 24-acre estate, of which 4 acres are gardens. The grounds are taken care of by a small number of volunteers and they form a fundamental part of the hospice facilities that our children and families can enjoy. Volunteers also assist with our corporate gardening days.

Core responsibilities
The primary tasks include:
•Your role will be to assist in all aspects of gardening including weeding, planting bulbs, herbaceous plants, and shrubs; pruning; edging lawns; digging/forking over soil and adding compost as required; sweeping up and general tidying , including the paved areas, driveway and car parks.
•Tools and equipment are to be cleaned as necessary and returned to their designated area when tasks are completed or at the end of the day.
•Volunteers will not be asked to use power tools unless specifically qualified and authorised to do so.
•Appropriate disposal of garden waste in the designated areas.
•To water plants - especially hanging baskets and boxes (water hose connections are situated around the building)
•To bring any construction / maintenance issues to the attention of the Facilities Manager.
•From time to time, to assist the facilities team with tasks where extra pairs of hands are needed.
•Volunteer alongside some of the corporate teams that garden for us on one off days. These normally take place on a Tuesday or Thursday from 9am – 4pm.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68ee73613643ab2066bc1971;
                            :activityTitle "Gardening ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68ef90a61a198af2bc6cfbde :address "Woodford Green IG8 9LB";
                            :latitude "51.6061936"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.0164066"^^xsd:double.
id:68ef922ee3e3101eb3a146f4 :activityDescription """We are looking for volunteers to help us run our popular Haven House Grotto in December, the grotto will be based at Northfields garden centre Chingford. 

We are looking for people that have experience in engaging with children and families and are happy and enthusiastic. For this role we would need you to wear full costumes on the dates (these will be provided). There will be a staff member available on each shift to support with the running of the day. By helping to run this grotto in the local community it will enable us to engage with more members of the local community raise funds and awareness of the work we do.


Duties will include :
Meeting and greeting children and families
Engaging and chatting with the children
Spreading the magic of Christmas
Helping serve refreshments to guests

Volunteers can chose to do an AM/PM or all day shift. 

There will be some refreshments on site but if volunteers want to bring lunch or any extra refreshments it is advised that they do as the shops are not nearby. """;
                            :activityOrganisation id:68ee73613643ab2066bc1971;
                            :activityTitle "Elf Squad and refreshment volunteers";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68ef922ee3e3101eb3a146f5 :address "Waltham Abbey, London E4 7RG";
                            :latitude "51.6605897"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-0.0041403"^^xsd:double.
id:68ef9333633128546f57190b :activityDescription """Help us to create new Allotment sites! (voluntary, ongoing, home-based, remote)

Green Allotments is a charity on a mission to create new allotment sites in England and Wales.  

We are currently looking for lovely volunteers for various roles which are all home-based: 

Volunteer Desk-based Researchers (Our most popular volunteering role!)
Occasional professional/specialist micro-volunteers 
Landscape Architect
Social Media Supporters
Welsh Language Translators / Gwirfoddoli Cyfieithwyr Cymraeg

There are no set hours when volunteering for us and you can turn down anything that you are offered. Obviously, we will treat you with dignity and respect.

We do not anticipate that you will incur expenses in this role. We expect our volunteers to already have an internet connection and be willing to use that as part of their volunteer role with Green Allotments CIO.

(At present we are unable to accept applications from under 18s, although we hope to be able to do so in the future as our charity grows)

""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:642610e5de05bf8ae7c9bce4;
                            :activityTitle "Help us to create new Allotment sites! (voluntary, ongoing, home-based, remote)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68ef938ac8a363a3049dccd4 :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:68ef945c0f33ca24856e4b42 :activityDescription """We have fundraising events throughout the year both at the hospice and in the local area. We could not run these events without the support of our volunteers as it is not possible to have staff members attending and co-ordinating all of these. Helping could be assisting at one of these events in several ways which can include marshalling, meeting and greeting, setting up or clearing down or running a stand. In the community you may be asked to run an information stand in the local community or have an engagement stand with a small fundraising game.

Core responsibilities

On site
Tasks will vary from event to event, but each volunteer will be sent a full brief the week before the event. The volunteer will then be expected to fulfil the task allocated to them on that day. On the day there is also a volunteer briefing on site and staff members act as zone supervisors on the day, so you always have a point of contact. Volunteers sign in and out of the volunteer hub each day.

In the community
Volunteers will be sent an outline about the event from the community organiser. They will liaise with the staff about what the event will look like and what they may need to bring for the event. Staff will organise any marketing material for volunteers and support with any supplies for an engagement game. Volunteers may be asked with supporting in taking chairs, table, marketing material and the gazebo over to the event.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68ee73613643ab2066bc1971;
                            :activityTitle "Event support volunteer ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68ef945c0f33ca24856e4b43 :address "Woodford Green IG8 9LB";
                            :latitude "51.6061936"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.0164066"^^xsd:double.
id:68ef9559c8a363a3049dcdda :activityDescription """Our Purple Pots are placed in different areas in the local community. This helps us raise vital funds for the charity and helps raise awareness of our charity.

The Ambassador role involves managing an area or a high street and keeping a check on the existing pots and emptying and replacing them when required. This includes local shops, pubs, businesses etc. in your allocated area. As an ambassador you will be required to keep a regular check on these pots. Once they are full the money is collected and should be dropped back as soon as possible to the hospice or in to one of our 7 retail shops. The role is very flexible, and pots can be managed around your working schedule. Volunteers will also be able to work from home and liaise with the team via email or phone. The community team will provide a detailed area sheet and all the office support.

Core responsibilities
The primary tasks include:

•Managing a particular area or a high street.
•Build relationships with faith groups in the area such as churches, mosques, synagogues
•Keeping a regular check on the existing boxes and replacing when required.
•Sourcing new businesses to place new pots in local shops, pubs, businesses etc.
•Drop collected pots to the head office as soon as possible
•The role is very flexible, and pots can be collected around your working schedule, work from home and liaise with the team via email or phone.
•Engage with business owners by building a relationship and see if they would be interested in fundraising for HH
•Engaging the businesses with community and challenge events which take place throughout the year
""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68ee73613643ab2066bc1971;
                            :activityTitle "Purple pot ambassadors";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68ef9559c8a363a3049dcddb :address "From Home";
                            :latitude "52.5647271"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-1.4671882"^^xsd:double.
id:68ef96a0be1b092c3274fae7 :activityDescription """Our complementary therapy service is led by volunteers that are trained and experienced in their field. They offer support on our premises to parents of children who are receiving care at Haven House. Haven House will ensure that therapies are offered to families and that this is promoted within the community. The family and community team will book all appointments for the therapists as well as therapists attending events such as coffee mornings and family days. The role is flexible so therapists may work once a month or when a therapy is requested.


Core responsibilities
•To provide complementary therapies to the parents and carers of children that use our services
•To maintain a high professional standard at all times
•To adhere to client confidentiality
•To liaise with the therapies manager and reception team when needed""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68ee73613643ab2066bc1971;
                            :activityTitle "Complimentary therapist ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68ef96a0be1b092c3274fae8 :address "Woodford Green IG8 9LB";
                            :latitude "51.6061936"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "0.0164066"^^xsd:double.
id:68ef99c4e3e3101eb3a148c0 :activityDescription """The facilities team ensure the smooth-running day to day of the hospice both inside and outside the building. The remit for the facilities team includes liaising with contractors, managing the housekeeping team, utilities, managing the upkeep of the building and the grounds, health and safety, space and office management and project managing any work that is carried out at the hospice. We also are looking for volunteers who could help us out on an ad-hoc basis setting up for our event throughout the year. This would be a few times a year between March - Decemenber time. 

We are looking for a volunteer who could join the team and help out generally day to day around the hospice and at some of our big on site events.


Core responsibilities
The primary tasks include:

•Helping with moving and lifting
•Some porter duties
•Helping to set up and clear down from events
•To attend events to generally help out
•Some light DIY duties such as painting, putting up shelves etc



""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68ee73613643ab2066bc1971;
                            :activityTitle "Facilities volunteer ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68ef99c4e3e3101eb3a148c1 :address "Woodford Green IG8 9LB";
