id:68efb62e86053d705c3386d6 :cause id:64093b552eed5dcadba508a3;
                            :organisationDescription "";
                            :organisationName "Canal & River Trust".
id:68efb768fff2fd12a3226a78 :activityDescription """Do you enjoy talking to people? Are you confident using a tablet to complete a short questionnaire? Come and join us to help gather valuable feedback from visitors at the National Waterways Museum, Ellesmere Port.

What you’ll do:
Observe and note the behaviours and general profile of visitors as they explore the site
Approach visitors in a friendly, engaging, and welcoming manner
Invite visitors to take part in a short survey, clearly explaining its purpose
Use a tablet to read out survey questions and accurately record visitor responses
Follow guidance on health, safety, and data privacy
Report any issues or feedback to your designated contact at Canal & River Trust

What we’re looking for:
Friendly, welcoming people that are happy to approach members of the public
People who can commit to a minimum of a couple of hours a week (either weekends/weekdays or both)
Basic knowledge of technology - you’ll be using a tablet (full training will be provided)

Why volunteer with us?
Lots of interaction with people, you’ll spend your shift talking to visitors and staff at the museum
An opportunity to learn new skills, either for future employability or just for the fun of it!
You’ll be part of a supportive and enthusiastic team
Your contribution will make a real difference to improving our museums

We look forward to hearing from you!""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:68efb62e86053d705c3386d6;
                            :activityTitle "Survey Volunteer at the National Waterways Museum, Ellesmere Port";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation false.
id:68efb768fff2fd12a3226a79 :address "South Pier Road, Ellesmere Port";
                            :latitude "53.2885107"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "-2.8913413"^^xsd:double.
id:68f05ff58d1c1c0c8ca0cb73 :activityDescription """We are looking for volunteers to help in our shops on reserves. Volunteers serve customers, stock shelves and make our shops a friendly place to visit. Profits made from our shops mean that we can continue to protect wildlife. 

In order to ensure that visitors have an enjoyable and safe visit, we need a team of volunteers to help everything run smoothly. When people visit our shops, we want them to have a warm welcome and to be able to talk to the team about the products, such as bird food and feeders. We also need to ensure that shelves are stocked, and the retail space is clean and tidy. All this work requires a team of friendly and supportive people to help out. We simply can't run our shops without volunteers. Profits made from our shops mean that we can continue to protect wildlife, so they're an important part of our work. 

Support and training will be provided but having the following skills or experience would be good: 
 
- Have good communication skills and enjoy talking to new people.
- Enjoy working as part of a team.
- Willing to be flexible and take on different tasks as and when needed. 
- Prior retail experience.

This is a rewarding role with a friendly team during which you will learn new skills and gain experience working in the hospitality industry. The money raised through our retail and catering contributes to nature conservation, through the so you’ll get satisfaction from making a difference.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Retail Volunteer ";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68f05ff58d1c1c0c8ca0cb74 :address "Lochwinnoch, Largs Road, Lochwinnoch, Renfrewshire, PA12 4JF, Scotland";
