id:68f1b16cf7915f22a8e6ab5f :activityDescription """Maintaining Flatford Wildlife Garden in the best condition for wildlife and to inspire visitors to make their own gardens welcoming to nature takes a lot of effort and many hands. We’re looking for someone to join the Thursday work party team at Flatford Wildlife Garden to help keep on top of basic garden maintenance tasks.

As a Gardening Volunteer you will be joining a regular work party to undertake practical habitat management tasks: 
- Maintaining flower beds
- Cutting and clearing vegetation. 
- Creating and maintaining visitor infrastructure, such as paths 
- Following annual work plans. 
- Following Health and Safety protocols. 

If you enjoy being outdoors, meeting new people and hands on conservation work, then this role could be the perfect opportunity for you. This role does involve a reasonable amount of physical activity, so will enable you to keep your fitness levels high, as well as helping your mental health and wellbeing. You will have the satisfaction of knowing that you are making a genuine contribution to nature conservation, and you might find it rewarding to safeguard nature in the area you are working to protect. 

We are a friendly and supportive team. If you are volunteering to learn new skills and gain knowledge about wildlife conservation work, you will find that our team will be more than happy to help you on that journey.""";
                            :activityOrganisation id:64119bf12a79fbd15e8912b6;
                            :activityTitle "Practical Reserve Work (Thursday Garden maintenance volunteer at Flatford Wildlife Garden)";
                            :allowsRemoteParticipation true.
id:68f1b16cf7915f22a8e6ab60 :address "Flatford Wildlife Garden, Flatford Road, East Bergholt, Colchester, Suffolk, CO7 6UL, England";
                            :latitude "51.959711"^^xsd:double;
                            :longitude "1.020152"^^xsd:double.
id:68f229a206abd725874e1612 :cause id:64093b532eed5dcadba50895;
                            :organisationDescription "We are an independent Day Centre providing day care services to older people in our local community, supporting carers and deliver hot freshly cooked meals in our local area.";
